Page 1 Hyderabad: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia|Hyderabad, India}}
{{wikipedia|Hyderabad, Sindh}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Haidarabad}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|hi|हैदराबाद|tr=haidarābād}} / {{bor|en|ur|حیدرآباد|tr=haidarābād}}, from {{m|hi|हैदर}} / {{m|ur|حیدر|tr=haidar|t=lion}} + {{m|hi|-आबाद}} / {{m|ur|آباد|t=-ābād|pos=placename suffix}}. Named in honour of the [[Caliph]] {{w|Ali Ibn Abi Talib}}, nicknamed "Haidar" for his lion-like valour in battles.<ref name="Everett-Heath2005">Everett-Heath, John. ''Concise Dictionary of World Place Names'', Oxford University Press, 2005 p&nbsp;223 ({{ISBN|978-0-19-860537-9}})</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhaɪdəɹəbɑːd/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-Hyderabad.wav|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{place|en|caplc|s/Telangana|c/India}}.
# {{place|en|district|s/Telangana|c/India}}.
# {{place|en|A <<former state>>, landlocked in south-central <<c/India>>, which was ruled from 1724 until 1948 by a line of [[nizam]]s}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|title=Britannica Concise Encyclopedia|page=916|isbn=1593394926
|passage=At Indian partition in 1947, the nizam chose to resume '''Hyderabad's''' independent status, but India invaded the state (1948) and took control.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|title=The Indian Political Science Review|volume=16|page=225
|passage=Maududi was born in 1903 at Aurangabad in '''Hyderabad''', India, into a family with a long religious tradition.}}
# {{place|en|city|p/Sindh|c/Pakistan}}.

