Page 5 Ashgabat: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Aşgabat}}
* {{alter|en|Ashkabad}}
* {{alter|en|Ashkhabad||via Russian}}
* {{alter|en|Ashqabat}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|tk|Aşgabat}}, from {{der|en|fa-cls|عِشْق‌آبَاد|lit=city of love}}, compound of {{af|fa-cls|عِشْق<t:love>|آبَاد<t:city>|nocat=1}}. 

Alternatively, some historians believe that the city was originally named after Ashk/Arshk, the founder of the [[Arsacid]] Dynasty, and hold that the term {{l|fa-cls|عِشْق}} was a reinterpretation influenced by folk etymology.

