==Ottoman Turkish==
[[Image:Yalova districts.png|thumb|Yalova province]]

===Etymology===
This city was previously known as {{m|ota|یالاق آباد|tr=Yalak Âbâd}}, from {{m|ota|یالاق|tr=yalak|t=trough}} + {{m|ota|آباد|tr=âbâd|t=prosperous}}. The current name appeared only in the 18ᵗʰ century and is assumed to be a contraction of {{m|ota|یالی|tr=yalı|t=shore, strand, beach}} and {{m|ota|اوا|tr=ova|t=plain, lowland}}.

===Proper noun===
{{ota-proper noun|tr=yalova}}

# {{place|ota|city/and/province|in|r/[[East Marmara]] region|c/Turkey|t=Yalova}}
#: {{syn|ota|یالاق آباد|tr=Yalak Âbâd}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

