==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{af|ru|Москва́|-абад}}, the suffix likely from {{der|ru|fa|آباد}}, an ending commonly found in Central Asian place names, for example {{m|ru|Ашхабад||{{w|Ashgabat}}}}, {{m|ru|Исламабад||{{w|Islamabad}}}}, etc.

===Proper noun===
{{ru-proper noun+|Москваба́д}}

# {{lb|ru|informal|derogatory}} [[:w:Moscow|Moscow]], seen as a city with a high migrant population (mainly referring to migrants from either Central Asian countries or the Caucasus)

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|Москваба́д|n=sg}}

{{c|ru|Moscow}}
-------- end text --------
