==Sanskrit==

===Alternative scripts===
{{sa-alt}}

===Pronunciation===
{{sa-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
Of unclear origin. Has been compared to {{cog|la|alvus|t=belly, bowels}} and {{cog|lt|eldijà|t=canoe}}.

====Noun====
{{sa-noun|g=f}}

# a [[pitcher]], a [[small]] [[water]] [[jar]]

=====Declension=====
{{sa-decl-noun-f}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|sa|dra}}; compare {{cog|ta|ஆர்|t=common mountain ebony}} and {{m|ta|ஆரம்|t=sandalwood}}.

====Noun====
{{sa-noun|g=m}}

# [[ebony]], [[black]] ebony

=====Declension=====
{{sa-decl-noun-m}}

===Etymology 3===
Of {{uncertain|sa|nocap=1}} origin. Has been suggested to derive from {{inh|sa|inc-pro||*HaHlu}}, from {{inh|sa|iir-pro||*HaHlu}}, from {{inh|sa|ine-pro|*h₂eHlu||t=edible root}}, and thus be cognate with {{cog|la|ālium|t=onion, garlic}}. However, Mayrhofer considers this derivation unconvincing, perhaps due to the general principle of specific plant names usually being borrowed from local substrates rather than being inherited in Indo-European languages.

====Noun====
{{sa-noun|g=n}}

# an [[esculent]] [[root]], [[elephant foot yam]], {{taxlink|Amorphophallus paeoniifolius|species}} (aka {{taxlink|Arum campanulatum|species}})
# {{lb|sa|neologism}} [[potato]]

