Page 1 A: -------- begin text --------
{{also/a|a|ᴀ}}
{{TOC limit|2}}
{{character info}}
{{character info|Ａ}}

==Translingual==

===Etymology 1===
From the {{der|mul|ett|-}} letter {{m|ett|𐌀}}, from the {{der|mul|grc|-}} letter {{m|grc|Α||alpha}}, derived from the {{der|mul|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤀||[[aleph]]}}, from the {{der|mul|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓃾}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|mul|/a/|qq=most languages}}

====Letter====
{{head|mul|letters}}

# {{ng|The first letter of the [[Appendix:Latin script|basic modern Latin alphabet]].}}

=====See also=====
{{Latn-script}}
* [[Appendix:Variations of "a"]]

====Symbol====
{{head|mul|symbols}}

# {{ng|Marks the first item in a list.}}
#: {{ux|mul|'''A'''. Go to the store. B. Get some food. C. Return home. D. Eat.}}
# A hypothetical item or person designated the first, usually when there are more than one.
#: {{ux|mul|Person '''A''' had 5 apples, and person B...}}
# [[ten|Ten]], especially used in [[base]]s above ten, such as [[duodecimal]], [[hexadecimal]], [[vigesimal]] and so on.
#: {{ux|mul|Decimal 270 can be converted as duodecimal 1'''A'''6 or vigesimal D'''A'''.}}
#: {{lb|mul|computing}} ''The variable was a byte with value '''A'''0, or 160 in decimal.''
# A standard size of dry cell battery, slightly larger than [[AA]].<ref>{{R:OCD2|page=1}}</ref>
# {{rfv-sense|mul|fragment=A Translingual Symbol sense 5}} A system of paper sizes with similar proportions, as [[A0]], [[A1]], [[A2]], etc.<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=1}}</ref>
# {{rfv-sense|mul|fragment=A Translingual Symbol sense 6}} An academic grade lower than A+ but greater than A-.
# {{lb|mul|linguistics}} A [[wildcard]] for an [[open]] vowel
# {{bond credit rating|lt=1|s=1|f=1|a bond is [[upper-medium]] [[grade]] with low [[risk]] of [[default]]}}
# {{lb|mul|clothing}} {{ng|[[bra|Bra]] [[cup size]].}}

=====Related terms=====
{{rel-top|Letters sharing the same origin as "A"}}
* Arabic {{m|mul|ا||tr=a|alif}}
* Coptic {{m|mul|Ⲁ||tr=a|alfa}}
* Cyrillic {{m|mul|А|tr=A}}
* Devanāgari {{m|mul|अ||tr=a|aksara}}
* Greek {{m|mul|Α||tr=A|Alpha}}
* Hebrew {{m|mul|א||tr=a|aleph}}
* Phoenician {{m|mul|𐤀}}
* Syriac {{m|mul|ܐ||tr=a|alaph}}
{{rel-bottom}}

=====See also=====
* {{qualifier|previous}} [[9]], {{qualifier|next}} [[B]]

===Etymology 2===
The abbreviation of a variety of terms.

====Symbol====
{{head|mul|symbols}}

# {{lb|mul|element symbol|obsolete}} Symbol for the element Argon, {{ng|changed after 1956 to}} [[Ar]].
# {{lb|mul|chemistry|physics}} Symbol for {{l|en|mass number||{{l|en|nucleon number}}}}. {{abbreviation of|mul|{{der|mul|en|atomic mass number}}}}.
# {{lb|mul|geometry}} [[area|Area]].
# {{lb|mul|international standards}} {{n-g|A category of vehicle licence under the {{w|Vienna Convention on Road Traffic}}, referring to [[motorcycle]]s.}}

====Noun====
{{head|mul|nouns}}

# {{lb|mul|physics|[[International System of Units]]}} [[ampere|Ampere]], a unit of [[electrical current]].
# {{lb|mul|genetics}} [[IUPAC]] 1-letter abbreviation for [[adenine]] in genetic code.
# {{lb|mul|amino acid}} {{IUPAC-1|alanine}} in proteins.
#: {{syn|mul|Ala}}
# {{lb|mul|music}} {{l|en|alto|Alto}}.

====Proper noun====
{{head|mul|proper nouns}}

# {{lb|mul|vehicle-distinguishing signs}} [[Austria]].

