==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|la|i}}, [[minuscule]] of {{m|la|I}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|en|/aɪ/|/ɪ/|/i/}}
* {{sense|letter name}} {{enPR|ī}}, {{IPA|en|/aɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-i.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|aye|eye}}

====Letter====
{{head|en|letters|lower case||upper case|I|plural|is|or|i's}}

# {{Latn-def|en|letter|9|i}}

=====Usage notes=====
The English letter {{m|en|i}} represents many different sounds, often the diphthong {{IPAchar|/aɪ/}} (from Middle English {{IPAchar|/iː/}}), as in the pronoun {{m|en|I}}, or {{IPAchar|/ɪ/}} as in {{m|en|bit|b'''i'''t}}.

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letters/en/simple}}

====Number====
{{head|en|numeral symbols|lower case||upper case|I}}

# {{Latn-def|en|ordinal|9|i}}

====Noun====
{{head|en|nouns|cat2=countable nouns|plural|ies}}

# {{Latn-def|en|name|I|i}}
#* the position of an '''i'''-dot (the dot of an ''i)''
#* i-mutation, '''i'''-[[umlaut]]

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{l|en|eye}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|en|i-adjective|i-breve|dot the i's and cross the t's|i-dotter|i-dotting|i-mutation|i-stem|i-word|long i|short i}}

=====Translations=====
{{see translation subpage|Noun}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Latin script letter names/en/simple}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|ang|ic|iċ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/aɪ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪ|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|aye|eye}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|en|pronouns}}

# {{lb|en|nonstandard}} {{altcase|en|I}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Benjamin Stillingfleet|Benj[amin] Stillingfleet]]|title=Miscellaneous Tracts Relating to Natural History, Husbandry, and Physick. To Which Is Added the Calendar of Flora.|edition=2nd|location=London|publisher={{...|Printed: And sold by}} R. and J. Dodsley,{{nb...|in Pall-Mall}}; S. Baker,{{nb...|in York-Street, Covent-Garden}}; and T. Payne,{{nb...|at the Muse Gate}}|year=1762|pages=30 and 32|passage=Here follow ſome few lines in the original, which not underſtanding '''i''' have omitted. {{...}} Laſtly that amidſt ſo many viciſſitudes of fortune, to which I have been expoſed, amongſt all the goods, '''i''' ſay, and evils, the joyfull and gloomy, the pleaſing, and diſagreeable circumſtances of life, thou endowedſt me with an equal, conſtant, manly, and ſuperior ſpirit on every occaſion.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Also used in instant messaging due to limitations of entering capitals on a mobile phone's keypad.
* Sometimes to indicate informality, primarily in typed media

===Etymology 3===
Abbreviations.

# {{lb|en|stenoscript}} a word-initial letter ⟨i⟩
# {{lb|en|stenoscript}} the long vowel /aɪ/ at the end of a word, or before a final consonant that is not /dʒ, v, z/. (Note: the final consonant is not written.)
# {{lb|en|stenoscript}} the words {{m|en|if}}, {{m|en|is}}, {{m|en|it}}, {{m|en|its}}

