==Danish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|da|non|í}}, from {{inh|da|gem-pro|*in}}, from {{inh|da|ine-pro|*en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|da|i|s=1}}
* {{homophones|da|I}}
* {{rhymes|da|iː}}

===Preposition===
{{head|da|prepositions}}

# [[in]], [[inside]]
# {{n-g|Indicates exponentiation.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Tre '''i''' femte.|Three '''to the power of''' five.}} (short for tre i femte potens, three in fifth power). [note that the exponent is in the ordinal form]
# [[for]] (some duration)
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Jeg har boet her '''i''' tre år.|I have lived here '''for''' three years.}}
# {{n-g|Used to indicate a past time or period when something took place.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Han fyldte seks år '''i''' mandags.|He turned six years old '''on''' Monday.}}
# {{n-g|Used to indicate regular presence in a location.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Pigen går '''i''' gymnasiet og er 17 år |The girl goes '''to''' high school and is 17 years old.}}
# {{n-g|Used in conjunction with time to indicate a number of minutes before a full hour.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Fem minutter '''i''' tolv.|Five minutes '''to''' twelve.}}
# {{n-g|Used when indicating that something is happening or repeated a number of times within each time period .}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Tre gange '''i''' timen.|Three times '''a''' day}}
# {{n-g|Indicates affiliation with a profession.}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|da|Professor '''i''' fysik|Professor '''of''' physics}}

