==Old Irish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|sga|hí|hi}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sga|cel-pro|*en}} (compare {{cog|cy|yn}}), from {{inh|sga|ine-pro|*h₁én}} (compare {{cog|en|in}}, {{cog|la|in}}, {{cog|grc|ἐν}}).

The third-person singular masculine and neuter inflected dative form {{m|sga|and}} is ''not'' derived from a contraction with a pronoun. Instead, it was originally an adverb with an independent etymology. See its page for its etymology.

===Preposition===
{{head|sga|prepositions|triggers eclipsis}}

# [[in]] {{+obj|sga|dat}}
# [[into]] {{+obj|sga|acc}}
# [[in regard to]], [[as to]] {{+obj|sga|dat}}
# [[as]] {{+obj|sga|acc}}
{{seeCites|sga}}

====Inflection====
{{sga-prep-infl
|1sg         = [[indium]]([[indiumm|m]])
|1sg-em      = {{l|sga|indiumsa}}
|2sg         = {{l|sga|indiut}}
|2sg-em      = [[indiutsu|indiuts]]([[indiutsiu|i]])[[indiutsu|u]]
|3sgm-dat    = {{l|sga|and}}
|3sgm-dat-em = {{l|sga|andsom}}
|3sgm-acc    = {{l|sga|ind}}
|3sgm-acc-em = {{l|sga|indsom}}
|3sgf-dat    = {{l|sga|indi}}
|3sgf-acc    = {{l|sga|inte}}
|3sgf-acc-em = {{l|sga|intesi}}
|1pl         = {{l|sga|indiunn}}
|1pl-em      = {{l|sga|indiunni}}
|2pl         = {{l|sga|indib}}
|2pl-em      = {{l|sga|indibsi}}
|3pl-dat     = {{l|sga|indib}}
|3pl-dat-em  = [[indibsom]], [[indibsem]]
|3pl-acc     = {{l|sga|intiu}}
}}

Combinations with the definite article:
* {{l|sga|isin}} {{q|accusative masculine/feminine singular}}
* {{l|sga|issa}} {{q|accusative neuter singular}}
* {{l|sga|[[isin]][[isind|(d)]]}} {{q|dative singular}}
* {{l|sga|isna}} {{q|accusative plural}}
* {{l|sga|isnaib}} {{q|dative plural}}

Combinations with possessive determiners:
* {{l|sga|im||in my}} {{q|1st person singular}}
* {{l|sga|inna}}, {{l|sga|na||in his/her/its/their}} {{q|3rd person}}

The form {{m|sga||i}} is unchanged in combination with a relative pronoun.

