* Thai: {{t+|th|ที่}} {{attention|th|Did I add this at the correct sense of "that"?}}
* Vietnamese: {{t+|vi|mà}}
* Welsh: {{t+|cy|a}}, {{t+|cy|y}}
* Zealandic: {{t|zea|dien-a|m}}, {{t|zea|die-a|f|p}}, {{t|zea|dat-a|n}}, {{t|zea|da|n}} {{qualifier|all forms unconjugated}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|degree}} To a given [[extent]] or [[degree]].
## {{ng|Denoting an equal degree.}}
##: {{ux|en|Here's the measurement – the ribbon must be '''that''' long, no longer and no shorter.}}
## {{ng|Denoting 'as much', 'no less'.}}
##: {{ux|en|She said we waited for three hours, but I'm sure it wasn't '''that''' long.}}
##: {{ux|en|It didn't seem like ten miles, but actually it ''was'' '''that''' far.}}
# {{lb|en|degree|in negative constructions}} To a great [[extent]] or [[degree]]; very, [[particularly]].
#: {{syn|en|so}}
#: {{ux|en|I was seen quite quickly — I didn't have to wait '''that''' long.}}
#: {{ux|en|I did the run last year, and it wasn't '''that''' difficult.}}
# {{lb|en|informal|Britain|Australia|in positive constructions}} To such an extent; [[so]].
#: {{ux|en|Ooh, I was '''that''' happy I nearly kissed her.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1693|author=w:John Hacket|chapter=Scrinia reserata: a Memorial offered to the great Deservings of John Williams|title=Archbishop Williams
|passage=This was carried with '''that''' little noise that for a good space the vigilant Bishop was not awak'd with it.}}

