==Bulgarian==

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{bg-IPA|а}}

====Letter====
{{head|bg|letter|lower case||upper case|А}}

# {{Cyrl-def|bg|letter|1|а}}

====See also====
* {{list:Cyrillic script letters/bg}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{bg-IPA|а}}

====Particle====
{{head|bg|particles}}

# {{ngd|used in orders for emphasis}}: [[let’s]], [[just]]
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''' върви де!|Come on, go ahead!}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''' да идем на кино.|Let’s go to the pictures.}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''' удари ме, ако смееш.|Just you hit me, if you dare.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Кажи де, '''а''' кажи!|Speak up, do!}}
# [[just]], [[about to]], [[on the point of]], [[almost]]
#: {{ux|bg|разперила криле, '''а'''-'''а''' да хвръкне|with wings spread out, about to fly off}}

====Interjection====
{{head|bg|interjections}}

# {{ngd|used to express surprise or wonder}}: {{l|en|ah}}, {{l|en|oh}}, {{l|en|ha}}, [[why]]
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', ето къде си бил!|'''Ah''', there you are!}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', значи ти хареса.|'''Oh''', so you liked it.}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А'''! Не те видях.|'''Oh'''! I didn't see you there.}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', Джейн, ти ли си!|'''Why''' Jane, it's you!}}
# {{ngd|used to express pleasure, relief}}: {{l|en|ah}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', пролетните цветя.|'''Ah''', the flowers of spring.}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', спомням си старите времена.|'''Ah''', I remember the good old days.}}
# {{ngd|used when you are not certain about something and you would like confirmation}}: {{l|en|eh}}, {{l|en|well}}, {{l|en|right}}, or translated with a [[tag question]]
#: {{ux|bg|Хареса ти, '''а'''?|So, you liked it, '''eh'''/'''did you'''?}}
#: {{ux|bg|Утре заминаваш, '''а'''?|You're leaving tomorrow, '''right'''?}}
# {{lb|bg|colloquial}} {{ngd|used to indicate that one did not hear what was said}}: {{l|en|eh}}, {{l|en|huh}}
#: {{ux|bg|‘Не съм гладен.’ ‘'''А'''?’ ‘Казах, че не съм гладен.’|‘I'm not hungry.’ ‘Eh?’ ‘I said I'm not hungry.’}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А'''? Какво каза?|Huh? What did you say?}}
# {{ngd|used to express understanding, recognition, or realization}}: {{l|en|oh}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', значи така работело.|Oh, so that's how it works.}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', сега ми дойде наум!|Oh, I’ve just thought of it.}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', да, сетих се!|Oh, yes, I remember.}}
# {{ngd|used to express displeasure, objection}}
#: {{ux|bg|Изпуснал влака … ама работа, '''а'''!|So he missed the train … what a damned nuisance!}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', той ще ми каже!|He's not the one to tell me!}}
#: {{ux|bg|Ще ми се плезиш, '''а'''!|Don't stick out your tongue at me!}}
# {{ngd|used to express criticism or disapproval}}: [[now]]
#: {{ux|bg|'''А'''-'''а''', така не може!|'''Now''', this sort of thing can’t go on/won’t do!}}
#: {{ux|bg|'''А''', Били, така не се говори на майка си!|'''Now''', Billy, that's no way to talk to your mother!}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*a||and, but}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|bg|[a]|q1=stressed|[ɐ]|[ə]|q2=unstressed}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|bg|conjunctions}}

# {{ngd|used to describe how two facts are different}}: [[whereas]], [[while]]
#: {{ux|bg|Мислехме си, че е арогантна, '''а''' всъщност просто беше много срамежлива.|We thought she was arrogant, '''whereas''' in fact she was just very shy.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Той има кафяви очи, '''а''' децата му имат зелени очи.|He has brown eyes '''whereas''' his children have green eyes.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Едни се раждат, '''а''' други умират.|Some are born '''while''' others die.}}
# {{ngd|used to introduce an idea that is different or opposite to the idea that is desired, expected or that you have stated previously}}: {{l|en|but}}, [[yet]], [[rather]]
#: {{ux|bg|Не музиката не харесвам, '''а''' самата банда.|It's not the music I don't like '''but rather''' the band themselves.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Тя получи повишението не заради късмет, '''а''' с усърдна работа.|She got the promotion not by luck '''but''' by hard work.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Стените не бяха бели, '''а''' по-скоро мръсно сиви.|The walls were not white, '''but rather''' a sort of dirty grey.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Той има добра работа, '''а''' като че ли никога няма пари.|He has a good job, '''and yet''' he never seems to have any money.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Мислех си, че те познавам, '''а''' колко съм грешал.|I thought I knew you, '''yet''' how wrong I was.}}
#: {{ux|bg|Видях го вчера, '''а''' не днес.|I saw him yesterday, not today.}}
# {{ngd|used to start a new sentence or clause that continues or adds to a previous sentence or clause}}: {{l|en|and}}
#: {{ux|bg|Минаха години и всичко се промени. '''А''' той все още не се завръщаше.|Years passed and everything changed. '''And''' he still hadn't come back.}}

