==Russian==

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{q|stressed}} {{ru-IPA|а}} {{audio|ru|Ru-01-буква-А.ogg}}
* {{q|unstressed}} {{ru-IPA|ə}} 

====Letter====
{{ru-letter}}

# {{Cyrl-def|ru|letter|1|а}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Cyrillic script letters/ru}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun||n-in|-}}

# {{Cyrl-def|ru|name|А|а}}
# {{Latn-def|ru|name|A|a}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Cyrillic script letter names/ru}}

====References====
* {{R:ru:Dal}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ru|but}}
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*a||and, but}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*ō}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*h₁ōd}} (presumed to be the ablative of {{m|ine-pro|*éy|*éy, h₁e}}). Cognate with {{cog|lt|õ||and, but}}.

Possible link with {{cog|lt|ar̃||question particle}}. Compare {{cog|ru|а||and, but}}, {{m|ru|и||and}} and {{m|ru|да||and, but}} with {{cog|lt|ar̃||if, whether}}, {{m|lt|ir̃||and}} and {{m|lt|dár||still, yet}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|stressed}} {{ru-IPA}} {{audio|ru|Ru-а.ogg}}
* {{qualifier|unstressed}} {{ru-IPA-manual|[ə]}}
* {{qualifier|unstressed, pre-tonal}} {{ru-IPA-manual|[ɐ]}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|ru|conjunction|cat2=one-letter words}}

# [[but]], [[and]] {{gl|deviates from the preceding idea in some manner; introduces a new or different meaning, as opposed to {{m|ru|но}}, which usually indicates contrarity}}
#: {{uxi|ru|Сего́дня тепло́, '''а''' вчера́ бы́ло хо́лодно.|It is warm today, '''but''' yesterday it was cold.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|Э́то не я́блоко, '''а''' гру́ша.|This is not an apple, '''but''' a pear.}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''А''' что?|How come?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''а''' то|'''or''' else}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mhr|bor=1|а}}
* {{desc|izh|bor=1|a}}
* {{desc|sjd|bor=1|а}}
* {{desc|vot|bor=1|a}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|ru|а ве́дь}}
* {{l|ru|а и́менно}}
* {{l|ru|а то́}}

====References====
* {{R:ru:Dal}}

===Etymology 3===
Compare {{cog|lt|à}}, {{m|lt|õ}}, {{m|lt|oà||expression of pain, surprise}}, as well as {{cog|got|𐍉||ah!}}, {{cog|la|ā}}, {{m|la|āh||expression of pain, anger}}, {{cog|grc|ἆ||ah!}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ru|аа|а́-а}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-а.ogg}}

====Interjection====
{{head|ru|interjection|head=а!}}

# [[oh]]! {{gloss|expressing surprise or realization}}

====Particle====
{{head|ru|particles}}

# {{ngd|colloquial particle used to seek confirmation}}: [[eh]]
#: {{syn|ru|ась<q:vernacular, humorous>}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ты|Ты]] [[слышать|слы́шишь]] [[я|меня́]], '''а'''?|Do you hear me, eh?}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[ты|Ты]] [[прийти|придёшь]] [[сего́дня]], '''а'''?|So are you coming today, then?}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1831|author=w:ru:Александр Пушкин<t:{{w|Alexander Pushkin}}>|title=w:ru:[[Борис Годунов (трагедия)|Борис Годунов]]|chapter=Замок воеводы Мнишка в Самборе|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Richard Pevear and Larissa Volokhonsky|title2=Boris Godunov|location2=New York|publisher2=w:en:Vintage Books|year2=2023|page2=|pageurl2=
|text=Он говори́т с одно́й мое́й Мари́ной,<br>Мари́ною одно́ю за́нят он…<br>А де́ло-то на сва́дьбу страх похо́же.<br>Ну — ду́мал ты, призна́йся, Вишневе́цкий,<br>Что дочь моя́ цари́цей бу́дет? '''а'''?|t=He only wants to talk with my Marina,<br>Marina is the only one who interests him…<br>The matter looks terribly like a wedding. Well—<br>Confess, Vishnevetsky, did you ever think<br>That my daughter would become a tsaritsa? '''eh'''?}}

===Etymology 4===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-а.ogg}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|ru|pronoun|indeclinable}}

# {{lb|ru|criminal slang}} [[he]], [[she]] or [[it]] (used to point to a particular person)

=====References=====
* {{R:ru:Pirozhkov}}

{{topics|ru|Units of measure}}

==Serbo-Croatian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sh|/a/}}

===Etymology 1===

====Letter====
{{sh-letter|upper=А}}

# {{Cyrl-def|sh|letter|1}}

====See also====
* {{list:Cyrillic script letters/sh}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|sh|sla-pro|*a||and, but}}, from {{inh|sh|ine-bsl-pro|*ō}}.

====Conjunction====
{{sh-conjunction}}

# [[but]], [[and]] (compare {{m|sh|а̏ли}})
#: {{uxi|sh|учио сам ц(иј)ело посл(иј)еподне, а ништа нисам научио|I studied for the whole afternoon, but I didn't learn anything}}
#: {{uxi|sh|а како бисте ви то направили?|and how would you do that?}}
# [[while]] (on the contrary), [[whereas]]
#: {{uxi|sh|столови су црвени, а столице су зелене|the tables are red, whereas the chairs are green}}
# {{lb|sh|with {{m|sh|да}} {{m|sh|не}}}} [[without]] (usually after negative verbs)
#: {{uxi|sh|не могу се укључити у расправу, а да не направим неред|I cannot enter a discussion without making a mess}}
#: {{uxi|sh|одлази, а да није рекао ни збогом|he's leaving without even saying goodbye}}
# ({{m|sh||а}} {{m|sh|и̏па̄к}}) [[and]] [[yet]]
#: {{uxi|sh|прави пријатељ зна све о теби, а ипак те воли|the real friend knows everything about you, and yet he loves you}}
# ({{m|sh||а}} {{m|sh|ка̏моли}}) not to mention, [[let alone]]
#: {{uxi|sh|у мору лоших в(иј)ести тешко је остати објективан, а камоли оптимистичан|in the sea of bad news it's hard to stay objective, let alone optimistic}}
# ({{m|sh||а}} + {{m|sh|и}} + {{m|sh|да}}) [[even if]]
#: {{uxi|sh|а и да јесам то направио, не би то учинило неку разлику|even if I did it, it wouldn't have made much of a difference}}
# ({{m|sh||а}} + {{m|sh|и}}) and [[so]], and [[also]], and [[too]]
#: {{uxi|sh|свиђају ми се плавуше, а и ја се покојој свидим|I like blondes, and some of them even like me}}
#: {{uxi|sh|били су жалосни, а и ја сам|they were sad, and so am I}}

===Etymology 3===
Attested since the 15th century. Probably of onomatopoeic origin. Compare {{cog|sl|a}}, {{cog|ru|а}}, {{cog|lt|õ}}, {{cog|la|ō}} and {{cog|grc|ὦ}}. These could all derive from Proto-Indo-European interjection {{m|ine-pro||ō|oh, ah}}, but each form in individual languages could easily be an independent, expressive formation.

====Interjection====
{{sh-interjection}}

# [[oh]], [[ah]]
#: {{uxi|sh|а да?|oh really?}}

===References===
* {{R:sh:HJP|fQ%3D%3D}}
* {{R:sh:HJP|eg%3D%3D}}
* {{R:sh:Skok:1971||1|1}}

