===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme|usually}} {{IPA|he|/ʔ/}}
* {{qualifier|letter name}} {{IPA|he|/ˈʔalef/}}
* {{audio|he|LL-Q9288_(heb)-Uziel302-א.wav}}

===Letter===
{{head|he|letter|tr='|sc=Hebr|Hebrew letter}}

# [[aleph|Aleph]] or [[alef]]: the first letter of the [[Hebrew]] [[alphabet]], coming before {{l|he|ב}}.
# The [[numeral]] 1 in Hebrew numbering.

====Usage notes====
* In Modern Israeli Hebrew, {{m|he|א|tr=’||alef}} represents either a glottal stop ({{IPAchar|/ʔ/}}), or has no pronunciation besides that of the vowel attached to it. The pronunciation varies from group to group.
* {{m|he|א|tr=’||alef}}—along with the other guttural letters, {{m|he|ע|tr=ʿ||ayin}}, {{m|he|ר|tr=r||resh}}, {{m|he|ה|tr=h||he}}, and {{m|he|ח|tr=ḥ||ḥêṯ}}—cannot receive a dagesh (the dot in {{m|he|בּ|tr=b||bet}}, which can appear in most other Hebrew letters), although there are rare examples where the Masoretes added a dagesh to it.
* {{m|he|א|tr=’||alef}} is sometimes used to denote a vowel (usually {{IPAchar|/a/}}) in words of Aramaic and Arabic origin, in foreign names{{,}} and in some other borrowed words.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|he|מ-א׳ ועד ת׳|tr=miálef ve'ád tav}}
* {{l|he|א״א|tr=álef álef}}
* {{l|he|סוג א׳|tr=sug álef}}
* {{l|he|יום א׳|tr=yom álef}}
* {{l|he|אינו יודע צורת א׳|tr=einó yodéa' tzurát álef}}
* {{l|he|לא ב-א׳ רבתי|tr=lo beálef rabbatí}}
* {{l|he|אלפבית|tr=álef beit}}
* {{l|he|א׳ אפס|tr=álef éfes}}

====See also====
* {{list:Hebrew script letters/he}}

