==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|letter name}} {{ar-IPA|وَاو}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/w/|/uː/}}, {{non-gloss|silent}} (in Classical Arabic)
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/w/|/u(ː)/|/oː/}} (in Arabic dialects and loanwords)

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|head='''و '''/''' ‍و'''|tr=wāw}}

# The twenty-seventh letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ه}} and followed by {{l|ar|ي}}.

====Symbol====
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''و '''/''' ‍و'''|tr=wāw}}

# The sixth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ه}} and followed by {{l|ar|ز}}.

====See also====
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* {{l|ar|ؤ}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:AllPages/و|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|و}}]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*wa}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|וְ־|tr=wə-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|وَ}} {{qualifier|MSA}}
* {{IPA|ar|/wɪ/|/w/}} {{qualifier|dialectal}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-و.ogg}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|وَ}}

# [[and]], "[[comma]]", "[[semi-colon]]"; a [[divider]] of [[word]]s or [[clause]]s, [[particle]] of [[connection]] or [[continuation]] [[often]] [[unnecessary]] to [[render]] in [[translation]]
## [[yet]], [[but]]; [[versatile]] [[conjunction]] [[determine]]d by [[context]]
# [[while]], [[at]] [[the]] [[same]] [[time]], [[and]] [[also]] [[do]], [[simultaneous]]ly, to [[do]] [[this]] [[and]] to [[do]] [[that]] [[concurrent]]ly
#: {{uxi|ar|لَا تَأْكُلِ السَّمَكَ '''وَ'''تَشْرَبَ اللَّبَنَ|subst=وَ/وَ-|t=Do not eat fish '''and''' drink dairy; (Proverb about illnesses coming from bad combinations; originally the supposed increased risk of contracting leprosy, a myth stemming from fish scales and the white color of milk.)}}
#: {{uxi|ar|لَا تَنْهَ عَنْ خُلُقٍ '''وَ'''تَأْتِيَ مِثْلَهُ|subst=وَ/وَ-|t=Do not say to stay away from a behavior, '''while''' you come with the likes of it; (Practice what you preach.)}}
# particle of [[rephrasing]] or [[mark]]ing a [[clause]] of [[adposition]]; [[and]] [[in]] [[other]] [[word]]s, [[that]] [[is]] [[to]] [[say]], [[additional]]ly [[call]]ed, [[i.e.]]
# [[with]], [[and]] [[also]], [[additional]]ly (with following accusative)
## {{lb|ar|mathematics}} [[+]], [[add]]ed to
# particle [[denote|denot]]ing an [[oath]] (with following genitive)
#: {{uxi|ar|'''وَ'''ٱللّٰهِ|subst='''وَ'''ٱللّٰهِ/'''وَ-'''لّٰهِ|t='''By''' God; '''And''' I swear by God}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Arabic conjunctions and prepositions that have only one letter, such as {{m-self|ar|وَ}}, are written as a prefix.
** The connection to the following word may however ''exceptionally'' be cut off by quotation marks enclosing foreign terms, emoji and similar intrusions of meta elements in the language of the internet.
** Sometimes editions of {{w|List of Shia books|Arabic texts}} procured in {{w|Islamic Republic of Iran|Iran}} do not adhere to the rules, instead following the non-joining practice of {{cog|fa|و|tr=va, o|t=and}}.
* Arabic tends to use the conjunctions {{m-self|ar|وَ}} and {{m|ar|أَو|t=or}} between every [[conjunct]] in a list, contrasting with the English tendency to use {{m|en|and}} and {{m|en|or}} only between the final two.
*: {{ux|ar|[[كتاب|كُتُبٌ]] [[طرد|'''وَ'''طُرُودٌ]] [[ورق|'''وَ'''أَوْرَاقٌ]]|subst=وَ/وَ-|t=books, parcels{{,}} '''and''' papers|lit=books '''and''' parcels '''and''' papers}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|وَلٰكِنَّ|tr=wa-lākinna}}, {{l|ar|وَلٰكِنْ|tr=wa-lākin}}
* {{l|ar|وَلَا|tr=wa-lā}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|وَ}} {{qualifier|MSA}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-و.ogg}}

====Preposition====
{{ar-con|وَ}} {{qualifier|with a following accusative}}

# [[with]]
#: {{uxi|ar|سِرْتُ '''وَ'''طُلُوعَ الْفَجْرِ|subst=وَ/وَ-|t=I got out with sunrise.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|أَنَا '''وَ'''إيّاكُم|subst=وَ/وَ-|t=I with you}}

