==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|alef}} {{qualifier|Hebrew, Persian}}
* {{l|en|alif}} {{qualifier|Arabic}}
* {{l|en|alaph}} {{qualifier|Syriac}}, {{l|en|olaph}} {{qualifier|Western Syriac}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|he|אלף|tr=álef}}. {{doublet|en|alpha|alif}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɑˌlɛf/|/ˈɑˌlɪf/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The first letter of the [[Proto-Canaanite alphabet]], and its descendants in descended Semitic scripts, such as {{cog|phn|𐤀|pos=ʾaleph}}, {{cog|arc|𐡀}}, {{cog|syc|ܐ|pos='ālaph}}, {{cog|he|א|pos=aleph}} and {{cog|ar|ا|pos=ʾalif}}.
# (mathematics) The [[cardinality]] of an infinite [[well-ordered]] (or well-orderable) set.
#: ''The axiom of choice is equivalent to the proposition that every infinite cardinal is an aleph.''

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|en|aleph-beth}}
* {{l|en|aleph-null}}
* {{l|en|aleph-one}}
* {{l|en|aleph-zero}}
* {{l|en|since aleph}}
{{der-bottom}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|alpha}}

