==Persian==

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|fa|/b/|q=phoneme, all dialects}}
** {{IPA|fa|[β]|a=Early,_,Classical,after a vowel}}
** {{IPA|fa|[β]|[w]|a=Early,_,Classical,between vowels}}
*** The phonemes /b/ and /w/ were not strongly distinguished inter-vocally until late Classical Persian.
* {{q|letter name}} 
** {{IPA|fa|/bɑː/|/beː/|a=Classical,Dari}}
** {{IPA|fa|/bɒː/|/be/|a=Iran}}
*** {{audio|fa|Fa-ب.ogg|a=Iran}}
** {{IPA|fa|/bɔː/|/beː/|a=Tajik}}

====Letter====
{{head|fa|letter|head='''ب '''/''' ب‍ '''/''' ‍ب‍ '''/''' ‍ب'''|tr=be}}

# The second letter of the [[w:Perso-Arabic alphabet|Perso-Arabic alphabet]]. It is preceded by {{m|fa|ا}} and followed by {{m|fa|پ}}. Its name is {{l|fa|به|tr=be}} or {{l|fa||بِ|tr=be}}.

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|fa|pal||tr=bʾ|ts=bē|t=out, away, forth|pos=also preverbal particle of unclear additional meanings}}, ultimately from {{inh|fa|ine-pro|*bʰe}}.<ref>{{cite-journal|title=The Verbal Particle BE in Middle Persian|author=Thomas Jügel|year=2013|journal=Münchener Studien zur Sprachwissenschaft|volume=67|issue=1|pages=29—56|url=https://www.academia.edu/5864870/The_Verbal_Particle_BE_in_Middle_Persian}}</ref>

In Classical Persian the prefix did not indicate the subjunctive, but had diverse and generally vague meanings depending on the context. The development into a subjunctive marker went hand in hand with the displacement of the simple present by the durative present in {{m|fa|می|tr=mi-}}. Thereby ''be-'' became more and more associated with the subjunctive position and was ultimately grammaticalised in this function. The use of simple present for the subjunctive is now literary, while its use for the indicative is archaic/poetic.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|fa|/bi-/|/bij-/|a=Classical}}
* {{a|fa|Dari}} 
** {{IPA|fa|/bɪ-/}}
** {{IPA|fa|/bʊ-/|q1=before a syllable with the vowel {{IPAfont|/ʊ/}}}}
** {{IPA|fa|/bij-/|q1=before a vowel}}
* {{a|fa|IR}}
** {{IPA|fa|/be-/|q1=in general}}
*** {{audio|fa|Fa-ب.ogg|a=Iran}}
** {{IPA|fa|/bo-/|q1=before a syllable with vowel {{IPAfont|/o/}}}}
** {{IPA|fa|/bij-/|q1=before a vowel}}
* {{IPA|fa|/bi-/|/bij/|/bu/|a=Tajik}}

====Prefix====
{{head|fa|prefix|tr=be-|head=ب‍ـ}}

# {{n-g|Marks the present [[subjunctive]] of most verbs.}}
#: {{ux|fa|می‌خوام پانکراستو بخورم.|tr=mi-xâm pânkrâs-et-o '''bo'''-xoram.|t=I want to eat your pancreas.|inline=y}}
#* {{quote-journal|fa|url=https://per.euronews.com/2020/09/27/macron-called-for-lukashenko-to-step-down|journal={{w|Euronews|Euronews Persian}}|year=2020|text=واضح است که لوکاشنکو باید برود.|tr=vâze ast ke lukâšenko bâyad '''be'''-ravad.|t=It is clear that Lukashenko must go.|title=ماکرون: لوکاشنکو باید برود |trans-title=Macron: Lukashenko must go}}
# {{n-g|Marks the [[imperative]] of most verbs.}}
#: {{ux|fa|این را ببین.|tr=in-râ '''be'''-bin.|t=Look at this.|inline=y}}
#: {{ux|fa|راحت بخواب.|tr=râhat '''be'''-xâb.|t=Sleep well.|inline=y}}
# {{lb|fa|archaic}} {{n-g|Adds an [[emphatic]] sense to a verb in the simple past.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Unlike the other verbal prefix {{m|fa|می|tr=mi-}}, the negative prefix {{m|fa|ن|نـ|tr=na-}} replaces {{m|fa||ب‍ـ|tr=be-}} rather than attaching to it:

* {{m|fa|بگو|tr=be-gu|t=say!}} > {{m|fa||نگو|tr=na-gu|t=don't say!}}

The prefix is not used with most compound verbs whose verbal element is {{m|fa|کردن|tr=kardan}} or {{m|fa|شدن|tr=šodan}}; in these cases, the imperative or subjunctive is marked by the bare present stem. In literary language, it may be also omitted for other verbs.

The verbs {{m|fa|بودن|tr=budan|t=to be}} and {{m|fa|داشتن|tr=dâštan|t=to have}} are irregular: the imperative and subjunctive of the former uses the stem {{m|fa|باش|tr=bâš}} without {{m|fa||ب‍ـ|tr=be-}}, and the latter uses the past participle {{m|fa|داشته|tr=dâšte}} in conjunction with {{m|fa|بودن|tr=budan}}, e.g. {{m|fa|داشته باش|tr=dâšte bâš|t=have!}}

