{{head|ar|letter|head='''ت '''/''' ت‍ '''/''' ‍ت‍ '''/''' ‍ت'''|tr=tāʔ}}

# The third letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. Its name is {{l|ar|تَاء}} and it has the sound of English '''[[t]]'''. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ب}} and followed by {{l|ar|ث}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ت '''/''' ت‍ '''/''' ‍ت‍ '''/''' ‍ت'''|tr=tāʔ}}

# The twenty-second letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ش}} and followed by {{l|ar|ث}}.
# {{short for|ar|تِلِفون|tr=tilifōn|t=telephone (number)}} Used before phone numbers.
#: {{ux|ar|ت. 12345678|tr=-|t=Phone No. 12345678}}
# An [[emoticon]] representing a face with a large [[smile]], more commonly used on languages that use the Perso-Arabic script like Arabic, Farsi, and Urdu.
#: ''بإمكانك، نأمل، حضور حفل الشواء غدًا{{sic}} ''ت''' ''

