===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|en|id=article|inh|enm>a>article|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|a}}, {{m|enm|an}}, from {{inh|en|ang|an|ān|one; a; lone; sole}}. More at {{m|en|one}}. The "n" was gradually lost before consonants in almost all dialects by the 15th century. Cognate with {{cog|gsw|a|t=a, an}}, {{cog|vmf|a|t=a, an}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{q|stressed}} {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪ/}}
* {{q|unstressed}} {{IPA|en|/ə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-a-stressed.ogg|a=US,stressed}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-a-unstressed.ogg|a=US,unstressed}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪ|ə|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|her|aa=non-rhotic,unstressed}}

====Article====
{{head|en|articles}}

# An unspecified example of (something); {{n-g|the [[indefinite article#Noun|indefinite article]]}}. {{defdate|from before 1150}}<ref name=SOED>Brown, Lesley, (2003)</ref>
#: {{ux|en|There was '''a''' man here looking for you yesterday.}}
#* {{RQ:Irving Tour on the Prairies|chapter=XX|page=151|passage=He had another formidable difficulty in getting him across the river, where both horses stuck for '''a''' time in the mire, and Beatte was nearly unseated from his saddle by the force of the current and the struggles of his captive.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Haunted House|chapter=The Mortals in the House|page=6|column=1|passage=The young man thanked me, and took his leave with some little precipitation, after declining '''a''' glass of liquor.}}
#* {{RQ:Collins Moonstone|volume=III|part=Fourth Narrative. Extracted from the Journal of Ezra Jennings.|pages=185|passage=Speaking as '''a''' servant, I am deeply indebted to you. Speaking as '''a''' man, I consider you to be '''a''' person whose head is full of maggots, and I take up my testimony against your experiment as '''a''' delusion and a snare.}}
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|chapter=Preface|page=vii|passage=With fresh material, taxonomic conclusions are leavened by recognition that the material examined reflects the site it occupied; '''a''' herbarium packet gives one only '''a''' small fraction of the data desirable for sound conclusions. Herbarium material does not, indeed, allow one to extrapolate safely: what you see is what you get {{...}}}}
#* '''2005''', Emily Kingsley (lyricist), Kevin Clash (voice actor), “A Cookie is a Sometime Food”, ''Sesame Street'', season 36, Sesame Workshop:
#*: ''Hoots the Owl:'' Yes a, fruit, is '''a''' {{SIC}}, any, time, food!
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170925022505/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-4/3168920.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Anna, do you have a pen?  —  Yes. I have a pen in my bag. I have '''a''' (stressed) …
#*:: {{audio|en|Anna, do you have a pen.ogg|a=US}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Moya Lothian-Mclean|title=A nose ring, a bicycle, a Radiohead album: I'm becoming a total cliche – and I quite like it|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240511032818/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/mar/09/nose-ring-bicycle-radiohead-cliche-urban-millennial|date=9 March 2023|passage=In retrospect, I realise, I had been unconsciously devoting '''a''' large amount of energy to negative choice, a concept I'm borrowing and adapting from sociologist Eva Illouz's 2019 treatise, The End of Love (by way of '''a''' viral Paris Review essay).}}
#* {{RQ:New Yorker|author=Sarah Larson|title=When the C.I.A. Turned Writers Into Operatives|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240521204031/https://www.newyorker.com/culture/podcast-dept/when-the-cia-turned-writers-into-operatives|date=21 May 2024|passage=The C.I.A. infiltrated not just magazines, radio, and movies but youth organizations and movements like Abstract Expressionism; all were meant to inspire '''a''' reverence for democracy and freedom, '''a''' project that, in Walker's telling, often tips into absurdity.}}
# One; {{n-g|used before {{l|en|score}}, {{l|en|dozen}}, {{l|en|hundred}}, {{l|en|thousand}}, {{l|en|million}}, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|I've seen it happen '''a''' hundred times.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Peter Cheyney|title=w:Sinister Errand|location=London|publisher=[[w:Collins Crime Club|Collins]]|year=1945|year_published=1952|page=8|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sinistererrand0000pete/page/8/mode/1up|passage=Everybody drinks a lot in wartime, but it seemed to me that I must have drunk enough to float '''a''' couple of battleships.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Sara Hylton|title=Separate Lives|location=London|publisher=w:Piatkus|year=1999|page=93|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/separatelives0000hylt_q8l5/page/93/mode/1up|isbn=0749905018|passage=You've seen it '''a''' dozen times already.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|title=The economics of skiing in America|url=https://www.economist.com/united-states/2024/02/27/the-economics-of-skiing-in-america|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/VKGcX|archivedate=8 May 2024|date=27 February 2024|passage=By the time he gets onto a chair, the pristine powder snow below the lift has already been chopped up by '''a''' hundred tracks, and the line to get back up stretches the length of a football field.}}
# {{n-g|Used in some phrases denoting quantity, such as {{m|en|a few}}, {{m|en|a good many}}, a {{m|en|couple}}, {{m|en|a little}}, {{m|en|a bit}}, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|He's '''a''' bit thick, isn't he?}}
#: {{ux|en|They asked me '''a''' few questions.}}
#* {{RQ:Alcott Little Women|part=II|chapter=My Lord and Lady|page=315|passage=But I was going to say, that while I was dawdling about abroad, I saw '''a''' good many talented young fellows making all sorts of sacrifices, and enduring real hardships, that they might realize their dreams. Splendid fellows, some of them, working like heroes, poor and friendless, but so full of courage, patience and ambition, that I was ashamed of myself, and longed to give them a right good lift.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Pay Equity: Empirical Inquiries|editors=Robert T. Michael; [[w:Heidi Hartmann|Heidi I&#91;rmgard&#93; Hartmann]]; Brigid O'Farrell|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=w:National Academy Press|year=1989|page=3|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/payequityempiric0000unse/page/3/mode/1up|column=2|isbn=0309039789|passage=The main influence here is job tenure—the men had been at their specific jobs '''a''' good while longer than the women.}}
#* {{RQ:SciAm|author=René M. van Westen|author2=Henk A. Dijkstra|author3=Michael Kliphuis|title=If the Atlantic Ocean Loses Circulation, What Happens Next?|url=https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/if-the-atlantic-ocean-loses-circulation-what-happens-next/|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/yz75s|archivedate=13 February 2024|date=13 February 2024|passage=Twenty years after the movie's release, we know '''a''' lot more about the Atlantic Ocean's circulation. Instruments deployed in the ocean starting in 2004 show that the Atlantic Ocean circulation has observably slowed over the past two decades, possibly to its weakest state in almost a millennium.}}
## {{n-g|Used before a [[numeral#Noun|numeral]].}}
##: {{ux|en|There are '''a''' few hundred orders that need to be fulfilled by tomorrow.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Alan Villiers|title={{w|Whalers of the Midnight Sun}}:{{nb...|A Story of Modern Whaling in the Antarctic}}|location=New York, N.Y.; London|publisher=w:Charles Scribner's Sons|year=1934|page=154|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/whalersofmidnigh0000vill/page/154/mode/1up|passage=The blues were eating leisurely, swimming about and opening their great mouths, spouting and filling their enormous stomachs with intense satisfaction. They had no idea of danger. There must have been about fifteen of them, peacefully feeding. One of them, its belly gorged probably with '''a''' few trillion plankton, seemed to be lying asleep on the surface.}}
##* {{RQ:Wired|author=Brian Friedberg|title=The Dark Virality of a Hollywood Blood-Harvesting Conspiracy|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240515201623/https://www.wired.com/story/opinion-the-dark-virality-of-a-hollywood-blood-harvesting-conspiracy/|date=31 July 2020|passage=The impact of hidden virality can't be stopped by retroactively banning '''a''' few thousand Twitter accounts; it is an iterative, memetic phenomenon that outpaces terms of service.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Don Winslow|title=City of Dreams|location=London|publisher=w:HarperCollins Publishers|year=2023|page=332|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/cityofdreams0000donw/page/332/mode/1up|isbn=9780008507824|passage=That was on the first day's walk. It took him until day three, after '''a''' good ten miles, to ask her out.}}
# {{n-g|Used in some adverbial phrases denoting the degree or extent of an [[action#Noun|action]], such as {{m|en|a little}}, {{m|en|a bit}}, {{m|en|a lot}}, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|The door was opened '''a''' little.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Deane H. Shapiro, Jr.|title=Precision Nirvana|location=Englewood Cliffs, N.J.|publisher=w:Prentice Hall, Inc.|year=1978|page=104|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/precisionnirvana00shap/page/n129/mode/1up|isbn=0136955770|passage=If, for example, you ask a child what he likes to do, he may say he doesn't know. However, if you watch him during free time, and note that he plays basketball '''a''' lot, you may infer that this is a high-probability behavior, and he finds it reinforcing.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James H. S. McGregor|title=Paris From the Ground Up|location=Cambridge, M.A.; London|publisher=w:Belknap Press|year=2009|page=163|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/parisfromgroundu00mcgr/page/163/mode/1up|isbn=9780674033160|passage=The bridge was shifted '''a''' bit to the east and rebuilt, this time with the shops of money-changers along both sides.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=Dana G. Smith|title=Even a Little Alcohol Can Harm Your Health, Research Shows|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240510015031/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/13/well/mind/alcohol-health-effects.html|date=13 January 2023|passage=You don't need to go cold turkey to help your health. Even reducing '''a''' little bit can be beneficial, especially if you currently drink over the recommended limits.}}
# The same; [[one and the same]]. {{n-g|Used in phrases such as {{l|en|of a kind}}, {{l|en|birds of a feather}}, etc.}}
#: {{ux|en|We are of '''a''' mind on matters of morals.}}
#: {{ux|en|They're two of '''a''' kind.}}
# [[any#Determiner|Any]]; [[every#Determiner|every]]; {{n-g|used before a noun which has become modified to limit its scope.<ref>Gove, Philip Babcock, (1976)</ref>}}
#: {{ux|en|'''A''' man who dies intestate leaves his children troubles and difficulties.}}
# [[any#Determiner|Any]]; {{n-g|used with a negative to indicate not a single one.}}<ref name=OCD>Lindberg, Christine A. (2007)</ref>
#: {{ux|en|It was so dark that we couldn't see '''a''' thing.}}
#: {{ux|en|He fell all that way, and hasn't '''a''' bump on his head?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Stephen R. Lawhead|Stephen Lawhead]]|title=The Mystic Rose Book|series=Celtic Crusades|seriesvolume=III|location=London;{{nb...|New York, N.Y.; Sydney, NSW; Toronto, Ont.}}|publisher=[[w:Book Club Associates|BCA]]|year=2001|page=180|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/mysticrosebookce0000step/page/180/mode/1up|passage=No, it is impossible. My conscience would give me not '''a''' moment's peace if I let you go. I would never forgive myself.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Sherry D. Ficklin|title=Queen of Someday: A Stolen Empire Novel|location=[Colony, T.X.]|publisher=Clean Teen Publishing|year=2014|page=116|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/queenofsomedayst0000fick/page/116/mode/1up|isbn=1940534909|passage=When had my own feelings become so muddled and complicated? Before I take '''a''' single step, he catches my arm, turning me to him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Daphna Rabinovitch|chapter=Fudge Truffle Tart|title=The Baker in Me|location=Vancouver, B.C.|publisher=w:Whitecap Books|year=2016|page=204|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bakerinme0000rabi/page/204/mode/1up|isbn=9781770502420|passage=My friend Cindy's husband, Michael Zahavi, a true chocoholic if there ever was one, adores this tart. In fact, when I visited their cottage up in Muskoka, Ontario one summer and brought this along as a treat, he got up in the middle of the night to nosh away at it, leaving us sleepyheads with nary '''a''' crumb the next day.}}
# {{n-g|Used before an adjective that modifies a noun (singular or plural) delimited by a numeral.}}
#: {{ux|en|The lottery jackpot is worth '''a''' staggering three hundred million dollars.}}
#: {{ux|en|The holidays are '''a''' mere one week away.}}
# One; someone named; {{n-g|used before a person's name, suggesting that the speaker knows little about the person other than the name.}}<ref name=OED>Oxford University Press, (2023)</ref>
#: {{ux|en|We've received an interesting letter from '''a''' Mrs. Miggins of London.}}
# {{n-g|Used before an adjective modifying a person's name, typically used to emphasize that person's current condition or emotional state.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robert Hancock|title=Ruth Ellis: The Last Woman To Be Hanged|location=London|publisher=[[w:Orion Publishing Group|Orion]]|year=1963|year_published=1993|page=35|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/ruthellis0000robe/page/35/mode/1up|isbn=9781857971118|passage=At Waterloo she asked George for £5 and said that she would go home by tube, and '''a''' relieved George watched her descend the Underground steps.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=David J. Bailey|title=The Storm|location=London|publisher=[[w:Austin Macauley Publishers|Austin Macauley Publishers Ltd.]]|year=2016|page=147|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/isbn_9781785548260/page/147/mode/1up|isbn=9781785548277|passage="There, I think that's done it," declared '''a''' triumphant John, "we just need to try it with the bar now, where is it?"}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2018|journal={{w|Associated Press}}|title=Rwandan court drops all charges against opposition figure|text="I will continue my campaign to fight for the rights of all Rwandans," '''a''' surprised but happy Rwigara told reporters after celebrating.}}
# Someone or something like; similar to; {{n-g|used before a [[proper noun#Noun|proper noun]] to create an example out of it}}.<ref name=OCD/> 
#: {{ux|en|The center of the village was becoming '''a''' Times Square.}}
#: {{ux|en|The man is '''a''' regular Romeo.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Frederic V. Grunfeld|title=Rodin: A Biography|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Henry Holt and Company|year=1987|page=88|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/rodinbiography00grun/page/88/mode/1up|isbn=0805002790|passage={{quote-gloss|Jules}} Pécher actually sculpted '''a''' sort of Statue of Liberty for the centerpiece of the monument, but for the rest he thought it advisable to call in Van Rasbourgh, and Rodin thus became a ghost sculptor to a ghost sculptor.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ed Macy|title=Hellfire|location=London|publisher=w:Harper Press|year=2009|page=134|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/hellfire0000macy_b2w2/page/134/mode/1up|isbn=9780007288212|passage=Billy fancied himself as a bit of '''a''' Han Solo, but he shook his head. 'Stop being a wuss.' He grinned. 'Your go.'}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Laura Erickson|title=The Love Lives of Birds: Courting and Mating Rituals|location=North Adams, M.A.|publisher=w:Storey Publishing|year=2020|page=81|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/lovelivesofbirds0000eric/page/81/mode/1up|isbn=9781635862751|passage=For the first 5 or 6 days after the eggs hatch, the mother spends most of her time keeping the chicks warm while the father provides most of their meals. All that work may be what prompts the female to leave the family. They share feeding duties more equally during the next week or 10 days, until the young leave the nest. Producing a second batch is easier if she skips the last grueling week or two of provisioning fledglings. She can recharge her batteries by moseying off and, while on vacation, looking for '''a''' new Casanova.}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{mainapp|English articles#Indefinite articles}}
* In standard English, the article ''a'' is used before consonant sounds, while ''[[an]]'' is used before vowel sounds; for more, see [[an#Usage_notes|''the usage notes about an'']].

