===Etymology 1===

====Article====
{{h|ro|article form}}

# {{feminine singular of|ro|al||of|pos=possessive article}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ro|la|ad}}, from {{inh|ro|ine-pro|*ád||near; at}}.

====Preposition====
{{ro-prep}}

# {{lb|ro|used with infinitive verbs}} ''the infinitive marker:'' [[to]]
#: {{uxi|ro|'''a''' fi|'''to''' be}}
# {{lb|ro|obsolete}} [[at]] (now almost completely replaced by {{m|ro|la}})
