==Persian==

===Etymology===
From the Arabic letter of the same form, with the phonetic value [[w:Voiced dental fricative|[ð]]].

===Pronunciation===
Phoneme: 
* {{IPA|fa|/z/}}

Letter name: 
{{fa-IPA|zāl|cls=ðāl,zāl}}

===Letter===
{{head|fa|letter|tr=z}}

# The eleventh letter of the [[w:Perso-Arabic alphabet|Perso-Arabic alphabet]]. Its name is {{m|fa|ذال|tr=zâl}}.

====Usage notes====
In Classical Persian, the letters' phoneme was irregularly pronounced as [[w:Voiced dental fricative|[ð]]] or as [[w:/z/|[z]]]. Modern varieties of Persian lack the letter's original Arabic phoneme [ð] entirely, and have shifted the phoneme [ð] to [z].

