==Arabic==

===Etymology===
From the Nabataean letter {{m|arc-nab|𐢙|tr=ṣ|t=ṣade}}, derived from the {{der|mul|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤑|tr=ṣ|t=ṣade}}, from an uncertain {{der|mul|egy|-}} hieroglyph ({{m|egy|𓇑}}?). See also {{m|syc|ܨ|tr=ṣ|t=ṣade}}, {{m|he|צ|tr=ts|t=tsadi}}, Cyrillic {{m|mul|Ц|sc=Cyrl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/sˤaːd/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/sˤ/}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ص '''/''' ص‍ '''/''' ‍ص‍ '''/''' ‍ص'''|tr=ṣād}}

# The fourteenth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ش}} and followed by {{l|ar|ض}}.
# [[Y]], unknown variable.
# [[a.m.]], before [[noon]] (abbreviation of {{l|ar|صباحا}})
#: See also: {{l|ar|م}}

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ص '''/''' ص‍ '''/''' ‍ص‍ '''/''' ‍ص'''|tr=ṣād}}

# The eighteenth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[Appendix:Abjad numerals|abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ف}} and followed by {{l|ar|ق}}.

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|ص|f|tr=ṣād}}

# The 38th [[sura]] (chapter) of the [[Qur'an]].

===See also===
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/ص|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|ص}}]]

