==Translingual==

===Letter===
{{mul-letter|sc=Arab}}

# Arabic letter ''ḍād''

==Arabic==

===Etymology===
It is hypothesized that the original pronunciation of the letter was a pharyngealised lateral fricative {{IPAchar|/ɮˤ/}}. Early on, its sound was merged with {{m|ar|ظ}} {{IPAchar|/ðˤ/}}, a merger that is reflected in all colloquial dialects. In dialects with stopping of dental fricatives, both were then shifted further to {{IPAchar|/dˤ/}}. When the ability to produce the sound {{IPAchar|/ɮˤ/}} waned some time after its loss from actual speech, the Quran readers reassigned the stop {{IPAchar|/dˤ/}} to {{m|ar||ض}} in order to maintain its distinction from {{m|ar||ظ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/dˤaːd/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}}
** {{IPA|ar|/dˤ/}} {{q|standard}}
** {{IPA|ar|/ðˤ/}} {{q|commonly in the Arabian Peninsula, Iraq and Tunisia.}}
** {{IPA|ar|/ɮˤ/}} {{q|hypothesized pronunciation; classical Arabic}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ض '''/''' ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض'''|tr=ḍād}}

# The fifteenth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ص}} and followed by {{l|ar|ط}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|لغة الضاد}}

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ض '''/''' ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض'''|tr=ḍād}}

# The twenty-sixth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ذ}} and followed by {{l|ar|ظ}}.

===See also===
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/ض|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|ض}}]]

