==Persian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|letter name}}
** {{IPA|fa|/ajn/|[ʔäjn]|a=Classical,Dari}}
** {{IPA|fa|/ejn/|[ʔejn~ʔajn]|a=Iran}}
* {{q|phonemes}} 
** {{IPA|fa|[ʔ]|a=formal,all dialects|qq=or deleted}}
** {{IPA|fa|[ɑː]|[oː]|[eː]|[w]|[j]|a=colloquial,Dari|qq=or deleted}}
* {{audio|fa|Fa-ع.ogg|a=Iran}}

* homophones: {{m|fa|ا|t=alif/alef}} (word-initial), {{m|fa|ء|t=hamza/hamze}} (other positions).

===Letter===
{{head|fa|letter|head=عـ / ـعـ / ـع / ع|tr='ayn ''or'' 'eyn}}

# The twenty-first letter of the [[w:Perso-Arabic alphabet|Perso-Arabic alphabet]]. It is preceded by {{lang|fa|[[ظ#Persian|ظ]]}} and followed by {{lang|fa|[[غ#Persian|غ]]}}. Its name is {{l|fa|عین}}.

====Usage notes====
* Since Persian approximated the Arabic {{m|ar|ع|tr=-}} (/ʕ/, "Voiced pharyngeal fricative") to a glottal stop /ʔ/, {{m|fa|ع}} does not have a distinct phoneme. As the glottal stop was already represented by the {{m|fa|ء|t=hamza/hamze}} in medial and final positions and {{m|fa-cls|ا|t=alif/alef}} in word-initial positions.

