==South Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|لِ}}.

===Preposition===
{{ajp-prep|head=لـ|tr=la-}}

# [[to]] {{q|someone}}; [[belonging]] to; [[for]]
# [[to]] {{q|a place}}
#: {{syn|ajp|على|tr=ʕala}}
# [[until]], [[up to]]
#: {{syn|ajp|حتّى|لحدّ|tr1=ḥatta|tr2=la-ḥadd}}

===Conjunction===
{{ajp-conjunction|head=لـ|tr=la-}}

# [[so that]] {{q|before a subjunctive verb}}
#: {{syn|ajp|حتّى|عشان|منشان|tr1=ḥatta-|tr2=ʕašan|tr3=minšān}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ajp|suffix|head=ـلـ|tr=-l-, il, -ill-}}

# [[to]]; [[for]] {{lb|ajp|indirect object suffix with an attached enclitic pronoun}}
#: {{syn|ajp|إلـ|tr=ʔil-|q=detached version for emphasis}}

====Usage notes====
* This suffix is attached to a verb expressing the indirect object.
* If the verb ends in a consonant cluster, the "-l-" is geminated and the stress shifts before an enclitic pronoun starting with a vowel.

====Inflection====
{{ajp-prep-inflection
|base={{l-self|ajp|ـلـ|tr=-l-}}
|1s={{l|ajp|ـلي|tr=-li, -illi}}
|2ms={{l|ajp|ـلك|tr=-lak, -illak}}
|2fs={{l|ajp|ـلك|tr=-lek, -illek}}
|3ms={{l|ajp|ـله|tr=-lo, -illo}}
|3fs={{l|ajp|ـلها|tr=-lha, -ilha}}
|1p={{l|ajp|ـلنا|tr=-lna, -ilna}}
|2p={{l|ajp|ـلكم|tr=-lkom, ilkom}}
|3p={{l|ajp|ـلهم|tr=-lhom, ihom}}
}}

