Page 61 fatha: -------- begin text --------
{{also|fatHa|fatḥa|faþa}}
==English==
[[Image:00-Fatha.png|thumb|right|A fatḥa]]

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|ar|فَتْحَة||an [[opening]]}}, {{ar-instance noun|nocat=1|lc=1}} of the verb {{m|ar|فَتَحَ||to [[open]]}}. Refers to the mouth position when pronouncing the {{IPAchar|/a/}} vowel.
{{root|en|ar|ف ت ح}} {{doublet|en|patach|ptaha}}, denoting the open vowel in the Hebrew and Syriac scripts.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|fatḥa}}, {{l|en|fatHa}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/fæt.ħæh/|a=UK}}

====Noun====
{{examples|{{l|ar||دَ}}:&nbsp; {{IPAchar|/da/}}.<br> {{l|ar||دَا}} or {{l|ar||دَى}}:&nbsp; {{IPAchar|/daː/}}}}
{{en-noun}}

# In [[Arabic]] [[script]], the [[vowel]] point for ''[[a]]'', appearing as a [[diagonal]] [[line]] placed above a letter (&thinsp;[[َ|{{lang|ar|ـَ}}]]&thinsp;) and designating a short ''a'' {{IPAchar|/a/}}. If the Arabic letters {{m|ar|ا}} (&lrm;{{m|ar|أَلِف}}) or {{m|ar|ى}} (&lrm;{{m|ar|أَلِف مَقْصُورَة}}) immediately follow, it indicates a long ''ā'' {{IPAchar|/aː/}}.
# The vowel designated by this mark.

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|in the Arabic script, the vowel point for "a" (fatḥa)}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|فَتْحَة|f}}
* Azerbaijani: {{t|az|fəthə}}
* Chinese:
*: Mandarin: {{t|cmn|開口符|tr=kāikǒufú}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|fatha}}
* French: {{t+|fr|fatha|m|f}}
* German: {{t|de|Fatha|n}}
* Japanese: {{t|ja|ファトハ|tr=fatoha}}
* Kazakh: {{t|kk|фатха}}
* Korean: {{t|ko|파트하}}
* Kurdish:
*: Central Kurdish: {{t+|ckb|سەر}}
*: Northern Kurdish: {{t+|kmr|fetha}}
* Malay: {{t|ms|baris atas}}, {{t|ms|baris di atas}}, {{t|ms|fathah}}
* Pashto: {{t+|ps|فتحه|f|tr=fatha}}, {{t+|ps|زور|m|tr=zor}}
* Persian: 
*: Classical Persian: {{t+|fa-cls|فَتْحَه}}, {{t+|fa-cls|زَبَر}}
*: Dari: {{t+|prs|فَتْحَه}}, {{t+|prs|زَبَر}}
*: Iranian Persian: {{t+|fa-ira|فَتْحِه}}, {{t+|fa-ira|زِبَر}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|фа́тха|f}}
* Tajik: {{t|tg|фатҳа}}, {{t|tg|забар}}
* Turkish: {{t+|tr|fetha}}, {{t+|tr|üstün}}
* Urdu: {{t|ur|زَبَر|m}}, {{t|ur|فَتْحَہ|m}}
* Uzbek: {{t+|uz|fatha}}, {{t+|uz|zabar}}
{{trans-bottom}}

====See also====
* {{pedia|Arabic diacritics}}
* {{l|en|kasra}}
* {{l|en|damma}} ([[ḍamma]])
* {{l|en|sukun}} ([[sukūn]])
* {{l|en|shadda}} ([[šadda]])
* {{l|en|tashkil}}, {{l|en|taškīl}}

===Etymology 2===
Alteration of {{m|en|father}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/fæðæ/|a=Geordie}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Geordie}} [[father]]

===Anagrams===
