==Kazakh==
{{kk-regional|[[У]], [[у]]|ۋ}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|kk|/waw ˌyʃ noˈqat/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|kk|/uw/|/ʊw/}} {{qualifier|back}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|kk|/ʉw/|/yw/}} {{qualifier|front}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|kk|/w/}} {{qualifier|consonantal}}

===Letter===
{{head|kk|letter|tr=w}}

# The twenty-sixth letter of the [[Kazakh]] in Arabic Script. It represents the [[Cyrillic]] letter [[У]].

====Forms====
{{ArabForm2}}

====Usage notes====
* Represents the back vowel dipthong /uw/ or /ʊw/, unless a small [[ٴ|ء]] (hamza) was placed in the beginning of the word. In Kazakh the Hamza marks that all vowels in the following word are fronted. 
* The letter ۋ cannot act as a vowel in the beginning of a word or when it is written proceeding another vowel. When ۋ is unable to make a vowel sound, it becomes the consonant sound /w/.

====See also====
* Previous letter: {{l|kk|ۇ}}
* Next letter: {{l|kk|ۆ}}
* {{list:Arabic script letters/kk}}

