# Alif [[maddah]]. A double-alif used to write the sequence {{IPAchar|/ʔaː/}}.

===Particle===
{{ar-particle|آ|tr=ʾā-}}

# A form of the initial interrogative particle that indicates a yes-or-no question. As it is written together with the following word, when this word begins with {{l|ar|ال|t=the}} they are orthographically morphed together and written with a {{l|ar|مَدَّة|tr=|}} diacritic instead of maintaining both.
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|10:59
|passage=قُلۡ أَرَءَيۡتُم مَّاۤ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّٰهُ لَكُم مِّن رِّزۡقࣲ فَجَعَلۡتُم مِّنۡهُ حَرَامࣰا وَحَلَـٰلࣰا قُلۡ '''ءَاۤللَّهُ''' أَذِنَ لَكُمۡ&nbsp;ۖ أَمۡ عَلَى ٱللَّٰهِ تَفۡتَرُونَ
|translation=<small>Sahih International: </small>Say, "Have you seen what Allah has sent down to you of provision of which you have made [some] lawful and [some] unlawful?" Say, "'''Has Allah''' permitted you [to do so], or do you invent [something] about Allah?"
|transliteration=qul ʾa-raʾaytum mā ʾanzala l-lahu lakum min rizqin fa-jaʿaltum minhu ḥarāman wa-ḥalālan qul '''ʾāllāhu''' ʾaḏina lakum ʾam ʿalā llāhi taftarūna}}

