===Alternative forms===
* Also the final or isolated form of [[ي]] in the Nile Valley, when typed on electronic devices, which looks similar in shape to the Persian [[ی]] in its final or isolated form.

===Etymology 1===

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|tr=-ā|head=ى}}
{{ArabForm}}

# Only written in the final position, transliterated ''ā''. Also called {{l|ar|أَلِف لَيِّنَة|gloss=flexible alif}}. In the rare case of a ''[[rasm]]'' version of Quran, it is the ''[[ي|yāʾ]]'' version.
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|19|30|passage=قَالَ إِنِّی عَبۡدُ ٱللَّهِ ءَاتَىٰنِیَ ٱلۡكِتَـٰبَ وَجَعَلَنِی نَبِیࣰّا|translation=Jesus declared, “I am truly a servant of Allah. He has destined me to be given the Scripture and to be a prophet.}}

