===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔalp-}}.

====Numeral====
{{number box|ar|1000}}
{{ar-numeral|أَلْف|m|d=أَلْفَانِ|pl=آلَاف|pl2=أُلُوف}}

# [[thousand]]
#: {{m|ar||أَلْفُ لَيْلَةٍ وَلَيْلَةٌ}} — One thousand and one nights (lit. "a thousand nights and a night")

=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|ar|أَلْف}} is a noun. When used with a corresponding noun, it governs that noun in the genitive singular, e.g. {{m|ar|أَلْفُ لَيْلَةٍ|t=one thousand nights}}. When used as part of larger numbers (2,000, 20,000, etc.), it behaves as a normal masculine noun, e.g. {{m|ar|أَلْفَانِ|t=two thousand}}, {{m|ar|خَمْسَةُ آلَافٍ|t=five thousand}}, {{m|ar|عِشْرُونَ أَلْفًا|t=twenty thousand}}.

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَلْف|pl=آلَاف|pl2=أُلُوف|pos=numeral}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|أَلْفِيَّة}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mt|elf}}
* {{desc|ary|ألف|tr=ʔalf}}
* {{desc|aa|álfi|bor=1}}
* {{desc|mfz|alp|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|elfu|bor=1}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔalap-|t=to be familiar with}}. From the root {{ar-root|ء ل ف}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|i|a}}

# to be or become [[familiar]] with, to become [[accustomed]], to [[share]] the [[yoke]], to [[be]] or [[become]] [[amicable]] or [[tame]]
#* {{RQ:Awwam|27|21|volume=2|pages=284–285|passage=وقيل أنه إذا طليت خلايا من داخلها بعصارة ورقه '''ألف'''ها النحل وأنجلبت إليها وقيل من ترنجان نوع بري نقول ضد ذلك وهو إذا طرح مع النحلة أحرجها.|translation=And it is said (about the lemon-balm ''[[Melissa officinalis]]'') that when one daubs beehives from the inner with an extract pressed from its leaves then the bees '''approve''' of it and are attracted to them and it is said of the lemon-balm’s wild form, the dead-nettle ({{taxlink|Lamium flexuosum|species}}), that one has to say against that that when it is advanced to a bee it drives it out.}}

