* {{qualifier|phoneme}} {{IPA|ckb|[v]}}

===Letter===
{{head|ckb|letter|sc=Arab|head='''ڤ '''/'''ـڤـ'''/''' ‍ڤـ'''/'''ـڤ'''|tr=v}}

# {{n-g|A letter of the Kurdish-Arabic alphabet, pronounced {{IPAchar|[v]}}}}

==Egyptian Arabic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|arz|/fe be ˈtælæt ˈnoʔɑtˤ/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|arz|/v/}}

===Letter===
{{head|arz|letter|head=ڤ|tr=fe be-tálat nóʾaṭ}} (fe with three dots)

# {{rfdef|arz}}

====Usage notes====
{{l|arz|ڤ|tr=fe be-tálat nóʔaṭ}} is not considered a distinct letter, but a variant of {{l|arz|ف|tr=fe}} that is sometimes used to write foreign names and loanwords with the phoneme {{IPA|arz|/v/}}. It can be written and pronounced as a {{l|arz|ف|tr=fe}} instead.

====Forms====
{{ArabForm}}

====See also====
* {{l|arz|پ|tr=be be-talat noʔaṭ}}
* {{l|arz|چ|tr=gim be-talat noʔaṭ}}

