===Nasalisation===
{{l|ur|غُنَائِیَّت}}

'''Nasalisation''' in Urdu typically occurs in four ways: 

# {{l|ur|غُنَّہ}} (or {{m|ur|نُونِ غُنَّہ}})
#: [[nasalization]] that occurs after the previous letter {{gl|ie. {{m|ur|رَن٘گ}} / {{m|ur|ڈَھن٘گ}} / {{m|ur|سَن٘گ}}}} – represented with the ''Noon Ghunna'' diacritic.
# {{l|ur|مَغْنُونَہ}}
#: [[nasalization]] that occurs blending with the preceding letter {{gl|ie. {{m|ur|آن٘چَل}} / {{m|ur|سَن٘وَرْنا}} / {{m|ur|کُن٘وارا}}}} – represented with the ''Noon Ghunna'' diacritic.
# {{l|ur|نُون بَطور مِیم}}
#: the [[nasalization]] which is pronounced as an 'm' {{gl|ie. {{m|ur|اَن٘بار}} / {{m|ur|سُن٘بَل}}}} – represented with the ''Noon Ghunna'' diacritic. 
# {{l|ur|نُونِ مَخْلُوط}}
#: the [[nasal]] (alveolar) consonant {{gl|ie. {{m|ur|دَھنْدَہ}} / {{m|ur|بَنْدَر}}}}

