Page 145 Template:ar-noun-inf-cons/documentation: Skipped, no changes
Page 145 Template:ar-noun-inf-cons/documentation: -------- begin text --------
{{documentation subpage}}
This template is for displaying the headword line of Arabic nouns in the informal/construct-state form, principally for nouns whose lemma ends in {{m|ar|ـٍ}} (e.g. {{m|ar|وَادٍ||[[valley]]}} and whose informal and nominative/genitive construct-state and definite-state forms end in {{m|ar|ـِي}}, written in unvocalized text with an extra letter. The reason to include a special entry for the informal/construct-state form is the fact that it is spelled differently in unvocalized text from the lemma, which is not the case for most nouns. This template can also be used for nouns whose lemma ends in {{m|ar|ـًى}} (e.g. {{m|ar|مُسْتَشْفًى||[[hospital]]}}) or {{m|ar|ـًا}} (e.g. {{m|ar|عَصًا||[[stick]]}}) by specifying the parameter {{para|acc|y}}, but there is less need to do so because the informal/construct-state form has the same unvocalized spelling as the lemma.

This template should go in the place where the headword-line template normally goes, but also provides the definition.

The equivalent template for adjectives is {{temp|ar-adj-inf-def}}.

==Parameters==
; {{para|1}}
: Vocalized headword.
; {{para|2}}
: Corresponding lemma form (i.e. the indefinite nominative).
; {{para|g}}
: Gender; defaults to <tt>m</tt> (masculine).
; {{para|gloss}}
: Gloss (definition) of word.
; {{para|acc|y}}
: Indicate that this form serves as the accusative construct state as well as the nominative and genitive. This is used for forms ending in ''-ā'', e.g. {{m|ar|مُسْتَشْفَى}}, construct state (all cases) of {{m|ar|مُسْتَشْفًى||[[hospital]]}}.

==Examples==
An entry should be formatted as follows, without a following definition:

<pre>
==Arabic==

===Noun===
{{ar-noun-inf-cons|وَادِي|وَادٍ|g=m|gloss=[[valley]]}}
</pre>

The code <code><nowiki>{{ar-noun-inf-cons|وَادِي|وَادٍ|g=m|gloss=[[valley]]}}</nowiki></code> produces the following:

{{ar-noun-inf-cons|وَادِي|وَادٍ|g=m|gloss=[[valley]]}}

This can also be used for plural construct states, using code as follows:

<code><nowiki>{{ar-noun-inf-cons|أَيَادِي|أَيَادٍ|g=p|gloss=[[hands]]}}</nowiki></code>

<includeonly>
[[Category:Arabic headword-line templates|noun-inf-cons]]
</includeonly>
-------- end text --------
