==Kazakh==
{{kk-regional|[[Ұ]], [[ұ]]/[[Ү]], [[ү]]|ۇ|[[Ū]], [[ū]]/[[Ü]], [[ü]]}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|kk|/waw ˌdamˈma/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|kk|/u/|/ʊ/}} {{qualifier|back}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|kk|/ʉ/|/y/}} {{qualifier|front}}

===Letter===
{{head|kk|letter|tr=u, ü}}

# The twenty-fifth letter of the [[Kazakh]] in Arabic Script. It represents the [[Cyrillic]] letter [[Ұ]] or [[Ү]].

====Forms====
{{ArabForm2}}

====Usage notes====
* Represents the back vowel phonemes /u/ and /ʊ/. Unless a small [[ٴ|ء]] (hamza) was placed in the beginning of the word. In Kazakh, the hamza marks that all vowels in the following word are fronted. If ۇ is the first letter and is representing a front vowel, it is combined with the hamza and the varient [[ٷ]] is used.

====See also====
* {{l|kk|ٷ}} (Word-initial, front-vowel)
* Previous letter: {{l|kk|و}}
* Next letter: {{l|kk|ۋ}}
* {{list:Arabic script letters/kk}}

==Uyghur==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ug|trk-pro|*ol}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ug|/u/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ug|/u/}}

===Letter===
{{head|ug|letter|tr=u}}

# The twenty sixth letter of the Uyghur alphabet.

====Forms====
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Isolated form !!Final form !! Medial form !! Initial form
|- style="font-size:300%; text-align:center; line-height:100%; font-family: Scheherazade, Lateef, 'Times New Roman';"
| ئۇ || ‍ۇ || ‍ۇ || ئۇ
|}

===Pronoun===
{{head|ug|pronoun|tr=u|sc=ug-Arab}}

# {{lb|ug|personal}} [[he]], [[she]], [[it]]
# {{lb|ug|demonstrative}} [[that]]

====Declension====
{{ug-decl-3rd}}

===See also===
{{ug-personal pronouns}}

* Previous letter: {{l|ug|ئو}}
* Next letter: {{l|ug|ئۆ}}

===Usage notes===
* In UEY (Uyghur Ereb Yëziqi), if a word begin with a vowel, there will always a hamza before the vowel letter. e.g. {{l|ug|ئېغىز}}. And when there is no consonant between two vowels, a hamza is always placed between them. e.g. {{l|ug|سائەت}}.
