===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ar|وَصْلَة}}. {{root|en|ar|و ص ل}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|wasla}}

# {{lb|en|linguistics}} A diacritic added to the Arabic letter [[alif]] {{m|ar|ا|tr=-}} to form {{m|ar|ٱ|tr=-}}, also called "hamzatu l-waṣli" - {{m|ar|هَمْزَةُ الْوَصْلِ}} or "alifu l-waṣli" - {{m|ar|أَلِفُ الْوَصْلِ}}. It denotes [[elision]] and is seldom used in practice in fully vocalised Arabic texts, only to highlight that the alif is silent {{m|ar|هَمْزَةُ ٱلْوَصْلِ}} = {{m|ar|هَمْزَةُ الْوَصْلِ}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|an Arabic diacritic denoting elision of the alif}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|وَصْلَة|f}}, {{t|ar|هَمْزَةُ الْوَصْلِ|f}}, {{t|ar|أَلِفُ الْوَصْلِ|f}}
* French: {{t+|fr|wasla|m}}
* German: {{t|de|Wasla|n}}
* Persian: {{t+|fa|وصله|tr=vasle}}
* Russian: {{t+|ru|ва́сла|f}}
* Tajik: {{t|tg|васла}}
* Uzbek: {{t|uz|vasla}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=aalsw|Waals}}

