* before a word-final {{l|fa|ه}}, [[ma'ruf|ma'rūf]] and [[majhul|majhūl]] diacritics are not clearly distinguished. 

* Though short vowels also have [[ma'ruf|ma'rūf]]-[[majhul|majhūl]] variants, [[majhul|majhūl]] short vowels likely will not be included in romanizations. Unlike the [[majhul|majhūl]] long vowels, which can appear anywhere, the [[majhul|majhūl]] short vowels only appear before glottal consonants, and are technically allophones.

===Additional information===
# {{l|fa|ـًا}}, {{l|fa|ـاً}}, {{l|fa|ءً}} (always word-final) – an 
#: For modern varieties {{l|fa|ـاً}} is preferred. For classical Persian, both  {{l|fa|ـًا}} and {{l|fa|ـاً}} are acceptable.
# All forms of hamza, including {{l|fa|ء}}, {{l|fa|ؤ}} and {{l|fa|ئ}} are transliterated as '
# The ([[ezafe|izāfa]]) vowel is transcribed differently depending on context:
#* {{l|fa|ـِ}} (always word-final, after consonants) – -i
#* {{l|fa|یِ}} (after the long vowels {{l|fa|ا|tr=ā}} or {{l|fa|و|tr=ū, ō}}) - -yi
#*: {{uxi|fa|آفریقایِ جنوبی|tr=āfrīqā-yi janūbī|South Africa}}
#* {{l|fa|یِّ}} (always word-final after {{l|fa|ی}}) - ī-yi
#*: {{uxi|fa|جَمْهُوریِّ کورِیا|tr=jamhūrī-yi kōriyā|Republic of Korea}}
#* {{l|fa|ـهٔ}}, the form {{m|fa|ـه‌ی}} is treated as a variant – a-yi.
#*: {{uxi|fa|[[خانهٔ]] کلان|tr=xāna'''-yi''' kalān|a big house|q=spelled with a hamza diacritic}}
#*: In spoken Dari هٔ may reduce to a short e (or i). So {{lang|fa|خانهٔ کلان}} may be pronounced as xāne kalān. It is not known if this will be included since this is the only Izāfa vowel with which this occurs.
#* {{uxi|fa|[[خانه|خانه‌ی]] کلان|tr=xāna'''-yi''' kalān|a big house|q=spelled with a a non-connecting ye}}
# {{l|fa|ـِیِّـ}} is transliterated as ''iyyi'', the only exception being for Izāfa when it is transliterated as ''ī-yi''.
# {{l|fa|ـّ}} ([[tashdid|tašdīd]]) – geminate consonant (Arabic shadda)
# Al- assimilation {{l|fa|الـ}} 
#* Only occurs in loaned compound terms from Arabic, as the article {{l|fa|الـ}} is typically dropped from the lemma form of all Arabic loanwords.
#* if {{l|fa|الـ}} is followed by one of the 'sun letters' of Arabic, the lām {{l|fa|ل}} will assimilate with the following letter.
#* if {{l|fa|الـ}} is part of a conjugation where the alif is silent, the alif is lam is transliterated as l- (or -l- if there is a ZWNJ)
#*: {{l|fa|حَبْلُ المَتِین|tr=hablu l-matīn}}
#*: {{l|fa|حَبْلُ‌المَتِین|tr=hablu-l-matīn}} (word with ZWNJ)
#*: {{l|fa-cls|فِالْحَال}} (example within a single word)  
# {{l|fa|ـه}} - when used as a colloquial copula in the 3rd person singular (he/she/it is) - -a (with a hyphen)
#: {{uxi|fa|تَهْران پایتَخْتِ ایرانه.|tr=ta(h)rān pāytaxt-i ērān'''-a'''.|t=Tehran '''is''' the capital of Iran.|q=colloquial}}
# [[ZWNJ]] – - (hyphen)
# Various governments of Afghanistan have recommended that the suffix {{lang|fa|ـگی}} have a space or ZWNJ when added to a word ending in {{lang|fa|ـه}}. This suggestion is not always observed, even in academic settings and by media broadcasters in Afghanistan. These spellings may be included as alternative forms.
#: {{uxi|fa|زنده‌گی|tr=zinda-gī|q=recommended spelling|t=-}}
#: {{uxi|fa|زندگی|tr=zindagī|q=common spelling|t=-}}
