===Other symbols or combinations===
# {{l|fa-ira|ـاً}}, {{l|fa-ira|ءً}} (always word-final) – an <small>(The position of [fatHatan] is after the alef, not before, as is the current practice with Arabic)</small>
# {{l|fa-ira|ء}} – ' (others: ʼ)
# {{l|fa-ira|ؤ}} – ' (others: ʼ)
# {{l|fa-ira|ئ}} – ' (others: ʼ)
# {{l|fa-ira|ـِ}} ([[ezafe|ezâfe]]) (always word-final, unmarked in regular writing) – -e
# {{l|fa-ira|ـیِ}} ([[ezafe|ezâfe]]) (after long vowels {{l|fa-ira|ا|tr=â}} or {{l|fa-ira|و|tr=u}}, unmarked in regular writing) - -ye
#: {{uxi|fa-ira|آفْریقایِ جُنوبی|South Africa}}
# {{l|fa-ira|ـیِ}} ([[ezafe|ezâfe]]) (always word-final with {{l|fa-ira|ی}}, unmarked in regular writing) - i-ye
#: {{uxi|fa-ira|جُمْهوریِ تاجیکِسْتان|Republic of Tajikistan}}
# {{l|fa-ira|ـهٔ}} (U+0647 U+0654), sometimes written as {{m|fa-ira|ـه‌ی}} (always word-final) – e-ye. <small>(Articles don't contain the hamze above "he", it is considered a diacritic and only used in the dsplay using {{para|head}}. Templates link to words without the hamze.)</small>
#: {{uxi|fa|[[خانِهٔ]] بُزُرْگ|tr=xâne'''-ye''' bozorg|a big house|q=spelled with a hamze diacritic}}
#: {{uxi|fa|[[خانه|خانِه‌ی]] بُزُرْگ|tr=xâne'''-ye''' bozorg|a big house|q=spelled with a a non-connecting ye}}
# {{l|fa-ira|ـه‌ای}} - e-yi
# {{l|fa-ira|نه|gloss=no, not}} - na (an exception)
# {{l|fa-ira|ـّ}} ([[tashdid]]) – geminate consonant (Arabic shadda)
# {{l|fa-ira|ـَ}} ([[fathe]]/[[zor]]) – a (Arabic fatha)
# {{l|fa-ira|ـِ}} ([[kasre]]/[[zir]]) – e (in modern Iranian, ''to check cases where it's "i"'') (Arabic kasra)
# {{l|fa-ira|ـُ}} ([[zamme]]/[[pish]]) – o (in modern Iranian, ''to check cases where it's "u"'') (Arabic damma). Used after consonants to make a short "o" sound. If used before {{m|fa-ira|و}} produces a diphthong "ow":
#: {{l|fa-ira|نُوْروز|tr=nowruz}}
# {{l|fa-ira|ـّ}} ([[shadda]]) – geminate consonant
# {{l|fa-ira|ـ۟}} ([[sukūn]]/sokun) - marks absence of a vowel. Rarely used in popular Persian vocalisations, especially on final consonants. It may be necessary to use consistently in strict vocalisations to avoid any misreadings, allow automation and signalling that a word IS vocalised.
# {{l|fa-ira|ـه}} (in the word-final position after consonants for a large number of words) - e (no hyphen) (note with [[ezafe|ezâfe]] the preferred spelling is {{l|fa-ira|ـهٔ}})
#: {{uxi|fa-ira|هَفْتِه|tr=haft'''e'''|week}}
# {{l|fa-ira|ـه}} - when used as a colloquial copula in the 3rd person singular (he/she/it is) - -e (with a hyphen)
#: {{uxi|fa-ira|تِهْرون پایْتَخْتِ ایرونِه.|tr=tehrun pâytaxt-e irun'''-e'''.|t=Tehran '''is''' the capital of Iran.|q=colloquial}}
# [[ZWNJ]] – - (hyphen)
# ''The use of hyphens for etymological reasons - suffixes, compound words, etc. when no ZWNJ is used is to be discussed. E.g. currently plural form suffix {{l|fa-ira|ـها}} is transliterated as "-hâ"'' regardless if ZWNJ is present or not. <small>(Apart from cases described above and ZWNJ, the use of hyphen is otherwise dispreferred. A space is transliterated as a space and the absence of space or ZWNJ is transliterated as nothing.)</small>
#: Below are transliteration examples to contrast the use of ZWNJ on connecting letters, space, nothing and non-connecting letters:
#: ZWNJ on joining letters {{l|fa-ira|کتاب‌ها|tr=ketâb-hâ}} (plural of {{l|fa-ira|کتاب|tr=ketâb}})
#: Space {{l|fa-ira|کتاب ها|tr=ketâb hâ}}
#: Nothing (joining letters are connected) {{l|fa-ira|کتابها|tr=ketâbhâ}}
#: Non-joining letters (no ZWNJ is used) {{l|fa-ira|اتوها|tr=otuhâ}} (plural of {{l|fa-ira|اتو|tr=otu}})

===Arabic loanwords===
# {{l|fa-ira|ـة}} (always word-final) – a(t) <small>(rare, only in unadapted borrowings from Arabic, normally adapted into Persian as {{m|fa-ira|ـت|tr=at}} or {{m|fa-ira|ـه|tr=e}})</small>
# {{l|fa-ira|الـ}} - al (normally), can be "al-" (with a hyphen), if identified as the Arabic definite article. "l" can change to the following consonant if it's a "sun letter","a" can change to "o" (Arabic "u") in [[ezafe|ezâfe]], e.g.
#: {{l|fa-ira|فارِغ‌ُالتَّحْصیل|tr=fâreğo-t-tahsil}} - here "l" is assimilated to "t" and "a" is changed to "o" following Arabic grammar rules.
# {{l|fa-ira|الـ}} - l or the next consonant (assimilated for Arabic "sun letters"). The alef is silent.
#: {{l|fa-ira|بِٱلْفِعْل}} from Arabic {{m|ar|بِٱلْفِعْلِ}} where the alif is silent ({{m|ar|أَلِف الوَصْل}})
</onlyinclude>
