==Galician==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|gl|roa-opt|en}}, from {{inh|gl|la|in}}, from {{der|gl|itc-pro|*en}}, from {{der|gl|ine-pro|*h₁én||in}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|gl|/eŋ/}}

====Preposition====
{{head|gl|prepositions}}

# [[in]]
# {{n-g|when preceding a verb or a complement of a verb it can denote an unfinished or continued action}}:
#: {{ux|inline=1|gl|O Manuel vai '''n'''a casa|Manuel went home (implying that eventually he'll be back)}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|gl|María beberrica '''n'''o licor|María is sipping the liquor}}
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1822|author=anonymous|title=A Parola Polêteca
|passage='''''En''' escoitalo, señor tio Calacú, xà o peléxo do meu corpo tembra. Sei que á tanta agua que acarrexóu amolentoulle os miolos, é por eso louquéa''
|translation='''While''' listening to you, my sir uncle Pumpkin, my body's skin trembles. Perhaps the much water you have carried softened you brain, and therefore you are going insane}}
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1853|author=Xosé Manuel Pintos|title=A Gaita Gallega
|passage=''xa morder ti ben non podes''<br>''con tal podrico nos dentes,''<br>''inda '''n'''o pan teño mentes''<br>''seique non podes chanchar''
|translation=you can no longer aptly eat<br>with such rottenness in you teeth,<br>even bread, I think,<br>probably you cannot gnaw [{{m|gl|chanchar}} means "bite", but ''en'' preceding {{m|gl|pan}}, "bread", implies a repeated action]}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The preposition ''en'' contracts to ''n-'' before articles, before third-person tonic pronouns, and before the determiners {{m|gl|algún}} and {{m|gl|outro}}.

