====Adverb====
{{head|gl|prepositions}}

# [[while]]; [[as soon as]] {{gloss|followed by the gerund of a verb, expresses [[immediacy]] or [[simultaneity]]}}
#: {{ux|inline=1|gl|'''En''' chegando mudas a roupa mollada|'''As soon as''' you arrive change your wet clothes}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1295|editor=R. Lorenzo|title=La traducción gallega de la Crónica General y de la Crónica de Castilla.|location=Ourense|publisher=I. E. O. P. F|page=111
|passage=''Et o conde, '''en''' chegando et ferindo logo ẽnos mouros, todo en hũu o fezo''
|translation=And the count, ['''just'''] arriving, and hurting promptly the Moors, all in one he did that}}
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1460|author=Rui Vasques|title=Corónica de Iria
|passage='''''en''' leendo perlos llibros algũus de canõicas antijgas, et preujlegios goticos dos santos catholicos et deuotos bispos de Yria et porla Escriptura, achey o fundamento para rreduzir aa memoria dos homes quanto durarõ çertas ydades''
|translation=['''while/after'''] reading books, some of them of ancient canons, and Gothic privileges of the saint Catholic and devout bishops of Iria, and through the Bible, I found the foundation for reducing to the mind of men for how long some ages lasted}}
#* '''1461''', X. Ferro Couselo (ed.), ''A vida e a fala dos devanceiros. Escolma de documentos en galego dos séculos XIII ao XVI''. 2 vols. Vigo: Galaxia, page 141:
#*: {{quote|gl|''dito testigo '''en''' seendo moço pequeno con seu tyo Afonso Dominges, guardando o gaando en Curro do Moyño, que le dixera o dito Afonso Domingees "bees, por aquy se parte ho término do conde do de Juan d'Estúñiga''
|translation=said witness ['''while/when'''] being a young boy and together with his uncle Afonso Domínguez, watching the cattle in Curro do Muíño, he was told by said Afonso Domínguez: "you see, here the term of the count limits with that of Xoán de Estúñiga"}}
#* {{quote-text |gl |year=1858 |author= Francisco María de la Iglesia |title= O orfiño da arquiña
|passage= Que pan e insinanza<br> Pardiola has de ter,<br> Roupiña e oficio<br> Para deprender;<br> E '''ende''' sendo grande<br> Si es home de ben,<br> Na Seña Duquesa<br> Madriña tamén
|translation= Such bread and teaching<br> By gosh you'll have!<br> Clothes and office<br> to learn;<br> And '''them when''' you're big<br> If you're a good man<br> our Lady the Duchess <br>will be also your protector}}

