===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*skey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|schit}}, {{m|enm|schyt}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*sċite|t=dung}} and {{m|ang|sċitte|t=diarrhoea}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skiti}} and {{m|gmw-pro|*skittjā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skitiz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skeyd-|t=to split, divide, separate}}. Related to {{cog|stq|Skiete}}, {{cog|fy|skyte}}, {{m|fy|skyt}}, {{cog|nl|schijt}}, {{cog|nds-de|Schiet}}, {{cog|de|Scheiße}}, {{cog|da|skidt}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|nn|skit}}, {{cog|nb|skitt}}, {{cog|is|skítur}}. Compare {{m|en|shite}}. {{doublet|en|scheisse}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{q|[[Appendix:Glossary#bowdlerization|bowdlerizations]]}} {{alter|en|s--t|s**t|s—t}} etc.
* {{alter|en|shite||Britain|Ireland}}
* {{alter|en|sheeyit|sheeit|sheit|shiet|shi|shii||AAVE}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable|colloquial|vulgar}} Solid [[excretory]] product evacuated from the [[bowel]]s; [[feces]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:feces}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Cholera and the super-loo|journal=The Economist|date=30 Jul 2011
|passage=The practice in most African and some Asian cities is for private lorries to suck up human waste and dump it in rivers. [...] In tackling the '''shit''' problem, economics could well be a clincher.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|colloquial|vulgar}} The act of [[shitting]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} [[rubbish|Rubbish]]; [[worthless]] matter.
#: {{ux|en|Throw that '''shit''' out!}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} [[stuff|Stuff]], [[thing]]s.
#: {{ux|en|I want your '''shit''' out of my garage by tomorrow.}}
#: {{ux|en|Fuck it. I don't feel like doing this '''shit'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1998|date=|writer=Jim Kouf; Ross LaManna|title=Rush Hour|location=California|publisher=New Line Cinema|passage=JAMES CARTER: You put your own '''shit''' in the back; I'm not a skycap.|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0Rl9Cxc7uZA}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2001|artist={{w|Mike Cooley (musician)|Mike Cooley}}|title=Zip City|passage=Don't know why I put up with this '''shit''' / When you don't put out and Zip City's so far away}}
#* {{quote-journal|en
|date=December 1, 2017
|author=Tom Breihan
|title=Mad Max: Fury Road might already be the best action movie ever made
|work=The Onion AV Club
|url=https://www.avclub.com/mad-max-fury-road-might-already-be-the-best-action-mov-1820691831
|page=
|passage=He’s physical and monosyllabic. He does all sorts of cool '''shit''', and he subtly rediscovers his own heroism without making a big thing out of it. But he’s a supporting character, and he knows it.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|colloquial|vulgar|definite|US}} ('''the shit''') The [[best]] of its kind.
#: {{ux|en|These grapes are the '''shit'''!}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Curtis Jackson; Rob Tewlow|composer=Reef Tewlow|artist=50 Cent|title=What Up Gangsta|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=94UmYrW5oto|album=Get Rich or Die Tryin'|year=2003|author=|location=New York City|publisher=Shady Records|passage=When gangsters bump my '''shit''', can they feel my hunger?}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} [[nonsense|Nonsense]]; [[bullshit]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:nonsense}}
#: {{ux|en|Everything he says is a load of '''shit'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|vulgar|colloquial}} A [[nasty]], [[despicable]] person, used particularly of men.
#: {{ux|en|Her son has been a real '''shit''' to her.}}
#: {{ux|en|I am a '''shit''' and a rotter.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} (''in negations'') [[anything|Anything]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:nothing}}
#: {{ux|en|We don’t have '''shit''' to live on.|q=We don’t have anything to live on.}}
#: {{ux|en|John can't sing for '''shit'''.|q=John can't sing at all.}}
#: {{ux|en|You ain't '''shit'''.|q=You're nothing; you aren't worth anything.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|vulgar|colloquial}} The smallest amount of [[concern]] or [[consideration]].
#: {{syn|en|fuck|damn}}
#: {{ux|en|I don't give a '''shit'''.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} A problem or difficult situation.
#: {{ux|en|I'm in some serious '''shit'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Some '''shit''' went down at the nightclub last night.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} A strong [[rebuke]].
#: {{ux|en|I gave him '''shit''' for being three hours late twice in one week.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|vulgar|colloquial}} Any recreational drug (e.g. [[cannabis]], [[heroin]], etc.).
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|page=28|passage=‘Now,’ he said, ‘if someone would close the curtains and light a joss-stick, I have here for your delight some twenty-four-carat black Nepalese cannabis resin which should be smoked immediately on account of it being seriously good '''shit'''.’}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|slang|vulgar}} Anything [[exceptional]] or [[remarkable]].
#: {{usex|en|I heard Bobby escaped from the police by jumping off a bridge into the river. Ain't that some '''shit'''?}}

