==Afrikaans==

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|af|nl|-st}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|af|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|plural|-ste}}

# {{n-g|appended to the stem of a verb, this suffix yields a [[verbal noun]]}}
#: {{sufex|af|dien|diens}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|af|nl|-s}} (a suffix for forming plurals).

====Suffix====
{{head|af|suffix|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{n-g|Used to form regular plurals of nouns that end in certain suffixes or syllables, such as ''-el'', ''-er'', ''-en'', ''-em'', ''-eur'', ''-aar'', ''-aard'', diminutive {{m|af|-ie}}, etc.}}
#: {{sufex|af|redakteur|redakteurs}}
# {{n-g|Used to form irregular plurals of many other nouns, chiefly of foreign origin.}}
#: {{sufex|af|ateljee|ateljees}}

===Etymology 3===
{{inh+|af|nl|-s}}, from the genitive case of Dutch masculine and neuter nouns and adjectives, {{inh|af|dum|-s}}, {{m|dum|-es}}, from {{inh|af|odt|-es}}, {{m|odt|-is}}, from {{inh|af|gem-pro|*-as}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-is}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|af|suffix|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{n-g|Used to form the partitive form of the adjective}}
#: {{l|af|nuut}} &rarr; iets nuut'''s'''
#: {{l|af|groot}} &rarr; niks groot'''s''' nie

