{{inh+|af|nl|-s}}, from earlier {{m|nl|-sch}}, from {{inh|af|dum|-sch}}, from {{inh|af|odt|-isc}}, from {{inh|af|gmw-pro|*-isk}}, from {{inh|af|gem-pro|*-iskaz}}, from {{der|af|ine-pro|*-iskos}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|af|suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes}}

# {{senseid|af|adjective}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to form adjectives of characteristic from nouns.}}
#: {{sufex|af|winter|t1=winter|winters|t2=wintery}}
#: {{sufex|af|spel|t1=game|speels|t2=playful}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Used to form adjectives or language names from [[place name]]s.}}
#: {{sufex|af|Engeland|t1=England|Engels|t2=English}}
#: {{sufex|af|Finland|t1=Finland|Fins|t2=Finnish}}

==Albanian==

===Etymology===
Possibly akin to {{cog|xcl|-իչ}}, both reconstructible to a tentative {{inh|sq|ine-pro||*-ikʷyo-s}}, from {{der|sq|ine-pro|
*kʷey-|t=to gather}},<ref>{{R:sq:Matzinger:2016|page=167}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:Olander:2022|13|page=228}}</ref> whence also {{cog|grc|ποιέω|t=to do}}, {{cog|sa|चिनोति|tr=cinóti|t=to arrange, pile up}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|sq|suffix}}

# {{senseid|sq|agent}} {{ng|Forms [[agent noun]]s}}.
#: {{syn|sq|-ar}}

====Usage notes====
* Becomes {{m|sq||-ës}} after consonants.
* When attached to {{m|sq||o}}- or {{m|sq||ua}}-stem verbs the stem and the suffix merge into {{m|sq||-ues}} in the modern standard, following Gheg practice, while traditionally made {{m|sq||-onjës}} following Tosk practice.
* Similarly, when attached to {{m|sq||e}}- or {{m|sq||ye}}-stem verbs they give rise to {{m|sq||-yes}} in Gheg and the modern standard, while {{m|sq||-enjës}} in Tosk and the old standard.

