==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|fi|clitic}}
Contracted from the second-person singular pronoun {{m|fi|sa}}, {{m|fi|sä}} ({{m|fi|sinä}} in modern standard language), but no longer tied to being used in second-person.

====Particle====
{{head|fi|particle|cat2=clitics}} {{tlb|fi|enclitic particle|somewhat|informal|or|familiar}}

# {{n-g|When appended to a second-person singular or plural imperative, gives the command or request slightly rude or impatient tone—often with different verbs and different independent particles adjacent, the tone is different.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Kuule'''s''' [[nyt]]!|Now '''do''' listen!|q=addressing one person. quite an established expression of frustration, speaker very impatient}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Kuulkaa'''s''' [[nyt]]!|Now '''do''' listen!|q=addressing many people, same tone as above}}
#: {{uxi|fi|Tee'''s''' nämä tehtävät.|'''Go''' do these tasks.|q=addressing one person, tone less impatient}}
# {{n-g|When appended to the particle {{m|fi|-pa|-pa/-pä}} that is appended to a second-person imperative, gives the command or request a slightly more persuasive or inspiring tone.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[laittaa|Laita]][[-pa|pa]]'''s''' lautaset pöytään.|Hey, ''go'' put the plates on the table.}}
# {{n-g|Mainly in informal contexts: a particle appended to an interrogative suffix {{m|fi|-ko|-ko/-kö}} of the verb conjugated in order to bring the conversation partner or a person outside the conversation, talked about, emotionally closer to the speaker, or to create familiarity into the conversation; also to express that closeness or familiarity—sometimes very difficult to translate ''well'' into English, in some cases corresponds to [[tag question]]s.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[jaksaa|Jaksat]][[-ko|ko]]'''s''' sinä?|May you make it ''maybe?''}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[ei|Ei]][[-kö|kö]]'''s''' Saara [[opiskella|opiskele]] [[oikeustiede|oikeustiete]]itä?|Saara studies law, ''[[nuh]]''?}}
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} {{n-g|appended to the shortened impersonal indicative present form (-''n'' omitted) to soften the command or request or to make it more persuasive.}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[tehdään|Tehdää'''s''']] tämä huomenna.|Let's ''go'' do this tomorrow.}}
# {{n-g|Softens interrogative words, particularly {{m|fi|mikä}}, {{m|fi|kuka}} and their inflected and derived forms, such as when the speaker expects the person addressed to know the answer.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Mikä'''s''' se Suomen pääkaupunki olikaan?|What was Finland's capital '''again'''?}}
#: {{ux|fi|Kuka'''s''' heistä olikaan sinun lapsesi?|Which of them was your child '''again'''?}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When attached to imperative forms, the gemination is ignored, unless another enclitic is also used before {{m|fi||-s}}, like with {{m|fi||-pas}}. Thus {{m|fi||laitas}} {{IPAchar|/lɑi̯tɑs/}}, but {{m|fi||laitapas}} {{IPAchar|/lɑi̯tɑpːɑs/}}.
* When directly attached to forms ending in {{m|fi||-n}} (e.g. passive forms), the {{m|fi||-n}} is often dropped (e.g. {{m|fi|miten}} → {{m|fi||mites}}).

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|fi|-s (clitic)}}

