==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=gyhʾn'|ts=gēhān|t= worldly creatures, world}},<ref>{{R:pal:Mackenzie:1971|gēhān|page=36}}</ref> from {{inh|fa|ira-pro||*gayθānām}}, the genitive plural form of {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*gay-θā-|t=living, existence}} (compare {{cog|ae|𐬔𐬀𐬉𐬚𐬁|𐬔𐬀𐬉𐬚𐬁-|t=world; creature}}),<ref>{{R:ira:ESIJa|vol=3|pages=107-8}}</ref> equivalent to [[Middle Persian]] {{affix|pal||tr1=gēh|tr2=ān|nocat=1}}, with the former component from {{der|fa|ira-pro|*ǰáyH-|t=to live}}, from {{der|fa|iir-pro|*ǰáyH-|t=to live}}, from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*gʷeyh₃-|t=to live}}.<ref>{{R:ira:Cheung|pages=222-3}}</ref>

The original meaning of the word in [[Old Iranian]] and [[Middle Persian]] was (worldly) creatures, but the term in late [[Middle Persian]] and in [[Persian|Modern Persian]] came to mean ‘world’ in general.

{{doublet|fa|کیهان|tr1=keyhân}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|jaˈhān|cls=jaˈhān,jiˈhān}}
* {{rhymes|fa|ɑːn|s=2}}

====Noun====
{{fa-regional|جهان|جهان|ҷаҳон}}
{{fa-noun|tr=jahân|pl=جهان‌ها}}

# [[world]]; [[universe]]
#: {{syn|fa|دنیا|tr1=donyâ|گیتی|tr2=giti|عالم|tr3=âlam}}
#: {{coi|fa-ira|'''جَهانِ''' آزاد|the free world}}
#* {{RQ:Masnavi|I|161|تا که نبض از نام کی گردد جهان<br>او بود مقصود جانش در جهان‌‌|tā ki nabz az nām-i kay gardad jihān<br>ō buwad maqsūd-i jān-aš dar '''jahān'''|{{...}}so that at whosoever's name her pulse should begin to throb, [he might know that] that person is the object of her soul's desire in the '''world'''.}}

