==Urdu==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ur|pra-sau|𑀅𑀧𑁆𑀧𑀸}}, from {{inh|ur|sa|आत्मन्|tr=ātmán||soul, spirit; self}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ur-IPA|āp}}

===Pronoun===
{{ur-pron|tr=āp|hi=आप}}

# {{lb|ur|formal|polite}} {{n-g|[[second person|second-person]] [[subjective]] or [[objective]] [[personal pronoun]], grammatically plural:}} [[you]], [[ye]]; [[Early Modern English]] formal [[ye]].
# {{lb|ur|rare|honorific}} {{n-g|[[third person|third-person]] subjective or objective personal pronoun:}} [[he]], [[she]], [[they]], [[him]], [[her]], [[them]]
#: {{ux|ur|'''آپ''' [[ﷺ]] نے فرمایا "جس شخص نے نکاح کرلیا اس نے اپنا آدھا دین مکمل کرلیا"۔|tr='''āp''' SAW ne farmāyā "jis śaxs ne nikāh karliyā us-ne apnā ādhā dīn mukammal karliyā".|'''He''' [[SAW]] said, "The person who gets married has completed half of his religion".}} 
# {{n-g|[[reflexive]] [[pronoun]]}}: [[oneself]], one's [[own]]
#: {{syn|ur|خود|tr=xud}}
#: {{uxa|ur|مشین '''آپ''' ہی چل پڑی|tr=maśīn '''āp'''-hī cal paṛī|the machine started on its '''own'''}}

====Usage notes====
* {{lang|ur|آپ}} is the most formal way of expressing "you" in Urdu and is used when addressing elders or those higher in social status. Because less formal forms could offend others, {{lang|ur|آپ}} is the safest way to express "you" unless there is reason to be less formal.
* Because {{lang|ur|آپ}} is grammatically plural (adjectives and verbs etc affected by it take their plural forms) even when there is only one person being referred to, the term {{lang|ur|آپ [[لوگ]]}} (literally: you people) can be used to specify that more than one person is being referred to because of [[w:T-V distinction|T-V distinction]].

====Declension====
{{ur-decl-pronoun|آپ|āp|آپ|āp|آپ نے|āp-ne|آپ کا|āp-kā|آپ کو|āp-ko}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ur|اپنے آپ|tr=apne-āp}}

====See also====
* {{l|ur|تو|tr=tū}} - {{n-g|informal, intimate, contemptuous  or possibly vulgar, grammatically singular}}
* {{l|ur|تم|tr=tum}} - {{n-g|[[semiformal]], familiar, grammatically plural}}
{{ur-personal_pronouns}}
-------- end text --------
