Page 15 تو: -------- begin text --------
{{also|پو|بو|بۄ|بۇ|Appendix:Variations of "tu"}}
==Arabic==

===Etymology===
In the sense of a knot from {{bor|ar|fa|تو|tr=tô|t=twist}}. In the sense of having been just a borrowing from {{bor|ar|arz|تَوّ|tr=taww}} in its meaning, also {{cog|mey|تو|tr=tow|t=instant}}, {{w|Mrazig|Marazīq}} {{cog|aeb|تاو|tr=tâu|t=moment}}, in view of {{cog|xsa|𐩻𐩥|t=until}} borrowed from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, in its more original meaning present in {{cog|xaa||ثَو ذَا|tr=ṯaw ḏā}} or {{m|xaa||تَو ذَا|tr=taw ḏā|t=until now}} and {{cog|ayn|تَو|t=in front of|tr=taw}}, and following this prepositional character still most notorious with personal suffixes. Possibly corresponding to {{doublet|ar|سَوْفَ|notext=1}} and {{cog|gez|ሶበ}}, {{m|gez|ሶቤ|t=when}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَوّ|m|pl=أَتْوَاء}}

# {{tlb|ar|obsolete}} a [[knot]], a [[twist]] or [[contortion]] in a [[rope]]; a [[rope]] that is twisted of a [[single]] [[strand]]
# [[instantaneousness]], [[immediacy]], [[onlyness]], the condition of having been [[present]] [[just]] i.e. [[recently]] and/or [[alone]]

====Usage notes====
Though parsing as a noun, the sense of an “instance” is of restricted use, often in the adverbial accusative {{m|ar|تَوًّا|t=just; in a bit}}, and in prepositional phrases {{m|ar||فِي التَوِّ}} and {{m|ar||لِلتَّوِّ|tr=li-t-tawwi}} which latter in particular also takes personal suffixes instead of the article, for the findability of which constructions this dictionary entry renders the following table:

====Inflection====
{{ar-prep-auto|لِتَوِّ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَوّ|pl=أَتْوَاء}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|تَوَّة|t=a short period}}

===References===
* {{R:xaa:Corriente|page=81b}}
* {{R:xaa:Corriente-Additions|page=41}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=203a}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=320–321}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=146a}}

==Kohistani Shina==

