==Urdu==

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ur|inc-sap|तुहुं|tr=tuhũ}}, from {{inh|ur|pra-sau|𑀢𑀼𑀫𑀁}}, {{m|pra-sau|𑀢𑀼𑀁}}, from {{inh|ur|sa|त्वम्}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ur-IPA|tū}}
* {{rhymes|ur|uː}}

====Pronoun====
{{ur-pron|head=تُو}}

# {{lb|ur|informal|intimate|contemptuous|possibly vulgar}} {{n-g|[[second-person singular]] [[subjective]] [[personal pronoun]]}}: [[you]], [[thou]]; [[Early Modern English]] [[thou]].
# {{lb|ur|dialectal|literary|religion}} {{n-g|second-person singular subjective personal pronoun, intimate or very polite}}: [[Thou]]
#: {{uxa|ur|اے خدا '''تو''' ہی میرا مددگار  ہے!|tr=ai xudā '''tū'''-hī merā madadgār hai!|O God, only '''Thou''' art my helper!}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{lang|ur|تو}} is the least formal way of expressing "you" in Urdu and is used when addressing those of much lower social status or those one has a close enough relationship with to justify the reduced formality. Because the less formal forms could offend others, {{lang|ur|آپ}} is the safest way to express "you" unless there is reason to be less formal, where {{lang|ur|تم}} would be appropriate. The usage of {{lang|ur|تو}} varies. In some cases speakers would use it to refer to babies or children or even close friends, while others would use it only to refer to those they consider socially inferior, and some consider its use for people to be very rude in any situation. However {{lang|ur|تو}}, when used to address deities reflects a sense of reverence and closeness commensurate with the lack of formalities.

====Determiner====
{{head|ur|determiner|head=تُو|tr=tū|plural|تم|g=s|Hindi spelling|तू}}

# {{lb|ur|informal|intimate|contemptuous|possibly vulgar}} the [[individual]] spoken or written to; [[you]], [[thou]], [[Early Modern English]] [[thou]].

=====Declension=====
{{ur-decl-pronoun|تُو|tū|تجھ|tujh|تو نے|tū-ne|تیرا|terā|تجھے|tujhe}}

====See also====
* {{l|ur|تم|tr=tum}} - {{n-g|[[semiformal]], familiar, grammatically plural}}
* {{l|ur|آپ|tr=āp}} - {{n-g|formal, polite, grammatically plural}}
{{ur-personal_pronouns}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ur|pra-sau|-}}, probably from {{der|ur|sa|ततस्||from there}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ur-IPA|to}}

====Conjunction====
{{ur-con|tr=to|hi=तो}}

# [[then]]

