{{ps-decl-adj-m-consonant|ارزان|arzān}}

====See also====
* {{l|ps|ارزانه|tr=arzāna}}

==Persian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=ʾlcʾn|ts=arzān|sc=Phlv}}, {{m|pal|𐫀𐫡𐫉𐫀𐫗|t=valuable, worthy|ts=arzān}}, from {{m|pal|tr=ʾlc|ts=arz|t=worth, value|sc=Phlv}} + {{m|pal|tr=-ʾn|ts=-ān|sc=Phlv}}, from {{der|fa|ira-pro|*Hárǰ-}}, from {{der|fa|iir-pro|[[*Hárǰʰati|*Hárǰʰ-]]|t=to be worth}}. Cognate with {{cog|xpr|𐫀𐫡𐫋𐫀𐫗|t=worthy|ts=aržān}}, {{cog|tly|ارژون|tr=erjon}}, {{cog|kmr|erzan}} and the following Iranian borrowings: {{cog|xcl|արժան||worthy; cheap}}, {{cog|syc|ܐܪܙܢ|tr=ʾarzān|t=cheap}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|ar`zān}}
* {{audio|fa|LL-Q9168 (fas)-Afsham23-ارزان.wav|a=Iran}}

===Adjective===
{{fa-regional|ارزان|ارزان|арзон}}
{{fa-adj|tr=arzân|c=+}}

# [[cheap]], [[inexpensive]]
#: {{ant|fa|گران|tr1=gerân|t1=expensive}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|year=c. 1260|chapter=3:1001|title={{w|Masnavi|The ''Masnavi''}}|author=w:Rumi|text=خویشتن را آدمی ارزان فروخت، بود اطلس خویش بر دلقی بدوخت|tr=xwēštan-rā ādamē '''arzân''' furōxt, būd atlas xwēš bar dalqē bidōxt|t=man sold himself for '''cheap'''; he was satin, but sewed himself to a dervish's rags.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fa|ارزانی|tr=arzâni}}
* {{l|fa|ارزان‌فروش|tr=arzân-foruš}}
* {{l|fa|حاجی‌ارزونی|tr=hâji-'arzuni}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|fa|ارزیدن|tr=arzidan|t=to cost, to be worth}}
* {{l|fa|ـان|tr=-ân}}

====Descendants====
