==Arabic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ar|aːn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Belonging to the family {{ar-root|ء|ن|ي}}, “to come or draw near”, “to be at or present”, “to happen or occur“, “to come to a point in time”. Related to {{m|ar|هُنَا|tr=|t=here, in this place; then, now, at this point}}, {{m|ar|أَنْ|tr=|t=that, that before us presently}}, {{m|ar|إِن|tr=|t=if possible; having the possibility to occur or happen, a chance of coming to be before us, of presenting itself}}, {{m|ar|إِنَّ|tr=|t=surely; now surely, now indeed}}, and {{m|ar|أَيْنَ|tr=|t=where, at which place}}. Related cognates with {{cog|akk|𒀭𒉡|tr=annu|t=now; see, look}}, {{cog|he|אָנָה|tr='ána|t=whither, to where}}, {{cog|uga|𐎀𐎐|tr=ản|t=where, at which place, to which point}}, {{cog|syc|ܐܢ|tr=ʾān|t=where, at a place; until when, how long}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|آن|m}}

# [[time]]
#: {{syn|ar|وَقْت|حِين|أَوَان}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|آن}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|ar|الْآنَ|آنِيّ|آنَذَاكَ}}

=====Descendants=====
* Kurdish:
*: {{desc|ckb|ئان|bor=1}}, {{l|ckb|عان}}
*: {{desc|sdh|ئان|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|آن|tr=ân|bor=1|t=moment}}
*: {{desc|ug|ئان|bor=1|t=moment, instant}}
* {{desc|tr|an|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
See above.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|i}}

# to [[come]], to [[near]] {{gloss|said of time}}
#: {{syn|ar|حَانَ|أَنَى}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|i|vn=أَيْن|passive=no}}

{{topics|ar|Time}}

