==Urdu==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ur|inc-sap|तुम्हि|tr=tumhi}}, from {{inh|ur|pra-sau|𑀢𑀼𑀫𑁆𑀳𑁂}}, from {{inh|ur|sa|युष्मान्||pos=acc. pl.}} adopting the initial sounds of {{m|sa|त्वम्|tr=tvám|pos=nom. sg.}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ur-IPA|tum}}

===Pronoun===
{{ur-pron|head=تُم|hi=तुम}}

# {{lb|ur|[[semiformal]]|familiar}} {{n-g|[[second person|second-person]] [[subjective]] or [[objective]] [[personal pronoun]], grammatically plural}}: [[you]], [[ye]]; [[Early Modern English]] [[ye]].
#: {{uxa|ur|کیا '''تم''' مجھ سے محبت کرتی ہو؟|tr=kyā '''tum''' mujh-se mohabbat kartī ho?|Do '''you''' love me?}}
#: {{uxa|ur| '''تم''' جیسے لوگوں کی ہی ضرورت ہے یہاں۔|tr='''tum''' jaise logõ kī hī zarūrat hai yahā̃.|People like '''you''' are needed here.}}

====Usage notes====
* {{lang|ur|تم}} is the mid level formal way of expressing "you" in Urdu and is used when addressing those of equal social status or those one has a close enough relationship with to justify the reduced formality. Because the less formal forms could offend others, {{l|ur|آپ}} is the safest way to express "you" unless there is reason to be less formal.
* Because {{lang|ur|تم}} is grammatically plural (adjectives and verbs etc affected by it take their plural forms) even when there is only one person being referred to, the term {{lang|ur|تم [[لوگ]]}} (literally: you people) can be used to specify that more than one person is being referred to.

===Determiner===
{{head|ur|determiner|head=تُم|Hindi spelling|तुम}}

# The [[individual]] or [[group]] spoken or written to; [[you]], [[ye]], [[Early Modern English]] [[ye]].
#: {{uxa|ur|'''تم''' احمق کوئی کام کے نہیں ہو۔|tr='''tum''' ahmaq ko'ī kām ke nahī̃ ho.|'''You''' idiots are of no use.}}

====Declension====
{{ur-decl-pronoun|تم|tum|تم|tum|تم نے|tum-ne|تمھارا|tumhārā|تمھیں|tumhẽ}}

===See also===
* {{l|ur|آپ}} - {{n-g|formal, polite, grammatically plural}}
* {{l|ur|تُو}} - {{n-g|informal, intimate, contemptuous  or possibly vulgar, grammatically singular}}
{{ur-personal_pronouns}}
