{{also|هم}}
==Urdu==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ur-IPA|ham}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ur|inc-ohi|हम}}, {{m|inc-ohi|हंम}}, from {{inh|ur|inc-sap|अम्हे|tr=amhe}}, from {{inh|ur|pra-sau|𑀅𑀫𑁆𑀳𑁂}}, from {{inh|ur|sa|अस्मे}}.

====Pronoun====
{{ur-pron|head=ہَم|hi=हम}}

# {{n-g|[[first-person plural]] [[subjective]] or [[objective]] [[personal pronoun]]:}} [[we]], [[us]]; {{plural of|ur|مَیں}}, {{m|ur|مُجھ}}
#: {{uxi|ur|'''ہَم''' ہون٘گے کامْیاب۔|'''we''' will be successful.}}
#: {{uxi|ur|'''ہَم''' سے نا کَبھی جُدا  ہونا۔|Don't ever separate from '''us'''.}}
# {{lb|ur|formal|majestic plural}} {{n-g|[[first-person singular]] subjective or objective personal pronoun:}} [[I]], [[me]]

=====Usage notes=====
Because {{m|ur|ہَم}} can mean both we and I ([[majestic plural]] or royal "we"), sometimes {{m|ur|[[ہَم]] [[لوگ]]}} is used to specifically denote the plural. Usually context makes it clear when {{m|ur|ہَم}} is being used for we or for I. It is inflected and used grammatically the same for both meanings.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ur|ہَماہَمی}}

====Determiner====
{{head|ur|determiner|head=ہَم|g=p|Hindi spelling|हम}}

# The speakers/writers, or the speaker/writer and at least one other person; [[we]], [[us]].
#: {{uxa|ur|'''ہَم''' پاکِسْتانی بَہُت مِہْمان نَواز ہوتے ہَیں۔|'''We''' Pakistanis tend to be very hospitable.}}
# {{lb|ur|formal|majestic plural}} The speaker/writer; [[I]], [[me]].

=====Declension=====
{{ur-decl-pronoun|ہَم|ham|ہَم|ham|ہَم نے|ham-ne|ہَمارا|hamārā|ہَمیں|hamẽ}}

====See also====
{{ur-personal_pronouns}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|ur|fa-cls|هَم|tr=ham}}, ultimately from {{der|ur|ine-pro|*somHós}}. Cognate of {{cog|en|same}}.

====Adverb====
{{ur-adv|head=ہَم|hi=हम}}

# [[also]]
# [[as well]]
# [[likewise]]
# [[equally]]
# [[together]]
# [[mutually]]

====Conjunction====
{{ur-con|head=ہَم|hi=हम}}

# [[whether]]
# [[either]]

===References===
* {{R:UR-HI-EN|هم}}
-------- end text --------
