Page 39 Template:fa-noun/documentation: Skipped, no changes
Page 39 Template:fa-noun/documentation: -------- begin text --------
{{documentation subpage}}
==Usage==
The template fa-noun is used exclusively for [[:Category:Persian nouns|Persian nouns]]. It has one mandatory field:

*<tt>tr=</tt>, put the [[romanization]] of the words.

It has three other optional parameters that should be used only if required.

*<tt>head=</tt>, the head word(s).
*<tt>pl=</tt>, the plural of the noun.
*<tt>pl2=</tt>, the second plural of the noun, use only if the first plural is already specified.

Many transliterations of plurals are given automatically by the template (provided that the transliteration of the headword is given with <tt>tr=</tt>). If the plural ends simply in {{l|fa|ـها|tr=-hâ}} (with or without the zero-width non-joiner), {{l|fa|ـان|tr=-ân}}, {{l|fa|ـیان|tr=-yân}}, or {{l|fa|ـات|tr=-ât}}, the transliteration of the plural form will be given automatically. Due to the limitations of the mechanism by which this process works, there are several exceptions for which transliterations of the plurals must be specified by the user.

Transliterations for Arabic broken-plurals, plurals ending in {{l|fa|ـگان|tr=-gân}} and those of words ending in {{l|fa|و|ـو|tr=-u}} and {{l|fa|ی|ـی|tr=-i}} whose plurals are pronounced {{l|fa|ـان|ـوان|tr=-ovân}} and {{l|fa|ـان|ـیان|tr=-iyân}}, respectively, must be specified with <tt>pltr=</tt> or <tt>pl2tr=</tt>.

Transliterations of multi-word plurals like {{l|fa|قوهای سیاه|tr=quhâ-ye siyâh}} must also be entered by the user.

===Examples===
For {{l|fa|همجنسگرا}}

<pre>{{fa-noun|tr=hamjens-gerâ|pl=همجنسگرایان|pl2=همجنسگراها}}</pre>

<includeonly>
[[Category:Persian headword-line templates|noun]]
</includeonly>
-------- end text --------
