==South Levantine Arabic==
{{ajp-root|ز ع ل}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|زَعْلَان}}. {{ajp-etym-intadj|زعل|tr=ziʕil|t=to get upset; to get angry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|zaʕlān<p:zaʕˈlæːn>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Khalil.rantissi-زَعلان.wav|a=al-Lidd}}

===Adjective===
{{ajp-adj|tr=zaʕlān|f=زعلانة|ftr=zaʕlāne|cpl=زعلانين|cpltr=zaʕlānīn}}

# [[upset]], [[sad]], [[distressed]]
# [[angry]], [[annoyed]], [[irritated]]

====Usage notes====
* Although the basic meaning of this word isn't “sad”, it's usage can be similar as “sad” in English when the sadness is mixed with upset or distress.

====See also====
* {{l|ajp|حزين|tr=ḥazīn|t=sad}}, {{l|ajp|حزنان|tr=ḥaznān|t=sad}}
* {{l|ajp|غضبان|tr=ḡaḍbān|t=angry, furious}}

