Page 110 طرخشقون: Skipped, no changes
Page 110 طرخشقون: -------- begin text --------
==Arabic==
{{was fwotd|ar|2019|August|10}}
[[File:Taraxacum officinale o Diente de león en Anaga.jpg|upright=1.60|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|طرخشقون}}]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|طَلْخَشْقُوق|طَلْخَشْقُون|طَرْخَشْقُوق|طَلَخَشْقُوق|طَلَخَشْقُون|طَرَخَشْقُوق|طَلَخْشَقُوق|طَلَخْشَقُون|طَرَخْشَقُوق|طَرْشَقُون|طَرْشَقُوق|طَلَخْقُوق|طَلَخْكُوك}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|pal||*tarrag-ī škōhān|lit=herb of the poor}}, so called because it is rarely eaten other than in times of famine. The former word is known in {{cog|fa-cls|تره|tr=tarra|t=herb}}, the latter widespread in {{cog|ira-mid|-}} but not continued into {{cog|fa-cls|-}} in the meaning “poor” though possibly identical to {{m|fa|شکوه|tr=šokuh|t=pomp, magnificence; gravity, reverence}}, {{m|fa-cls|شکوه|tr=šikūh|t=fear, terror}}, {{m|fa|شکوخ|tr=šokux, šekux|t=slip, stumble, fall}}, exposing the plural ending {{m|fa|ـان|tr=-ân}}. The variant forms of the phytonym commencing with {{m|ar||طَلـ}} relate to {{m|fa|تلخ|tr=talx|t=bitter}}, endings in {{m|ar||ـق}} to {{m|fa|چکوک|tr=čakuk|t=[[purslane]]}}, which is not a known word anymore. The combined plant-name is in Neo-Persian barely recorded as {{m|fa|تلخ‌چکوک|tr=talx-čakuk}}, {{m|fa|تلخ‌جکوک|tr=talx-jakuk}}, {{m|fa|تلخ‌چوک|tr=talx-čuk}}, {{m|fa|تلخ‌جوک|tr=talx-juk|t=[[wild succory]]}}, ousted by {{m|fa|کاسنی|tr=kâsni}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|ar|now most common}} {{ar-IPA|طَرْخَشْقُون}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طَرْخَشْقُون|head2=طَرَخَشْقُون|head3=طَرَخْشَقُون|m}}

# [[dandelion]] ({{taxfmt|Taraxacum|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|هِنْدِبَاء}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|33|volume=2|page=601|passage=يؤخذ طرخشقون مجفف وعدس ونورة أجزاء سواء ويسحق الجميع وينخل ويعجن بسمن بقري عتيق ثم يوضع منه على فتيلة ويدخل في الناصور نافع وربما نفع وربما نفع منه الكي بالنار.|translation=One takes dried dandelion and lentils and lime at equal parts and grinds all and sieves and kneads with old cow butter and then one applies from it unto a wick and enters the fistula. It may be successful, however cauterization might prove more effective.}}
# [[common chicory]], [[Belgian endive]] ({{taxfmt|Cichorium intybus|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|هِنْدِبَاء بَرِّيَّة}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|طَرْخَشْقُون|head2=طَرَخَشْقُون|head3=طَرَخْشَقُون}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mul|''[[Taraxacum]]''}}
*: {{desc|pt|taráxaco|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|fa|طلخشکوک|طلخ شکوک}}
* {{desc|syc|ܛܪܫܩܘܩܐ|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{cite-book|de|last=Colditz|first=Iris|title=Zur Sozialterminologie der iranischen Manichäer. Eine semantische Analyse im Vergleich zu den nichtmanichäischen iranischen Quellen|location=Wiesbaden|publisher=Harrassowitz Verlag|year=2000|series=Iranica|seriesvolume=5|chapter=Mp. ''(i)škōh'', parth. ''iskōh''. Etymologie und semantische Entwicklung|pages=166 seqq.|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Zur_Sozialterminologie_der_iranischen_Ma/j9vCWI2LDQoC?gbpv=1&pg=PA166&printsec=frontcover|isbn=978-3-447-04255-0}}.
* {{R:xaa:Corriente|page=327}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=2|page=33}}
