Page 126 نجران: -------- begin text --------
==Arabic==
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ن ج ر}} in the sense {{m|ar|نَجْر|t=a root or stock or shape or figure}} {{suffix|ar||ـَان}} the sense of door-sill develops, and the walled city of Nejran, part of the {{w|Himyarite Kingdom}}, that already called it in its {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}} inscriptions {{m|xsa|𐩬𐩴𐩧𐩬|ts=nagrānu}}, had many gates. The same derivation for the sense of “thirsty” works from {{m|ar|نَجْر|t=heat; violent thirst}}.

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|نَجْرَان|f}}

# {{place|ar|A <<city>> in <<c/Saudi Arabia>> in the southwest close to [[Yemen]]|t1=Najran}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَجْرَان|state=ind-def}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَجْرَان|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# a [[horizontal]] piece of wood serving as the [[foot]] or [[sill]] of a [[door]] upon which it turns

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَجْرَان}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adjective|نَجْرَان}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# affected by a [[heating]] [[thirst]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|نَجْرَان}}
-------- end text --------
