{{also|Appendix:Variations of "an"}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|-ian||euphonic variant, also spelled -aean or -æan}}
* {{alter|en|-n||when added to a word ending in ''a''}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|-an}}, regularly {{m|enm|-ain}}, {{m|enm|-ein}}, {{m|enm|-en}}, from {{der|en|fro|-ain}}, {{m|fro|-ein}}, or before ''i'', {{m|fro|-en}} (modern {{cog|fr|-ain}}, {{m|fr|-en}}, feminine {{m|fr|-aine}}, {{m|fr|-enne}}), from {{der|en|la|-ānus}} (feminine {{m|la|-āna}}), which forms adjectives of belonging or origin from a noun, being {{m|la|-nus}} [cognate with {{cog|grc|-νος}}] preceded by a vowel, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*-nós}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|-en}}. Compare with {{m|en|-in}}, {{m|en|-ine}}.

===Suffix===
{{en-suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes|cat3=noun-forming suffixes}}

# Of or pertaining to; {{non-gloss definition|an adjectival suffix appended to various words, often nouns, to make an adjective form}}. {{qualifier|Often added to words of Latin origin, but also used with words of other origins. When a word ends in ''a'', {{m|en|-n}} is used instead.}}
#: {{syn|en|-al|-ar|-ese|-esque|-ic|-id|-ish|-like|-oid|-ous|-y}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|Rome|[[Roman|Rom'''an''']]}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Appended to nouns to form an [[agent noun]]}}. {{qualifier|When males with a profession are distinguished from females, males are ''-an'', females ''-(i)enne''.}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|comedy|comedian}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|history|historian}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|en}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|of or pertaining to}}
* Arabic: {{t+|ar|ـِيّ}}
* Catalan: {{t+|ca|-à}}
* Czech: {{t+|cs|-ský}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|-lainen}}, {{t+|fi|-läinen}}
* Galician: {{t|gl|-an|m}}, {{t|gl|-á|f}}
* German: {{t+|de|-isch}}
* Hungarian: {{t+|hu|-i}}, {{t+|hu|-s}}
* Ido: {{t|io|-an-}}
* Interlingua: {{t|ia|-an}}
* Italian: {{t+|it|-ano}}
* Latin: {{t|la|-ānus}}
* Portuguese: {{t+|pt|-ão|m}}, {{t+|pt|-ano|m}}, {{t|pt|-ana|f}}
* Spanish: {{t+|es|-ano}}
* Swedish: {{t|sv|-sk}}, {{t+|sv|-isk}},
{{trans-bottom}}

{{trans-top|agent noun suffix}}
* Hungarian: {{t+|hu|-ász}}, {{t+|hu|-ész}}, {{t|hu|-ikus}}
* Interlingua: {{t|ia|-ano|m}}, {{t|ia|-ana|f}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=an|n.a.|NA|-na|N/A|N.A.|n/a|Na|na}}

==Azerbaijani==

===Suffix===
{{az-suffix-forms|a=an|ə=ən|v=y}}
{{head|az|suffix form}}

# {{non-gloss|Postconsonantal form of {{m|az|-ən}} after the vowels A / I / O / U.}}

==Bikol Central==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bcl|phi-pro|*-an}}, from {{inh|bcl|poz-pro|*-an}}, from {{inh|bcl|map-pro|*-an}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|bcl|suffix}}

# a place where a large quantity of the thing meant by the root is put, planted, or can be found
#: {{suffixusex|bcl|basura|t1=trash|basurahan|t2=trash can}}
# a place where the action expressed by the root is performed
#: {{suffixusex|bcl|kawat|t1=play|kawatan|t2=playground}}

==Cebuano==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ceb|-han}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*-an}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*-an}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*-an}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ceb|/an/}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ceb|suffix|verb-forming suffix||inchoative|gi- -an|contemplative|-an|imperative|-i|negative|-i}}

# {{n-g|locative trigger verb suffix}}; to [[do]] at, in, on a [[place]]
#: {{ux|ceb|palit'''an''' nako ang tindahan og kendi|I will buy candy at the store {{q|'''store''' is focused.}}}}
## {{n-g|directive verb suffix}}; to do at, [[towards]] [[someone]]
##: {{uxi|ceb|gikataw-'''an''' niya ang lalaki|he laughed at the man}}
## {{n-g|partitive verb suffix}}; to do to a [[part]] of something
##: {{uxi|ceb|gikuha'''an''' niyag gamay ang keyk|he took a little of the cake.}}
# {{n-g|benefactive trigger verb suffix}}; to do [[something]] for someone/something [[else]]
#: {{ux|ceb|palit'''an''' nako ang bata og keyk|I will buy cake for the child {{q|'''child''' is focused.}}}}
## {{n-g|causative verb affix}}; to do [[because of]], [[due to]]
##: {{uxi|ceb|unsay gihilak'''an''' nimo?|What is it you are crying about?}}
# {{lb|ceb|with adjective bases}} to [[consider]] something as
#: {{uxi|ceb|lisor'''an''' siya mag-Tinagalog|He finds speaking in Tagalog hard}}
# {{lb|ceb|with noun bases}} to [[put]] something on someone; to [[give]] someone
#: {{uxi|ceb|sero'''han''' ta ka|I will give you a zero}}
#: {{uxi|ceb|sapatos'''an''' nako ang bata|I will put shoes on the child}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|ceb|ma- -an|mag- -an|tig- -an|pag- -an|paga- -an|ka- -an|kina- -an|gin- -an}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ceb|suffix|noun-forming suffix}}

# {{lb|ceb|added to nouns and verbs}} {{n-g|indicates a place where such objects are found, placed, or action done}}
#: {{syn|ceb|-anan|ka- -an}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|humay|t1=rice|humayan|t2=rice paddy}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|tinda|t1=to sell|tindahan|t2=store}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|tuba|t1=palm toddy|tubaan|t2=place where toddy is sold}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|basketbol|basketbolan|t2=basketball court}}
# {{lb|ceb|uncommon}} {{n-g|indicates an object used as an instrument}}
#: {{syn|ceb|pang-}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|baid|t1=to sharpen|bairan|t2=whetstone}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ceb|suffix|adjective-forming suffix}}

# {{lb|ceb|added to nouns}} {{n-g|characterized by having something in abundance}}; [[-ful]]
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|utok|t1=brain|utokan|t2=brainy}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|kuwarta|t1=money|kuwartahan|t2=rich}}
# {{lb|ceb|uncommon|added to adjectives or verbs}} {{n-g|characterized by being or doing such}}; [[-ly]]
#: {{syn|ceb|-on|-anon}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|talaw|t1=to back off|talawan|t2=cowardly}}
#: {{suffixusex|ceb|langas|t1=moving about a lot|langasan}} {{q|same meaning}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|ceb|-in- -an}}

===References===
* {{R:Wolff 1972|41}}

==Chuukese==

===Suffix===
{{head|chk|suffix}}

# {{lb|chk|added to possessive nouns}} [[his]], [[hers]], [[its]]

====Related terms====
{{chk-possessive adjectives}}

==Cimbrian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cim|gmh|-en}}, a merger of various terminations in {{inh|cim|goh|-}} reflecting different conjugational patterns, namely {{m|goh|-an}}, {{m|goh|-ōn}}, {{m|goh|-en}} ({{m|goh|-ien}}), and {{m|goh|-nen}}, from {{der|cim|gem-pro|*-aną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-ōną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-janą}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-āną}}, and {{m|gem-pro|*-naną}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|-en}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|cim|suffix}}

# {{ngd|A suffix of all verbs in their infinitive form.}}

