==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
From earlier {{m|fi|-han}}, {{m|fi|-hVn|pos=now dialectal}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*-hën}}, {{m|urj-fin-pro|*-sën|pos=passive or reflexive suffix}}, the same as the third-person singular possessive suffix (see the possessive suffix entry on {{m|fi|-Vn|id=illative}}). Initial {{m|fi||-ta-}} is from the passive marker {{m|urj-fin-pro|*-tta-}}.

====Suffix====
{{fi-suffix|var=än}}

# {{lb|fi|personal}} {{n-g|Forms the [[impersonal]] [[indicative]] [[present]] forms of verbs, appended to the first infinitive.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Attached to the passive verb stem.

===Etymology 2===
See {{m|fi|-Vn|id=illative|pos=illative suffix}}.

====Suffix====
{{fi-suffix|var=än}}

# {{q|case suffix}} {{n-g|A suffix variant for the illative singular, see {{m|fi|-Vn}}.}}
#: {{sufex|fi|laiva|laivaan}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|fi|possessive}}
See {{m|fi|-Vn|id=possessive|pos=possessive suffix}}.

====Suffix====
{{fi-suffix|var=än}}

# {{lb|fi|possessive}} {{n-g|A variant for the third-person suffix {{m|fi|-nsa}}.}}

=====Usage notes=====
See the usage notes under {{m|fi|-Vn|id=possessive}} and {{m|fi|-nsa}}.

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|fi|a=an|-na}}

[[Category:Finnish case suffixes]]
[[Category:Finnish personal suffixes]]
[[Category:Finnish possessive suffix variants]]

