==Hungarian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hu-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|hu|ɒn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{rfe|hu}}

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|adverb}} {{lb|hu|[[deadjectival]] adverb-forming suffix}} {{n-g|Added to an [[adjective]] to create an [[adverb]].}}
#: {{afex|hu|pontos|t1=accurate|pontos'''an'''|t2=accurate'''ly'''}}
# {{senseid|hu|number}} {{lb|hu|[[denumeral]] and [[depronominal]] adverb-forming suffix}} {{n-g|Added to a [[numeral]] or a [[pronoun]] with this sense to create an [[adverb]], expressing the number of people.}}
#: {{afex|hu|hat|t1=six|hat'''an'''|t2=six people, six of us/you/them}}
#: {{uxi|hu|'''Hatan''' mentünk moziba.|'''Six of us''' went to the cinema.}}
#: {{afex|hu|nyolc|t1=eight|nyolc'''an'''|t2=eight people, eight of us/you/them}}
#: {{uxi|hu|'''Nyolcan''' vannak a szobában.|There are '''eight people''' in the room.}}
#: {{afex|hu|hány|t1=how many|hány'''an'''|t2=how many (of us/you/them)}}
#: {{afex|hu|néhány|t1=some, a few|néhány'''an'''|t2=some (of us/you/them)}}
#: {{afex|hu|sok|t1=many|sok'''an'''|t2=many (of us/you/them)}}
#: {{uxi|hu|'''Sokan''' vannak a meghívottak, de kevesen a választottak.|For '''many''' are called, but few are chosen.}}
#: {{afex|hu|millió|t1=million|millió'''an'''|t2=a million (of us/you/them)}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{U:hu:adverb-an}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|hu|pos=adverb}}

===Etymology 2===
{{rfe|hu}}

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|verb}} {{lb|hu|verb-forming suffix}} {{n-g|Added to a [[stem]] ― often an [[onomatopoeia]] ― to form a [[verb]] expressing an [[instantaneous]] action.}}
#: {{m|hu|katt'''an'''|t=to click, to make one clicking sound}}
#: {{m|hu|robb'''an'''|t=to explode}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{q|verb-forming suffix}} Variants:
*: '''{{l|hu|-on|id=verb}}''' is added to some back-vowel words
*: '''{{l|hu|-an|id=verb}}''' is added to back-vowel words
*: '''{{l|hu|-en|id=verb}}''' is added to front-vowel words

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|hu|pos=verb}}

===See also===
* [[Appendix:Hungarian suffixes]]

===Further reading===
* {{sense|suffix of the adverb of number}} {{R:Rounds 2001}}, p.&nbsp;189 {{nowrap|(p. 204 in the PDF)}}

{{cln|hu|terms with multiple lemma etymologies|terms with multiple morpheme etymologies}}

==Indonesian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|id|[-an]}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|id|ms|-an}}, from {{inh|id|ms-cla|-ان|tr=an}}, from {{inh|id|poz-mly-pro|*-an}}, from {{inh|id|poz-pro|*-an}}, from {{inh|id|map-pro|*-an}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|id|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes}}

# {{n-g|Added to a noun}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for collectivity}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|laut|t1=sea|lautan|t2=ocean}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for place}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|pangkal|t1=origin|pangkalan|t2=base}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for value}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|ribu|t1=thousand|ribuan|t2=}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for measurement result}}; [[-s]]
##: {{suffixusex|id|kilo|t1=kilo|kiloan|t2=}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} [[-s]]; {{n-g|Suffix for quantity (about value)}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|ratus|t1=hundred|ratusan|t2=hundreds}}
## [[-ly]], specifying time intervals, having the sense of "occurring at such intervals".
##: {{suffixusex|id|hari|t1=day|harian|t2=daily}}
# {{n-g|Added to an verb to create an noun}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for object}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|makan|t1=to eat|makanan|t2=food}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for place}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|kubur|t1=to bury|kuburan|t2=grave}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for result}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|didik|t1=to educate|didikan|t2=}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for tool}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|timbang|t1=to weigh|timbangan|t2=balance}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for way or method}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|pimpin|t1=to lead|pimpinan|t2=leader}}
# {{n-g|Added to an adjective to create an noun}}
## {{n-g|Suffix for having property}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|asin|t1=salty|asinan|t2=pickle}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} {{n-g|Suffix for intensity (quality or quantity)}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|tinggi|t1=high|tinggian|t2=higher}}
# {{n-g|Suffix for similarity}}

===Etymology 2===
{{sl|id|jv|-ꦲꦤ꧀}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|id|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes}}

# {{n-g|verb-forming}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} to [[use]] of [base]
##: {{suffixusex|id|sepeda|t1=bicycle|sepedaan|t2=to ride a bicycle}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} to [[hold]] or to [[have]] [base]
##: {{suffixusex|id|selamat|t1=safe|selamatan|t2=to celebrate with offerings to the spirits to assure the safety}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|rujak|t1=a kind of salad|rujakan|t2=to have ''rujak'' to be eaten or made}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} to [[do]] as indicated by the [base]
##: {{suffixusex|id|sendiri|t1=alone|sendirian|t2=by oneself}}
# {{n-g|noun-forming}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} the location of [base]
##: {{suffixusex|id|sekolah|t1=school|sekolahan|t2=school complex}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} the cost of [base]
##: {{suffixusex|id|becak|t1=rickshaw|becakan|t2=rickshaw fare}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} [base]-[[usage]]
##: {{suffixusex|id|sepeda|t1=bicycle|sepedaan|t2=bicycle-riding}}
## {{lb|id|colloquial}} event of [base]
##: {{suffixusex|id|selamat|t1=safe|selamatan|t2=celebration with offerings to the spirits to assure the safety}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|rujak|t1=a kind of salad|rujakan|t2=''rujak'' eating or production}}
##: {{suffixusex|id|susu|t1=milk|susuan|t2=breast-feeding period}}

===Etymology 3===
{{sl|id|jv|-ꦲꦼꦤ꧀}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|id|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes}}

# {{lb|id|colloquial}} [[suffering]] of [base]
#: {{suffixusex|id|koreng|t1=ulcer|korengan|t2=serious infection disease}}
#: {{suffixusex|id|uban|t1=grey hair|ubanan|t2=grey haired condition}}

===Derived terms===
{{der4|id|
| ber- -an
| ke- -an
| peng- -an
| per- -an
}}
{{suffixsee|id}}

===References===
* {{cite-book|id|author=Badan Pengembangan dan Pembinaan Bahasa|title=Tata Bahasa Baku Bahasa Indonesia|trans-title=Standard Grammar of Indonesian Language|url=https://acuanbahasa.kemdikbud.go.id/book/12/5cb467d936a24|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220613233214/https://acuanbahasa.kemdikbud.go.id/book/12/5cb467d936a24|archivedate=13 June 2022|edition=4|location=Jakarta|publisher=Kementerian Pendidikan dan Kebudayaan|year=2017|isbn=978-979-069-263-3|accessdate=8 July 2022}}
* {{cite-book|author=James N. Sneddon|title=Indonesian : a comprehensive grammar|year=2010|publisher=Roultedge|location=London|edition=2|isbn=978-0-415-58154-7|oclc=564132877}}

