==Ojibwe==

===Final===
{{head|oj|final|cat2=verb finals|cat3=inanimate intransitive verb finals}}

# be in a state or condition

====Derived terms====
* {{l|oj|waaban}}
* {{l|oj|aawan}}

====See also====
* {{l|oj|-aa}}
* {{l|oj|-izi}}

====References====
* The Ojibwe People's Dictionary https://ojibwe.lib.umn.edu/word-part/an-final

===Suffix===
{{head|oj|suffix|cat2=noun suffixes|cat3=verb suffixes|cat4=verb class markers}}

# {{non-gloss definition|A suffix denoting the [[plural]] of an inanimate noun}}
# {{non-gloss definition|A suffix denoting the obviative form of an animate noun}}
# {{non-gloss definition|A suffix denoting the [[second-person singular]] [[imperative]] of a transitive inanimate verb (vti)}}

====Usage notes====
As the suffix denoting the second-person singular imperative form, '''-an''' also acts as the class marker for unmarked ''(-am theme)'' transitive inanimate verbs (vti).

====See also====
* {{l|oj|-n}}
* {{l|oj|-iin}}
* {{l|oj|-oon}}
* {{l|oj|-wan}}
* {{l|oj|-yan}}

[[Category:Ojibwe imperative verb suffixes]]

