==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|gd|sga|-án}}, from {{inh|gd|pgl|-ᚐᚌᚅᚔ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|gd|/an/}}

====Usage notes====
The non-[[schwa]] clear vowel {{IPAchar|/a/}} distinguishes this from the homograph plural suffix {{m|gd||-an}} which is pronounced {{IPAchar|/ən/}} i.e. with a schwa.

====Suffix====
{{head|gd|suffix|g=m}}

# {{n-g|A masculine suffix used to form [[noun]]s meaning a smaller form of something, often used for male [[given name]]s.}}
#: {{m|gd|Cailean}}, {{m|gd|Eòghan}}, {{m|gd|Ailean}}, {{m|gd|Beathan}}
#: {{m|gd|clàran}}, {{m|gd|clachan}}, {{m|gd|bioran}}

===Etymology 2===
Cognate to {{cog|ga|-anna}}, {{cog|gv|-yn}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|gd|/ən/}}

====Suffix====
{{head|gd|suffix|g=p|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Used to form [[regular]] [[plural]]s of nouns.}}
#: {{suffixusex|gd|clach|t1=stone|clachan}}
#: {{suffixusex|gd|damh|t1=ox, stag|damhan}}
#: {{suffixusex|gd|leannan|t1=lover, sweetheart|leannanan}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|gd}}

