==Spanish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|es|la|-ant}}, the third-person plural present active indicative ending of first conjugation verbs.

====Suffix====
{{head|es|suffix form}}

# {{n-g|Suffix indicating the [[third-person plural]] (also used with {{m|es|ustedes}}) [[present]] [[indicative]] of {{m|es|-ar}} verbs.}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|es|la|-eant}}, {{inh|es|la|-ant}}, and {{inh|es|la|-iant}}, the third-person plural present active subjunctive endings of second, third, and fourth conjugation verbs, respectively.

====Suffix====
{{head|es|suffix form}}

# {{n-g|Suffix indicating the [[third-person plural]] (also used with {{m|es|ustedes}}) present subjunctive of {{m|es|-er}} and {{m|es|-ir}} verbs.}}
# {{n-g|Suffix indicating the third-person plural [[imperative]] of {{m|es|-er}} and {{m|es|-ir}} verbs.}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|es|-en}}

