{{also|its|ITS|its'|'its}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|i's}} {{qualifier|eye dialect}}
* {{l|en|it'sa}} {{q|pseudo-Italian}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪts/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-it's.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪts|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|its}}

===Etymology 1===
[[contraction|Contraction]] of ‘[[it]] [[is]]’, ‘it [[has]]’ or 'it [[was]]'.

====Contraction====
{{en-cont|head=it’s}}

# {{contraction of|en|[[it]] [[is]]}}
#: {{ux|en|'''it’s''' too expensive;&nbsp; '''it’s''' coming right for us!; [[it's a free country|'''it's''' a free country]]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1743|author=Martin Marley|title=The Good Confessor|page=307|passage=[...], guided not by his own Will, but by the Medick Science, which dictates, that '''it's''' recessary, beneficial, and convenient to alter, mix, and temper this medicine, and fit it to the Disposition, and Constitution of the Patient[.]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-21|author=w:Oliver Burkeman
|volume=189|issue=2|page=48|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.theguardian.com/technology/2013/may/10/conscious-computing-twitter-facebook-google The tao of tech]
|passage=The dirty secret of the internet is that all this distraction and interruption is immensely profitable. Web companies like to boast about{{...}}and so on. But the real way to build a successful online business is to be better than your rivals at undermining people's control of their own attention. Partly, this is a result of how online advertising has traditionally worked: advertisers pay for clicks, and a click is a click, however '''it's''' obtained.}}
# {{contraction of|en|[[it]] [[has]]}}
#: {{ux|en|'''It’s''' been a long time since I’ve had cheesecake.}}
# {{contraction of|en|[[it]] [[was]]}}
#: {{ux|en|'''It’s''' the same stoneground flour from this week that we used to make last week's strudel.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Dominique Roques
|title=Pico Bogue - Volume 4 - Striking the Balance|chapter=|url=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/Pico_Bogue_Volume_4_Striking_the_Balance/ZjN_DQAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0|page=31|passage=I guess for you '''it's''' the past that had a surprise in store.}}
# {{lb|en|dialectal}} [[there's|There's]], [[there is]]; [[there're]], [[there are]].
#: {{ux|en|'''it's''' a fine line between love and hate;&nbsp;'''it's''' a package for you by the door}}

=====Usage notes=====
* See [[its#Usage notes|Usage under “its”]]

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|it is}} {{l|en|’tis}}
* {{sense|it was}} {{l|en|’twas}}

=====Translations=====
