===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|adjectival}} 
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyg-|id=like}}
From {{inh|en|enm|-ly}}, {{m|enm|-li}}, {{m|enm|-lik}}, {{m|enm|-lich}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-līċ}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*-līk}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*-līkaz||having the body or form of}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*līką||body}} (whence {{m|en|lich}}). In form, probably influenced by {{cog|non|-ligr|t=-ly}} (Norwegian Bokmål -lig, Faroese -ligur, Icelandic -legur). Cognate with {{cog|nl|-lijk}}, {{cog|de|-lich}}, {{cog|da|-lig}} and {{cog|sv|-lig}}. {{doublet|en|-like}}.

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes|cat3=productive suffixes}}

# {{ngd|Used to form [[adjective]]s from [[noun]]s, the adjectives having the sense of "[[behaving]] [[like]], or having a [[nature]] [[typical]] of what is denoted by the noun"  Similar in meaning to [[-like]] but most often paired with animate nouns.}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|man|manly}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|friend|friendly}}
# {{ngd|Used to form adjectives from nouns, the adjectives having the sense of "[[appearing]] [[like]], [[resembling]], or having the [[likeness]] of what is denoted by the noun".}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|bloom|bloomly}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|priest|priestly}}
# {{ngd|Used to form adjectives from nouns specifying time intervals, the adjectives having the sense of "[[occurring]] at such [[interval]]s".}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|month|monthly}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|day|daily}}

