===Etymology 2===
{{root|enm|ine-pro|*leyg-|id=like}}
From {{inh|enm|ang|-līċe}}, itself a combination of the adjective-forming suffix {{m|ang|-līċ}} (see etymology 1 above) and the adverbial suffix {{m|ang|-e}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|enm|-lich|-liche|-lyche|-lych|-li|-lie|-lye|-like|-lik|-licke|-lyke|-lyk|-lycke|-leche|-le|-lei|-loche|-lice|-liȝ|-luche}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|enm|/-liː/|/-liːt͡ʃ(ə)/|/-lit͡ʃ(ə)/}}

====Suffix====
{{head|enm|suffix|comparative|-lyere|superlative|-lyest}}

# {{senseid|enm|adverbial}} Used to form [[adverb]]s from adjectives, and nouns; the adverbs having the sense of "in the manner of what is denoted by the adjective/noun".
# Optionally appended to adverbs without suffixes with no change to the meaning.

=====Usage notes=====
* As with its adjectival equivalent, ''-ly'' is generally the most common variant of this suffix, though in some words, other variants may be more common, such as ''-lich(e)''.

=====Derived terms=====
