===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|hi|fa-cls|ـانه|tr=-āna}}.

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|ur=ـانہ}}

# {{lb|hi|somewhat|_|productive}} [[-ly]], [[like]] ..., {{non-gloss definition|forms adjectives}}
#: {{suffixusex|hi|दोस्त|दोस्ताना|gloss1=friend|gloss2=friendly}}

===Derived terms===
{{suffixsee|hi|pos=adjective}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|hi|pra-sau|-𑀆𑀯𑁂𑀤𑀺}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-आपयति}}.

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|ur=ـانا}}

# {{lb|hi|highly|_|productive}} {{n-g|forms [[transitive]] or [[causative]] verbs from other verbs}}
#: {{suffixusex|hi|उठना|उठाना|t1=to rise|t2=to raise}}
# {{n-g|forms verbs from nouns or adjectives}}
#: {{suffixusex|hi|दफ़न|दफ़नाना|t1=burial|t2=to bury}}

=====Usage notes=====
Almost all [[Perso-Arabic]] and learned Sanskrit [[tatsama]] borrowings are nominal. Most of these nominals are verbalized as compound verbs with some base verb, usually {{m|hi|करना}}, as in {{m|hi|साफ़ करना|t=to clean}}. A smaller number of verbs are formed directly from the noun with suffixes like {{m|hi|-ना}} and this one.

=====Conjugation=====
{{hi-conj}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|hi|pos=verb}}

