Page 1 من: Skipped, no changes
Page 1 من: -------- begin text --------
==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-wes-pro|*min}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|מִן|tr=min}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مِنْ}}

====Preposition====
{{ar-prep|مِنْ}}

# {{n-g|having [[w:en:partitive|partitive]] effect}}: [[of]], [[some]] of, parts of, one of
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|11|78|passage=أَلَيْسَ '''مِنْكُمْ''' رَجُلٌ رَشِيدٌ|t=Is there not a right-minded man '''among you'''?}}
# made of
#: {{ux|ar|تِمْثَالٌ '''مِنَ''' الرُّخَامِ|a statue '''of''' marble}}
#: {{ux|ar|خَاتَمٌ '''مِنْ''' ذَهَبٍ|a ring '''of''' gold, a gold ring}}
# containing, including
#: {{ux|ar|كُوبٌ '''مِنَ''' الْقَهْوَةِ|a cup '''of''' coffee}}
# [[pertaining]] to
# [[to wit]]
# [[from]], [[away]] from, [[out of]]
# {{qualifier|time}} [[at]], [[on]]
# in [[relation]] to, [[with respect to]]
# [[due to]], [[owing to]]
#: {{ux|ar|مَاتَ '''مِنَ''' الْعَطَشِ|He died '''of''' thirst.}}
# {{lbl|ar|used to construe certain verbs}}
#: {{ux|ar|تَمَكَّنُوا '''مِنْهُ'''|They took power '''over him'''.}}
# [[between]]; [[in]] [[contrast]] [[with]]
#: {{ux|ar|مَيَّزَ الْجَيِّدَ '''مِنَ''' الرَّدِيءِ|He differentiated/discerned '''between''' the good and the bad}}
#: {{ux|ar|عَرَفَ الْحَقَّ '''مِنَ''' الْبَاطِلِ|He knew truth '''from''' falsehood}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|220|passage=وَٱللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ الْمُفْسِدَ '''مِنَ''' الْمُصْلِحِ|And Allah knows the corrupter '''from''' the amender.|subst=وَٱللّٰهُ/وَ-لّٰهُ}}
# {{lb|ar|negative polarity item}} [[any]]
#: {{usex|ar|هَلْ فِي ذَٰلِكَ '''مِنْ''' شَكٍّ؟|Is there '''any''' doubt about that?}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|41|47|passage=وَمَا تَحْمِلُ '''مِنْ''' أُنْثَىٰ وَلَا تَضَعُ إِلَّا بِعِلْمِهِ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|35|3|passage=هَلْ '''مِنْ''' خَالِقٍ غَيْرُ ٱللّٰهِ يَرْزُقُكُمْ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَاءِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ|t=Is there '''any''' creator other than Allah who provides for you from the heaven and earth?|subst=وَ/وَ-}}
# [[than]] {{qualifier|with comparatives}}

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|مِنْ|ni=+}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|مِمَّا}}
* {{l|ar|مِمَّ}}
* {{l|ar|مِمَّنْ}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ بَابِ أَوْلَى}}
* {{l|ar|[[من بعد|مِنْ بُعْدٍ/بَعْدُ]]|t=from afar}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ بَعْدِ|t=after}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ قَبْلُ|t=from the front}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ قَبْلِ|t=before}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ قُبُلِ|t=by, from the part of}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ حَيْثُ|t=from where, whence}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ دُونِ|t=without}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْ غَيْرِ|t=without}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mt|minn}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*mann-}}. Cognates include {{cog|arc|מן|tr=man}}, {{cog|gez|መኑ|tr=männu}} and {{cog|am|ማን }}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَنْ}}

====Pronoun====
{{ar-pron|مَنْ|m}}

# {{lb|ar|interrogative}} [[who]]?
# {{lb|ar|interrogative}} [[which]]?, [[which]] one?
# {{lb|ar|relative}} [[who]], the one who, he who, those who, everyone who
# {{lb|ar|conditional}} [[whoever]]
#: {{usex|ar|مَنْ [[جَدَّ]] [[وَجَدَ]]|[[seek and ye shall find]]|lit='''Whoever''' strives will find}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|99|7-8
|passage=فَ'''مَنْ''' يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيْرًا يَرَهُ<br>وَ'''مَنْ''' يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ شَرًّا يَرَهُ
|translation=So '''whoever''' does an atom's weight of good will see it, <br> And '''whoever''' does an atom's weight of evil will see it.
|subst=وَ'''مَنْ'''/وَ-'''مَنْ''',فَ'''مَنْ'''/فَ-'''مَنْ'''}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Grammatically a masculine singular, the pronoun is semantically gender- and number-neutral.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|لِمَن}} ،{{l|ar|فَمَن}} ،{{l|ar|أَفَمَن}}

===Etymology 3===
{{ar-rootbox|م ن ن}}
The noun is modelled on a large scale upon {{bor|ar|arc|מַנָּא}} / {{m|syc|ܡܢܐ|tr=mannā}} from the same root.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u}}

# to be [[kind]], [[kindly]], [[benign]], [[gracious]], [[benevolent]] ({{l|ar|عَلَى}})
# to [[show]], to [[grant]], to [[confer]] ({{l|ar|عَلَى}})
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[cut off]], to [[curtail]]
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[jade]], to [[tire]]
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[decrease]], to [[diminish]], to [[reduce]]
# to [[reproach]], to [[upbraid]] {{+obj|ar|&transitive<with ''the benefit received''> + :عَلَى<whom>}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|26|22|passage=وَتِلْكَ نِعْمَةٌ '''تَمُنُّهَا''' عَلَيَّ أَنْ عَبَّدتَّ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ|t=And this is the past favour wherewith thou reproachest me: that thou hast enslaved the Children of Israel.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u|passive=y|vn=مَنٌّ،مِنَّة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَنّ|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|مَنَّ|form=I}}
# [[favor]], [[benefit]], [[blessing]], [[boon]]
# [[gracious]] [[bestowal]], [[gift]], [[largess]]
# [[manna]]
#* {{RQ:Quran|20|80|passage=يَٰبَنِي إِسْرَاءِيلَ قَدْ أَنْجَيْنَٰكُمْ مِّنْ عَدُوِّكُمْ وَوَٰعَدْنَٰكُمْ جَانِبَ ٱلطُّورِ ٱلْأَيْمَنَ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْ'''مَنَّ''' وَٱلسَّلْوَىٰ|t=O sons of Israel, We did deliver you from your enemy and We did covenant with you on the right side of the Mount [Sinai] and We did send down unto you the '''manna''' and the quails.}}
#* {{RQ:SVD|Exodus|16|35|passage=وَأَكَلَ بَنُو إِسْرَاءِيلَ ٱلْ'''مَنَّ''' أَرْبَعِينَ سَنَةً حَتَّىٰ جَاءُوا إِلَىٰ أَرْضٍ عَامِرَةٍ.|t=And the sons of Israel have eaten the '''manna''' [for] forty years, until their coming to the land to be inhabited.}}
# {{lb|ar|countable}} a [[sweet]] [[liquid]] [[substance]] such as [[honey]], [[nectar]], or [[manna]]; [[honeydew]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَنّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|مَنّ|m|sing=مَنَّة}}

# {{c|ar|Hemipterans}} [[aphid]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|مَنّ}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Ahrens-Christliches|part=1|page=25}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel-V|page=21}}
* {{R:ar:Jeffery-Foreign|pages=271–272}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{bor|ar|arc|מָנָא|tr=mānā}}<!--({{cog|jpa|מָנָא|tr=mānā}} – {{cog|tmr|מַנְיָא|tr=manyā}} with plural {{m|arc|מְנֵי|tr=manē}} and {{m|arc|מְנׅין|tr=mnīn}}, {{cog|syc|ܡܲܢܝܵܐ|tr=manyā}} with plural {{m|syc|ܡ̈ܢܝܼܢ|tr=mənīn}} and {{m|syc|ܡ̈ܢܲܝܵܐ|tr=mənayā}}, {{cog|arc-imp|𐡌𐡍𐡉𐡀}} with absolute state {{m|arc|𐡌𐡍𐡄}} and plural absolute state {{m|arc|𐡌𐡍𐡉𐡍}})-->, from {{der|ar|akk|𒈠𒉡𒌑|tr=manû}}, whence also {{cog|sux|𒈠𒈾|tr=ma-na|ts=mana}} and {{cog|he|מָנֶה|tr=mānḗ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَنّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَنّ|m|pl=أَمْنَان}}

# {{c|ar|Units of measure}} a [[historical]] [[unit]] of [[mass]] – translatable as [[mina]] or [[maund]] – varying usually between ca. 1–3 [[kilogram]]s, however in some cases also going up over 40 [[kilogram]]s.

