==North Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|apc|ar|مِن|t=from, of, than}}. Possibly conflated with {{inh|apc|ar|مُنْذُ||since, for}} in some senses.

====Preposition====
{{head|apc|preposition|tr=min, mn, mni}}

# [[than]]
# [[from]], [[of]]
#: {{ux|apc|تعبت من الحكي
| tr = tʿibt '''mni''' l-ḥaki|I’m tired '''of''' talking.
}}
# [[ago]]
#: {{ux|apc|شفتك من كم يوم|tr=šiftak '''min''' kam yōm|t=I saw you a few days '''ago'''.}}
# [[since]]
#: {{ux|apc|من إيام المدرسة مش حاكيين
|tr='''min''' ʾiyyām il-madrase miš ḥākyīn|t=We haven't spoken '''since''' [our] school days.
}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The underlying form is ''min'', but the pronunciation is determined by the phonotactical environment. The medial ''-i-'' will usually be deleted following vowels (including epenthetic linking vowels as in the example above).
* Suffixes are attached to the stem ''minn-'', for example {{m|apc|منك|tr=minnak|t=from you}}. The third-person singular feminine merges with the first-person plural as {{m|apc|منا|tr=minna|t=from her; from us}}. However, the feminine may also be realized as {{m|apc|منها|tr=minha}}, and the plural occasionally as {{m|apc|منِنا|tr=minina|pos=specifically {{IPAchar|/mɪnina/}}}}, to avoid confusion. (The latter change is rarer, but can be seen somewhat-more-commonly in analogous dialectical derivations of the stem {{m|apc|إن|tr=inn-|t=that}}.)

====Conjunction====
{{head|apc|conjunction|tr=min}}

# [[since]] ... was/were; {{ngd
|followed by a personal pronoun + [[و]] to express a now-untrue past state}}
#: {{ux|apc|من أنا وصغير|tr='''min''' ana w-ẓḡīr|t='''ever since''' I was little}}
#: {{ux|apc|من نحنا وبالمدرسة مش حاكيين
|tr='''min''' niḥna w-bi-l-madrase mish ḥākyīn|t=We haven't spoken '''since''' we were in school.
}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|apc|ar|[[مَا]] [[إنَّ]]}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|apc|adverb|tr=mann}}

# {{lb|apc|false verb}} [[not]] to [[be]] {{q|always followed by a personal suffix}}
#: {{ux|apc|المحل منو مفتوح|tr=l-maḥall '''mannu''' maftūḥ|t=The shop '''isn’t''' open.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|apc|مش|tr=miš}}
* {{l|apc|مان|tr=mān}} {{q|regional}}

