==Persian==
{{fa-regional|من|من|ман}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fa|pal|𐫖𐫗|tr=man|t=me (early), I (later)}} from {{inh|fa|peo|𐎶𐎴|ts=mana|t=me}} from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*máHm}} from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*máHm||accusative singular of *aȷ́ʰám}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|मा|t=me}}, {{cog|ae|𐬨𐬀𐬥𐬀|t=me}}, {{cog|grc|ἐμέ|t=accusative of  "ἐγώ"}}, and {{cog|la|me|t=accusative of "ego"}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|fa|مو<tr:mu>|مه<tr:ma>||dialectal}}

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|man|kbl=ma}}
* {{audio|fa|Fa-من.ogg|a=Iran}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|fa|pronoun|head=مَن|tr=man}}

# [[I]]
#: {{syn|fa|بنده<tr:bande><q:dated>|اینجانب<tr:injâneb>}}
#: {{uxi|fa|من'' رفتم''.|I went.|tr='''man''' raftam.}}
#: {{uxi|fa|او ''من'' را دید.|He saw me.|tr=u '''man''' râ did.}}
# {{lb|fa|generally with following {{m|fa|را}}}} [[me]]
#: {{syn|fa|بنده<tr:bande><q:dated>|اینجانب<tr:injâneb>}}
# {{lb|fa|at the end of a Genitive [[ezafe]]}} [[my]]

=====Usage notes=====
* When acting as the grammatical object, the form {{m|fa||من را|tr=man râ}} is used. Which can be contracted into {{m|fa|مرا|tr=marâ}}.
* {{a|fa|colloquial|IR}} when acting as the grammatical object it is commonly contracted with {{m|fa|را|tr=râ}} into {{m|fa|منو|tr=mano}}.

====See also====
{{fa-personal pronouns}}
{{prs-personal pronouns}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|fa|pal|-}}, from {{der|fa|akk|𒈠𒉡𒌑|tr=manû}}.

