|page=385
|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=xGBYRAIfExsC&pg=PA385
|text={{...}}Yang-yüeh {{lang|zh|楊粵}},⁴⁰ reaching as far as '''O''' {{lang|zh|鄂}}.⁴¹{{...}}He then enthroned his elder son K'ang {{lang|zh|康}}⁴³ as King of Kou Tan {{lang|zh|句亶}},⁴⁴ his middle song Hung {{lang|zh|紅}} as King of '''O''' {{lang|zh|鄂}},⁴⁵ and his younger son Chih-tz'u {{lang|zh|執疵}} as King of Yüeh-chang {{lang|zh|越章}}.⁴⁶}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|O-ch'eng}}, {{l|en|O-chou}}

