{{fa-IPA|kū}}

====Adverb====
{{head|fa|adverb|tr=ku}}

# {{lb|fa|colloquial|or|poetic}} [[where]] [[is]]...
#: {{syn|fa|[[کجا]][[است|ست]]|tr=kojâ-st}}
#: {{uxi|fa|مدادت کو؟|tr=medâd-et '''ku'''?|t='''Where is''' your pencil?}}
#: {{uxi|fa|مرده کو؟|tr=mard-e '''ku'''?|t='''Where is''' the man?|q=colloquial}}
#* {{RQ:Masnavi|III|1174|[[بعد از]] [[آن]] [[گفتن|گفتند]] [[ای]] [[مادر]] [[بیا]] / [[گور]] [[بابا]] کو [[تو]] [[ما]] [[را]] [[ره]] [[نما]]|ba'd az ân goftand ey mâdar biy-â / gur-e bâbâ '''ku''' to mâ râ rah namâ|Afterwards they said, "Come, O mother, '''where is''' our father's grave? Do thou show us the way."}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|chapter=Ghazal 470 ({{w|Sīne mālāmāl-e dard ast}})|title={{lang|fa|{{w|lang=fa|دیوان حافظ}}}}|trans-title=[[divan|Divān]] of {{w|Hafez|Ḥāfeẓ}}|author={{w|Hafez|Xāja Shams-ud-Dīn Moḥammad Ḥāfeẓ-e Shīrāzī}}|text=[[سوختن|سوختم]] [[در]] [[چاه]] [[صبر]] [[از]] [[بهر]] [[آن]] [[شمع]] [[چگل]]<br>[[شاه]] [[ترک|ترکان]] [[فارغ]] [[است]] [[از]] [[حال]] [[ما]] کو [[رستم|رستمی]]|tr=suxtam dar čâh-e sabr az bahr-e ân šam'-e čegel<br>šâh-e torkân fâreğ ast az hâl-e mâ '''ku''' rostami|t=I burnt in the well of patience on account of that candle of Chigil;<br>The king of the Turks cares not for my condition, '''where is''' a Rostam?|year=late 1300s}}
# {{lb|fa|archaic}} [[where]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|chapter=baxš 28 (nešastan-e Bahrām ruz-e došanbe dar gonbad sabz o afsāne goftan doxtar-e pādšāh-e eqlim sevom)|title={{lang|fa|{{w|lang=fa|هفت پیکر}}}}|trans-title=[[Haft Peykar]]|author={{w|Nizami Ganjavi|Hakim Nizāmi Ganjavi}}|text=کو [[شد]] [[آن]] [[دعوی]] [[دوازده]] [[فن]]<br>[[و]] [[آن]] [[همه]] [[مردی]] [[این]] [[نه]] [[مرد]] [[و]] [[نه]] [[زن]]|tr='''ku''' šod ân davi davâzdah fan<br>vânhame mardi in na mard o na zan|t=;<br>|year=}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|kō}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=ku}}

# {{alternative form of|fa|کوی|tr=kuy|t=street; city block}}.

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|kō}}

====Contraction====
{{head|fa|contraction|tr=ku}}

# {{contraction of|fa|[[که]] [[او]]|tr=ke u|t=that he/she...; which...}}
#* {{RQ:Masnavi|III|4|[[این]] [[چراغ]] [[شمس]] کو [[روشن]] [[بود]] / [[نه]] [[از]] [[فتیل]] [[و]] [[پنبه]] [[و]] [[روغن]] [[بود]]|in čerâğ šams '''ku''' rowšan bud / na az fatil o panbe o rowğan bud|This lamp, the sun, '''which is''' bright—it is not by means of wick and cotton and oil.}}

==Urdu==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ur|inc-ohi|काहू}}, {{m|inc-ohi|काहु}}, from {{inh|ur|pra-sau}}, from {{inh|ur|sa|कक्षे||in the armpit|tr=kákṣe}}, locative singular of {{m|sa|कक्ष||[[armpit]]|tr=kákṣa}}, from {{inh|ur|inc-pro|*káṭṣas}}, from {{inh|ur|iir-pro|*káćšas}}, from {{inh|ur|ine-pro|*koḱs-|*kóḱsos|joint}}.<ref>{{cite-book|chapter=The diverse origins of the Hindi simple postpositions|title=Grammaticalization and the Rise of Configurationality in Indo-Aryan|last=Reinöhl|first=Uta|year=2016|isbn=9780198736660}}</ref> Compare {{cog|dcc|کو|tr=kū}}, {{cog|bra|कौ}}, {{cog|as|-ক|tr=-k}}.

The semantic development of the terms was ''in the armpit'' > ''at the side'' > ''towards'' > ''to''. Deccani (and other Southern dialects of Hindustani) had a parallel development which also includes a locative sense.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ur-IPA|ko}}

===Postposition===
{{ur-post|tr=ko|hi=को}}

# {{n-g|marks the [[dative]] [[case]]}}: [[to]]
#: {{uxa|ur|میرے بھائی '''کو''' پانی دیں۔|Please give some water '''to''' my elder brother.|tr=mere bhāī '''ko''' pānī dẽ.}}
#: {{uxa|ur|لاہور کو|tr=lāhaur ko|to Lahore}}
#: {{uxa|ur|اوپر کو|tr=ūpar ko|upwards}}
# [[in]], at the [[time]] of
#: {{uxa|ur|میں شام '''کو''' گھر لوٹوں گا۔|tr=ma͠i śām '''ko''' ghar lauṭū̃ gā.|I will return home '''in''' the evening.}}

====Usage notes====
{{m|ur|کو|tr=ko}} marks the dative. It can be used as a postfix similar to {{m|en|-wards}} (e.g. {{m|ur||اوپر کو|tr=ūpar ko|upwards}}; {{m|ur||آگے کو|tr=āge ko|afterwards}}).

It is suffixed to oblique forms of pronouns as well, e.g. the dative of {{m|ur|میں||tr=ma͠i|I}} is {{m|ur||مجھ کو|tr=mujh ko}}.

===References===
<references/>
* {{R:Ox HI-EN|head=को}}
* {{R:UR-HI-EN}}
* {{R:Turner-comp|ká}}
