==South Levantine Arabic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|mā<p:mæː>|ma<p:ma>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما.wav|a=Ramallah}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|مَا|t=not}}.

====Particle====
{{head|ajp|particle|tr=mā|tr2=ma}}

# [[don't]], [[didn't]] {{qual|used to negate a verbal phrase}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[ما]] [[بدّ|بدّه]] [[إجا|ييجي]] [[على|ع]][[حفلة|الحفلة]].|tr='''mā''' biddo yīji ʕal-ḥafle|t=He '''doesn't''' want to come to the party.}}
#: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما بده ييجي عالحفلة.wav|a=Ramallah}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[ما]] [[قال|قلت]][[ل|لّو]][[ش]]؟|tr='''ma''' ʔult-illū'''š'''?|t=You '''didn't''' tell him?}}
#: {{syn|ajp|ـش|لا|tr1=-š|tr2=la|q2=imperative}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Usually this {{m-self|ajp|ما|tr=mā}} is stressed. However, it can optionally be used together with {{m-self|ajp|ـش|tr=-š}}, in which case the stress shifts to the end of the verbal phrase.
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[كتب]]|tr='''mā''' katab|t=he didn't write}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما كتب.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[كتب]][[ش]]|tr='''ma''' katabš|t=he didn't write}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما كتبش.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[نسي|تنسى]]|tr='''mā''' tinsa|t=don't forget}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما تنسى.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[نسي|تنسا]][[ش]]|tr='''ma''' tinsāš|t=don't forget}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما تنساش.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[حكى|بحكي]] [[إنكليزي]]|tr='''mā''' biḥki ʔinglīzi|t=he doesn't speak English}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما بحكي إنكليزي.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[حكى|بحكي]][[ش]] [[إنكليزي]]|tr='''ma''' biḥkīš ʔinglīzi|t=he doesn't speak English}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-ما بحكيش إنكليزي.wav|a=Ramallah}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|ajp|مش|tr=miš}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|مَا|t=what}}.

====Particle====
{{head|ajp|particle|tr=ma}}

# {{ngd|used to link a preposition to a verbal phrase}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[بعد]] [[ما]] [[راح]]|tr='''baʕd-ma''' rāḥ|t='''after''' he went}}
# {{ngd|used to turn a question word into a relative determiner}}; -[[ever]]
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[إيمتى]] [[ما]] [[بد]][[ك]]|tr='''ʔēmta-ma''' biddak|t='''whenever''' you want}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[شو]] [[ما]] [[قال]]|tr='''šū-ma''' ʔāl|t='''whatever''' he said}}
# {{ngd|used before an elative adjective to indicate surprise or other strong feelings in an exclamation}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[ما]] [[أحلى|أحلا]][[ها]]!|tr='''ma''' ʔaḥlā-ha!|t='''how''' beautiful she is!}}
#: {{syn|ajp|أمّا}}
# {{ngd|used before a verbal phrase to contradict a statement or subvert an expectation}}; [[does]], [[did]]
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[ليش]] [[ما]] [[راح]]؟ [[ما]] ([[هو]]) [[راح]]!|tr=lēš '''mā''' rāḥ? '''ma''' (huwwe) rāḥ!|t=Why '''didn't''' he go? He '''did''' go!}}
#: <small>Invariable form:</small> {{l|ajp|ماهو|tr=mahū}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In all these senses the {{m-self|ajp|ما|tr=ma}} is unstressed. In the fourth sense, the contradicting phrase should be uttered with rising intonation to distinguish this sense of {{m-self|ajp|ما|tr=ma}} from the sense of negation. When a subject pronoun is used in the fourth sense, {{m-self|ajp|ما|tr=ma}} precedes it; this yields the invariable form {{l|ajp|ماهو|tr=mahū}} used before nominal phrases with the same meaning.

