==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|fa|pal|tr=OLE|sc=Phlv}}, {{m|pal|𐭥𐭫𐭤}}, {{m|pal|𐫀𐫇𐫏|t=he; she; that|ts=ōy|sc=Mani}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|fa|اورا|tr=urâ, ôrâ||as grammatical object}}
* {{alt|fa|اوی|tr=uy||archaic}}

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|ō|kbl=ū|haz=ū}}
* {{homophone|fa|آن|qq1=colloquial Dari}}
* {{audio|fa|Fa-او.ogg|a=Iran}}

====Pronoun====
{{fa-regional|او|او|ӯ}}
{{head|fa|pronoun|tr=u}}

# [[she]], [[he]], [[they]] {{gloss|meaning the third-person singular, of unknown or irrelevant gender, but animate}}
#: {{syn|fa|اون<q:colloquial>}}
#: {{ux|prs|«او کُجَاسْت؟» «مَن نَمی‌دَانَم، اَمَّا مَن اورَا پیشْتَر دِیدَم»|t="where is he?" "I don't know, but I saw him earlier"|footer={{qual|Dari|more formal}}}}
# {{lb|fa|Hazaragi|Kabuli}} {{alt form|fa|آن|from=colloquial|nocap=1|tr=ân|t=it}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In many colloquial varieties or Persian, the terms {{l|fa|آن|tr=that, it}} and {{l|fa|او|tr=he, she, they}} have merged. In Iran this is typically realized as {{l|fa-ira|اون}}, in Afghanistan this is typically realized as {{l|prs|اُو}}. 
** In both Iran and Afghanistan the plural of these terms has similarly combined in colloquial speech, which is typically realized as {{l|fa|اونا}} in both regions.
* When the pronoun is acting as a grammatical object, it is combined with the direct-object particle {{l|fa|را|tr=râ}} as {{l|fa|او را|tr=u râ, ô râ}} or contracted into a single word as {{l|fa|اورا|tr=urâ, ôrâ}} 
* {{lb|fa|Iran|colloquially}} contracted to {{m|fa||اونو|tr=uno}} when used with the direct-object particle {{l|fa|را|tr=râ}}.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fa|وی|tr=vay, vey}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|fa|همو|tr=hamu}}

=====See also=====
{{fa-personal pronouns}}{{prs-personal pronouns}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|fa|/aw/|a=Dari, various regions}}
* {{IPA|fa|/ow/|a=Iran, various regions}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr2=ow|tr=aw}}

# {{alt form of|fa|from=colloquial|آب|tr=âb|t=water; liquid; juice}} in various regions.

