==Persian==

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|yā}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|fa|pal||tr=ʾywp|ts=ayāb|sc=Phlv}}, {{desc|pal|𐫀𐫏𐫀𐫁|tr=ʾyʾb|ts=ayāb|sc=Mani|sclb=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|xpr|𐫀𐫃𐫀𐫖|tr=ʾgʾm|ts=āgām|sc=Mani}}. Further etymology unclear; not found in Old Persian.

====Conjunction====
{{fa-regional|یا|یا|ё}}
{{head|fa|conjunction|tr=yâ}}

# [[or]]
#: {{ux|fa|امروز یا فردا می‌روید؟|tr=emruz '''yâ''' fardâ mi-ravid?|q=more literary|t=-}}
#: {{ux|fa|امرو یا فردا می‌رین؟|tr=emru '''yâ''' fardâ mi-rin?|q=more colloquial|t=Are you going today '''or''' tomorrow?}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|author=w:Hafez|trans-title={{w|The Divān of Hafez}}|title=fa:دیوان حافظ|year=c. 1390|chapter=Ghazal 12|url= https://ganjoor.net/hafez/ghazal/sh12|text=عزم دیدار تو دارد جانِ بر لب آمده<br>باز گردد یا برآید؟ چیست فرمان شما؟|tr=azm-i dîdâr-i tu dârad jân-i bar lab âmada<br>bâz gardad '''yâ''' bar-âyad? čî-st farmân-i šumâ?|t=My soul, resolved to see you, has come to the edge;<br>Shall it go back, '''or''' come forth? Which do you command?|footer=(romanization in Classical Persian)}}
# [[either]]
#: {{ux|fa|یا امروز یا فردا|tr='''yâ''' emruz '''yâ''' fardâ|t='''either''' today '''or''' tomorrow}}

