====Verb====
{{en-verb|+|oning|oned|pres_ptc2=onning|past2=onned}}

# {{lb|en|Singapore|Philippines|Malaysia|Nigeria|transitive|colloquial}} To [[switch on]].
#: {{syn|en|turn on}}
#: {{ux|en|Can you '''on''' the light?}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|en|non|ón}}, {{m|non|án||without}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*ēnu}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ēno}}, {{m|gem-pro|*ino||without}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḗnu||without}}. Cognate with {{cog|frr|on||without}}, {{cog|dum|an}}, {{m|dum|on||without}}, {{cog|gml|āne||without}}, {{cog|de|ohne||without}}, {{cog|got|𐌹𐌽𐌿||without, except}}, {{cog|grc|ἄνευ||without}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|ohn}}

====Preposition====
{{en-prep}}

# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialectal|Scotland}} [[without|Without]].{{rfex|en}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Usually followed by a present participle, as ''being'', ''having'', etc.

===Etymology 3===
From {{der|en|ja|音読み|tr=on'yomi|lit=sound reading}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|?}}

# In the Japanese language, a pronunciation, or reading, of a [[kanji]] character that was originally based on the character's pronunciation in Chinese, contrasted with [[kun]].
#: {{ux|en|Most kanji have two kinds of reading, called "on" and "kun".}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|kun}}

