# [[#English|on]], [[in]], [[at]], [[among]] {{+obj|ang|acc/dat/ins}}
#: {{ux|ang|'''On''' þæm huse|'''In''' the house}}
#* '''late 9th century''', [https://books.google.ca/books?id=xtM0rOEXqJIC&pg=PA52&redir_esc=y#v=snippet&q=seonne&f=false translation] of [[w:Orosius|Orosius’]] ''History Against the Pagans''
#*: {{quote|ang|...and ðā syndon swȳþe fæġere and lustsumlīce '''on''' tō sēonne...|...and those are very beautiful and pleasant to look '''at'''...}}
#* '''Early 11th c.''', [[w:Defensor|Defensor's]] [https://archive.org/details/defensorslibers00rhodgoog/page/n246/mode/2up translation] of  ''{{w|Liber Scintillarum}}''
#*: {{quote|ang|''...nā besēoh þū '''on''' wīfes hiw...''|...do not look '''at''' a woman's appearance...}}
# [[#English|on]], [[during]] {{+obj|ang|acc}}
#: {{ux|ang|'''On''' midne winter|'''In''' mid-winter}}
# [[#English|onto]], [[into]] (to express [[allative]] motion or a change of state) {{+obj|ang|acc}}
#: {{ux|ang|'''On''' þæt hus|'''Into''' the house}}
#: {{ux|ang|Heo awende þa boc '''on''' Englisc|She translated the book '''into''' English}}

