====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|regional|_|US|chiefly|Midwest|and|West}} [[along|Along]], [[together]] with others, in a group, etc.
#: {{ux|en|Do you want to come '''with'''?}}
<!--Examples exist in plays by Chicagoan {{w|David Mamet}}, such as ''{{w|American Buffalo}}.''<ref>[http://positiveanymore.blogspot.com/2006/04/chicago-dialect.html Chicago Dialect]</ref>-->

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|withe}}, {{m|enm|wiþþe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wiþþe}}. More at {{m|en|withe}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{alternative form of|en|withe}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Judges|chapter=16|verse=7|passage=And Samson said unto her, If they bind me with seven green '''withs''' that were never dried, then shall I be weak, and be as another man.}}

===References===
<references/>

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=hitw|Whit|whit}}

[[Category:English heteronyms]]

==Middle English==

===Preposition===
{{head|enm|preposition}}

# {{alt form|enm|wiþ}}
#* '''1300s?''', ''Political, Religious and Love Poems'', “An A B C Poem on the Passion of Christ”, ed. {{w|Frederick James Furnivall}}, 1866
#*: {{quote|enm|Al þus '''with''' iewys I am dyth, I seme a wyrm to manus syth.}}
#* '''1430?''', “The Love of Jesus” in ''Hymns to the Virgin and Christ'', ed. {{w|Frederick James Furnivall}}, 1867, p.26
#*: {{quote|enm|Þirle my soule '''with''' þi spere anoon,}}
#* {{RQ:Chaucer Workes|title=The Legende of Good Women|subtitle=Prologue|folio=ccxvii|verso=yes|column=2|passage=Hypſiphile, betrayed '''with''' Jaſoun, / Maketh of your trouth neyther boſte ne ſoun}}
#* {{RQ:Chaucer Canterbury Tales|Prologue|passage=Whan Zephirus eek '''with''' his sweete breeth<br />Inspired hath in every holt and heeth|translation=When Zephyr also '''with''' his sweet breath<br />Hath inspired in every wood and heath}}

==Old Saxon==

===Etymology===
A shortened form of [[withar]] {{qualifier|against}}, cognate with {{cog|ang|wiþ||against, opposite, toward}} and {{m|ang|wiþer}}.

===Preposition===
{{osx-prep}}

# [[against]], {{l|en|with}}, [[toward]]
#: {{ux|osx|Uuesat iu so uuara uuiðar thiu, '''uuið''' iro fēcneon dādiun, sō man uuiðar fīundun scal|t=Be careful against them, '''against''' their dreadful actions, just like one must be (careful) against his enemies}} (''Heliand, verse 1883'')

====Related terms====
* [[withar]]
* [[with-]]
* [[withar-]]

==Southwestern Dinka==

===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|shk|nya weth}}.

===Noun===
{{head|dik|noun|plural|wiɛth}}

# [[arrow]]
# [[needle]], [[pin]], [[quill]]

===References===
