=====See also=====
* {{l|en|breeze block}}
* [[w:Beaufort_scale|Wikipedia article on the Beaufort scale]]

====Verb====
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|intransitive}}

# {{lb|en|usually|_|with ''along''}} To move casually, in a carefree manner.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=11 October 2023|author=Dafydd Pritchard|work=BBC Sport|title=Wales 4-0 Gibraltar|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67002497|passage=Resting most of their first-choice players for Sunday's vital Euro 2024 qualifier against Croatia, Wales started with four debutants and '''breezed''' into an early lead thanks to headers by captain Ben Davies and Kieffer Moore.}}
# {{lb|en|weather}} To [[blow]] gently.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Hermione Hoby|title=Julia Roberts interview for August: Osage County – 'I might actually go to hell for this&nbsp;...': Julia Roberts reveals why her violent, Oscar-nominated performance in August: Osage County made her feel 'like a terrible person' &#91;print version: 'I might actually go to hell for this&nbsp;...' (18 January 2014, p.&nbsp;R4)&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/film/10584525/Julia-Roberts-interview-for-August-Osage-County-I-might-actually-go-to-hell-for-this....html|newspaper={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Review)|date=21 January 2014|passage=She's sitting opposite a window that's gently '''breezing''' into her face, wafting her hair into cover-girl perfection&nbsp;...}}
# To take a horse on a light run in order to understand the running characteristics of the horse and to observe it while under motion.
# {{lb|en|of fish}} To [[swim]] near the surface of the water, causing [[ripple]]s in the surface.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1970| title=Commercial Fisheries Review - Volume 32 |author=| page=37| passage=The first was a school of medium-sized ( 10-pound average ) fish that '''breezed''' frequently but bit poorly. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1979| title=The Tuna/Porpoise Problem: Dedicated Vessel Research Program|author=Frank T. Awbrey; Thomas Duffy; WIlliam E. Evans; C. Scott Johnson; Wesley Parks; John DeBeer| page=10| passage=The Queen Mary stood by while a speedboat moved ahead of a '''breezing''' school of tuna to deploy the sound projector and a sonobuoy (Figure 6). }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011| title=Fly Fishing the Baja and Beyond |author=Mike Rieser | page=143| passage=An intermediate line has its place when chasing '''breezing''' tuna that are moving at mach speed on the surface.}}

