===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|brese}}, from {{inh|en|ang|brēosa}}, variant of {{cog|ang|brimsa|t=gadfly}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*bremusī|t=gadfly}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰerem-|t=to make a noise, buzz, hum}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|brems||horsefly, warblefly}}, {{cog|de|Bremse||gadfly, horsefly}}, {{cog|da|bremse||gadfly, horsefly}}, {{cog|sv|broms||gadfly, horsefly}}. Related also to {{cog|enm|brimse||gadfly}}, {{cog|fr|brize||gadfly}}, {{cog|ang|bremman||to rage, roar}}, {{cog|la|fremō||roar, snort, growl, grumble}}. See also {{l|en|bream}}.

====Alternative forms====
