==Persian==

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-regional|تا|تا|то}}
{{fa-IPA|tā}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=OD|ts=tā|t=until, so that}}, from {{der|fa|peo|𐎹𐎠𐎫𐎠|ts=yātā}}, from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*HyátʰaH||as, like}}, from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*yós|*Hyós}}. Compare {{cog|sa|यथा}}.

====Preposition====
{{head|fa|preposition|head='''تا'''|tr=tâ}}

# [[until]]; [[as far as]]; [[up to]] (in time or space)
#: {{uxi|fa|تا پارسال|tr='''tâ''' parsâl|t='''until''' last year}}
#: {{uxi|fa|تا اندازه‌ای|tr='''tâ''' andâze-'i|t='''up to''' an extent}}
#: {{ux|fa|تا کنارِ پنجره رفتم.|tr='''tâ''' kenâr-e panjere raftam.|t=I went '''up to''' the windowside.}}
#: {{ux|fa|فاصله اصفهان تا تهران|tr=fâsele-ye esfahân '''tâ''' tehrân|t=distance from Isfahan '''to''' Tehran}}
# [[than]] {{gloss|used in comparisons}}
#: {{syn|fa|از|tr=az}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|than}} While Persian most commonly uses the preposition {{l|fa|از|tr=az}} for comparisons, {{l|fa|تا|tr=tâ}} is also used, especially when the object of comparison is the direct object of the verb or a prepositional phrase. When {{l|fa|از|tr=az}} is used, the object of comparison precedes the verb, but when {{l|fa|تا|tr=tâ}} is used, it follows the verb. The fact that {{l|fa|تا|tr=tâ}} is used together with the object marker or a preposition can help reduce ambiguity:
*: {{usex|fa|من پدرم را بیشتر از مادرم می‌بینم.|tr=man pedar-am râ bištar az mâdar-am mi-binam.|t=I see my father more than my mother [does] / I see my father more than [I see] my mother.}}
*: {{usex|fa|من پدرم را بیشتر می‌بینم تا مادرم را.|tr=man pedar-am râ bištar mi-binam tâ mâdar-am-râ.|t=I see my father more than [I see] my mother.}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|fa|conjunction|head='''تا'''|tr=tâ}}

# {{lb|fa|usually in the initial clause}} [[as long as]], [[so long as]], [[as far as]]
#: {{uxi|fa|تا یادش می‌آید|tr='''tâ''' yâd-aš mi-âyad|t='''as far as''' he remembers}}
#: {{ux|fa|تا مادرم آنجاست او باید برود.|tr='''tâ''' mâdar-am ânjâ-st u bâyad beravad.|t='''As long as''' my mother is there, he should go.}}
#: {{ux|fa|تا تو نروی٬ مادرت نمی‌آید.|tr='''tâ''' to na-ravi, mâdar-at ne-mi-âyad.|t=Your mother will not come '''until''' you go.|lit='''As long as''' you do not go, your mother will not come.}}
# {{lb|fa|usually in the initial clause}} [[by the time]], [[when]]
#: {{ux|fa|تا رسیدم دختر رفته بود.|tr='''tâ''' residam doxtar rafte bud.|t='''By the time''' I arrived, the girl had left.}}
#: {{ux|fa|تا درسم را تمام کردم، کار خوبی پیدا کرده بودم.|tr='''tâ''' dars-am râ tamâm kardam, kâr-e xubi peydâ karde budam.|t='''By the time''' I finished my studies, I had found good job.}}
# {{lb|fa|in the initial clause|taking the main stress of the sentence}} [[as soon as]]
#: {{syn|fa|همینکه|tr=haminke}}
#: {{ux|fa|تا من دیدمش، خانه را ترک کردم.|tr='''tâ''' man didam-eš, xâne râ tark kardam.|t='''As soon as''' I saw him, I left the house.}}
# {{lb|fa|in a subsequent clause}} [[until]]
#: {{ux|fa|مادرت نمی‌آید تا تو بروی.|tr=mâdar-at ne-mi-âyad '''tâ''' to beravi.|t=Your mother will not come '''until''' you go.}}
# {{lb|fa|with subjunctive|in a subsequent clause}} [[to]]; [[in order to]]; [[so that]]
#: {{syn|fa|تا اینکه|tr1=tâ in-ke|که|tr2=ke}}
#: {{uxi|fa|رفتم تا او را ببینم.|tr=raftam '''tâ''' u râ bebinam.|t=I went '''to''' see him.}}
#* {{RQ:Masnavi|5|1480—1481|الله الله قسم مسکین بعد من<br> وا مگیریدش ز حرص خویشتن<br> '''تا''' بماند بر شما کشت و ثمار<br> در پناه طاعت حق پایدار.|{{xlit|fa-cls|اَللّٰه اَللّٰه قِسْمِ مِسْکِین بَعْدِ مَن<br> وَا مَگِیرِیدَش زِ حِرْصِ خْویشْتَن<br> '''تَا''' بِمَانَد بَر شُمَا کِشْت و ثِمَار<br> دَر پَنَاهِ طَاعَتِ حَقّ پَایْدَار.}}|For God's sake, for God's sake, after I am gone, do not on account of your covetousness withhold the portion of the poor,<br>'''So that''' the crops and fruit may remain [as a] permanent [blessing bestowed] on you under the safeguard of your obedience to God.|footer={{q|Classical Persian romanization}}}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|fa|pal||tr=tʾk'|ts=tāg|t=item; unit; single}}, already used as a classifier in MP. {{doublet|fa|طاق|tr1=tâq|t1=odd (of a number); unique}}, which apparently passed through Arabic.

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=tâ}}

# {{ng|The generic [[classifier]], used as a counting unit for numbers greater than one. Obligatory in colloquial Persian.}}
#: {{ux|fa|دیروز ۲۴تا کتاب خریدم.|tr=diruz bist-o-čahâr '''tâ''' ketâb xaridam.|t=Yesterday I bought twenty-four books.}}
#: {{ux|fa|این ۶تا بهتر از همه هستند.|tr=in šeš '''tâ''' behtar az hame hastand.|t=These six are the best.}}
# [[fold]]
#: {{syn|fa|لا|tr=lâ}}
# [[match]]; [[equal]]; [[peer]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{col2|fa
|تا کردن<tr:tâ kardan><t:to fold>
|بی تا<tr:bi tâ><t:matchless>
|یکتا<tr:yektâ><t:unique>
|همتا<tr:hamtâ><t:equal; match>
}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|fa|نفر|tr=nafar|pos=classifier for humans}}

