==Kamkata-viri==

===Noun===
{{head|bsh|noun|tr=Katë́}}

# {{alt form of|bsh|Katë́|t=[[Kata]], [[Katë]]}}

==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
{{unknown|fa}}, but thought to be related to colloquial {{cog|tg|қатӣ}}, with the same meaning.

Both terms are suggested to be from a Turkic language, but there is little consensus on the matter.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|dari=ka`tē,ka`tī|kbl=`kati,`kat,`kad|haz=`kati,`kat,`kad}}
:* In some dialects, this term may be perceived as /kad/ or /kat/

====Preposition====
{{fa-regional|با|با|бо|dari2=کتی|tg2=қатӣ}}
{{head|fa|preposition|tr=katē|tr2=katī}}

# {{lb|fa|Dari|Hazaragi|more|_|colloquial}} [[with]], [[by]], [[alongside]]
#: {{syn|fa|با|tr=bâ|q=Iranian; formal in Dari}}
#: {{uxi|fa|برنج '''کتی''' گوشت می‌خایی یا تو آلی خو می‌ری|tr=birinj '''kat(ē)''' gōšt mē-xāyī yā tū ālē xaw mē-rī|t=-|footer={{q|Dari|colloquial}}}}
#: {{uxi|fa|برنج '''کتی''' گوشت می‌خواهی یا تو حالا خواب می‌روی|tr=birinj '''katē''' gōšt mē-xāhī yā tū hālā xāb mē-rawī|t=do you want rice '''and/alongside''' meat or will you go to bed now?|footer={{q|Dari|more formal}}}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|ka`tī}}

====Proper noun====
{{fa-proper noun|tr=kati}}

