Page 1 been: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Been|beeñ|be·en|be- -en}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|been|pos=past participle}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bēon|(ġe)bēon}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|be|en<id:past participle>}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/bɪn/|a=GenAm,RP,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-been.ogg|a=US}}
** {{homophones|en|bin}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɪn|s=1}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɛn/|a=GenAm,particularly common in the Great Lakes, Midwest}}
** {{homophones|en|Ben}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɛn|s=1}}
* {{IPA|en|/biːn/|a=RP,US dialectal,CA}}
** {{audio|en|En-uk-been.ogg|a=UK}}
** {{homophones|en|bean}}
** {{rhymes|en|iːn|s=1}}

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{inflection of|en|be||past|part}}.
#: {{ux|en|All the fries have '''been''' eaten.}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''been''' here since yesterday. {{q|dialectal, e.g. AAVE, omitting ''have''}} }}
# {{lb|en|Southern US|or|AAVE}} {{inflection of|en|be||remote past|form}}.
#: {{ux|en|He '''been''' had that job.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''been''' knew they was doing this.}}
#* '''2013''', DayQuan Miller, ''Back Blocks'', StealthMode Entertainment, page 147:
#*: She was disloyal, Casper was disloyal, so them muthafuckas gotta go. Like you said[,] we '''been''' knew we was going to have to kill Frost, so let's do it and Light too.” Star said. “Say no more. I'ma handle Kisha myself.” Max said walking to the door.

=====Further reading=====
* {{cite-book|en|year=2015|author=Alexander Pollatsek|author2=Rebecca Treiman|title=The Oxford Handbook of Reading|publisher=Oxford Library of Psychology|isbn=9780199324576|page=433|passage=For example, the remote past “been” is used as part of the verb to express something that took place in the distant past: 'he <u>been</u> reading story books.'}}
* {{cite-book|en|year=2020|author=Mary Kohn|author2=Walt Wolfram|author3=Charlie Farrington|author4=Jennifer Renn|author5=Janneke Van Hofwegen|title=African American Language: Language development from Infancy to Adulthood|publisher=Cambridge University Press|isbn=9781108876742|page=231|text=Remote past 'been' ([RPB], coded on word) = ''been'' is used to mark action in the remote past; in such cases the word ''been'' is always stressed (e.g., he been[RPB] had that job; I been[RPB] bought her clothes).}}

===Etymology 2===
Either from {{inh|en|enm|been|pos=infinitive||to be}} (from {{inh|en|ang|bēon}}), or from a dialectal use of the preceding past tense form as an infinitive form (compare dialectal use of {{m|en|I's|(I)'s}}, {{m|en|is|(I) is}} in the first person, {{m|en|am|(he) am}} in the third person, etc).

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb}}

# {{lb|en|Southern US|or|AAVE|rare}} {{synonym of|en|be|pos=infinitival sense}}.
#: {{ux|en|It [[useta]] '''been''' five foot long.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|year2=1969|title=Minstrel Gags and End Men's Hand-book|publisher=Dick and Fitzgerald|publisher2=Literature House|location=New York|location2=New York|page=83|passage="Bones", says he, "I tink dey's a-goin' to '''been''' a war ober de Alabamy question{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1888|author=w:Mary Augusta Ward|title=Robert Elsmere|publisher=w:Macmillan and Company|location=London|page=20|chapter=Book I|url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=Y281AAAAMAAJ|passage=Yur a boald 'un to tell the missus theer to hur feeace as how ya wur 'tossicatit whan ya owt to '''been''' duing yur larful business.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966|year_published=1985|quotee=DARE Tape SC10|editors=Frederic G. Cassidy; Joan Houston Hall|entry='''be''' v|title=w:Dictionary of American Regional English|publisher=w:Harvard University Press|page=178|volume=1|url=https://archive.org/details/dictionaryofamer01arie|passage={{...}}But one time it use' to '''been''' so cold right first of the winter.}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|been|pos=plural indicative form}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|be|en|id2=plural present}}.

====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} {{inflection of|en|be||p|simple|pres}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1584|author=w:George Peele|title=The Arraignment of Paris|section=I, ii
|passage=My love is fair, my love is gay,<br>As fresh as '''been''' the flowers in May;}}
#* {{RQ:Nathaniel Baxter Ourania|sig=G|passage=Theſe Beaſtes '''been''' of higheſt Regard and Price / To pleaſure Princes and to murder vice.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Pericles|act=II|scene=Prologue|pageref=21|passage=Where when men '''been''', there's ſeldome eaſe,}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1641|author=w:Ben Jonson|title=The Sad Shepherd|section=I, iii
|passage=O Friar, those are faults that are not seen,<br>Ours open, and of worse example '''been'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|tlr=Edward Fairfax|title=Godfrey of Bulloigne: Or, The Recovery of Jerusalem|page=8|section=20|year=1686|url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=HScJAAAAQAAJ|passage=Some of green Boughs their slender Cabbins frame, / Some lodged were ''Tortoſa's'' streets about, / Of all the Hoſt the Chief of Worth and Name / Aſſembled '''been''', a Senate grave and ſtout;}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{inh|en|enm|been}}, {{m|enm|bene}}, {{m|enm|ben}}, {{m|enm|beon}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bēon|t=bees}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|bee|-en|pos2=plural ending|id2=plural noun}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/biːn/}}

====Noun====
{{head|en|noun form}}

# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialectal}} {{plural of|en|bee}}

===References===
Vaux, Bert and Scott Golder. 2003. The Harvard Dialect Survey: been. Cambridge, MA: Harvard University Linguistics Department.

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=been|Bene|Eben|NEbE|bene|eben|neeb}}

