===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/beːn/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-been.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|been}}
* {{rhymes|nl|eːn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|bêen}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|bēn}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*bain}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*bainą}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|n|-en|beentje}}

# {{topics|nl|Body parts}} [[leg]], [[limb]] of a person, horse (other animals' would have ''[[poot#Dutch|poten]]'') and certain objects (again many have ''poten'')
#: {{ux|nl|De '''benen''' van een passer.|inline=1|The legs of a pair of compasses.}}
# {{lb|nl|mathematics}} [[side]], [[leg]]
#: {{ux|nl|De '''benen''' van een hoek.|inline=1|The sides of an angle.}}
# the upper part of a sock, above the ankle.

=====Usage notes=====
* The contemporary plural ''benen'' is derived from an analogy to other nouns with regular plurals. Originally, ''been'' was left unchanged in the plural; such use is preserved only in [[set phrase]]s like {{m|nl|op de been||upright, standing, awake}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|n|-eren|pl2=benen|beentje}}

# {{topics|nl|Body parts}} [[bone]], constituent part of a skeleton.
#: {{syn|nl|bot|knook|knekel}}
#: {{ux|nl|De archeologen vonden oude '''beenderen''' van een dinosaurus in de opgraving.|The archaeologists found ancient '''bones''' of a dinosaur in the excavation.}}
# {{topics|nl|Body parts}} {{lb|nl|uncountable}} bone, the chalky material bones are made of.
#: {{syn|nl|bot}}

