==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Montaigut toit 0707.jpg|thumb|Tiled '''roofs''' covering buildings.]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹuːf/|/ɹʊf/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹuf/|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-roof.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹʊf/|a=Inland North}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-roof2.ogg|a=Inland North}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹuːf/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|en-uk-roof.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹuf/|a=Canada}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɹʊf/|a=Ottawa Valley}}
** {{audio|en|En-ca-roof.ogg|a=CA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʊf|uːf|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|rof}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hrōf|t=roof, ceiling; top, summit; heaven, sky}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hrōfą|t=roof}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|s|rooves}}

# {{lb|en|architecture}} The [[external]] [[covering]] at the [[top]] of a [[building]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''roof''' was blown off by the tornado.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|text='Twas the house I'd seen the '''roof''' of from the beach.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1931|author=Robert L. May|title=Rudolph, The Red-Nosed Reindeer|publisher=Montgomery Ward|section=draft|text=The very first sound that you’ll hear on the '''roof'''<br>(Provided there’s fog) will be Rudolph’s small hoof.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1984|author=w:Rock Master Scott & the Dynamic Three|title=[[:w:The Roof Is on Fire|The '''Roof''' Is on Fire]]|text=The '''roof''', the '''roof''', the '''roof''' is on fire!<br>We don't need no water: Let the [[motherfucker]] burn!<br>Burn, [[motherfucker]], burn!}}
# The [[top]] [[external]] [[level]] of a [[building]].
#: {{ux|en|Let's go up to the '''roof'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1962|author=w:Gerry Goffin; et al.|title=[[:w:Up on the Roof (song)|Up on the '''Roof''']]|text=When this old world starts getting me down<br>And people are just too much for me to face,<br>I climb way up to the top of the stairs<br>And all my cares just drift right into space<br>On the '''roof''', it's peaceful as can be<br>And there, the world below can't bother me...}}
# The [[upper]] [[part]] of a [[cavity]].
#: {{ux|en|The palate is the '''roof''' of the mouth.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 1, 2011|author=John Sinnott|work=BBC Sport|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/15045618.stm|title=Aston Villa 2-0 Wigan|text=As Bent pulled away to the far post, Agbonlahor opted to go it alone, motoring past Gary Caldwell before unleashing a shot into the '''roof''' of the net.}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} The surface or bed of rock immediately overlying a bed of coal or a flat vein.
# {{lb|en|climbing}} An [[overhanging]] [[rock]] [[wall]].

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|cover at top of building}} {{l|en|rooftop}}, {{l|en|tect}} {{qualifier|obsolete, rare}}, [[thatch]]
* {{sense|in a cavity}} {{l|en|ceiling}}

