===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|rofen}}, {{m|enm|roven|t=to roof}}, from the noun (see above).

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cover]] or [[furnish]] with a roof.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James George Frazer|title=The Golden Bough|year=1911|volume=11|page=264|text=A trench about ten feet deep was dug in the ground and '''roofed''' over with sticks and earth so as to form a dark tunnel.}}
# To [[traverse]] buildings by walking or climbing across their roofs.
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[put]] into [[prison]], to [[bird]].
#* {{quote-av|en|date=1998-03-04|title=w:Beverly Hills, 90210|episode=Law and Disorder|season=08|number=22|passage=Did you see them, David? I mean, did you see them looking at me? I-I'm walking out of the court, and everybody was practically – yeah, they were gawking. {{...}} I mean, Noah '''roofed''' me, I proved it, end of story.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2000-01-01|lyricist=Mr. Metaphor|artist=Word A' Mouth; Block McCloud; Mr. Metaphor|title=Stupid|album=The Will Tell Compilation Vol. 1: Thats Right Inc.|passage=I’m open, [[hype]] off the [[chronic]] I was smoking, feeling [[zooted]]<br/>That Brooklyn shit got me stupid<br/>I’m loose, kid – that’s what the [[overproof]] did<br/>What the [[ruck]] you looking at, son? You’ll get '''roofed''', kid!}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2012-11-15|artist=w:Action Bronson|title=Brown Bag Wrap|album=w:Rare Chandeliers|passage=Inhale the mystical, the blue shit<br/>See me on the stoop shit, act stupid at the park, the ball, get '''roofed'''<br/>Baby see the cops, the drugs, she [[boof]]ed it<br/>Foie gras at every meal, that means I triple-[[goose]]d it}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2018-05-05|lyricist=AM|artist={{w|Skengdo & AM}} of 410|title=Attempted 1.0|text=You don’t want war, you’re shook of it<br/>Hella man dash when their friend got '''roofed'''}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[shelter]] as if under a roof.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1865|author=Thomas Greenbury|title=Pleasant Rambles Over Moors, Mountains, Mines, and Waterfalls|text=They reached him: the pieces of rock had '''roofed''' him over—he was without injury or scratch.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=78TZL2LEhBIC&pg=PA42&dq=%22They+reached+him:+the+pieces+of+rock+had%22&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwja5sv9j-XwAhVYXM0KHRcPCdkQ6AEwAnoECAYQAg}}
#* {{RQ:James Ambassadors|passage=It built him softly round, it '''roofed''' him warmly over, it rested, all so firm, on selection.}}

