====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[thoroughly|Thoroughly]]; [[completely]]; from [[beginning]] to [[end]].
#: {{ux|en|Let's talk '''over''' the project at tomorrow's meeting.}}
#: {{ux|en|Let me think that '''over'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm going to look '''over''' our department's expenses.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1661|author={{w|John Fell (bishop)|John Fell}}|title=The Life of the most learned, reverend and pious Dr. H. Hammond|url=http://archive.org/stream/a615775104worduoft/a615775104worduoft_djvu.txt
|passage=During the whole time of his abode in the university he generally spent thirteen hours of the day in study; by which assiduity besides an exact dispatch of the whole course of philosophy, he read '''over''' in a manner all classic authors that are extant{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|often in compounds}} To an [[excessive]] degree; [[overly]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Agatha Christie|title=Murder on the Orient Express|location=London|publisher=HarperCollins|year=1934|year_published= 2017|chapter=12|page=158|passage=She seemed a placid creature altogether - eminently respectable - perhaps not '''over''' intelligent.}}
# From an [[upright]] position to a [[horizontal]] one.
#: {{ux|en|He tipped the bottle '''over''', and the water came gushing out.}}
#: {{ux|en|That building just fell '''over'''!}}
#: {{ux|en|He bent '''over''' to touch his toes.}}
# [[horizontally|Horizontally]]; [[left]] to [[right]] or right to left.
#: {{ux|en|Slide the toilet-paper dispenser's door '''over''' when one roll is empty in order to reveal the other.}}
#: {{ux|en|I moved '''over''' to make room for him to sit down.}}
# From one side of something to another, passing above it.
#: {{ux|en|The fence is too high. I don't think I'll be able to get '''over'''.}}
# From one [[position]] or [[state]] to another.
#: {{ux|en|Please pass that '''over''' to me.}}
#: {{ux|en|He came '''over''' to our way of thinking on the new project.}}
#: {{ux|en|Come '''over''' and play!}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll bring '''over''' a pizza.}}
# [[overnight|Overnight]] {{gloss|throughout the night}}.
#: {{ux|en|We stayed '''over''' at Grandma's.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can I sleep '''over'''?}}
# {{lb|en|US|usually|with ''do''}} [[again|Again]]; another time; once more; over again.
#: {{ux|en|I lost my paper and I had to do the entire assignment '''over'''.}}

