##: {{ux|en|There is a bridge '''over''' the river.}}
##: {{ux|en|I looked out '''over''' the sea.}}
##* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=3|passage=My hopes wa'n't disappointed. I never saw clams thicker than they was along them inshore flats. I filled my dreener in no time, and then it come to me that 'twouldn't be a bad idee to get a lot more, take 'em with me to Wellmouth, and peddle 'em out. Clams was fairly scarce '''over''' that side of the bay and ought to fetch a fair price.}}
##* {{quote-text|en|year=1918|author=w:Dora Sigerson Shorter|title=Sick I Am and Sorrowful
|passage=If I saw the wild geese fly '''over''' the dark lakes of Kerry...}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-29|volume=407|issue=8842|page=72–3|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/science-and-technology/21580133-how-microbes-promote-liver-cancer-overweight-punch-gut A punch in the gut]
|passage=Mostly, the microbiome is beneficial. It helps with digestion and enables people to extract a lot more calories from their food than would otherwise be possible. Research '''over''' the past few years, however, has implicated it in diseases from atherosclerosis to asthma to autism.}}
## In such a way as to cover.
##: {{ux|en|Drape the fabric '''over''' the table.}}
##: {{ux|en|There is a roof '''over''' the house.}}
## From one [[physical]] [[position]] to another via an [[obstacle]] that must be [[traverse]]d [[vertically]], first [[upwards]] and then [[downwards]].
##: {{ux|en|The dog jumped '''over''' the fence.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'll go '''over''' [the fence] first and then help you.}}
##: {{ux|en|Let's walk '''over''' the hill to get there.}}
## {{lb|en|figurative}} Transmitted using a particular medium
##: {{ux|en|A stern voice boomed '''over''' the loudspeaker.}}
##: {{ux|en|The message came '''over''' FM radio.}}
# {{n-g|Expressing comparison.}}
## More than; to a greater degree.
##: {{ux|en|I prefer the purple '''over''' the pink.}}
## [[beyond|Beyond]]; [[past]]; [[exceeding]]; too [[much]] or too [[far]].
##: {{ux|en|I think I’m '''over''' my limit for calories for today.}}
## {{lb|en|in certain collocations}} As [[compared]] to.
##: {{ux|en|Sales are down this quarter '''over''' last.}}
# {{n-g|Indicating relative status, authority, or power}}
#: ''The owner's son lorded it '''over''' the experienced managers.''
#: ''The prince ruled '''over''' a portion of the kingdom.''
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} [[divide|Divided]] by.
#: {{syn|en|on|q=uncommon}}
#: {{ux|en|Two '''over''' six equals one '''over''' three.}}
# {{lb|en|poker}} {{n-g|Separates the [[three of a kind]] from the [[pair]] in a [[full house]].}}
#: <span style="color: red">9♦</span>9♠9♣<span style="color: red">6♥</span>6♠ = nines '''over''' sixes
# [[finish with|Finished with]]; [[done with]]; from one [[state]] to another via a [[hindrance]] that must be [[solve]]d or [[defeat]]ed; or via a third state that represents a significant difference from the first two.
#: {{ux|en|We got '''over''' the engineering problems and the prototype works great.}}
#: {{ux|en|I am '''over''' my cold and feel great again.}}
#: {{ux|en|I know the referee made a bad call, but you have to get '''over''' it [your annoyance with the referee's decision].}}
#: {{ux|en|She is finally '''over''' [the distress of] losing her job.}}
#: {{ux|en|He is finally '''over''' his [distress over the loss of the relationship with his] ex-girlfriend.}}
# [[while|While]] [[use|using]], {{non-gloss definition|especially}} while [[consume|consuming]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990|author=w:Seymour Chatman|title=Coming to Terms|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=loD1JXOtmTYC&pg=PA100&dq=relax|page=100|publisher=[[w:Cornell University Press|Cornell]]|isbn=0801497361
|passage=Six diners in business clothes—five attractive young women and a balding middle-aged man—relax '''over''' cigarettes.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1998|author=Marian Swerdlow|title=Underground Woman|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=jIK3DGkOwYkC&pg=PA88&dq=croissants|page=88|publisher=[[w:Temple University Press|Temple]]|isbn=1566396107
|passage=Sunday had been my favorite day at Woodlawn. A long <small>W.A.A.</small><!--original is small-caps--> [="work as assigned" period], having coffee and croissants with Mark '''over''' the Sunday ''Times''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Sara Pennypacker|title=The Great Egyptian Grave Robbery|page=79|publisher=[[w:Scholastic Corporation|Scholastic]]|isbn=9780545207867
|passage='''Over''' meatloaf and mashed potatoes (being careful not to talk with his mouth full), Stanley told about his adventure.}}
# [[concerning|Concerning]] or [[regarding]].
#: {{ux|en|The two boys had a fight '''over''' whose girlfriend was the best.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-10|volume=408|issue=8848|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21583277-worlds-biggest-polluter-going-green-it-needs-speed-up-transition-can-china Can China clean up fast enough?]
|passage=It has jailed environmental activists and is planning to limit the power of judicial oversight by handing a state-approved body a monopoly '''over''' bringing environmental lawsuits.}}
# Above, implying superiority after a contest; in spite of; notwithstanding.
#: {{ux|en|We triumphed '''over''' difficulties.}}
#: {{ux|en|The bill was passed '''over''' the veto.}}
#: {{ux|en|It was a fine victory '''over''' their opponents.}}
# Expressing [[causation]]; [[due to]], as the result of
#: {{ux|en|He was fired '''over''' that.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=May 24, 2024|magazine=w:Financial Review
|title=[https://www.afr.com/technology/microsoft-ceo-should-be-fired-over-cyber-failure-20240523-p5jg4q]
|passage=Microsoft CEO should be fired over cyber failure}}

=====Usage notes=====
When used in the context of "from one location to another", ''over'' implies that the two places are at approximately the same height or the height difference is not relevant. For example, if two offices are on the same floor of a building, an office worker might say ''I'll bring that '''over''' for you'', while if the offices were on different floors, the sentence would likely be ''I'll bring that up [down] for you.'' However, distances are not constrained, e.g. ''He came '''over''' from England last year and now lives in Los Angeles'' or ''I moved the stapler '''over''' to the other side of my desk.''

