==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|ōver}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*ovar}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*obar}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*uber}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*upér}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*upo}}. Compare {{cog|de|ober}}, {{cog|en|over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈoː.vər/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-over.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|over}}
* {{rhymes|nl|oːvər|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{nl-adv}}

# [[#English|over]], [[above]]
# {{lb|nl|postpositional}} {{l|en|over}} (implying motion)
#: {{ux|nl|Kijk uit, er steekt een hond de straat '''over'''.|Look out, a dog is crossing '''over''' the street.}}
# [[remaining]], [[left over]]
#: {{ux|nl|Na het feest was er bijna geen eten meer '''over'''.|After the party there was barely any food '''remaining'''.}}
# [[passing]] by, going away
#: {{ux|nl|De pijn gaat weer '''over'''.|The pain is '''going away''' again.}}
# Denotes an imitative action, [[again]], once again
#: ''Ik schrijf je brief '''over'''''.
#:: I will transcribe your letter.

