==Translingual==

===Symbol===
{{mul-symbol}}

# {{ISO 639|2&3|Punjabi language|Punjabi}}

==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pæn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-pan.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|panne}}
* {{rhymes|en|æn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|panne}}, from {{inh|en|ang|panne}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*pannā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*pannǭ}}, from {{der|en|LL.|panna}}, from {{der|en|la|patina|t=broad, shallow dish, pan, stewpan}}, from {{der|en|grc|πατάνη|t=kind of flat dish}}, which is probably from {{der|en|qsb-grc|-}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fy|panne}}, {{cog|stq|Ponne}}, {{cog|nl|pan}}, {{cog|nds-de|Panne}}, {{m|nds-de|Pann}}, {{cog|de|Pfanne}}, {{cog|da|pande}}, {{cog|sv|panna}}, {{cog|is|panna}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|pans|pen|pl2qual=humorous}}
[[File:Pfanne (Edelstahl).jpg|thumb|upright=1.13|A pan (1)]]

# A wide, flat [[receptacle]] used around the house, especially for [[cooking]].
# The contents of such a receptacle.
# A [[cylindrical]] receptacle about as [[tall]] as it is [[wide]], with one long [[handle]], usually made of [[metal]], used for cooking in the home.
# {{lb|en|Ireland}} A deep plastic receptacle, used for washing or food preparation; a basin.
# A wide receptacle in which gold grains are separated from gravel by washing the contents with water.
# {{lb|en|geography|geology}} An [[expanse]] of [[level]] [[land]] [[locate]]d in a [[depression]], [[especially]]
## A [[pond]] or [[lake]], [[considered]] as the [[expanse]] of [[land]] upon which the [[water]] [[sit]]s.
## {{lb|en|especially|_|South Africa}} A [[dry lake]] or [[playa]], [[especially]] a [[salt flat]].
## {{lb|en|South Africa}} {{syn of|en|playa lake|nodot=a}}: a [[temporary]] [[pond]] or [[lake]] in a [[playa]].
## {{short for|en|salt pan|nodot=a}}: a [[flat]] [[artificial]] [[pond]] [[use]]d for [[collect]]ing [[mineral]]s from [[evaporate]]d [[water]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} {{short for|en|hardpan|nodot=a}}: a [[hard]] [[substrate]] [[such as]] is [[form]]ed in pans.
# {{lb|en|geology|obsolete|_|South Africa}} {{syn of|en|pipe|nodot=a}}: a [[channel]] for [[lava]] within a [[volcano]]; the [[cylindrical]] [[remain]]s of [[such]] [[channel]]s.
# Strong adverse [[criticism]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=20 Aug 77|volume=5|number=7|journal=Gay Community News|page=10|author=Robert Etherington|title=John Horne Burns and His Enemies|text=The notices ''The Gallery'' received, while hardly '''pans''', were only mixed.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|Irish}}<ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''<sup>1</sup>|noformat=1|id=1078249498}}</ref> A loaf of [[bread]]; a [[pan-loaf]]. {{defdate|from 1970s|refn=OED}}
# {{label|en|obsolete}} The [[chamber pot]] in a [[close stool]]; {{label|en|now}} the [[base]] of a [[toilet]], [[consisting]] of the [[bowl]] and [[its]] [[support]].
# A [[bedpan]].
#* '''1977-1980''', [[w:Lou Sullivan|Lou Sullivan]], personal diary, quoted in '''2019''', Ellis Martin, Zach Ozma (editors), ''We Both Laughed In Pleasure''
#*: She yanks the '''pan''' out from under me & it spills all over the bed. Then she's got to change the sheets! Unreal.
# {{lb|en|slang}} A human [[face]], a [[mug]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1946|author=[[w:George Johnston (novelist)|George Johnston]]|title=Skyscrapers in the Mist|page=121|text="He's a foreign-looking guy with thinnish black hair and a meaty sort of '''pan'''."}}
#* {{RQ:William Burroughs Letters|page=92|passage=Dave and I have parted company, and I hope I never see his junky '''pan''' again.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1953|author=w:Raymond Chandler|title=The Long Goodbye|page=103|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2010
|passage=This was the kind of operator who would tell you to be there at nine sharp and if you weren't sitting quietly with a pleased smile on your '''pan''' when he floated in two hours later on a double Gibson, he would have a paroxysm of outraged executive ability […].}}
# {{lb|en|roofing}} The bottom flat part of a roofing panel that is between the [[rib]]s of the panel.
# A closed [[vessel]] for [[boil]]ing or [[evaporate|evaporating]] as part of [[manufacture]]; a [[vacuum pan]].
# {{lb|en|firearms}} The part of a [[flintlock]] that holds the [[priming]].
#: {{coi|en|[[flash in the pan|flash in the '''pan''']]}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1743|author={{w|Robert Drury (sailor)|Robert Drury}}|title=The Pleasant, and Surprizing Adventures of Mr. Robert Drury, during his Fifteen Years Captivity on the Island of Madagascar|url=https://archive.org/details/pleasantandsurp00drurgoog|pages=95–96|location=London
|passage={{...}} he pull’d the Trigger, but Providence being pleas’d to preserve me for some other Purpose, the Cock snapp’d, and miss’d Fire. Whether the Prime was wet in the '''Pan''', or by what other Miracle it was I escap’d his Fury, I cannot say {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1863|author=Sheridan Le Fanu|title=w:The House by the Churchyard|passage=And he {{...}} glared on the cold pistols that hung before him—ready for anything. And he took down one with a snatch and weighed it in his hand, and fell to thinking again; and, as he did, kept opening and shutting the '''pan''' with a snap, {{...}}}}
# The [[skull]], considered as a vessel containing the [[brain]]; the [[brainpan]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} The [[brain]], seen as one's intellect.
#* '''14th century''', {{w|Geoffrey Chaucer}}, ''{{w|The Canterbury Tales}}'': ''[[s:The Canterbury Tales/The Friar's Prologue and Tale|The Friar's Tale]]'',
#*: Unto the devil rough and black of hue
#*: Give I thy body and my '''pan''' also."
# {{lb|en|carpentry}} A [[recess]], or [[bed]], for the [[leaf]] of a [[hinge]].
# {{lb|en|musical instrument}} {{short for|en|steelpan}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Pnina Werbner|title=Black and Ethnic Leaderships|page=122
|passage=The steel band transforms the people who play in it and dance to it, and fosters links between them. {{...}} He learned to play the '''pan''' and filled in for absent members.}}

