==Classical Syriac==

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{syc-root-entry|ܒ|ܢ|ܐ}} related to building. Compare {{cog|ar|بَانِي|tr=bānī}} and {{cog|he|בַּנַּאי|tr=bannaʾy}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[bannɑjɑ(ʔ)]|aa=singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[bannɑje(ʔ)]|aa=plural}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun|m|ܒܢܝܐ}}

# [[builder]], [[founder]], [[constructor]]

=====Inflection=====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܒܢܝ}}

===Etymology 2===
From the root {{syc-root-entry|ܒ|ܢ|ܐ}} related to building.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[b(ə)nɑjɑ(ʔ)]|aa=singular}}
* {{IPA|syc|[b(ə)nɑje(ʔ)]|aa=plural}}

====Noun====
{{syc-noun|m|ܒܢܝܐ}}

# [[building]], [[erecting]], [[constructing]]

=====Inflection=====
{{syc-decl-noun-m|ܒܢܝ}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|syc|[b(ə)najjɑ(ʔ)]}}

====Noun====
{{head|syc|noun form}}

# {{inflection of|syc|ܒܪܐ||emphatic|p}}

===References===
