Page 40 تنبان: -------- begin text --------
{{also|تنبأن}}
==Persian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|تمبون|tr=tombun||colloquial Tehrani}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|fa|توبان|tr=tôbân}}, from {{inh|fa|pal|-}}, Lurish {{l|lrc|تمو|tr=temo}}. Akin to {{cog|ar|تُبَّان}} from the same. Borrowed early into {{cog|trk|-}}, {{cog|ota|طومان|tr=tuman}}, {{cog|az|tuman}}. Ultimately derived as equivalent to {{af|fa|تن|tr1=tan|t1=body|ـبان|tr2=-bân|t2=-keeper}} – similar to {{m|fa|تنوره|tr=tanura|t=cuirass, corselet; a part of dress worn by dervishes from their middle}}, better known as {{cog|ar|تَنُّورَة}}, with a different suffix.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fa|/tombɒn/|a=IR}}

===Noun===
{{fa-regional|تنبان|تنبان|тунбон}}
{{fa-noun|tr=tonbân|pl=تنبان‌ها}}

# [[breeches]]
# {{lb|fa|colloquial}} [[trousers]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|fa|شلوار|tr=šalvâr}}, {{l|fa|ازار|tr=ezâr}}, {{l|fa|چاقچور|tr=čâqčur}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|hy|թումբան|bor=on}}
* {{tooltip|borrowed|→}} Kamkata-viri:
*: {{desc|xvi|tamón}}
*: {{desc|bsh-kat|tamón}}

===References===
* {{R:Eilers:1962|pages=222–223}}

