Page 51 تبن: Skipped, no changes
Page 51 تبن: -------- begin text --------
{{also|بتن|تثن}}
==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ث ن ي}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|تَبَنٍّ|m|cons=تَبَنِّي}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|تَبَنَّى|form=V}}
# [[adoption]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَبَنٍّ}}

===Etymology 2===
Likely borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|תִּבְנָא}} / {{m|syc|ܬܒܢܐ|tr=teḇnā|t=straw}}, which is suspected mainly because of the varying vocalization, and also because this root is underdeveloped or it has the unrelated meaning of a “bowl”. The Aramaic might in turn come from {{der|ar|akk|𒅔𒉡𒁕|ts=tibnu|t=straw}} but can likewise be cognate. Else the word is only present in {{cog|he|תֶּבֶן|tr=teḇen|t=straw}}, in which language there is nothing to relate to either.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|تِبْن|m|head2=تَبْن|pl=أَتْبَان}}

# [[straw]]; [[hay]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|تِبْن|head2=تَبْن|pl=أَتْبَان|number=coll,pl}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|تِبْنِيّ|t=straw-related; straw-coloured}}
* {{l|ar|تَبَّان|t=straw vendor}}
* {{l|ar|مَتْبَن|t=place where the straw is stacked}}
* {{l|ar|تَبَنَ|t=to give straw to}}
* {{l|ar|تَبَّنَ|t=to feed straw to; to [[bung]], to [[cork]]}}
* {{l|ar|تَتَبَّنَ|t=to be [[bung]]ed, to be [[cork]]ed}}

===Etymology 3===
{{denominal verb|ar}} of {{m-self|ar|تِبْن|t=straw}}. In the “to bung” sense allegedly motivated by {{der|ar|es|taponar}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|i}}

# to give straw to, to feed with [[straw]]; to sell [[straw]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|i|vn=تَبْن}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to feed with [[straw]]
# to [[bung]], to [[cork]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|تَبْن|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|تَبَنَ|t=to give straw to}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَبْن}}

===Etymology 4===
{{unc|ar}} with possible connection to {{cog|akk|𒋰𒉌𒌈
|ts=tabnītu|t=an offering basket, a place to deposit tribute to a ruler or offerings before deities|lit=well-arranged, well-made or constructed}} and {{cog|akk|𒁀𒀀𒉡|ts=bānu|t=a ewer, vessel that fills up other vessels|lit=that which does what it was made for; a by-name for a ewer in ritual texts}}, therefore distantly being connected to {{ar-root|ب ن ي}}.

{{rfquote|ar|notext=1}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|تِبْن|m}}

# a [[great]] [[bowl]] that can [[satisfy]] the [[thirst]] of [[twenty]], a [[vessel]] used to [[fill]] [[drink]]ing [[cup]]s
# a [[generous]] [[chieftain]], one who [[give]]s [[large]] [[amount]]s
# a [[wolf]] for its [[thirst]] for [[blood]] being likened to a [[great]] [[vessel]]'s [[amount]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|تِبْن}}

===Etymology 5===
Like the more productive root {{ar-root|ط ب ن|nocat=1}}, from which there is with the like meanings {{m|ar|طَبِنَ}} and {{m|ar|طَبِن}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|i|a}}

# to be [[sagacious]], to be [[callid]], to be [[skillful]] in [[know]]ing, to be [[minute]] in [[inspection]]

