==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|ar|pal||tr=mlcpʾn'|ts=marz(o)bān|t=margrave}}, whence {{cog|fa|مرزبان|tr=marzbân}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَرْزُبَان}}
* {{ar-IPA|مَرْزَبَان}}

{{swp|lang=ar}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَرْزُبَان|m|pl=مَرَازِبَة|head2=مَرْزَبَان}} {{tlb|ar|historical}}

# [[marzban]], [[margrave]], [[march]] [[warden]], [[satrap]], a [[Sassanian]] governor of a [[frontier]] [[province]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَرْزُبَان|m|pl=مَرَازِبَة|head2=مَرْزَبَان}}

===Etymology 2===
Also found in {{bor|ar|syc|ܡܪܙܒܢܐ|tr=marzəbānā|t=a serving of grain}} and {{cog|axm|մարզպան|t=a measure of grain or liquid}}. This is probably a suffigation of the word treated at {{m|ar|مِرْزَاب|t=spout}}, i.e. “a spout full of grain”.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَرْزَبَان}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَرْزَبَان|m|pl=مَرَازِيب}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{tlb|ar|Medieval|_|Aleppo}} a {{l|en|dry measure}} for [[grain]], a fourth of a {{l|ar|مَكُّوك}}, ca. 26.25 liters
# {{tlb|ar|Medieval|_|Mesopotamia}} a {{l|en|liquid measure}} for [[wine]], a sixteenth of a {{l|ar|مِشْقَاع}}, 1.875 liters

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَرْزَبَان|m|pl=مَرَازِيب}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|mrzbn|N}}
* {{R:ar:Hinz-Maße|page=45}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=1075}}
* {{cite-book|year=1978|title=The Arithmetic of Al-Uqlīdisī: The Story of Hindu-Arabic Arithmetic as told in Kitāb al-Fuṣūl fī al-Ḥisāb al-Hindī|publisher=Reidel|last=Saiden|first=A. S.|location=Dordrecht & Boston|isbn=978-94-009-9774-5|pages=379–380|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=m8XtCAAAQBAJ&lpg=PA379&pg=PA380#v=onepage}}

{{c|ar|Units of measure|Government}}

