Page 1 lineage: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|linage}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|linage}}, from {{der|en|fro|linage}}, from {{m|fro|ligne}}, from {{der|en|la|linea||line}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|line|-age}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪn.i.ɪd͡ʒ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lineage.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[descent|Descent]] in a [[line]] from a common [[progenitor]]; [[progeny]]; descending line of [[offspring]] or ascending line of [[parentage]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Kyd Edward 3|page=47|act=III|scene=iii|passage=Edwards great '''linage''' by the mothers ſide, / Fiue hundred yeeres hath helde the ſcepter vp,}}
#* {{RQ:Bunyan Pilgrim's Progress|page=95|passage={{...}}; and therefore they were to me now no more than if they had never been of my '''Linage'''; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Homer Pope et al Odyssey|book=IV|page=146|passage=Accept this welcome to the ''Spartan'' court; / The waſte of nature let the feaſt repair, / Then your high '''lineage''' and your names declare: / Say from what ſcepter'd anceſtry ye claim, / Recorded eminent in deathleſs fame?}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Bride of Lammermoor|volume=II|page=301|passage=To counterbalance those foreign centinels{{sic}}, there mounted guard on the other side of the mirror two stout warders of Scottish '''lineage'''; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Hawthorne House Seven Gables|passage=“Ah, but these hens,” answered the young man,—“these hens of aristocratic '''lineage''' would scorn to understand the vulgar language of a barn-yard fowl. I prefer to think—and so would Miss Hepzibah—that they recognize the family tone. For you are a Pyncheon?”}}
#* {{RQ:Hardy Tess|passage=To produce Tess, fresh from the dairy, as a d’Urberville and a lady, he had felt to be temerarious and risky; hence he had concealed her '''lineage''' till such time as, familiarized with worldly ways by a few months’ travel and reading with him, he could take her on a visit to his parents and impart the knowledge while triumphantly producing her as worthy of such an ancient line. It was a pretty lover’s dream, if no more. Perhaps Tess’s '''lineage''' had more value for himself than for anybody in the world beside.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=July 19, 2011|author=Ella Davies|title=Stick insects survive one million years without sex|work=BBC|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/nature/14122050|passage=They traced the ancient '''lineages''' of two species to reveal the insects' lengthy history of asexual reproduction.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023|author=Ulf Mattsson|title=Controlling Privacy and the Use of Data Assets|volume=2|publisher=CRC Press|isbn=9781000924350|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=pA7JEAAAQBAJ&pg=PT149&dq=%22data+lineage%22&hl=&cd=6&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22data%20lineage%22&f=false|text=Data '''lineage''' is not a new concept, but modern business requirements far outstrip the siloed, limited features of the past. {{...}} The demand for data '''lineage''' comes from both technical and business users, including data architects, data engineers, data stewards, analysts and data scientists, as well as business managers, compliance professionals, and technical specialists.}}
# {{lb|en|advertising}} A number of [[line]]s of [[text]] in a [[column]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1927|author=William Leonard Crum|title=Advertising Fluctuations, Seasonal and Cyclical|passage=Total newspaper advertising '''lineage''' in the North Atlantic region}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=01 Dec 81|volume=12|number=20|journal=Gay Community News|page=4|author=Ronnie Allen|title=The ''Herald'': Shunning and Insulting|text=These are mere excerpts of longer pieces by Sullivan on Boy George, and I have left out more pieces because of the limits of space. Let me add, the '''lineage''' in Sullivan's column devoted to Boy George in 1984 exceeds the '''lineage''' in the rest of the ''Herald'' devoted to all news of gays and lesbians in the same period of time.}}
# A [[fee]] or [[rate]] paid per line of text.

====Derived terms====
{{der2|en|lineage temple|lineage zone}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|line}}
* {{l|en|lineal}}
* {{l|en|linear}}

