==English==
{{wikipedia|sweat (disambiguation)|sweat}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|swĕt}}, {{IPA|en|/swɛt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-sweat.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sweyd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|swete}}, {{m|enm|swet}}, {{m|enm|swate}}, {{m|enm|swote}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swāt}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*swait-}}, {{m|gem-pro||*swaitą}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*swoyd-|t=to sweat}}, o-grade of {{m|ine-pro|*sweyd-|t=to sweat}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|swit}}, {{cog|nl|zweet}}, {{cog|de|Schweiß}}, {{cog|da|sved}}, {{cog|sv|svett}}, {{cog|yi|שוויצן}} ({{cog|en|shvitz}}), {{cog|la|sudor}}, {{cog|fr|sueur}}, {{cog|it|sudore}}, {{cog|es|sudor}}, {{cog|fa|خوی|tr=xway|t=sweat}}, {{cog|sa|स्वेद|tr=svéda}}, {{cog|lt|sviedri}}, {{cog|txb|syā-}}, {{cog|sq|djersë}}, and {{cog|cy|chwys}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[fluid|Fluid]] that exits the [[body]] through [[pore]]s in the [[skin]] usually due to [[physical]] [[stress]] and/or [[high]] [[temperature]] for the purpose of regulating body temperature and removing certain compounds from the [[circulation]].
#: {{syn|en|perspiration}}
# The state of one who sweats; [[diaphoresis]].
#: {{ux|en|Just thinking about the interview tomorrow puts me into a nervous '''sweat'''.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Hard work; [[toil]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Moisture issuing from any substance.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1613|author={{w|William Browne (poet)|William Browne}}|title=Britannia's Pastorals
|passage=The Muses' friend (grey-eyed Aurora) yet <br> Held all the meadows in a cooling '''sweat''', <br> The milk-white gossamers not upwards snow'd, <br> Nor was the sharp and useful-steering goad}}
#* {{RQ:Mortimer Husbandry|passage=the '''sweat''' of hay or grain in a mow or stack}}
# A short [[run]] by a [[racehorse]] as a form of [[exercise]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1740|author=Henry Bracken|title=Farriery improv'd
|passage=A Horſe that gains Fleſh in hard Exerciſe, should be ſweated at leaſt twice in ten Days; and he ſhould run near five Miles in Puſhes, that the Sweat may have Time to diſcharge. Those Horſes which are ſweat without Covering, or with a very thin one, should run a long '''Sweat''', as wel call it, and ſtand a conſiderable while afterwards with a thick Blanket or two over them, from Head to Tail; otherwiſe the '''Sweat''' will not come out well.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1840|author=Richard Darvill|title=A Treatise on the Care, Treatment, and Training of the English Race Horse
|passage=There are some horses so very delicate, and have to run such short lengths, that they may not require a '''sweat''' during the whole time of their being in training.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=Gerald Hammond|title=The Language of Horse Racing
|passage=A '''sweat''' was, accordingly, a training run for a racehorse: a notice in The London Gazette in 1705 advertises a race for hunters that have not 'been kept in '''sweats''' above 12 weeks before the day of Running'.}}
# {{lb|en|historical}} The [[sweating sickness]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Hilary Mantel|title=Wolf Hall|page=131|publisher=Fourth Estate|year_published=2010
|passage=When the '''sweat''' comes back this summer, 1528, people say, as they did last year, that you won't get it if you don't think about it.}}
#* {{RQ:Holinshed Chronicles|passage={{...}}who both died within one houre of the '''sweat''' at Cambridge}}
# {{lb|en|British|military slang|especially WWI}} A [[soldier]] (especially one who is old or experienced).<!-- compare http://www.thefreedictionary.com/sweat and sources at [[old sweat]] -->
# {{lb|en|video games|slang}} An extremely or excessively [[competitive]] player.
#: {{syn|en|tryhard}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.sportskeeda.com/fortnite/news-how-exactly-sweats-ruining-fortnite-addressing-never-ending-try-hards-vs-casual-debate|work=Sportskeeda|passage=Casuals believe that '''sweats''' are ruining Fortnite. '''Sweats''' think that casuals just need to get better at the game. It's a never-ending debate that will never end, despite what anyone tries to say, but it's worth taking a look at regardless.|title=How exactly are 'sweats' ruining Fortnite? Addressing the never ending try-hards vs casual debate|date=2021-10-13|author=Zachary Roberts}}

