==Latin==
{{number box|la|3}}

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|la|terr}}, from {{inh|la|itc-ola|*tris}}, from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tris}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*trís}}. Cognate with {{cog|grc|la|τρίς|t=thrice}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Adverb===
{{la-num-adv|ter|type=freq}}

# [[thrice]], [[three]] [[times]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|4|690-691|quote='''Ter''' sēsē attollēns cubitōque adnīxa levāvit,<br/>'''ter''' revolūta torō est [...].|trans=''Lifting herself '''three times''', [Dido] had tried to raise upon her elbow, and '''thrice''' she had rolled back upon the bed [...].''}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|5|247–248|quote=‘'''ter''' voluī prōmittere opem, '''ter''' lingua retenta est:<br/>īra Iovis magnī causa timōris erat’|trans=''“'''Thrice''' I wanted to promise help, '''thrice''' [my] tongue was stayed:<br/>the anger of mighty Jupiter was the reason for [my] fear.”''<br/>(The poetic voice is that of [[w:Flora (mythology)|Flora]].)}}
#* {{quote-book|la|year=2004|url=http://ephemeris.alcuinus.net/archi2004/nuntii/eph2/index.php|title=Ephemeris|text=Olafur Ragnar Grimsson '''ter''' iam primarius minister Islandiae electus est.|t=Olafur Ragnar Grimsson has been elected as the president of Iceland for a '''third''' time.}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|la||Ter}} is a prefix or suffix designating the third instance of a thing, thus following {{m|la|bis||second}} and preceding {{m|la|quater||fourth}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|ternus}} {{qualifier|distributive numeral}}
* {{l|la|teruncius}}

