==Old Prussian==

===Etymology===
Perhaps cognate to {{cog|lt,lv|te|t=here!, here you are!}},<ref name=LEW>{{R:lt:LEW|head=tè|page=1071}}</ref><ref name=Schmalstieg>{{cite-book|author=[[w:lt:William Riegel Schmalstieg|William R. Schmalstieg]]|title=An Old Prussian Grammar|publisher={{w|Pennsylvania State University Press|Pennsylvania State UP}}|year=1974|pages=106, 112, 113|isbn=0-271-01171-8}}</ref> or to the related {{cog|lt|-}} prefix {{m|lt|te-}},<ref name=LEW /><ref name=CPMBL>{{R:bat:CPMBL|page=288|section=458a}}</ref> which can either express the [[hortative]] mood — as in ''tedirba'', "may he work" — or, more pertinently, the meaning "only" — as in ''teturiu'', "I have only". Possibly more distantly related to {{cog|ru|тепе́рь|t=now}}<ref name=LEW /><ref name=Schmalstieg /> and to {{cog|grc|τῆ|t=here!}}.<ref>{{R:bat:EDBIL|entry=te|page=462}}</ref>

Alternatively, the Prussian morpheme {{m|prg||-er-}} may be functionally equivalent to {{cog|lv||-ik-}}, {{cog|lt||-ik-}}, {{m|lt||-iek-}}. For example, {{m|prg|er|t=until}} parallels {{cog|lt|iki}}, {{m|lt|ik}}, and {{m|prg|erains|t=everyone}} parallels {{cog|lv|ikviens}}. Under this hypothesis, ''ter'' would be composed of {{m|prg||t-|pos=demonstrative prefix}} + {{m|prg||-er|pos=suffix denoting extent}}, and thus be equivalent to {{cog|lt|tik|t=only}} or {{m|lt|tiek|t=that much}}.<ref>{{cite-book|de|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/endzelin-altpreussische-grammatik-1944/page/143|oclc=7459119|title=Altpreussische Grammatik|author={{w|Jānis Endzelīns}}|location=Riga|publisher=Latvju Grāmata|year=1944|page=143|section=202b}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|en|url=https://www.journals.polon.uw.edu.pl/index.php/bl/article/view/396|title=On distributive pronouns in the Baltic languages|journal=Baltic Linguistics|author=Daniel Petit|issn=2081-7533|year=2015|volume=6}}</ref>

===Adverb===
{{head|prg|adverb}}

# {{def-uncertain|prg}} 1. [[only]], [[merely]]; 2. [[than]], [[other than]].
#: {{coi|prg|ter ains|t=alone|lit=only one}}
#* {{RQ:prg:Enchiridion|115|25|bhe kai ſteſmu nimaſſi kittawidin pogalbton boūt / '''ter''' kai tans praſtan Crixtiſnan is Deiwan naunagimton|t=and that he may not be helped in any other way / '''[only; other than]''' that he was born new through baptism out of God}}

====Usage notes====
In the Old Prussian corpus, this only occurs one time outside of the combination {{m|prg|ter ains}}; see the quotation above. In the original German text of the Catechism, the word {{m|de|denn|t=than}} was used:
: {{ux|de|nocat=1|vnnd das jhm nicht anders geholffen werden moͤge / '''denn''' das es durch die Tauffe auß Gott Newgeboren|t=and that he may not be helped in any other way / '''than''' that he was born new through baptism out of God}}
Accordingly, Nesselmann glosses ''ter'' as {{m|de|als|t=than}},<ref>{{R:prg:Nesselmann|page=187}}</ref> which has displaced {{m|de|denn}} in this sense in modern German. However, there are good reasons to think that it may literally mean "only", discussed in the etymology above, and this is the meaning assumed by Fraenkel,<ref name=LEW /> Endzelīns,<ref name=CPMBL /> and Mažiulis.<ref>{{R:prg:Mažiulis|id=2417|head=ter}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|lt|title=Prūsų kalbos paminklai|trans-title=Prussian-language monuments|volume=2|page=221|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/maziulis-prusu-kalbos-paminklai-t.-2-1981/page/221|author={{w|Vytautas Mažiulis}}|year=1981|publisher=Mokslas|location=Vilnius}}</ref> Schmalstieg mentions both potential meanings.<ref name=Schmalstieg />

===References===
<references />

==Portuguese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|pt|têr||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|pt|itc-pro|ine-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|teer}}, from earlier {{inh|pt|roa-opt|tẽer}}, {{inh|pt|la|teneo|tenēre}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA|têr}}
* {{hyph|pt|ter}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb}}

# to [[have]]
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[own]]; to [[possess]]; to [[have]]; to [[have got]]
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tenho''' uma bela casa.|translation=I '''have''' a beautiful house.}}
## {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to be [[rich]], to have plenty of [[money]]; or, to have enough money to live [[comfortably]]
##: {{ux|pt|Os caridosos sempre ajudam os que menos '''têm'''.|translation=The charitable always help those who don’t '''have enough'''.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[have]] as a [[component]] or to [[consist]] of
##: {{ux|pt|Esta frase '''tem''' cinco palavras.|translation=This sentence '''has''' five words.}}
##: {{ux|pt|As lanças '''têm''' cabos compridos.|translation=Spears '''have''' long shafts.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[have]] {{gl|to be related in some way to, with the object identifying the relationship}}
##: {{ux|pt|Este livro '''tem''' dono.|translation=This book '''has''' an owner.}}
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tenho''' três irmãs.|translation=I '''have''' three sisters.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to be in [[possession]] of; to have as part of one’s [[personal effects]]; to [[have]] [[in hand]]
##: {{ux|pt|O senhor '''tem''' a sua carteira?|translation=Do you '''have''' your wallet '''on you'''?}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to consist of a certain amount of [[unit of measurement|units of measurement]]
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tenho''' quarenta anos.|translation=I am forty years old.|lit=I '''have''' forty years}}
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tenho''' 1,78 m de altura.|I '''am''' 1.78 m tall.}}
##: {{ux|pt|Esta caneta '''tem''' dez centímetros.|translation=This pen '''is''' ten centimeters '''long'''.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to have a certain [[characteristic]]
##: {{ux|pt|Este jogo não '''tem''' graça.|translation=This game isn’t fun.|lit=this game doesn’t '''have''' fun}}
##: {{ux|pt|As palavras que dizes '''têm''' significado.|translation=The words you say '''have''' meaning.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} to be [[afflicted]] with a certain [[disease]] or other [[medical]] [[condition]]
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tens''' um resfriado.|translation=You '''have''' a cold.}}
## {{lb|pt|transitive}} {{n-g|indicates that the subject has an event (the object) scheduled}}
##: {{ux|pt|'''Temos''' uma partida de xadrez daqui a uma semana.|translation=We '''have''' a chess match in a week.}}
## {{lb|pt|Brazil|intransitive}} to [[receive]] one’s [[wage]]
##: {{ux|pt|Ainda não '''tive''' esse mês.|translation=I still haven’t '''received my wage''' this month.}}
# {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} [[must]]; to [[have to]] {{+obj|pt|:de(inf)/:que(inf)<do something>}}
#* {{quote-book|pt|year=2003|author=w:J. K. Rowling; w:Lia Wyler|title=Harry Potter e a Ordem da Fênix|publisher=Rocco|page=538
|passage=Sinto muito '''ter de''' contradizê-la, Minerva, mas, como pode ver no meu bilhete, Harry tem obtido resultados muito fracos nas minhas aulas...|t=I'm sorry to contradict you, Minerva, but, as you can see in my note, Harry has obtained very weak results in my classes...}}
# {{lb|pt|auxiliary}} to [[have]]
## {{lb|pt|imperfect indicative forms followed by a masculine singular past participle}}; {{n-g|forms the past [[perfect]]}}
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tínhamos''' já comido bolo.|We '''had''' eaten cake already.}}
## {{lb|pt|present indicative forms followed by a masculine singular past participle}} {{n-g|forms the present [[perfect progressive]]}}
##: {{ux|pt|'''Tenho''' comido muita carne ultimamente.|translation=I '''have been''' eating a lot of meat lately.}}
## {{lb|pt|conditional forms followed by a masculine singular past participle}} {{n-g|forms the [[conditional perfect]]}}
##: {{ux|pt|Eu o '''teria''' comprado, se tivesse dinheiro.|translation=I '''would have''' bought it, if I had money.}}
# {{lb|pt|Brazil|impersonal|transitive}} [[there be]] {{gl|to exist, physically or abstractly}}
#: {{syn|pt|haver}}
#: {{ux|pt|Amanhã '''terá''' aula.|translation='''There will be''' class tomorrow.}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Tem''' países em guerra naquela região.|translation='''There are''' countries at war in that region.}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[give birth]] to
#: {{ux|pt|A vaca '''terá''' um bezerro.|translation=The cow '''will give birth to''' a calf.}}
#: {{ux|pt|Estou '''tendo''' gêmeos!|translation=I'm '''having''' twins!}}
# {{lb|pt|transitive}} to [[consider]] {{gl|assign some quality to}} {{+obj|pt|dirobj<someone> + :por/:como(copulative&noun&or&adjective)}}
#: {{ux|pt|Todos '''têm''' João por inteligente.|translation=Everyone '''considers''' John to be intelligent.}}
#: {{ux|pt|João o '''tinha''' como amigo.|translation=John '''considered''' him a friend.}}
# {{lb|pt|intransitive}} to [[go to]]; to [[interact]] {{+obj|pt|:com<with someone>}}
#* '''1948''', [[w:Holy Bible|Bíblia Sagrada]], edição [[w:João Ferreira de Almeida|Almeida Revista e Corrigida]], [[w:Book of Proverbs|Provérbios]] 6:6
#: {{ux|pt|Vá '''ter com''' a formiga, ó preguiçoso; considera os seus caminhos e sê sábio.|translation=
'''Go to''' the ant, you sluggard; consider its ways and be wise.}}

====Usage notes====
For verbs that distinguish between ''particípio passado curto'' (short {{l|en|past participle}}) and ''particípio passado longo'' (long past participle) — for example {{m|pt|morrer||to die}}, whose short past participle is {{m|pt|morto}} and long is {{m|pt|morrido}} — when {{m|pt|ter}} is used as an {{l|en|auxiliary}} verb, the long past participle must be used (like {{m|pt|haver}}, and unlike {{m|pt|ser}} and {{m|pt|estar}}).

