==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ə/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|ər|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/ɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us--er.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|-or|;|-a<aa:non-rhotic>}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|inh|id=agent suffix|enm>-er>agent suffix|tree=1}}
{{inh+|en|enm|-ere|id=agentive}}, {{m|enm|-er}}, from {{inh|en|enm|-ere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-ere}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*-ārī}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*-ārijaz}}, usually thought to have been borrowed from {{der|en|la|-ārius}}. However, Gąsiorowski suggests that *-ārijaz is a native formation; he derives it from earlier *-azrijaz, which he etymologises as a zero-grade form of *-sōr suffixed with *-ih₂, creating a suffix *-sr-ih₂ for forming feminine agent nouns, which was then masculinised by attaching *-ós. Cognate with {{cog|stq|-er}}, {{cog|fy|-er}}, {{cog|nl|-er}}, {{cog|nds-de|-er}}, {{cog|de|-er}}, {{cog|da|-er}}, {{cog|sv|-are}}, {{cog|is|-ari}}.

Compare the synonymous but unrelated {{der|en|fro|-or}}, {{m|fro|-eor}} ({{der|en|xno|-}} variant {{m|fro|-our}}), from {{der|en|la|-tor|-(ā)tor}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*-tōr}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|en|-'er}} {{qualifier|following an abbreviation, or sometimes following a number}}

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|cat3=productive suffixes}}

# {{senseid|en|agent noun}} {{lb|en|added to verbs}} A [[person]] or [[thing]] that does an action indicated by the root verb; {{non-gloss definition|used to form an [[agent noun]]}}.
#: {{antonyms|en|-ee}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|read|reader}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|cook|cooker}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|compute|computer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|run|runner}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|toast|toaster}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|swim|swimmer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|[[do]] [[good]]|do-gooder}}
# {{senseid|en|patient}} {{lb|en|added to verbs|informal}} A person or thing to which the root verb is done or can be done satisfactorily.
#: {{suffixusex|en|look|looker|gloss2=an attractive person}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|keep|keeper|gloss2=a person or thing worth keeping}}
# {{senseid|en|occupation}} {{lb|en|added to nouns, chiefly denoting occupations}} A person whose occupation is the root noun; {{lb|en|more broadly|occasionally with adjectives}} a person characterized by the root.
#: {{suffixusex|en|astrology|astrologer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|baby boom|baby boomer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|conlang|conlanger}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|cricket|cricketer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|trumpet|trumpeter}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|zine|ziner}}
# {{senseid|en|measurement}} {{lb|en|added to numbers, measurements or nouns denoting quantified sets}} A person or thing to which a certain number or measurement applies.
#: {{suffixusex|en|six|sixer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|six foot|six-footer}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|three-wheel|three-wheeler}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|first grade|first grader}}
# {{senseid|en|entertainment}} {{lb|en|slang|chiefly|entertainment|with few limitations}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to form nouns shorter than more formal synonyms}}.
#: {{suffixusex|en|percent|percenter|gloss2=commission agent}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|[[one]] [[hand]]|one-hander|t2=one-man show}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|oat|oater|gloss2=a Western-themed movie}}
# {{senseid|en|ideology}} {{lb|en|added to nouns}} A person who is associated with, or supports a particular [[theory]], [[doctrine]], or political [[movement]].
#: {{suffixusex|en|birth|birther}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|[[flat]] [[earth]]|flat-earther}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|truth|truther}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|woke|woker}}
# {{senseid|en|relational}} {{lb|en|added to nouns or occasionally adjectives|generally}} A thing that is related in some way to the root, such as by location or purpose.
#: {{suffixusex|en|bacon|baconer|t2=pig raised for bacon}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|chocolate chip|chocolate chipper|t2=cookie containing chocolate chips}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|sternwheel|sternwheeler|t2=vessel driven by a sternwheel}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The suffix may be used to form an agent noun of many verbs. In compound or phrasal verbs, the suffix usually follows the verb component (as in {{m|en|passerby|pass'''er'''by}} and {{m|en|runner-up|runn'''er'''-up}}) but is sometimes added at the end, irrespective of the position of the verb component ({{m|en|do-gooder|do-good'''er'''}}) or is added to both components for humorous effect ({{m|en|washer-upper|wash'''er'''-upp'''er'''}}).
* The occupational sense is often applied generally to members of a group, as in {{m|en|crewer||a member of a crew}} and {{m|en|Z-lister||one on the [[Z-list]]}}; fans and hobbyists, as in {{m|en|K-popper||a fan of [[K-pop]]}}, and those who use a particular tool or instrument, as in {{m|en|JavaScripter||a programmer who uses [[JavaScript]]}}.
* The entertainment slang sense is sometimes referred to as the ''[[w:Variety (magazine)|Variety]]'' '''''-er'''''.

