===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|-ere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-ware|pos=suffix denoting residency or meaning "inhabitant of"}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*-wari}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*warjaz||defender, inhabitant}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wer-||to close, cover, protect, save, defend}}.

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix}}

# {{senseid|en|inhabitant}} {{lb|en|added to a proper noun}} Suffix denoting a [[resident]] or [[inhabitant]] of (the place denoted by the proper noun); {{non-gloss definition|used to form a [[demonym]]}}.
#: {{suffixusex|en|New York|New Yorker}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|London|Londoner}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|Dublin|Dubliner}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|New England|New Englander}}
# Suffix denoting residency in or around a place, district, area, or region.
#: {{suffixusex|en|island|islander}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|highland|highlander}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|eastend|eastender}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|en|id=inhabitant}}

