==Catalan==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ca|la|-ārius}}. Compare the borrowed doublet {{doublet|ca|-ari|notext=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ca-IPA|[é(r)]}}

===Suffix===
{{ca-noun|m}}

# {{n-g|forms nouns meaning the location or object where something is usually found}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|vespa|gloss1=wasp|vesper|gloss2=wasp nest}}
# {{n-g|forms nouns meaning a plant which is cultivated to produce something}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|garrofa|gloss1=carob|garrofer|gloss2=carob tree}}
# {{n-g|forms nouns meaning the purpose of something or an object used for that purpose}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|tovallola|gloss1=towel|tovalloler|gloss2=towel rail}}

====Usage notes====
* The equivalent suffix {{m|ca|-era}} can be used to form feminine nouns with these meanings, but usually only the masculine or feminine form will be found in Catalan.

===Suffix===
{{ca-adj}}

# {{n-g|forms nouns and adjectives referring to an inhabitant of somewhere}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|Brasil|gloss1=Brazil|brasiler|gloss2=Brazilian}}
# {{n-g|forms nouns and adjectives referring to engaging in a profession}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|camió|gloss1=truck|camioner|gloss2=truck driver}}
# {{n-g|forms nouns and adjectives referring to being prone to some activity or characteristic}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|mentida|gloss1=lie|mentider|gloss2=liar, deceptive}}
# {{n-g|forms relational adjectives}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|llet|gloss1=milk|lleter|gloss2=milk [relational adjective], dairy}}
#: {{suffixusex|ca|pel·lícula|gloss1=film|pel·liculer|gloss2=film [relational adjective], filmic, cinematic}}

====Usage notes====
* Because these senses are used to form adjectives of two forms or nouns referring to animate objects, both the masculine and feminine forms will be found in Catalan, with the lemma entry found at the masculine form.

