==Danish==

===Suffix===
{{da-suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Forms [[agent noun]]s from verbs, with the sense "someone or something that [verb]s".}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Forms [[plural]] forms of many nouns.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Forms the [[present tense]] of many verbs.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Forms [[demonym]]s.}}
#: {{suffixusex|da|Berlin|-er|berliner}}
#: {{suffixusex|da|Paris|-er|pariser}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Forms informal action nouns from verbs.}}
# {{lb|da|especially definite}} {{non-gloss definition|Forms informal abbreviations of nouns, with elision.}}
#: {{suffixusex|da|hotdog|hotter}}
#: {{suffixusex|da|fjernsyn|t1=television|fjerner}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Forms a piece of currency from numbers.}}
#: {{suffixusex|da|fem|t1=five|femmer|t2=fiver, five pounds/dollars/kroner/etc.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Forms a die throw result from numbers.}}
#: {{ux|da|Du skal slå mindst en '''treer''' for at komme videre.|You must throw at least a '''three''' to move on.}}

====Usage notes====
Senses 1 and 3 often lead to heteronymic pairs. For example, from {{m|da|løbe||run}} [ˈløːb̥ə] comes {{m|da|løber||runs}} [ˈløːˀb̥ɐ] (verb form) and {{m|da|løber||runner}} [ˈløːb̥ɐ] (noun), distinguished by [[stød]].

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|da}}

