==Turkish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|tr|/ˈær/}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|tr|ota|ـر|tr=-r, -er}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*-ür}}. Cognate with {{cog|otk|𐰼|ts=-(e)r}}. Negative {{m|tr|-mez}} are from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*-meŕ}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*-me}} + {{m|trk-pro|*-er}} or {{m|trk-pro|*-ür}} ({{cog|az|-ər|t=indefinite future suffix}} — {{m|az|-məz}}, but {{m|az|-ir|t=simple present suffix}} — {{m|az|-mir}}).

====Suffix====
{{head|tr|suffix}}

# Simple present and aorist tense marker

====Suffix====
{{tr-suffix|head=-er [[-mez]]}}

# [[as soon as]]
#: {{ux|tr|Eve gel'''ir''' gel'''mez''' duş alırım.|'''As soon as''' I get home, I take a shower.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Can change to {{m|tr|-ir}} ({{m|tr|almak}} → {{m|tr|alır}}, but {{m|tr|içmek}} → {{m|tr|içer}}). There are some rules governing the usage of ''-er/ir'', the former is used in case of monosyllabic stems, while the latter is used elsewhere; with the exceptions of 14 verbs below which uses ''-ir'' on the aorist
*{{m|tr|almak}} — {{m|tr|alır}}
*{{m|tr|bilmek}} — {{m|tr|bilir}}
*{{m|tr|bulmak}} — {{m|tr|bulur}}
*{{m|tr|denmek}} — {{m|tr|denir}}
*{{m|tr|durmak}} — {{m|tr|durur}}
*{{m|tr|gelmek}} — {{m|tr|gelir}}
*{{m|tr|görmek}} — {{m|tr|görür}}
*{{m|tr|kalmak}} — {{m|tr|kalır}}
*{{m|tr|olmak}} — {{m|tr|olur}}
*{{m|tr|ölmek}} — {{m|tr|ölür}}
*{{m|tr|sanmak}} — {{m|tr|sanır}}
*{{m|tr|varmak}} — {{m|tr|varır}}
*{{m|tr|vermek}} — {{m|tr|verir}}
*{{m|tr|vurmak}} — {{m|tr|vurur}}
The suffix ''-r'' is used after verb stems ending in a vowel. Unlike most negations of tense suffixes which regularly uses the suffix {{m|tr|-me}}, negative aorist suffix is {{m|tr|-mez}} instead of ''*-mer''.

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|tr}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|tr|-r}}
* {{l|tr|-ar}}
* {{l|tr|-ir}}
* {{l|tr|-mez}}

