===Verb===
{{en-verb|pres_ptc2=plummetting|past2=plummetted}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[drop]] swiftly, in a direct manner; to [[fall]] [[quickly]].
#: {{ux|en|After its ascent, the arrow '''plummeted''' to earth.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kate Conger; Lauren Hirsch|title=Elon Musk Suggests Buying Twitter at His Original Price|work=The New York Times|date=2022-10-04|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/10/04/technology/elon-musk-twitter-deal.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Some speculated Twitter’s stock would '''plummet''', while another said the company would not have to be owned by “a moron,” using an expletive to refer to Mr. Musk.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 December 14|author=Christian Wolmar|title=No Marston Vale line trains... and no one in charge seems to 'give a damn'|journal=RAIL|issue=972|page=46|text=Passenger numbers had been rising sharply. But the replacement of the services by buses, which take far longer because of the number of stations in out-of-the-way villages on the route, will ensure they '''plummet''' again.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to drop swiftly}} {{l|en|dive}}, {{l|en|drop}}, {{l|en|fall}}

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|to drop swiftly}} {{l|en|ascend}}, {{l|en|rise}}, {{l|en|rocket}}, {{l|en|soar}}, {{l|en|skyrocket}}

