From {{der|arc|akk|𒄙|ts=turru, ṭurru|t=yarn, twine, wire, string; a twist of fibers}}, possibly a loan from or influenced by {{der|arc|sux|𒄙|tr=dur|t=strip}} or rather related to the native verb {{der|arc|sem-pro|*tawar-|t=to go about, to circle, to turn about, to encompass, to come around again; to plait, to braid}}. Cognate to {{cog|he|תּוֹר|tr=tōr|t=line}}, and {{noncog|fa|تار|tr=târ|t=cord, string}} is possibly related by phono-semantic matching.

====Pronunciation====
