# {{senseid|ar|be-pious}} {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to be [[righteous]], to be [[pious]], to be [[godly]], to be  [[reverent]], to be [[religious]]
## {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to [[straighten up]], to [[reform]]
##: {{syn|ar|صَلَحَ|اِسْتَقَام|t1=to reform|t2= to straighten up}}
##: {{ant|ar|فَجَرَ|t=to be sinful}}
# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to be [[kind]] or [[generous]] to {{+obj|ar|:بِ}}
#: {{syn|ar|أَحْسَنَ}}
# {{lb|ar|intransitive|transitive}} to [[respect]] or to be [[respectful]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<to elders, one's parents or grandparents, old kinsmen, a deity, and so on>}}, to [[honor]], to [[revere]]; to [[obey]]
#: {{syn|ar|وَقَّرَ|t=to revere, to venerate}}
#: {{ux|ar|بَرَّ الصَّبِيُّ وَالِدَيْهِ وَرَبَّهُ|The boy obeyed his parents and his Lord.}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[deem]] (an act) [[true]], [[sincere]], or [[pious]]; to [[accept]] or [[bless]] (a religious ritual)
#: {{syn|ar|قَبِلَ|بَارَك}}
#: {{ux|ar|بَرَّ اللهُ حَجَّهُ وَصَلَاتَهُ|Allah accepted his pilgrimage and his prayer.}}
## {{lb|ar|intransitive|of an act, especially religious rituals, such as pilgrimages}} to be [[true]], [[sincere]], or [[pious]]
##: {{ux|ar|بَرَّ حَجُّهُ وَصَلَاتُهُ|His pilgrimage and prayer were pious.}}

