==Persian==
{{wikipedia|lang=fa}}
[[File:City in the Iranian Azerbaijan.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|fa|تبریز}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
{{unk|fa}}.

After the earliest resemblance it has been<ref>{{cite-book|last=Herzfeld|first=Ernst Emil|authorlink=Ernst Herzfeld|title=Archaeological History of Iran|year=1935|publisher=The British Academy|page=12–19|url=https://archive.org/details/in.gov.ignca.14939|location=London}}</ref> implied of {{der|fa|xur|-}} origin by being equated with {{cog|akk-nas|-}} mentions of cities {{m|akk||tr=Tarwi, Tarui}} and {{m|akk||tr=Tarmakisa, Tarwakisa}} in the Sangibutu = {{w|lang=de|Gilzanu}} = Baru = Bāri district occupied by [[Urartu]],<ref>{{cite-book|authorlink=Daniel David Luckenbill|last=Luckenbill|first=Daniel David|title=Ancient Records of Assyria and Babylonia Volume 2: Historical Records of Assyria From Sargon to the End|year=1927|location=Chicago|page=8 and 85|publisher=The University of Chicago Press|volume=2|url=https://isac.uchicago.edu/research/publications/misc/ancient-records-assyria-and-babylonia-volume-2-historical-records-assyria}}</ref> which equation however has been reckoned far-fetched,<ref name="Lockhart">{{cite-book|last=Lockhart|first=Laurence|year=1960|title=Persian Cities|location=London|publisher=Luzac|page=10}}</ref> seemingly because this region is to the west of Lake Urmia, “though it must be stressed that the concept of a linear boundary wholly fails to express the complex patterns of relationships which existed between neighbouring regions and interspersed peoples,”<ref>{{cite-book|title=Neo-Assyrian Geography|last=Liverani|first=Mario|publisher=Università di Roma La Sapienza|location=Rome|series=Quaderni di geografia storica|seriesvolume=5|year=1995|pageurl=https://www.google.de/books/edition/Neo_Assyrian_Geography/IaoMAQAAMAAJ?gbpv=1&bsq=%22Baru%22+%22Urartu%22&dq=%22Baru%22+%22Urartu%22&printsec=frontcover|page=33}}</ref> leading to the suggestion of Iranian origin since the area of Tabriz was territory of the Medes known by another homonymous Sangibuti, possibly equivalent to {{m|fa|تو|tr=taw|t=pool, puddle}} + {{m|fa|ریختن|ریز|t=flow|tr=rēz}} as in {{m|ar|إِبْرِيق}} referring to the springs of mineral water that rise on the slopes of {{w|Mount Sahand}};<ref name="Lockhart"/> however a place-forming suffix {{m|fa||ـویج|tr=-vīj}} is known, attached to {{m|ar|تر|tr=tar|t=fresh, moist}} in the {{w|Sarpol-e Zahab County}} village name {{m|fa|ترویج|tr=tarvij|lit=watery place}}.<ref>{{R:fa:Akbarzadeh:2019|page=86}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|tab`rēz}}
* {{audio|fa|LL-Q9168 (fas)-Mazanin (مازنین)-تبریز.wav|a=Iran}}

