Page 44 Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/-teros: Skipped, no changes
Page 44 Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/-teros: -------- begin text --------
{{reconstructed}}
==Proto-Indo-European==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ine-pro|*-eros}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ine-pro|suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Contrastive or oppositional adjectival suffix.}}

====Usage notes====
In Proto-Indo-European, ''X-teros'' meant "one which is especially X", "one which is more X than other things", "one which is X as opposed to something else". Compare:
* Sanskrit: {{l|sa|उद्}} → {{l|sa|उत्तर||upper}}
* Greek: {{l|grc|δεξιός||right}} → {{l|grc|δεξιτερός||right}} (as opposed to "left")
* Latin: {{l|la|māter||mother}} → {{l|la|mātertera||maternal aunt}} (literally "the mother one").

In some daughters the suffix was grammaticalized as the marker of a comparative degree in adjectives:
* Greek: {{l|grc|γλυκύς||sweet}} → {{l|grc|γλυκύτερος||sweeter}}

In some daughters it attracted various pronominal adjectives (determiners), i.e. words meaning "other":
* Sanskrit: {{l|sa|अन्यतर}}
* Latin: {{l|la|alter|al-ter}}
* Gothic: {{l|got|𐌰𐌽𐌸𐌰𐍂|𐌰𐌽-𐌸𐌰𐍂}}
or possessives:
* Greek: {{l|grc|ἡμέτερος|ἡμέ-τερος}}
* Latin: {{l|la|noster|nos-ter|our}}
* Old Irish: {{l|sga|náthar||of us two}}

====Inflection====
{{ine-decl-adj|-tero}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ine-pro}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|gem-pro|*-þeraz|*-drê}}
* {{desc|grk-pro|*-teros}}
** {{desc|grc|-τερος|-τερός}}
*** {{desc|el|-τερος}}
* {{desc|itc-pro|*-teros}}
** {{desc|la|-ter}} {{q|perhaps}}, {{l|la|-iter}} {{q|perhaps}}
* {{desc|iir-pro|*-taras}}
** {{desc|inc-pro|*-taras}}
*** {{desc|sa|-तर}}
** {{desc|ira-pro|*-tarah}}
*** {{desc|ae|-𐬙𐬀𐬭𐬀}}
*** {{desc|hac|تەر|tr=-tar}}
*** Kurdish:
**** {{desc|ckb|تر}}
**** {{desc|kmr|-tir}}
*** {{desc|pal|tr=-tar}}
**** {{desc|fa|ـتر|tr=-tar}}
*** {{desc|zza|-yer|-êr}}

===See also===
* {{l|ine-pro|*-yōs}}

===References===
* Marek Majer (2012), ''[https://www.academia.edu/1699228/What_happened_to_Proto-Indo-European_kWotero-_in_Slavic What happened to PIE kʷotero- in Slavic?]''
