Page 1 caste: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|pt|-}} or {{bor|en|es|casta||lineage, breed, race}}, of uncertain origin. The OED derives it from Portuguese {{m|pt|casto||chaste}}, from {{der|en|la|castus}}.
Coromines (1987) argues instead for a hypothetical {{der|en|got|-}} form {{m|got|*𐌺𐌰𐍃𐍄𐍃}}, cognate with {{cog|en|cast}}, from Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*kastuz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂ǵ-es-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|käst|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/kɑːst/}}
* {{IPA|en|/kast/|a=Northern England,Scotland}}
* {{IPA|en|/kæst/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-caste.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|cast|;|karst|aa=non-rhotic,trap-bath split}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːst|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of the [[hereditary]] [[social]] [[class]]es and [[subclass]]es of South Asian [[society|societies]] or similar found historically in other cultures.
#: {{hypo|en|Brahmin|Kshatriya|Shudra|Vaishya|varna}}
#* {{quote-journal|en| date=April 6, 2017| author=Samira Shackle| title=On the frontline with Karachi’s ambulance drivers| work=the Guardian| url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/apr/06/on-the-frontline-with-karachis-ambulance-drivers| passage=Pakistan is a conservative, religious state. The {{w|Edhi Foundation}} is unusual in its ignoring of '''caste''', creed, religion and sect. This strict stance has led to some criticism from religious groups.}}
# A separate and fixed order or class of persons in society who chiefly associate with each other.
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Redheap|page=89|passage=It was an evidence of the peculiar nature of '''caste''' in country towns[.]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Agatha Christie| title=w:Murder on the Orient Express| location=London| publisher=HarperCollins| year=1934| year_published=2017| chapter=5| page=236| passage='I believe, Messieurs, in loyalty - to one's friends and one's family and one's '''caste'''.'}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay Bunyan|The tinkers then formed a hereditary '''caste'''.}}
# {{lb|en|zoology}} A [[class]] of [[polymorphous]] [[eusocial]] [[insect]]s of a particular [[size]] and [[function]] within a [[colony]].
#: {{ux|en|In [[beehive]]s, most [[bee]]s belong to the [[worker]] '''caste'''.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|en|anticaste|casted|casteist|castelike|castemate|castewise|intercaste|intracaste|noncaste|outcaste|subcaste|supercaste|casteism|casteist|casteless|castelike|caste mark|castemate|castewise|caste-ridden|half-caste|lose caste|quarter-caste}}

