==Galician==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|gl|casta}}

===Etymology===
Probably from {{der|gl|got|*𐌺𐌰𐍃𐍄𐍃}}, from {{der|gl|gem-pro|*kastuz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*kastōną||to throw, cast}}, compare {{cog|en|cast}}.<ref>{{R:es:DCECH|casta}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|/ˈkaste̝/}}

===Noun===
{{gl-noun|f}}

# [[species]], [[race]] or [[kind]]
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1853|author=Juan Manuel Pintos|title=A Gaita Gallega|location=Pontevedra|publisher=Impr. de D. José e D. Primitivo Vilas|page=29
|passage=''Por aquí nacen os ricos polo outro probes labregos. Estas son as dúas '''castes''' que hai en todo o mundo inteiro''.
|translation=Here the rich people are born, there the poor peasants; these are the two '''races''' that there are in the whole world}}
# [[quality]]
#* {{quote-text|gl|year=1859|author=Ramón Barros Silvelo|title=Un dia de desfertuna|page=3
|passage=''Dime logo que o probe do animal ou é de mala '''caste''', ou ben non come''
|translation=He readily told me that the animal [that I was selling] either was of bad quality, or either it didn't eat}}
# [[progeny]]; group of people that share a common ancestor
#: {{syn|gl|estirpe|fruxe|liñaxe}}
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1853|author=Juan Manuel Pintos|title=A Gaita Gallega|location=Pontevedra|publisher=Impr. de D. José e D. Primitivo Vilas|page=8
|passage=''{ soy llamado Pedro Luces ... } - To to to, vamos con tento que un home con ese nome pode ser '''caste''' do demo.''
|translation={I am called Peter Lights...} —Wo wo wo! Let us be careful: a man with that name could de a Devil's '''child'''.}}

====Derived terms====
