{{head|it|preposition}}

# [[with]], [[together]]
#: {{ant|it|senza}}
# {{lb|it|rowing}} [[coxed]]

=====Usage notes=====
* When followed by the definite article, ''con'' may be combined with the article to produce the following combined forms (marking these combined forms in writing is old-fashioned, and very rarely used apart from ''col'' and ''coi''; however, it has always been very common in speech, and it still is):

: {| class="wikitable"
|-
! ''con'' + article
! Combined form
|-
| con + {{l|it|il}}
| {{l|it|col}}
|-
| con + {{l|it|lo}}
| {{l|it|collo}}
|-
| con + {{l|it|l'}}
| {{l|it|coll'}}
|-
| con + {{l|it|i}}
| {{l|it|coi}}
|-
| con + {{l|it|gli}}
| {{l|it|cogli}}
|-
| con + {{l|it|la}}
| {{l|it|colla}}
|-
| con + {{l|it|le}}
| {{l|it|colle}}
|}

===Etymology 2===
Alternative form of {{m|it|com}}, {{apocopic form|it|come|nocap=1}}, found before consonants other than ⟨b⟩, ⟨m⟩, ⟨p⟩.

