# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To [[endow]] with a soul or [[mind]].
#: {{syn|en|besoul|ensoul}}
# To [[beg]] on All Soul's Day.
#: {{cot|en|trick-or-treat}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1981|title=Squire and tenant: life in rural Cheshire, 1760-1900  |author= Geoffrey Scard |page=93 |ISBN= |passage=All Souls' Day was celebrated by '''souling''', a custom going back to pre-Reformation days: soul cakers and mummers toured the village begging for a soul cake — a plain, round, flat cake seasoned with spices. }}

