===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵenh₁-}}
From {{bor|en|fr|génie|t=genius, genie}}, a {{psm|fr|ar|جِنّيّ|tr=jinnī|nocap=1|nocat=1}}.
{{root|en|ar|ج ن ن}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-genie.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒiː.ni/}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːni|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|genii|s}}

# {{lb|en|Islam}} A [[jinn]], a [[being]] descended from the [[jann]], normally invisible to the human eye, but who may also appear in [[animal]] or [[human]] form.
# {{lb|en|mythological creature}} A fictional magical being that is typically bound to obey the commands of a mortal possessing its container.
#: {{ux|en|'''genie''' in a bottle}}

