===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|UK|military|slang}} A new [[recruit]] at {{w|Royal Military Academy Sandhurst}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1842|title=The United Service Magazine
|passage=I and the other "'''Johns'''," as I soon discovered all new-comers at Sandhurst were, and are still, styled, although at the time I was unconscious of it, managed to troop in after the A company, but although not two minutes after them, found all the different messes already seated and hard at work.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author=Verity McInnis|title=Women of Empire|passage=To avoid bullying, first-year “'''Johns'''” (from Johnny Raw) “fagged” for senior classmen known as “Regs.” Fagging included making beds, running messages, and smuggling contraband.}}
# {{label|en|US|slang|archaic}} {{alternative case form of|en|john|nodot=a}}: a [[toilet]], [[lavatory]], [[outhouse]], or [[chamber pot]].

====Synonyms====
* ''See'' '''[[Thesaurus:toilet]]''', '''[[Thesaurus:bathroom]]''', ''and'' '''[[Thesaurus:chamber pot]]'''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Cousin John}}

[[Category:en:Individuals]]

==Cebuano==

===Etymology===
From {{der|ceb|en|John}}, from {{der|ceb|enm|Johannes}}, {{m|enm|John}}, {{m|enm|Johan}}, from {{der|ceb|xno|Jehan}}, {{m|fro|Johan}}, from {{der|ceb|la|Iōhannēs}} (variant of {{m|la|Iōannēs}}), from New Testament Greek {{m|grc|Ἰωάννης}}, from {{der|ceb|hbo|-}} {{m|he|יוֹחָנָן|tr=Yōḥānān}}, perhaps contracted from a former {{m|he|יְהוֹחָנָן||God is gracious|tr=Yəhōḥānān}}.

===Proper noun===
{{head|ceb|proper noun}}

# {{given name|ceb|male|from=English < Hebrew}}

