==Arabic==
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From a {{bor|ar|ira-mid}} [[past participle]] {{m|und||āfrīd|t=created}}, originally an elliptic expression for {{m|und||*dīw afrīt|t=demon’s creation}}, or from the root {{ar-root|ع|ف|ر}} related to “ash”, compare for the derivation type {{m|ar|عَكْرُوت|t=scoundrel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عِفْرِيت}}
** {{a|ar|Moroccan}} {{ary-IPA|ʕafrīt}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj|عِفْرِيت|pl=عَفَارِيت|f=عِفْرِيتَة|fpl=عِفْرِيتَات}} {{tlb|ar|classical|formal|dialectal}}

# [[malicious]], [[mischievous]], [[wicked]], [[knave]]
# [[crafty]], [[cunning]], [[sly]], [[wily]]
# [[clever]], [[fast]], [[strong]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|عِفْرِيت|pl=عَفَارِيت}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|عِفْرِيت|m|pl=عَفَارِيت|f=عِفْرِيتَة}}

# [[afreet]], [[afrit]], [['afrit]], [[efreet]], [[ifreet]], [[ifrit]]; Supernatural being from Arabian folklore.
# [[demon]], [[devil]], [[fiend]], [[evil]] [[spirit]];  Any infernal being regardless of its morals.
#: {{synonyms|ar|شَيْطَان|مَارِد}}
# [[goblin]], [[sprite]], [[genie]], [[gremlin]], [[elf]]; Any supernatural being in general.
#: {{synonyms|ar|جَانّ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|عِفْرِيت|pl=عَفَارِيت}}

