==Vietnamese==

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
Claimed to be derived from {{ncog|km|យក្ខ}} or related to {{m|vi|trăn||python}}, {{m|vi|rắn||snake}}, or even {{ncog|ms|macan||tiger}} by various [[folk etymology|folk etymologies]].

More likely from a descendant of {{der|vi|ar|جن|tr=jinn}} or {{m|ar|جان|tr=jānn}}. Compare {{cog|cjm|ajin}}, {{cog|ms|jin}}.

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|cls=con|[[陳]], [[𤠶]]}}

# {{lb|vi|mythology}} a kind of [[monster]] in [[Vietnamese]] [[folklore]], arguably a [[yaksa]], a [[tiger]] monster or a [[snake]] monster
# {{lb|vi|Western|_|mythology}} [[ogre]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{vi-der|bà chằn|chằn tinh}}

===Etymology 2===
{{rfe|vi}}

====Verb====
{{vi-verb}}

# to [[widen]] and [[loosen]] something
#:{{syn|vi|nới}}

{{C|vi|Mythological creatures}}
