==Assyrian Neo-Aramaic==

===Etymology 1===
[[File:LocationGhana.png|thumb|{{lang|aii|ܓܢܐ}}]]
[[File:Flag of Ghana.svg|thumb|{{lang|aii|ܐܬܐ ܕܓܢܐ}}]]
{{intnat|aii}} from {{bor|aii|ar|غَانَا}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|aii|[ˈɣɑːnɑː]|a=Standard}}

====Proper noun====
{{aii-proper noun|ܓ݂ܵܢܵܐ|f}}

# {{place|aii|country|cont/Africa|t=Ghana}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|aii|ܓ݂ܵܢܵܝܵܐ|t=Ghanaian}}

===Etymology 2===
{{aii-root|ܓ ܢ ܐ}}
From {{inh|aii|arc|גְּנָא|tr=gənā}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|aii|[ˈɡɑːneː]|a=Standard}}

====Verb====
{{aii-verb|ܓܵܢܹܐ|prp=ܓܢܵܝܵܐ|pp=ܓܸܢܝܵܐ}}

# to [[lie down]], [[recline]]
# {{lb|aii|with {{m|aii|ܫܸܡܫܵܐ|t=sun}}}} (of the sun) to [[set]]
#: {{uxi|aii|ܗ݇ܘܹܐ ܠܵܗ̇ '''ܒܸܓܢܵܝܵܐ''' ܫܸܡܫܵܐ|t=The sun is '''setting'''.}}
# {{lb|aii|with {{m|aii|ܝܲܘܡܵܐ|t=day}}}} (of the day) to get [[late]], [[turn]] [[dark]], turn into [[evening]]
#: {{uxi|aii|'''ܓܢܹܐ ܠܹܗ''' ܝܲܘܡܵܐ|t=It '''got late'''.|lit=The day '''reclined'''.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{aii-conj-verb/A1|ܓ|ܢ|ܐ}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|aii|[ˈɡan.neː]|a=Standard}}

====Noun====
{{head|aii|noun form|head=ܓܲܢܹ̈ܐ|g=f-p}}

# {{inflection of|aii|ܓܲܢܬ݂ܵܐ||p|cons|t=garden, park}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{bor|aii|kmr|giyan|گيان|tr=giyan}}; related to {{cog|fa|جان|tr=jân}}. The sense of “self, oneself” is a calque of the original word {{m|aii|ܪܘܼܚܵܐ}}, where this sense is not found in the Kurdish source word.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|aii|ܓܝܵܢܵܐ}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|aii|[ɡɑːnɑː]|a=Standard}}
* {{IPA|aii|[ɡjɑːnɑː]|a=Nineveh Plains}}
* {{IPA|aii|[d͡ʒɑːnɑː]|a=Urmian}}

====Noun====
{{aii-noun|ܓܵܢܵܐ|f|pl=ܓܵܢܹ̈ܐ|pl2=ܓܵܢܵܬ݂ܹ̈ܐ}}

# {{lb|aii|dialectal}} [[self]], [[oneself]], [[same]]
#: {{syn|aii|ܢܲܦ̮ܫܵܐ|ܝܵܬ݂ܵܐ|ܩܢܘܿܡܵܐ|ܪܘܼܚܵܐ}}
# {{lb|aii|dialectal}} [[spirit]]
#: {{syn|aii|ܪܘܼܚܵܐ}}

=====Inflection=====
{{aii-infl-noun-m-fempl|ܓܵܢ|ܓܵܢ}}

{{cln|aii|nouns with irregular gender}}
