==Turkish==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|tr|ota|جان هولیله|tr=can havliyle}},<ref>{{R:ota:Sami:1899|467|جان هولیله}}</ref> from {{m|ota|جان|tr=cān, can}} and {{m|ota|هول|tr=havl, havil}},<ref>{{R:tr:Nişanyan|can}}</ref><ref>{{R:tr:Nişanyan|havil}}</ref> equivalent to {{af|tr|can<gloss:life, soul, heart>|hevl<alt:havl><gloss:fright, terror>|-i<pos:possessive suffix>|-yle|lit=with terror for (one's) life/soul}}, or {{m|tr|can}} + {{m|tr|havli}} + {{m|tr|ile}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|tr|/ˈd͡ʒan.hav.lij.le/}}
* {{hyphenation|tr|can|hav|liy|le}}

===Adverb===
{{tr-adv}}

# Out of [[fear]] for one's life, [[for dear life]], [[desperately]].

====Related terms====
{{rel3|tr|candan|canla başla|babacan|cana yakın|can yoldaşı|canciğer}}

