==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology===
Possibly a reduced form of {{m|gd|nuair|t=when}} (MacBain)<ref>{{R:MacBain|head=dar|page=123}}</ref> or possibly from early modern ''an tan a, an dan a'', from {{inh|gd|sga|in tan|t=when}} from acc. sg. of {{der|gd|sga|tan|t=time}} (Seosamh Watson).<ref>{{R:ga:SnaG|chapter=9|page=690|section=§19.5|text=Ar chónaisc neamhaithnidiúla eile a áirítear i nGaeilge na hAlban tá (…) /ə/,/də/, /dər/, /dər ə/ (? < ''an tan a'') ‘nuair’}}</ref> <!-- Possibly also related to {{m|sga|dia|dïa|t=when}} + the augment -ro-, cf. Irish ''lá dá rabhas, dár éirgheas''? No sources deriving it from there though. -->

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gd|/t̪ər/|/t̪ar/}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|gd|conjunctions}}

# {{lb|gd|Ross-shire|Inverness-shire|Mull|Perthshire}} [[when]] {{gl|relative/non-interrogative}}
#: {{syn|gd|nuair}}
#* {{quote-book|gd|author=Roy G. Wentworth|title=Rannsachadh air Fòn-eòlas Dualchainnt Ghàidhlig Gheàrrloch, Siorrachd Rois|year=2005|page=3|url=https://www.dias.ie/celt/celt-publications-2/celt-gaidhlig-ghearrloch/|text=Bha sinne air na cuairteachdainn leis a’ Ghàidhlig '''dar a''' bha sinn nana cloinn|t=We had been surrounded with Gaelic '''when''' we were children}}

