==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪl.dɪŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-building.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-building.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪldɪŋ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|build|ing}}

===Etymology 1===
[[File:Fotothek df roe-neg 0006285 033 Blick auf die Wohnbauten Straße der III. Weltfes.jpg|thumb|white '''buildings''' in Leipzig]]
From {{inh|en|enm|byldynge}}, {{m|enm|buyldyng}}, {{m|enm|byldyng}}, {{m|enm|buldynge}}, {{m|enm|buldyng}}, {{m|enm|boldyng}}, equivalent to {{af|en|build|-ing|id2=gerund noun}}. Compare also related {{cog|enm|bold|t=edifice, castle, mansion}}, from {{cog|ang|bold|t=building, dwelling, house}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The act or process by which something is [[build|built]]; [[construction]].
#: {{syn|en|construction}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''building''' of the bridge will be completed in a couple of weeks.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A closed [[structure]] with [[wall]]s and a [[roof]].
#: {{syn|en|edifice|Thesaurus:building}}
#: {{ux|en|My sister lives in that apartment '''building'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-19|author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/marktran Mark Tran]
|volume=189|issue=6|page=1|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2013/jul/12/war-denying-children-education Denied an education by war]
|passage=One particularly damaging, but often ignored, effect of conflict on education is the proliferation of attacks on schools{{...}}as children, teachers or school '''buildings''' become the targets of attacks.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=@thepunbible|work=w:Twitter|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/2ByK2|archivedate=28 June 2024|url=https://x.com/thepunbible/status/1787486593437012233|date=6 May 2024|passage=[[why|Why]] [[doesn't]] [[Italy]] [[finish]] [[their]] '''buildings'''}}
# {{lb|en|math}} {{syn of|en|Tits building}}

