{{also|Appendix:Variations of "ed"}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|-d}} {{qualifier|now standard only after ''-e''}}
* {{l|en|-'d}} {{qualifier|chiefly {{l|en|poetry}}}}
* {{l|en|-èd}} {{qualifier|chiefly {{l|en|poetry}}}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|in verbs, past participles, and some denominal adjectives}}
** {{qualifier|after a vowel or a [[voiced]] consonant other than a {{IPAchar|/d/}}}} {{enPR|d}}, {{IPA|en|/d/}}
** {{qualifier|after a [[voiceless]] consonant other than a {{IPAchar|/t/}}}} {{enPR|t}}, {{IPA|en|/t/}}
** {{qualifier|after a {{IPAchar|/d/}} or {{IPAchar|/t/}}}} same as below
* {{sense|other denominal adjectives}}
** {{enPR|ĭd|a=UK}}, {{IPA|en|/ɪd/}}
** {{enPR|ĭd|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ɪd/}} ''or'' {{enPR|əd}}, {{IPA|en|/əd/}}
** {{enPR|əd|a=AU}}, {{IPA|en|/əd/}}

{{rel-top|Other dialects}}
* {{a|en|HK}} 
** {{q|after a {{IPAchar|/d/}} or {{IPAchar|/t/}}}} {{IPA|en|/əd/}}
** {{q|after vowels}} {{IPA|en|/d/|/dəd/}}
** {{q|after other consonants}} {{IPA|en|/dəd/}}
{{rel-bottom}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|verb-past-tense}}
From {{inh|en|enm|-ede}}, {{m|enm|-eden}}, from {{inh|en|ang||-ode}}, {{m|ang||-odon|pos=class 2 weak past ending}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*-ōd-}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-ōdēdun}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|-ede|t=-ed|pos=first person singular past indicative ending}}, {{cog|sv|-ade|t=-ed}}, {{cog|is|-aði|t=-ed}}.

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{n-g|Used to form [[past tense]]s of (regular) [[verb]]s. In linguistics, it is used for the base form of any past form. See ''[[-t]]'' for a variant.}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|point|pointed}}
#: {{ux|en|He point'''ed''' at the dog.}}

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|past tense}}
* Dzongkha: {{t|dz|ཅི}}
* Esperanto: {{t+|eo|-is}}
* Hungarian: {{t|hu|[[-t]]/[[-tt]]/[[-ott]]/[[-ett]]/[[-ött]]}}
* Japanese: {{t|ja|-た|tr=-ta}}
* Norwegian:
*: Bokmål: {{t+|nb|-a|}}, {{t+|nb|-et}}, {{t|nb|-te}}, {{t|nb|-de}}, {{t|nb|-dd}}, {{t|nb|-tt}}, {{t|nb|-tø}}, {{t|nb|-øt}}, {{t|nb|-øyt}}
*: Nynorsk: {{t|nn|-a}}, {{t|nn|-te}}, {{t|nn|-de}}, {{t|nn|-dd}}, {{t|nn|-tt}}, {{t|nn|-aut}}
* Persian: {{t+|fa|ـده|tr=-de}}, {{t+|fa|ـد|tr=-d}}, {{t+|fa|ـته|tr=-te}}, {{t+|fa|ـت|tr=-t}}
* Polish: {{t|pl|-ł}}
* Russian: {{t+|ru|-л|m}}, {{t+|ru|-ла|f}}, {{t+|ru|-ло|n}}, {{t+|ru|-ли|p}}
* Spanish: {{t+|es|-ado}}
* Swedish: {{t+|sv|-de}}, {{t+|sv|-t}}
* Ukrainian: {{t|uk|-в|m}}, {{t|uk|-ла|f}}, {{t|uk|-ло|n}}, {{t|uk|-ли|p}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymon|en|id=past participle|inh|enm>-ed>past participle}}
From {{inh|en|enm|-ed}}, from {{inh|en|ang||-od|pos=class 2 weak past participle}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*-ōdaz}}.

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix|cat2=inflectional suffixes}}

# {{n-g|Used to form [[past participle]]s of (regular) [[verb]]s. See ''[[-en]]'' and ''[[-t]]'' for variants.}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|point|pointed}}
#: {{ux|en|He has point'''ed''' at the dog.}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|en|adjective}}
From {{inh|en|enm|-ed}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-od||pos=adjective suffix}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*-ōdaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*-eh₂tos}}. While identical in appearance to the past participle of class 2 weak verbs, this suffix was attached directly to nouns without any intervening verb. Cognate with {{cog|la|-ātus}} (whence also a {{glossary|doublet}} {{m|en|-ate}}).

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes}}

# {{senseid|en|having}}{{non-gloss definition|Used to form [[possessional adjective]]s from [[noun]]s, in the sense of having the object represented by the noun.}}
#: {{ant|en|-less}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|point|pointed}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|horn|horned}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|hoof|hooved}}
# {{senseid|en|having-compound}} {{non-gloss definition|As an extension of the above, used to form possessional adjectives from adjective-noun pairs.}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|red|hair|red-haired}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|left|hand|left-handed}}
#: {{suffixusex|en|two|[[prong|prong(s)]]|two-pronged}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|en}}

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|having an object}}
* Dutch: {{t+|nl|-ig}}, {{t+|nl|ge- -d}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|-kas}}
* Hungarian: {{t|hu|[[-s]]/[[-os]]/[[-as]]/[[-es]]/[[-ös]]}}
* Indonesian: {{t+|id|ber-}}
* Japanese: {{t+|ja|気味|tr=kimi}}
* Malay: {{t+|ms|ber-}}
* Persian: {{t+|fa|ـدار|tr=-dâr}}
* Swedish: {{t+|sv|-ig}}, {{t+|sv|-ad}}
{{trans-bottom}}

{{trans-top|having an object of a particular quality}}
* Dutch: {{t+|nl|-ig}}, also as a past participle: {{t+|nl|ge-}} + {{t+|nl|-d}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|-nen}}
* Hungarian: {{t|hu|[[-ú]]/[[-ű]]/[[-jú]]/[[-jű]]}}
