==Welsh==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*-hed}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*-isetos}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|cy|/ɛd/|a=cy-N,standard,colloquial}}
** {{IPA|cy|/ad/|a=cy-N,colloquial}}
* {{IPA|cy|/ɛd/|a=cy-S}}

====Suffix====
{{head|cy|suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Forms an [[equative]] of an adjective of one or two syllables.}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|gwan|t1=weak|gwanned|t2=as weak}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|rhad|t1=cheap|rhated|t2=as cheap}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|cynt|t1=faster, earlier, sooner|cynted|t2=as fast, as early, as soon}}

=====Usage notes=====
Causes [[fortition]] of final voiced consonant of adjectival roots.

===Etymology 2===
Reduced form of {{m|cy|-fed}}. Cognate with {{cog|kw|-es}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|cy|/ɛd/|a=cy-N,standard,colloquial}}
** {{IPA|cy|/ad/|a=cy-N,colloquial}}
* {{IPA|cy|/ɛd/|a=cy-S}}

