==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡæləʊz/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡæloʊz/|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡæləs/|a=now dialectal}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-gallows.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æləʊz|q1=UK|æloʊz|q2=US|æləs|q3=now dialectal|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|galwes}}, {{m|enm|galewes}}, plural of {{m|enm|galwe}}, {{m|enm|galowe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gealga}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*galgō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*galgô}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰalgʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰalg-||long switch, rod, shaft, pole, perch}}. The plural construction probably refers to the vertical and horizontal beams.

Compare {{cog|fy|galge}}, {{cog|nl|galg}}, {{cog|de|Galgen}}, {{cog|da|galge}}, {{cog|is|gálgi}}.

For the pronunciation {{IPAchar|/ˈɡæləs/}}, compare {{m|en|bellows}}, {{m|en|bodice}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|gallows|+|pl2qual=rare}}

# Wooden [[framework]] on which persons are put to death by [[hanging]]. {{defdate|from 1300s}} [[Category:en:Capital punishment]]
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1728
|chapter=The Atheist, or, the Second Part of the Solider's Fortune
|title=The Works of Mr. Thomas Otway
|volume=2
|author=w:Thomas Otway
|location=London
|page=37
|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=yF1AAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA37
|passage=No, Sir, 'tis fear of Hanging. Who would not ſteal, or do Murder, every time his Fingers itch'd at it, were it not for fear of the '''Gallows'''?
}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|obsolete}} A [[wretch]] who deserves to be hanged.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1590
|author=w:William Shakespeare
|title=s:Love's Labour's Lost
|passage=Ay, and a shrewd unhappy '''gallows''' too. / You'll ne'er be friends with him: a' kill'd your sister.
}}
# {{lb|en|printing|obsolete}} The [[rest]] for the [[tympan]] when raised.
# {{lb|en|colloquial|obsolete}} [[suspenders|Suspenders]]; [[braces]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1882|author=George William Sheldon|title=The Story of the Volunteer Fire Department of the City of New York|page=67
|passage=The last pair of "'''gallowses'''" made by Mr. Gratacap was an order from Mr. Brokaw, the clothier.}}
# Any contrivance with posts and [[crossbeam]] for suspending objects.
#* '''1971''', Mario Puzo, Francis Ford Coppola, ''The Godfather'' (screenplay, third draft)
#*: Lit by the moonlight through the window, he can see a FIGURE in the hospital bed alone in the room, and under a transparent oxygen tent. {{...}} Tubes hang from a steel '''gallows''' beside the bed, and run to his nose and mouth.
# The main frame of a [[beam engine]].

=====Synonyms=====
