==Old Persian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|peo|ira-pro|*dāráyati}}, from {{inh|peo|iir-pro|*dʰāráyati}}, from {{inh|peo|ine-pro|*dʰer-|*dʰoréyeti|to hold}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|धारयति}}, {{cog|la|firmus}} and {{cog|lt|derė́ti}}.

===Verb===
{{head|peo|verb|ts=dārayatiy}}

# to [[hold]], [[have]]
#* Inscription of the [[w:Ariaramnes of Persia|Ariaramnes]], at [[w:Hamedan|Hamadan]] (AmH), on a gold tablet, lines 4-7
#*: {{lang|peo|sc=Xpeo|𐏐 𐎴𐎱𐎠 𐏐 𐎰𐎠𐎫𐎡𐎹 𐏐 𐎠𐎼𐎡𐎹𐎠𐎼𐎶𐎴 𐏐 𐎧𐏁𐎠𐎹𐎰𐎡𐎹}}
#*: {{lang|peo|sc=Xpeo|𐏐 𐎡𐎹𐎶 𐏐 𐎭𐏃𐎹𐎠𐎢𐏁 𐏐 𐎱𐎠𐎼𐎿𐎠 𐏐 𐎫𐎹 𐏐 𐎠𐎭𐎶 𐏐 '''𐎭𐎠𐎼𐎹𐎠𐎷𐎡𐎹'''}}
#*: {{lang|peo|sc=Xpeo|𐏐 𐏃𐎹 𐏐 𐎢𐎺𐎿𐎱𐎠 𐏐 𐎢𐎶𐎼𐎫𐎡𐎹𐎠 𐏐 𐎶𐎴𐎠 𐏐 𐎲𐎥}}
#*: {{lang|peo|sc=Xpeo|[𐏐] 𐎺𐏀𐎼𐎣 𐏐 𐎠𐎢𐎼𐎶𐏀𐎭𐎠 𐏐 𐎳𐎼𐎠𐎲[𐎼 𐏐] 𐎺𐏁𐎴𐎠}}
#*:: : n-p-a : ϑ-a-t-i-y : a-r-i-y-a-r-m-n : x-š-a-y-ϑ-i-y
#*:: : i-y-m : d-h-y-a-u-š : p-a-r-s-a : t-y : a-d-m : '''d-a-r-y-a-mi-i-y'''
#*:: : h-y : u-v-s-p-a : u-m-r-t-i-y-a : m-n-a : b-g
#*:: [:] v-z-r-k : a-u-r-m-z-d-a : f-r-a-b-[r :] v-š-n-a
#*::: : napā : ϑātiy : Ariyāramna : xšāyaϑiya
#*::: : iyam : dahyāuš : Pārsā : tya : adam : '''dārayāmiy'''
#*::: : hya : uvaspā : umartiyā : manā : baga
#*::: : vazraka : Auramazdā : frābara : vašnā
#*:::: Ariaramnes the King says: This country Persia which '''I hold''', which is possessed of good horses, of good men, the Great God Ahuramazda bestowed it upon me.

