{{ar-verb|Iq}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[roll]], to [[trundle]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|Iq}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|تَدَحْرَجَ}}

==Egyptian Arabic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|arz|دَقْلِج|tr1=daʔlig}}

===Etymology===
Dissimilated from {{m|arz|دَحْدَر|tr=daḥdar}}, {{m|arz|دَعْدَر|tr=daʕdar}} – juxtapose with {{cog|apd|دَرْدَق|tr=dardaɡ}} –, from {{m|arz|دَرْدَر|tr=dardar}}, from well-known {{der|arz|ar|دَرَّ}}, which is from {{m|ar|دَارَ}} of manifest Semitic inheritance.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|arz|/daħraɡ/}}

===Verb===
{{head|arz|verb|tr=dahrag|head=دَحْرَج|{{ar-form|Iq|nocap=1}}||noun|دَحْرَجَة|f2tr=daḥraga}}

# {{lb|arz|transitive}} to [[trundle]], to [[roll]]
# {{lb|arz|transitive|nautical}} to [[parbuckle]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|arz|اِتْدَحْرَج|tr=itdaḥrag}}, {{l|arz|اِدَّحْرَج|tr=iddaḥrag|t={{lb|arz|intransitive|nocat=1}} to roll}}
* {{l|arz|دُحْرِيج|tr=duḥrīg|t=dry earth with which cereals are mixed; common vetch which occurs as an impurity in cereals}}

