==Sanskrit==

===Alternative scripts===
{{sa-alt}}

===Pronunciation===
{{sa-IPA|a=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|sa|ine-pro|*dʰerh₃-}}
From {{inh|sa|inc-pro|*dʰā́raH}}, from {{inh|sa|iir-pro|*dʰā́raH}}, from {{inh|sa|ine-pro||*dʰórh₃-eh₂}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*dʰerh₃-||to leap, spring}}. Cognate with {{cog|ae|𐬛𐬁𐬭𐬁}}, {{cog|ang|daru}} (whence {{cog|en|dere}}). Compare also {{cog|en|dart}}, ultimately from {{cog|frk|*darōþu}}.

An alternative theory espoused by Lubotsky and Mayrhofer derives the word from {{inh|sa|ine-pro||*dʰṇh₂-reh₂}}, from {{der|sa|ine-pro|*dʰenh₂-|t=to set in motion, flow}} and thus cognate to {{m|sa|धन्|t=to move, run}}.<ref name=EWAia>{{R:sa:EWAia|vol=1|pages=788-9}}</ref><ref name=IAIL>{{R:inc:IAIL}}</ref>

Possibly related to {{cog|fa|[[درد#Etymology_2|درد]]|tr=dord|t=dregs}}.<ref>{{R:ira:ESIJa|vol=2|page=356}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{sa-noun|g=f|tr=dhā́rā}}<ref>{{R:MW|515/3}}</ref><ref>{{R:CDIAL|dhāˊrā|6793}}</ref>

# [[stream]] or [[current]] of [[water]]
# [[flood]], [[gush]], [[jet]], [[drop]] (of any [[liquid]]), [[shower]], [[rain]] (also figuratively of [[arrows]], [[flowers]], etc.)
# [[current]], [[torrent]]
# a [[leak]] or [[hole]] in a [[pitcher]] etc.
# the [[pace]] of [[horse]]
# [[uniformity]], [[sameness]] (as of [[flowing]] [[water]])
# [[custom]], [[usage]]
# [[continuous]] [[line]] or [[series]]
# {{lb|sa|figuratively}} [[family]] [[line]]

