==Persian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=srdʾl|ts=sālār}}, a pre-Middle Persian compound of {{m|pal|𐭫𐭥𐭩𐭱𐭤|tr=LOYŠE|ts=sar|t=head}} + {{m|pal|tr=-dʾr|ts=-dār|t=-holder, -keeper}}, with the regular phonetic shift *sar(a)-dàr(a)- > *sardàr > *sarlàr > sālār. Compare {{m|fa|دل|tr=del}}, {{m|fa|گل|tr=gol}} for the phonetic change. Note {{cog|xcl|սաղար}}, an Iranian borrowing. {{doublet|fa|سردار|tr1=sardâr}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|sā`lār}}
* {{rhymes|fa|ɑːr|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=sâlâr|pl=سالار‌ها|pl2=سالاران}}

# [[leader]]
# military [[commander]]
# {{label|fa|dated}} [[hakim]], [[king]]

