Page 159 دارفلفل: -------- begin text --------
==Arabic==
{{wp|lang=ar|دار فلفل|دارفلفل}}
[[File:Piper longum kz01.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|دَارْفِلْفِل}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
{{univerbation|ar|[[دَار]] [[فِلْفِل]]}}, {{m|ar|[[دَار]] [[ال]][[فِلْفِل]]|t=house of pepper}}, originally denoting “the whole house of pepper-like spices”. The similarity to {{noncog|fa|دار|tr=dâr|t=tree}} is coincidental, and in Persian, {{m|fa|دارفلفل|tr=dârfelfel}} is used less often than the Arabic, because of the existence of other words for this item in Persian, and the sometimes mentioned form {{m|fa||دارپلپل|tr=dârpelpel}} is rare.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَارْفِلْفِل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَارْفِلْفِل|m}}

# [[long pepper]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَارْفِلْفِل}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|bor=1|axm|դարիպղպեղ|դարապղպեղ}}
* {{desc|fa|دارفلفل|tr=dârfelfel|bor=1|alts=1}}
* {{desctree|ota|دارفلفل|tr=dar-ı filfil|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Biruni|vol=IV|page=439}}
* {{R:xcl:AG|page=138}}
* {{R:ar:Venzlaff|page=78, footnote 83}}

==Ottoman Turkish==
[[File:Nieuhof-Description-générale-de-la-Chine-1665 0866.tif|thumb|right|{{lang|ota|دارفلفل}}|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ota|دار فلفل|tr1=dar-fülfül, dar-filfil, dar-ı fülfül, dar-ı filfil}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ota|ar|دَارْفِلْفِل}}.

===Noun===
{{ota-noun|tr=darfülfül, darfilfil}}

# [[long pepper]]

====Descendants====
* {{desc|tr|darülfülfül|darıfülfül|darifülfül}}
* {{desc|bor=1|bg|дарфирфи́р|дар-фирфи́р|дара́-фирфир}} {{q|дарѣ́-фирфир}}, {{l|bg|дара́-фирфил}}

