{{topics|hy|Military|People}}

==Old Armenian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|xcl|հրամատար}}

===Etymology===
An {{bor|xcl|ira}} borrowing: compare {{cog|peo|tr=framātar|t=master, lord}}, {{cog|pal||tr=plmʾtʾl|ts=framādār|t=commander, ruler, chief|sc=Phlv}}. For the constituents see {{cog|xcl|հրամայեմ}}, {{m|xcl|հրաման}} and {{cog|fa|ـدار|tr=-dâr}}. The form {{m|xcl||հրամանատար}} is either a folk-etymological reshaping of {{m|xcl|հրամատար}} as {{affix|xcl|հրաման|-ա-|տանիմ|t1=command|alt3=-տար|t3=to carry|nocat=1}} or is borrowed from a parallel Iranian form: compare {{cog|sog|tr=frmʾndʾr|ts=framāndār|t=governor, tutor|sc=Syrc}}, {{cog|fa|فرماندار|tr=farmândâr|t=governor}}.

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun}}

# [[ruler]], [[governor]]

====Declension====
{{xcl-noun-ի-ա}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|xcl|հրամանատարություն}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|xcl|հրաման}}, {{l|xcl|հրամայեմ}}
* {{l|xcl|հրապարակ}}
* {{l|xcl|սաղար}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|hy|հրամանատար|bor=1}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:xcl:HAB}}
* {{R:xcl:NHB}}
* {{R:ira:Iranica|FRAMADĀR|year=2000|author=Chaumont, Marie-Louise|url=http://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/framadar}}
* {{R:xcl:AG|page=182}}
* {{R:xcl:Meyer|page=16}}
* {{R:xcl:Bedr}}

{{topics|xcl|People|Government}}
