==Moroccan Arabic==

===Etymology===
From {{af|ary|دار|tr1=dār|t1=[[house]]|[[بيض|بيضا]]|tr2=bayḍa|t2=[[white]]}}: a [[calque]] of the original {{calque|ary|pt|-|notext=1}} name {{m|pt|casa|Casa}} {{m|pt|branco|Branca}} ("White House"), changed to [[Casablanca]] when the Spanish assumed control of the city.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ary-IPA|ed-dār el-bayḍa|ed-dār el-bīḍa}}

===Proper noun===
{{ary-proper noun|g=f|head=الدار البَيْضا|tr=ed-dār el-bayḍa|head2=الدار البِيضا|tr2=ed-dār el-bīḍa}}

# {{tcl|ary|Casablanca|id=Q7903}}
#: {{syn|ary|كازابلانكا|tr=kāzablanka|كازا|tr2=kāza}}
