Page 171 سقم: Skipped, no changes
Page 171 سقم: -------- begin text --------
==Arabic==
{{ar-rootbox|س ق م}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَقَم}}
* {{ar-IPA|سُقْم}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَقَم|m|head2=سُقْم|pl=أَسْقَام}}

# [[sickness]], [[disease]], [[illness]]
#: {{syn|ar|مَرَض}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=1377 {{C.E.}}|author=w:en:Ibn Khaldun|title=تاريخ ابن خلدون|publisher=Dar Al-Fikr|location=Beirut|edition=1st|year_published=1981|volume=1|page=386|passage=وَٱنْصِبْ لِمَرْضَى الْمُسْلِمِين دُورًا تَأْوِيهِمْ وَقُوَّامًا يَرْفِقُونَ بِهِمْ وَأَطِبَّاءَ يُعَالِجُونَ {{quoted term|أَسْقَامَهُمْ}} وَأَسْعِفْهُمْ بِشَهَوَاتِهِمْ مَا لَمْ يُؤَدِّ ذٰلِكَ إِلَى إِسْرَافٍ فِي بَيْتِ الْمَالِ.|translation= Set up houses for Muslims who are ill, to shelter them. (Appoint) attendants in these houses who will handle them kindly, and (appoint) physicians who will treat {{quoted term|their diseases}}. Comply with their desires so long as it does not lead to waste in the treasury.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَقَم|head2=سُقْم|pl=أَسْقَام}}

==Moroccan Arabic==
{{ary-rootbox|س ق م}}

===Etymology===
A secondary form from اسْتَقَام from the root {{ar-root|ق و م}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ary-IPA|saqqam}}

===Verb===
{{ary-verb|II|head=سقّم|tr=saqqam|np=يسقّم|nptr=ysaqqam}}

# to [[fix]]
#: {{syn|ary|صلح|tr1=ṣlaḥ|صلّح|tr2=ṣallaḥ|عدّل|tr3=ʕaddal|صوّب|tr4=ṣawwab|صاوب|tr5=ṣāweb|صايب|tr6=ṣāyib}}
# to [[do]]
#: {{syn|ary|دار|tr1=dār|عمل|tr2=ʕmal}}

====Conjugation====
{{ary-conj-faʕʕal-yfaʕʕal|س|ق|م|s|q|m}}
