Page 1 give: Skipped, no changes
Page 1 give: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{slim-wikipedia}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰebʰ-}}
From {{der|en|enm|given}}, from {{der|en|non|gefa||to give}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*gebaną||to give}}. Merged with native Middle English {{m|enm|yiven}}, {{m|enm|ȝeven}}, from {{der|en|ang|ġiefan}}, from the same Proto-Germanic source (compare the obsolete inherited English {{glossary|doublet}} {{doublet|en|yive|notext=1}}).

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|gĭv}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡɪv/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-give.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-to give.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪv|s=1}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb|gives|giving|gave|given}}

# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To [[move]], [[shift]], [[provide]] something abstract or concrete to someone or something or somewhere.
## To [[transfer]] one's possession or holding of (something) to (someone).
##: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:give}}
##: {{ant|en|get|obtain|receive|take}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' him my coat.}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' my coat to the beggar.}}
##: {{ux|en|When they asked, I '''gave''' my coat.}}
## To make a [[present]] or [[gift]] of.
##: {{ux|en|I'm going to '''give''' my wife a necklace for her birthday.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''gave''' a pair of shoes to her husband for their anniversary.}}
## To [[pledge]].
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' him my word that I'd protect his children.}}
## To [[provide]] (something) to (someone), to [[allow]] or [[afford]].
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' them permission to miss tomorrow's class.}}
##: {{ux|en|Please '''give''' me some more time.}}
## To cause (a sensation or feeling) to exist in (the specified person, or the target, audience, etc).
##: {{ux|en|It '''gives''' me a lot of pleasure to be here tonight.}}
##: {{ux|en|The fence '''gave''' me an electric shock.}}
##: {{ux|en|My mother-in-law '''gives''' me nothing but grief.}}
##: {{ux|en|it's '''giving''' me bad vibes — It's '''giving''' me old Hollywood (vibes)}}
##* {{quote-book|en|date=2023-02-21|author=Lakita Wilson|title=Last Chance Dance|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9780593525630|page=81
|text="The outfit is '''giving''' me eighties fitness video vibes, but you wear it well." }}
## {{lb|en|slang|transitive}} To [[give off#Verb|give off]] (a certain [[vibe#Noun|vibe]] or [[appearance#Noun|appearance]]). {{defdate|2019?&ndash;}} {{q|Compare {{m|en|giving}}.}}
##: {{ux|en|it's '''giving''' old Hollywood (vibes)}}
##* {{quote-web|en|date=2022-10-25|author=Medina Azaldin; ELLE Beauty Team|title=30 Halloween Nail Art Trends To Get You In The Mood For Trick Or Treat|passage=[subtitle:] It's '''giving''' Wednesday Addams at the salon... }}
##* {{quote-journal|en|author=Sophie Williams|title=Kylie Jenner is giving Marilyn Monroe vibes in her latest Instagram post|work=[[w:Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]]|url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/fashion/a44033747/kylie-jenner-marilyn-monroe-vibes/|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/PowwP|archivedate=10 September 2023|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher={{w|Hearst Communications}}|date=30 May 2023|issn=0010-9541|oclc=1770745|passage=It's '''giving''' old Hollywood}}
##* {{RQ:NYT|author=Wilson Wong|title=Gov Ball Raves on in Pink, Amid Rain and Smoke|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/06/12/style/governors-ball-weather.html|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/lf7mP|archivedate=12 June 2023|date=12 June 2023|passage=Your outfit is '''giving''' more romance than bloodshed. Are you currently in love?}}
##* {{quote-web|en|author=Rachel Krause|quotee=Gabby Ragsdale|title=4 Students On The Back-To-School Outfits They're Shopping Their Closets For|work={{w|Refinery29}}|url=https://www.refinery29.com/en-us/sustainable-fall-school-outfits|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/BgeIc|archivedate=10 September 2023|date=20 July 2023|passage=This outfit '''gives''' 'college girl that knows what she's doing' and even though I am the furthest from that, I'll take it.}}
## To [[carry out]] (a physical interaction) with (something).
##: {{ux|en|I want to '''give''' you a kiss.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''gave''' him a hug.}}
##: {{ux|en|I'd like to '''give''' the tire a kick.}}
##: {{ux|en|I '''gave''' the boy a '''push''' on the swing.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''gave''' me a wink afterwards, so I knew she was joking.}}
##* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|page=68|passage=Then came a maid with hand-bag and shawls, and after her a tall young lady. She stood for a moment holding her skirt above the grimy steps, with something of the stately pose which Richter has '''given''' his Queen Louise on the stairway,{{...}}.}}
## To pass (something) into (someone's hand, etc.).
##: {{ux|en|'''Give''' me your hand.}}
##: {{ux|en|On entering the house, he '''gave''' his coat to the doorman.}}
## To cause (a disease or condition) in, or to transmit (a disease or condition) to.
##: {{ux|en|My boyfriend '''gave''' me chlamydia.}}
##: {{ux|en|He was convinced that it was his alcoholism that '''gave''' him cancer.}}
##* {{RQ:Temple Miscellanea|part=3|page=331|passage=Study '''gives''' strength to the mind; conversation, grace: the first apt to '''give''' stiffness, the other suppleness: one '''gives''' substance and form to the statue, the other polishes it.}}
## To provide or [[administer]] (a [[medication]])
##: {{ux|en|The doctors '''gave''' me morphine for the pain.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provide]], as, a [[service]] or a [[broadcast]].
#: {{ux|en|They're '''giving''' my favorite show!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|title=Business Law Today
|text=We hope that the need to "'''give''' good e-mail" in response to questions from clients and potential clients will in fact induce firms to get serious about storing and reusing their expertise – and even become open to tailoring {{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Iain Aitken|title=Value-Driven IT Management: Commercializing the IT Function|page=153
|passage={{...}}who did not have a culture in which ''''giving''' good presentation' and successfully playing the internal political game was the way up.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Christopher Matthew Spencer|title=The Ebay Entrepreneur|page=248
|passage=A friendly voice on the phone welcoming prospective new clients is a must. Don't underestimate the importance of '''giving''' good "phone".}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2012-01-01|author=George Zinkan|title=Advertising Research: The Internet, Consumer Behavior, and Strategy|publisher=Marketing Classics Press|isbn=9781613112717|page=28
|text=Social skills are required to meet new people in a chat room and maintain contact over time (“Do you '''give''' good e-mail?”). The Internet provides people with an opportunity to reinvent or misrepresent themselves.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2016-11-25|author=Gabrielle Jamela Hosein; Lisa Outar|title=Indo-Caribbean Feminist Thought: Genealogies, Theories, Enactments|publisher=Springer|isbn=9781137559371|page=54
|text=He '''gives''' good face too, posing for the camera with hands on waist, eyes forward, legs crossed (Fig. 4.1).}}
# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To [[estimate]] or [[predict]] (a duration or probability) for (something).
#: {{ux|en|I '''give''' it ten minutes before he gives up.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'd '''give''' it a 95% chance of success.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll '''give''' their marriage six months.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[yield]] or [[collapse]] under pressure or force.
#: {{syn|en|give way|bend|cede|flex|move|yield}}
#: {{ant|en|resist}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Lincoln at Gettysburg|chapter=prologue|author=w:Garry Wills|page=21|year=1992|passage=A soldier noticed how earth "'''gave'''" as he walked over the shallow trenches.}}
#: {{ux|en|One pillar '''gave''', then more, and suddenly the whole floor pancaked onto the floor below.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[lead]] (onto or into).
#: {{ux|en|The master bedroom '''gives''' onto a spacious balcony.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2022-02-03|author=Terry Marsh|title=Walking the Dales Way: Ilkley to Bowness-on-Windermere through the Yorkshire Dales|publisher=Cicerone Press Limited|isbn=9781783628759
|text=Beyond the stile stands an attractive row of riverside trees – alder, hazel, beech, hawthorn and ash. Go across to the far corner of a field, where a through-stile '''gives''' onto a small, lightly wooded hill,{{nb...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|dated}} To provide a [[view]] of. <!--W1913-->
#: ''His window '''gave''' the park.''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Pierre Lagayette|title=Nature et progrès: interactions, exclusions, mutations|publisher=Presses Paris Sorbonne|isbn=9782840503880|page=61
|text=Columbus dwellers of Woodland Meadow Apts may not find themselves in a perfectly bucolic setting, as the residential complex '''gives''' onto a military defense logistics ground.}}
# To [[exhibit]] as a product or result; to produce; to [[yield]].
#: ''The number of men, divided by the number of ships, '''gives''' four hundred to each ship.''
# To cause; to make; used with the infinitive.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|II|viii|page=171|passage=But there the duke was '''given''' to understand&nbsp;/ That in a gondola were seen together&nbsp;/ Lorenzo and his amorous Jessica.}}
# To cause (someone) to have; produce in (someone); [[effectuate]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1997|author=Jim Smoke|title=How a Man Measures Success|page=82|passage="Can do" gives me a choice, while "should do" '''gives''' me a complex.}}
# To allow or admit by way of supposition; to [[concede]].
#: {{syn|en|allow|concede|grant}}
#: ''He can be bad-tempered, I'll '''give''' you that, but he's a hard worker.''
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=2|page=39|passage=I '''give''' not heaven for lost.|year=1873}}
# To attribute; to assign; to adjudge.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1777|author=w:Richard Brinsley Sheridan|title=w:The School for Scandal|page=6|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=FzZBAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA6|passage=I don't wonder at people '''giving''' him to me for a lover.}}
# To communicate or announce (advice, tidings, etc.); to pronounce or utter (an opinion, a judgment, a shout, etc.).
#: {{ux|en|The umpire finally '''gave''' his decision: the ball was out.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|_|or|_|religion}} To grant power, permission, destiny, etc. (especially to a person); to allot; to allow.
#* {{RQ:KJV|1=Deuteronomy|2=12|3=1|text=These ''are'' the statutes and judgments, which ye shall observe to do in the land, which the Lᴏʀᴅ God of thy fathers '''giveth''' thee to possess it, all the days that ye live upon the earth.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1700|author=[[w:Nicholas Rowe (writer)|Nicholas Rowe]]|title=w:The Ambitious Stepmother|page=13|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=DMzkD1EWOR8C&pg=PA13|passage=once again<br>'Tis '''given''' me to behold my friend.}}
#* {{RQ:Homer Pope et al Odyssey|book=III|passage=Then '''give''' thy friend to shed the sacred wine.}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive}} To devote or apply (oneself).
#: {{ux|en|The soldiers '''give''' themselves to plunder.}}
#: {{ux|en|That boy is '''given''' to fits of bad temper.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To become soft or moist.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1590|author=John Smyth|title=A Discourse {{...}}concerning{{...}}weapons|passage=Some moyst weather hath‥caused the powder to '''give''' and danke.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To shed tears; to weep.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|IV|iii|page=94|passage=Whose eyes do never '''give''' / But through lust and laughter.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To have a [[misgiving]].
#* '''c. 1608-1634''', {{w|John Webster}}, ''{{w|Appius and Virginia}}'', [https://archive.org/details/appiusvirginiatr00webs/page/16/mode/1up page 16]
#*: My mind '''gives''' ye're reserv'd / To rob poor market women.

