==Chinese==

===Etymology===
Probably from clipping of {{der|yue|en|give a shit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|yue|/kɪf⁵⁵/}}

===Verb===
{{head|zh|verb}}{{cln|yue|lemmas|verbs}}

# {{lb|zh|Hong Kong Cantonese|neologism|chiefly in the negative}} to [[give a shit]]; to [[care]] about; to [[pay attention]] to someone

==Danish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|da|gi'||representing the spoken language|}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|da|non|gefa}}, from {{der|da|gem-pro|*gebaną}}, cognate with {{cog|en|give}} and {{cog|de|geben}}. The Germanic verbs go back to {{der|da|ine-pro|*gʰebʰ-||to give}} (hence {{cog|sa|गभस्ति|tr=gábhasti|gloss=arm}}); rather than {{m|ine-pro|*gʰeh₁bʰ-||to grab}} (whence {{noncog|la|habeō||to have}}).

===Pronunciation===
