===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To provide or furnish with teeth.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1815|author=w:William Wordsworth|title=The Brothers
|passage=His Wife sate near him, teasing matted wool, / While, from the twin cards '''toothed''' with glittering wire / He fed the spindle {{…}}}}
# To [[indent]]; to [[jag]].
#: ''to '''tooth''' a saw''
# To lock into each other, like [[gear wheel]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1678|author=w:Joseph Moxon|title=Mechanick Exercises: or the Doctrine of Handy-works|url=https://www.worldcat.org/title/mechanick-exercises-or-the-doctrine-of-handy-works/oclc/53476216|page=260|text=Whereas if the Header of one side of the wall, '''toothed''' as much as the Stretcher on the other side, it would be a stronger Toothing, and the joints of the Header on one side, would be in the middle of the Headers of the course they lie upon of the other side}}

