==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/dɑn/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-dan.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|dan}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɑn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|dan}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|than}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*þan}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*þan}}.

====Adverb====
{{nl-adv}}

# [[then]], at that time {{gloss|in the future}}
#: {{ux|nl|Morgen wordt het beter weer, maar '''dan''' moet ik weer naar mijn werk.|Tomorrow the weather will be better, but then I must go to work again.}}
# then, after that
#: {{ux|nl|Eerst moet je je tanden poetsen, '''dan''' mag je naar bed.|First you need to brush your teeth, then you may go to bed.}}
# then, in that case
#: {{ux|nl|Als het niet had geregend of gesneeuwd had, '''dan''' moet de auto toch veilig zijn.|If it had not rained or snowed, then the car must still be safe.}}

=====Usage notes=====
The adverb ''dan'' is often used in Dutch after an imperative with a preceding conditional clause:
* {{ux|nl|Als u de tijd hebt, bezoekt u '''dan''' in ieder geval de haven.|If you have the time, then be sure to visit the harbour.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{qualifier|in the past}} {{l|nl|toen}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|nl|nochtans}}

