==Maltese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|mt|dana|da}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|mt|ar|ذَا||this, that}}. The [[paragogic]] ''-n'' probably spread from the plural, where it originated by analogy with {{m|mt|hawn||here}} and/or with the plural ending {{m|mt|-in}} (compare {{cog|arq|هادون|tr=hādūn}} alongside {{m|arq|هادو|tr=hādū}}). Some earlier scholars instead suspected a connection with {{cog|arc|דנה|tr=dənā|t=this, that}}, but this was based on the widely obsolete theory of a Punic substratum in Maltese.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|mt|/daːn/}}

===Determiner===
{{mt-det|f=din|p=dawn}}

# [[this]]

====Usage notes====
* May contract with the following article: {{m|mt||dan ir-raġel → dar-raġel|t=this man}}. The full form is commoner, however, except in expressions like {{m|mt||dax-xahar|t=this month}}.
* The feminine singular contracts to {{m|mt||di-}}, the plural to {{m|mt||da-}} like the masculine: {{m|mt||dil-ġimgħa|t=this week}}, {{m|mt||das-snin|t=these years}}.

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|mt|dak}}
* {{l|mt|hedan}}, {{l|mt|hedak}}

