==Welsh==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/dan/}}
* {{rhymes|cy|an}}

===Etymology 1===
[[soft mutation|Soft mutation]] of {{l|cy|tan||under}}. From {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*tan}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-pro||*tanai}}, dative of {{m|cel-pro|*tanā}}, from {{inh|cy|ine-pro|*tn̥néh₂}}.

====Preposition====
{{head|cy|preposition|triggers [[soft mutation]] on a following noun}}

# [[under]]
#: {{syn|cy|islaw}}
# {{lb|cy|literary}} {{soft mutation of|cy|tan||under}}
#: {{syn|cy|islaw}}

=====Usage notes=====
In literary Welsh, {{l|cy|tan}} can mean both "under" and "until". In Welsh usage today, however, {{l|cy|dan}} (originally the soft mutation of {{l|cy|tan}}) has become a preposition in its own right with the meaning "under" whereas {{l|cy|tan}} means "until", retaining the meaning "under" in certain expressions, compound words and place names. Modern {{l|cy|dan}} or {{l|cy|tan}} are not usually mutated. {{l|cy|o dan}} is an alternative to {{l|cy|dan}}.

=====Inflection=====
{{cy-personal-prep-literary|danof|danot|dano|dani|danom|danoch|danynt}}
{{cy-personal-prep-colloquial|[[dano]] [[i]]/[[fi]], [[dana]]|[[danot]] [[ti]], [[danat]]|dano|dani|danon|danoch|danyn}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|cy|o dan}}

