Page 14 دانستن: Skipped, no changes
Page 14 دانستن: -------- begin text --------
==Persian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|دونستن|tr=dunestan|دونسن|tr2=dunessan||colloquial Iranian}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal|YDOYTWN-stn'|tr=dānistan}}, from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*ȷ́ānáHti}}, from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*ǵn̥néh₃ti}}.

Related to {{l|fa|شناختن|tr=šenâxtan|t=recognize}}, {{cog|kmr|zanîn}}, {{cog|bal|زانگ|tr=zánag}}, {{cog|sa|जानाति}}, {{cog|en|know}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|dānis`tan|teh=dūnis`tan,dūnis`san}}
* {{audio|fa|Danestan.ogg|a=Iran}}

===Verb===
{{fa-regional|دانستن|دانستن|донистан}}
{{fa-verb|tr=dânestan|prstem=دان|tr2=dân}}

# to [[know]] (something)
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:{{w|lang=fa|دیوان شمس تبریزی}}|trans-title={{w|Divan-i Shams-i Tabrizi|Dīvān-i Shams-i Tabrīzī}}|author={{w|Rumi|Jalāl ad-Dīn Mohammad Rūmī}}|year=c. 1250|text=خوش باش که هر که راز '''داند'''<br>'''داند''' که خوشی خوشی کشاند|tr=xwaš bāš ki har ki rāz '''dānad'''<br>'''dānad''' ke xwašī xwašī kašānad|t=Be happy, for everyone who '''knows''' [this] secret '''knows''' that happiness attracts happiness.|footer=(Classical Persian transliteration)}}
# {{lb|fa|in the simple past}} to come to [[know]]; to [[realize]]
#: {{syn|fa|فهمیدن|tr=fahmidan}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|chapter={{w|Shirazi Turk}}|title=fa:{{w|lang=fa|دیوان حافظ}}|trans-title=[[divan|Divān]] of {{w|Hafez|Ḥāfeẓ}}|author={{w|Hafez|Xāja Shams-ud-Dīn Moḥammad Ḥāfeẓ-e Shīrāzī}}|text=من از آن حسن روزافزون که یوسف داشت '''دانستم'''<br>که عشق از پرده عصمت برون آرد زلیخا را|tr=man az ān husn-i rōz-afzōn ki yūsuf dāšt '''dānestam'''<br>ki išq az parda-yi ismat birūn ārad zulayxā rā|t='''I have learnt''', from that daily-increasing beauty that Joseph had,<br>That Love will bring Zoleykha out from behind the curtain of modesty.|year=late 1300s|footer=(Classical Persian transliteration)}}
# to [[consider]]; to [[deem]]

====Usage notes====
* In the simple past tense, it means "learned; realized; came to know"; to mean "knew", one must use the imperfect tense with {{m|fa|می|tr=mi}}. This simple past tense use is not very common in colloquial language.
* Similar to many European languages, Persian has two verbs used for knowing something and knowing someone. {{l|fa|دانستن|tr=dânestan}} is used for having knowledge about places or things; but {{l|fa|شناختن|tr=šenâxtan}} is used for recognizing and knowing people. Compare {{cog|de|kennen}} and {{m|de|wissen}}; {{cog|fr|savoir}} and {{m|fr|connaître}}; {{cog|es|saber}} and {{m|es|conocer}}.

====Conjugation====
{{prs-conj|دانست|dānist|دان|dān}}
{{fa-conj-lit|دانست|dânest|دان|dân}}
{{fa-conj-colloq|دونست|dunest|دون|dun}}

====Derived terms====
{{col2|fa
|دانا<tr:dânâ>
|دانایی<tr:dânâ'i>
|نادان<tr:nâdân>
|نادانی<tr:nâdâni>
|دانش<tr:dâneš>
|دانشمند<tr:dânešmand>
|داننده<tr:dânande>
|دانستنی<tr:dânestani>
}}

