==Persian==
[[File:Sinapis alba subsp. alba sl7.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|fa|اسپندان}} – {{taxfmt|Sinapis alba|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|سپندان|tr=sepandân}}

===Etymology===
Containing the word for “white”, now {{m|fa|سفید|tr=safêd}}. Probably also confounded with {{m|fa|سپند|اسپند|tr=espand|t=Syrian rue}} and containing {{m|fa|دان|tr=dân|t=seed}}. Forms auslauting in {{IPAchar|/ɾ/}} are contaminated by {{m|fa|کندر|tr=kondor|t=olibanum-tree; olibanum}}-

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|ispandān}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=espandân}}

# [[white mustard]] ({{taxfmt|Sinapis alba|species}})

====Descendants====
* {{desc|bor=1|ar|أَسْبَنْدَار|أَسْبَنْذَار|أَسْبِنْدَار|أَسْبِنْذَار|أَسْفِنْدار|أَسْفِنْذَار|أَسْفَنْد}} {{q|obsolete, uncommon}}
* {{desc|ur|اسپندان|tr=ispandān|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:Flattery-Schwartz|page=143}}

{{C|fa|Crucifers}}
