Page 159 بوزیدان: Would save with comment = convert {{suf|fa}} to {{af|fa}}
Page 159 بوزیدان: -------- begin text --------
{{also|بوزيدان}}
==Persian==

===Etymology===
Apparently a {{inh|fa|pal|-}} genitive ([[ezafe]]) construction of {{m|fa-cls|بوز|tr=bawz}}, {{m|fa-cls|بز|tr=biz|t=bee}}, alternatively {{m|fa-cls|بوز|tr=bōz}}, {{m|fa-cls|بوزه|tr=bōza}}, {{m|fa-cls|پوز|tr=pōz}}, {{m|fa-cls|پوزه|tr=pōza|t=snout, beak}} of {{m|fa|ـی|tr=-ī}} {{af|fa|^|ـدان|tr2=-dān}}, if one assumes not the rare {{taxlink|Pseudohandelia|genus}} to constitute the original meaning, only later falsified with more easily obtainable herbs, since {{taxlink|Pseudohandelia|genus}} exposes umbels attractive to bees rather than calyces likenable to snouts.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|būzīdān}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=buzidân}}

# {{vern|sweet pellitory|nopedia=1}} ({{taxlink|Pseudohandelia umbellifera|species}}, once {{taxlink|Pyrethrum umbelliferum|species}}, {{taxlink|Tanacetum umbelliferum|species}})
# {{lb|fa|as a replacement}} [[ashwagandha]] ({{taxfmt|Withania somnifera|species}})
# {{lb|fa|as a replacement}} {{vern|green-winged orchid}} or {{vern|green-veined orchid}} ({{taxlink|Anacamptis morio|species}}, syn. {{taxlink|Orchis morio|species}})

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ar|بُوزِيدَان|bor=1|alts=1}}
* {{desc|axm|բուզիտան|բուզիդան|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ota|بوزیدان|tr=buzidan|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ur|بوزیدان|tr=būzīdān|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:mul:Hartwich:1897|entry=Tanacetum|page=331}}
* {{R:axm:Seidel|page=263 Nr. 386}}
* {{R:fa:Steingass|page=206|بوزيدان}}
* {{R:fa:Vullers|L|I|page=276b}}

{{C|fa|Asparagales order plants|Nightshades|Anthemideae tribe plants}}
