{{also|DISH}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Dish MET DP317306.jpg|thumb|Renaissance dish, from 1520, made of [[maiolica]] (tin-glazed earthenware)]]
[[File:Dish (coppa)- The story of Aeneas- Queen Dido of Carthage welcomes Aeneas and his son. MET DT3439.jpg|thumb|Renaissance dish, from circa 1520, made of maiolica]]
[[File:Dish with The Discovery of Achilles MET DP319570.jpg|thumb|Renaissance dish with The Discovery of Achilles, from circa 1555-1560, made of maiolica]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|dissh}}, {{m|enm|disch}}, from {{inh|en|ang|disċ|t=plate; bowl; dish}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*disk|t=table; dish}}, from {{der|en|la|discus}}.  {{doublet|en|dais|desk|disc|discus|disk|diskos}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|disch|t=dish; plate}}, {{cog|nl|dis|t=table}}, {{cog|nds-de|Disk}}, {{m|nds-de|Disch|t=table}}, {{cog|de|Tisch|t=table}}, {{cog|da|disk|t=dish; counter}}, {{cog|sv|disk|t=dish; counter}}, {{cog|is|diskur|t=dish; plate}}, {{cog|fi|tiski|t=desk, counter; dish}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|dĭsh}}, {{IPA|en|/dɪʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-dish.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪʃ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[vessel]] such as a [[plate]] for holding or serving food, often flat with a depressed region in the middle.
#: {{syn|en|plate}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Judges|v|25|text=She brought forth butter in a lordly '''dish'''.}}
# The contents of such a vessel.
#: {{syn|en|dishful|plate|plateful}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''dish''' of stew}}
# {{lb|en|metonym}} A specific type of prepared food.
#: {{ux|en|a vegetable '''dish'''}}
#: {{ux|en|this '''dish''' is filling and easily made}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|II|i|passage=Let's carve him a '''dish''' fit for the gods}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} [[tableware|Tableware]] (including [[cutlery]], etc, as well as [[crockery]]) that is to be or is being washed after being used to prepare, serve and eat a meal.
#: {{ux|en|It's your turn to wash the '''dishes'''.}}
# {{lb|en|telecommunication}} A type of [[antenna]] with a similar shape to a plate or [[bowl]].
#: {{ux|en|satellite '''dish'''}}
#: {{ux|en|radar '''dish'''}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A sexually attractive person.
#: {{syn|en|babe|fox}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=Westwood Studios|title=Lands of Lore: The Throne of Chaos|publisher=Virgin Games
|passage=Have you seen the new apothecary? I think her name is Sadie. What a '''dish'''!}}
# The state of being [[concave]], like a dish, or the degree of such [[concavity]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''dish''' of a wheel}}
# A hollow place, as in a field.
# {{lb|en|baseball|slang}} The [[home plate]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Paul Byrd|title=Free Byrd: The Power of a Liberated Life|page=4
|passage=He said, "I don't like your chances at the '''dish''' [home plate] tonight."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author=Loren Long; Phil Bildner|title=Magic in the Outfield|page=40
|passage=At the plate, Graham pounded the '''dish''' three times, just like Bubbles did whenever he was up, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Conor Kelley|title=The Catcher's Handbook|page=87
|passage=Also, if you end up getting to the baseball, your pitcher needs to be covering home plate, which pitchers occasionally forget to do. However, if the ball stays near the '''dish''' and you have a pitcher on the mound who isn't a space-case, you've got a good shot to get the runner out.}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A [[trough]] in which [[ore]] is [[measure]]d.
# {{lb|en|mining}} That portion of the [[produce]] of a [[mine]] which is paid to the land owner or [[proprietor]].
# {{lb|en|slang|uncountable}} [[gossip|Gossip]].

