{{also|Increase}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|encrease}} {{q|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱer- (grow)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|encresen}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|encreistre}}, from {{der|en|la|increscere||increase}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|increscō}}, from {{m|la|in||in, on}} + {{m|la|crescō||grow}}.

The noun is from {{inh|en|enm|encres}}, from the verb.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|verb}} {{enPR|ĭnkrēsʹ}}, {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈkɹiːs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-increase-verb.ogg|a=US}}
* {{sense|noun}} {{enPR|ĭnʹkrēs}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈɪnkɹiːs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-increase-noun.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|in|crease}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːs|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} (of a [[quantity]], etc.) To become [[large]]r or greater.
#: {{ux|en|His rage only '''increased''' when I told him of the lost money.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Genesis|7|17|passage=The waters '''increased''' and bare up the ark.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|act=II|scene=i|passage=The heavens forbid / But that our loves and comforts should '''increase''', / Even as our days do grow!}}
#* {{RQ:Swift Modest Proposal|page=7|passage=I have reckoned upon a Medium, that a Child juſt born vvill vveigh 12 pounds, and in a ſolar Year if tollerably nurſed '''encreaſeth''' to 28 Pound.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=UN Study: China, US, Japan Lead World AI Development|url=https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/un-study-china-us-japan-lead-world-ai-development/4769094.html|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190207184548/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/un-study-china-us-japan-lead-world-ai-development/4769094.html|archivedate=7 February 2019|work=w:Voice of America|date=3 February 2019|passage=The report said that deep learning methods '''increased''' from just 118 patent requests in 2013 to nearly 2,400 in 2016.}}
#*: {{audio|en|The report said that deep learning methods increased from just 118 patent requests in 2013 to nearly 2,400 in 2016.ogg|a=US}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make (a quantity, etc.) larger.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/fenella-saunders Fenella Saunders]| magazine=w:American Scientist| title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/tiny-lenses-see-the-big-picture Tiny Lenses See the Big Picture]| passage=The single-imaging optic of the mammalian eye offers some distinct visual advantages. Such lenses can take in photons from a wide range of angles, '''increasing''' light sensitivity. They also have high spatial resolution, resolving incoming images in minute detail.}}
# To [[multiply]] by the production of [[young]]; to be [[fertile]], [[fruitful]], or [[prolific]].
#* {{RQ:Hale Mankind|passage=Fishes are infinitely more numerous of '''increasing''' than Beasts or Birds, as appears by the numerous Spawn.}}
# {{lb|en|astronomy|intransitive}} To become more nearly full; to show more of the surface; to [[wax]].
#: {{ux|en|The Moon '''increases'''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|become larger}} {{l|en|wax}}, {{l|en|go up}}, {{l|en|grow}}, {{l|en|rise}}, {{l|en|soar}} (rapidly), [[shoot up]] (rapidly); See also [[Thesaurus:increase]]
* {{sense|make larger}} {{l|en|increment}}, {{l|en|raise}}, {{l|en|up}} {{qualifier|informal}}; See also [[Thesaurus:augment]]
* {{sense|multiply by production of young}} {{l|en|proliferate}}, {{l|en|propagate}}, {{l|en|teem}}
* {{sense|to show more of the surface}} {{l|en|wax}}

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|become larger}} {{l|en|decrease}}, {{l|en|drop}}, {{l|en|fall}}, {{l|en|go down}}, {{l|en|plummet}} (rapidly), [[plunge]] (rapidly), {{l|en|reduce}}, {{l|en|shrink}}, {{l|en|sink}}; See also [[Thesaurus:decrease]]
* {{antsense|make larger}} {{l|en|cut}}, {{l|en|decrease}}, {{l|en|decrement}}, {{l|en|lower}}, {{l|en|reduce}}; See also [[Thesaurus:diminish]]
* {{antsense|multiply by production of young}}
* {{antsense|to show more of the surface}} {{l|en|wane}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|increasable}}
* {{l|en|Increase}}

