===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An amount by which a quantity is increased.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/philip-j-bushnell Philip J. Bushnell]
|magazine=w:American Scientist|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/4/solvents-ethanol-car-crashes-amp-tolerance Solvents, Ethanol, Car Crashes & Tolerance]
|passage=Surprisingly, this analysis revealed that acute exposure to solvent vapors at concentrations below those associated with long-term effects appears to increase the risk of a fatal automobile accident. Furthermore, this '''increase''' in risk is comparable to the risk of death from leukemia after long-term exposure to benzene, another solvent, which has the well-known property of causing this type of cancer.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2018|url=https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/china-s-melting-glacier-brings-visitors-concern-over-climate-change/4627742.html|title=VOA Learning English > China's Melting Glacier Brings Visitors, Adds to Climate Concerns
|passage=She says an '''increase''' in melting from climate change may put that at risk. [[File:She says an increase in melting from climate change may put that at risk.ogg]]}}
# For a quantity, the act or process of becoming larger
# [[offspring|Offspring]], [[progeny]]
#* {{RQ:Nashe Lenten Stuffe|page=2|passage=That infortunate imperfit Embrion of my idle houres [[w:The Isle of Dogs (play)|the Ile of Dogs]] before mentioned, breeding vnto me ſuch bitter throwes in the teaming as it did, and the tempeſtes that aroſe at his birth, ſo aſtoniſhing outragious and violent as if my braine had bene conceiued of another Hercules, I was ſo terrifyed with my owne '''encreaſe''' (like a woman long trauailing to bee deliuered of a monſter) that it was no ſooner borne but I was glad to run from it.}}
# {{lb|en|knitting}} The creation of one or more new [[stitch]]es; see {{w|Increase (knitting)}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|amount by which a quantity is increased}} {{l|en|gain}}, {{l|en|increment}}, {{l|en|raise}} {{qualifier|US, said of pay}}, {{l|en|rise}}, {{l|en|uptick}}; See also [[Thesaurus:adjunct]] or [[Thesaurus:acquisition]]
* {{sense|act or process of becoming larger}} {{l|en|enlargement}}, {{l|en|expansion}}; See also [[Thesaurus:augmentation]]

====Antonyms====
* {{antsense|amount by which a quantity is increased}} {{l|en|cut}}, {{l|en|decrease}}, {{l|en|decrement}}, {{l|en|drop}}, {{l|en|fall}}, {{l|en|loss}}, {{l|en|lowering}}, {{l|en|reduction}}, {{l|en|shrinkage}}; See also [[Thesaurus:decrement]]
* {{antsense|act or process of becoming larger}} {{l|en|decline}}, {{l|en|decrease}}, {{l|en|diminishment}}; See also [[Thesaurus:diminution]]

