Page 2 luggage: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
1590s, {{suffix|en|lug|age|t1=to drag}}, literally “that which is lugged, dragged around”.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> Duplicate ''-g-'' is to clarify pronunciation of the vowel ‘u’ (which is pronounced unchanged from {{m|en|lug}}). Compare {{m|en|baggage}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lŭg'ĭj|a=UK,US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈlʌɡɪd͡ʒ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-luggage.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌɡɪdʒ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|lug|gage}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}
[[File:Mozambique 160.jpg|thumb|upright|A man carrying his '''luggage''' (1).]]

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[bag]]s and other [[container]]s that hold a [[traveller]]'s [[belongings]].
#* '''August 4, 1726''', {{w|Jonathan Swift}}, [[s:The Works of the Rev. Jonathan Swift/Volume 14/Letter: Swift to Pope - 7|letter]] to {{w|Alexander Pope}}
#*: I am gathering up my '''luggage''', and preparing for my journey.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[contents]] of such containers.
# {{lb|en|countable|nonstandard|_|or|_|obsolete}} A specific [[bag]] or [[container]] holding a traveller's belongings.
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=The African Repository and Colonial Journal| volume=34| year=1858| passage=I assisted some time ago in cutting up a tree, that made tolerably good turns or '''luggage''' for nineteen or twenty persons, which could be procured for about two dollars at the stump.|page=13|title=Letter from Rev. George L. Seymour}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Report of the Midnapore and Burdwan Cyclone of the 15th and 16th of October 1874| author=W. G. Willson| year=1875| passage=The passengers injured who could not get out were removed out by the railway staff, and then taking part of the '''luggage''' the train started back for Burdwan.| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=enUIAAAAQAAJ&dq=%22the%20luggages%22&pg=PA61#v=onepage&q=%22the%20luggages%22&f=false}}
#* {{RQ:MacInnes City of Spades|year=1964|page=15|passage=Namely, leaving my '''luggages''' at the Government hostel, to go straight out by taxi (oh, so slow, compared with our sleek Lagos limousines!) to the famous central Piccadilly Tube station where I took a onestop ticket, went down on the escalator, and then ''ran up the same steps in the wrong direction''.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|baggage}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|en|hold luggage|cabin luggage|carry-on luggage|checked luggage|hand luggage|left luggage|left-luggage office|luggage cart|luggage hold|luggage rack|luggage car|luggage van}}

