Page 3 appreciate: Skipped, no changes
Page 3 appreciate: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Etymology===
Originated 1645–55 from {{bor|en|ML.|appreciatus||valued or appraised}}, from {{der|en|LL.|appretiatus||appraised}}, from {{m|la|ap-}} (form of {{m|la|ad-||towards}}) + {{der|en|la|pretium|preti(um)|price}} (English {{m|en|precious}}) + {{m|la|-ate|-atus}}.

Cognate to {{cog|fr|apprécier}}. Latin root also origin of English {{doublet|notext=1|en|appraise}}, which has various Romance cognates.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈpɹiː.ʃi.eɪt/|/əˈpɹiː.si.eɪt/|/əˈpɹɪʃ.i.eɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-appreciate.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ap|pre|ci|ate}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To be [[grateful]] or [[thankful]] for.
#: {{syn|en|esteem}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''appreciate''' your efforts.}}
#: {{ux|en|We sincerely '''appreciate''' your help.}}
#: {{ux|en|Any aid will be warmly '''appreciated'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To view as [[valuable]].
#: {{syn|en|esteem}}
#: {{ux|en|You must learn to '''appreciate''' time.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To be fully [[conscious]] of; [[understand]]; be [[aware]] of; [[detect]].
#: {{syn|en|grasp}}
#: {{ux|en|It is essential for the reader to '''appreciate''' how important this argument is.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''appreciate''' that what I'm asking you to do is very difficult.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1883|author={{w|John Lubbock, 1st Baron Avebury|John Lubbock}}|title=On the Senses, Instincts and Intelligence of Animals, With Special Reference to Insects
|passage=to test the power of bees to '''appreciate''' colour}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title=w:Mass Effect 3|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2012|system=PC|scene=Normandy SR-2|oclc=962368035|passage=Eve: You learn to '''appreciate''' the light by living in the dark.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|transitive}} To increase in value.
#: {{ant|en|depreciate}}
#: {{ux|en|The value of his portfolio '''appreciated''' by 80% over eight years.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1809|author={{w|David Ramsay (historian)|David Ramsay}}|title=History of South Carolina
|passage=lest a sudden peace should '''appreciate''' the money}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Romance|page=234|volume=I|passage=Laughter may be generally classed under three heads,—forced, silly, or vulgar; but hers is the most sweet, real, ''spirituelle'' sound possible—it so '''appreciates''' the wit, which it increases as it catches—it speaks of spirits so fresh, so youthful!}}

====Usage notes====
* This is a [[catenative]] verb that takes the ''gerund (-ing)''. See [[Appendix:English catenative verbs]]

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|appretiate}} {{qualifier|archaic}}
* {{l|en|'preciate}} {{q|pronunciation spelling}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|en|appreciatable|appreciater|appreciator|apprecihate|disappreciate|misappreciate|reappreciate|underappreciate|much appreciated}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|appraise}}
* {{l|en|appreciation}}
* {{l|en|appreciative}}
* {{l|en|precious}}

