Page 4 Scheherazade: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|Scheherezade}}
* {{alt|en|Shahrazad}}
* {{alt|en|Shahrzad||as a given name}}
* {{alt|en|Sheherazade}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Scheherazade}}, from {{der|en|ru|Шехераза́да}}, from {{der|en|fa|شهرازاد|tr=šahrâzâd}}, alternative form of {{m|fa|شهرزاد|tr=šahrzâd|lit=child of the city|pos=from {{af|fa|شهر|t1=city|tr1=šahr|ـزاد|t2=child of|tr2=-zâd|nocat=1}}}}.<br/>Popularized by the fictional character below.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʃəˌhɛɹəˈzɑːd(ə)/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ʃəˈhɛɹəzɑd/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːd|ɑːdə|s1=4|s2=5}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|en|female|from=Persian}}.
# A fictional character, the [[wife]] and [[storyteller]] of the king [[Shahryar]] in ''{{w|One Thousand and One Nights}}''.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|Scheherazadean}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|female given name}}
* Arabic: {{t+|ar|شَهْرَزَاد|f}}
* Armenian: {{t|hy|Շահրազադ}}
