==Pashto==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|ps|ine-pro|*ǵʰéslom|*(sm̥-)ǵʰéslo-}}. Indo-Iranian cognates include {{cog|bal|ہزار|tr=hazár}}, {{cog|fa|هزار|tr=hezâr}}, {{cog|kmr|ھەزار}} and {{cog|sa|सहस्र|tr=sahásra}}. Akin to {{cog|xcl|հազար|}}, an Iranian borrowing.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ps|/zər/}}

====Numeral====
{{head|ps|numeral|tr=zër}}

# [[thousand]]

=====Declension=====
{{ps-decl-noun-2|زر
|zër
|زره
|zëra
|زر
|zër
|زرو
|zëro
|
|
|
|}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|ps|iir-pro|-}} (compare {{cog|peo|𐎭𐎼𐎴𐎹|ts=daraniya-}}, {{cog|sa|हिरण्य||gold}}), probably ultimately from a derivative of the {{der|ps|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰel-||yellow; gleam; to shine}}. Compare {{cog|cu|злато||gold}}, {{cog|lv|zelts}}, {{cog|en|gold}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ps|/zar/}}

====Noun====
{{ps-noun|g=m|tr=zar}}

# [[metal]]

[[Category:Pashto cardinal numbers]]

==Persian==
{{wikipedia|lang=fa}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|fa|gold}}
From {{der|fa|pal|*zarr||gold}}, from {{der|fa|xpr|*zarn||gold}}; the inherited form would have started with a D, as is seen in {{cog|peo|𐎭𐎼𐎴𐎹}}. Ultimately from a derivative of {{der|fa|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-||yellow; gleam; to shine}}. Indo-Iranian cognates include {{cog|kmr|zêrr}}, and {{cog|sa|हिरण्य}}. Other cognates include {{cog|cu|злато}}, {{cog|lv|zelts}}, and {{cog|en|gold}} and {{m|en|yellow}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|zarr,zar}}

====Noun====
{{fa-regional|زر|زر|зар}}
{{fa-noun|tr=zar}}

# [[gold]]
#: {{syn|fa|طلا|tr=talâ}}

