==Georgian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ka-IPA}}
* {{ka-hyphen}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ka|terror}}
From {{uder|ka|oge|ზარი|id=terror}}.

====Noun====
{{ka-noun}}

# [[terror]], [[fear]]; [[consternation]]
#: {{ux|ka|შიშის ზარის დაცემა|to strike with terror|inline=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ka|bell}}
From {{uder|ka|oge|ზარი|id=noise}}. The sense "call" is probably a {{semantic loan|ka|ru|звоно́к|nocap=1}}.

====Noun====
{{ka-noun|ზარები}}

# {{lb|ka|Middle Georgian}} [[tumult]], [[noise]]
#: {{uxi|ka|ზარი და ზეიმი|noisy rejoicing}}
# [[bell]]
# [[call]] (particularly by phone)

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|ka|lament}}
From {{bor|ka|fa|زار|tr=zâr|id=lament}}.

====Noun====
{{head|ka|noun}}

# [[lamenting]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ka|გლოვის ზარი}}

===Etymology 4===
{{etymid|ka|dice}}
From {{bor|ka|fa|زار|tr=zâr|id=die}}.

====Noun====
{{ka-noun|ზარები}}

# {{lb|ka|dated|colloquial}} [[die]] {{gloss|object used in [[games of chance]]}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ka|კამათელი}}

===Etymology 5===
{{etymid|ka|gold}}
From {{bor|ka|fa|زر|tr=zar|id=gold}}.

====Noun====
{{head|ka|noun}}

# {{lb|ka|Tbilisi}} [[gold]] [[thread]]
#: {{syn|ka|ოქრომკედი}}

====References====
* {{R:ka:Grishashvili|url=http://www.nplg.gov.ge/gwdict/index.php?a=term&d=30&t=2625|page=98}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ka:Rayfield|url=http://www.nplg.gov.ge/gwdict/index.php?a=term&d=46&t=81818}}

==Laz==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|lzz|ზაი||alternative spelling}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|lzz|ota|زار|tr=zar||die}}, from {{der|lzz|ar|زَهْر||cube, die}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|lzz|/ˈzɑɾi/|/ˈzɑ(ɹ)i/}}
* {{hyph|lzz|ზა|რი}}

===Noun===
{{head|lzz|noun|Latin spelling|zari}}

# [[dice]] {{gloss|a cube-shaped game tool used in games such as backgammon, with six spots numbered one through six}}
#: {{ux|lzz|თავლა ოსთერუ ვაგიჩქინ დო '''ზარის''' მუ აკვან?|If you don't know how to play backgammon, what do you want '''from the dice'''?}}
# {{lb|lzz|dialectal|Vizha}} [[fortune]], [[chance]], [[luck]]
#: {{syn|lzz|იგბალი|შანსი}}
#: {{ux|lzz|გოწონერი წანა მიღურტუ '''ზარი'''|I was lucky last year|lit=Last year I had '''luck'''}}

==Old Georgian==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|oge|terror}}
From the first word of the idiomatic {{bor|oge|xcl||*զարհի հարկանել|t=to dread, to fear|lit=to be struck to fear}}, attested in the later form {{m|xcl||զահի հարկանել}}. See {{m|xcl|զ-|t=to}}, {{m|xcl|ահ|t=fear}} and {{m|xcl|հարկանեմ|t=to strike}}

