==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*nem-}}
As an adjective, from {{inh|en|enm|numeral}}, {{m|enm|numerall}}, from {{der|en|la|numerālis||pertaining to a number}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=numerāl|pos=adj|id=MED30007}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''adj''. and ''n.''|noformat=1|id=2831179172}}</ref> from {{m|la|numerus||a number}}.

As a noun, via {{bor|en|frm|numeral}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=n}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|nyo͞oʹm(ə)rəl|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈnjuːməɹəl/|/ˈnjuːmɹəl/}}
* {{enPR|no͞oʹm(ə)rəl|a=GenAm}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈnuməɹəl/|/ˈnumɹəl/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-numeral.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|nu|mer|al}}, {{hyphenation|en|num|eral|nocaption=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[symbol]] that is not a [[word]] and represents a [[number]], such as the [[Arabic numeral]]s 1, 2, 3 and the [[Roman numeral]]s I, V, X, L.
# A [[representation]] of a [[number]] composed of such symbols.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966|author=Robert Lee Morton|title=Modern Mathematics Through Discovery|page=97|passage=Compare the '''numeral''' for the product with the original decimal '''numeral'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q63116}}{{lb|en|linguistics}} A number word, a simple or compound [[word]] for a [[number]] often having particular grammatical attributes depending on the language.
#: {{hyponyms|en|cardinal numeral|ordinal numeral|distributive numeral|multiplicative numeral|multiplier|collective numeral}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Laurie Bauer; Rodney Huddleston|chapter=Lexical word-formation|title=The Cambridge Grammar of the English Language|page=1715|passage=We use the term '''numeral''' for linguistic expressions and '''number''' for meanings. For example, ''five'' is a '''numeral''' expressing the number "5" - and ''fifteen hundred'' and ''one thousand five hundred'' are different '''numerals''' expressing the same number, "1,500".}}
# {{lb|en|card games}} A card whose [[rank]] is a [[number]] (usually including the [[ace]] as 1).
#: {{ux|en|Jacks, queens, and kings are not '''numerals'''.}}

