==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*sana}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=Fi-sana-native.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[word]] {{gloss|unit of language, text or storage}}
#: {{ux|fi|Tässä virkkeessä on viisi '''sanaa'''.|This sentence has five '''words'''.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Emme sanoneet '''sanaakaan'''.|We didn't say '''a word'''.}}
# [[word]]; [[say]] {{gl|figuratively: someone's opinion or statement, especially a decisive or emphatic one, or a promise}}
#: {{ux|fi|Luotan '''sanaasi'''.|I'll take '''your word''' for it.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Sinun pitää aina saada viimeinen '''sana'''.|You always have to have the last '''word'''.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Minulla ei ole mitään '''sanaa''' tähän asiaan.|I have no '''say''' in this matter.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Ennen mies maansa myö kuin '''sanansa''' syö.|A man will sell his land before going back on his '''word'''.}}
# {{lb|fi|religion|with capital initial letter}} [[Word]], [[Scripture]]
# [[lesson]] {{gloss|section of the Bible or other religious text read as part of a divine service}}
#: {{uxi|fi|päivän '''Sana'''|'''Lesson''' of the Day}}
# {{lb|fi|music|in the plural}} [[lyrics]] {{gloss|words to a song}}
#: {{syn|fi|[[laulun]] [[sanat]]|lyriikka|sanoitus}}

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-kala|san|||a}}

