===Etymology===
Akin to {{cog|av|сон}} and {{cog|lbe|шин}} and {{cog|udi|усен}}.

===Noun===
{{head|bdk|noun}}

# [[year]]

==Bulgarian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|bg|cu|санъ}} (u-stem), probably of {{der|bg|trk-ogr}} origin. Cognate with {{cog|tr|san||reputation}}, {{cog|tk|san||account}}, {{cog|kk|санау||count}}, {{cog|tt|san||number}} and akin to dialectal {{cog|tr|sаnаmаk||to take into account}}, {{cog|uz|sanamoq||to count}} from {{cog|trk-pro|*sā(j)-||to count, to determine}}. Through another suffix is perhaps {{cog|bg|самчия||(old-time) governor}}.

===Noun===
{{bg-noun|сан|m}}

# {{lb|bg|literary|obsolescent}} [[rank]], [[administrative]] [[position]]

