Page 13 սմբուկ: -------- begin text --------
==Armenian==
[[Image:Aubergine.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|hy|Սմբուկ}}]]

===Etymology===
Unattested in Old or Middle Armenian. Several dictionaries list {{m|hy||սմբուկ}} as a dialectal word,<ref>{{R:fa:GD|պաթինկեան|page=404a}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Norayr|aubergine|page=107b}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:HBus|section=2776|page=571}}</ref><ref>{{R:hy:Ayvazean|page=32a}}</ref> but Ačaṙyan is unable to identify it in any dialect.<ref name=HAB>{{R:xcl:HAB|vol=IV|page=234ab}}</ref> However, the word is in fact recorded in Istanbul, {{w|Diyarbakır}}, {{w|Sivas}}, {{w|Palu, Elazığ|Palu}} and {{w|Çarsancak}}.<ref>{{R:hy:Bdoyan|page=118b}}</ref><ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սմբուկ|vol=V|page=367a}}</ref> Note also {{w|Süveydiye}} dialect {{m|hy|սմպըկ}}, {{m|hy|սմբըկ}} referring to a kind of edible greens equivalent to {{noncog|tr|[[almacık]] [[diken|dikeni]]}}.<ref>{{R:hy:Andreasyan|page=158}}</ref><ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սմպըկ|vol=V|page=367b}}</ref>

The origin is {{unk|hy|title=unknown}}.<ref>{{R:xcl:HSB|page=685b}}</ref>

Ačaṙyan derives from {{affix|hy|lang1=ar|أَنَب|tr1=anab|t1=eggplant|-ուկ}}, via a form {{m|hy||*ամբուկ}}, wherein {{m|hy||ա}} was then confused with similar-looking {{m|hy||ս}}.<ref name=HAB/> But because the word is dialectal, such a literary confusion is unlikely.

Perhaps from an assumed root {{m|hy||*սում(բ)-|t=smooth; shaven}} or the like {{suffix|hy||-ուկ}}, thus "the smooth one", referring to the smooth, glossy surface of the eggplant fruit, which root may also be contained in dialectal {{m|hy|սմբուլ||t=polished, smooth|id=smooth}},<ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սմբուլ³|vol=V|page=367a}}</ref> {{m|hy|սմպատ||having a smooth head}},<ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սմպատ|vol=V|page=367a}}</ref> {{m|hy|սմպըլիկ|t=having a shaven head}},<ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սմպըլիկ|vol=V|page=367b}}</ref> {{m|hy|սմբըլիկ|t=leafless}},<ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սմբըլիկ|vol=V|page=366b}}</ref> {{m|hy|սնուկ||very smooth}},<ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սնուկ|vol=V|page=372a}}</ref> {{m|hy|սնեցնել|սըն-եցնել|to smooth, polish}}<ref>{{R:hy:HLBB|սընեցնել|vol=V|page=320a}}</ref> and the uncertain given name {{m|axm|Սմպուկս}}.<ref>{{R:xcl:HAnB|Սմպուկս|vol=IV|page=564}}</ref> The {{m|hy||-բ-}} after {{m|hy||-մ-}} may be [[epenthetic]] in dialects: compare the examples given in Martirosyan 2010.<ref>{{R:xcl:Martirosyan|pages=37, 437, 442}}</ref> This assumed root may be borrowed from {{der|hy|ira}}, ultimately from {{der|hy|ira-pro|*saH-||to whet, cut}}, from {{der|hy|ine-pro|*ḱeh₃-||to sharpen}}, whence {{cog|bal|alt=سای-|ساینغ|tr=sāy-|t=to shave}}, {{cog|ckb|سوون|t=to whet, sharpen}}, {{cog|gzi|tr=sǖn-|t=to rub, shave off}}, {{cog|fa|ساد|tr=sâd|t=smooth, plane}}, {{cog|srh|suδγ|t=flat, smooth (surface)}}, {{cog|fa|سان|tr=sân|t=whetstone}}, {{cog|ckb|ھەسان|t=whetstone}}, and according to Horn also {{cog|fa-cls|سنباده|tr=sumbāde|t=whetstone}},<ref>{{R:fa:Horn|page=153, footnote 1}}</ref> to which the Iranian borrowing {{m|xcl|սմպատակ||touchstone}} is related (J̌ahukyan considers {{m|xcl||-ատակ}} in the latter an Iranian suffix, as in {{m|xcl|յիշատակ}}).<ref>{{R:xcl:Jahukyan:1993|page=262}}</ref> For the Iranian root see Cheung,<ref>{{R:ira:Cheung|pages=325—326}}</ref> without the Armenian. Compare also {{cog|zza|sımıltkun||hairless, smooth}}.<ref>{{R:zza:Yilmaz|sımıltkun|page=134b}}</ref>

Typologically compare {{noncog|ar|كُوسَا|t=zucchini, courgette|lit=smooth, beardless}}. For another figurative usage in the dialects compare {{m|hy|լոլիկ|t=tomato|lit=the round one}}.

===Pronunciation===
