==Old Armenian==

===Etymology===
The origin is {{unc|xcl|nocap=1}}.<ref name=HAB>{{R:xcl:HAB|vol=III|pages=396–397}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:AG|page=477}}</ref> Often connected with {{cog|fa-cls|افسان|tr=afsān}}, {{m|fa|فسان|tr=fasân}}, {{m|fa|سان|tr=sân}}, {{m|fa|آسیانه|tr=âsiyâna, âsyâna}},<ref>{{R:fa:GD|pages=711, 715}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Hiwnk|page=88}}</ref> {{cog|sa|शान}}, {{cog|os|ссон}}, {{m|os|инсойнӕ|t=whetstone}}.<ref>{{R:os:Abaev|vol=IV|page=278}}</ref> Attempts<ref>{{R:xcl:Lagarde:1850|page=354}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Lagarde:1851|pages=74, 214}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Lagarde:1854|pages=515–516}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Tērvišean:Naxal|page=59}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:HSB|page=552a}}</ref> to derive from {{cog|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-||sharp}} (whence {{cog|grc|ἀκόνη}}, {{cog|cu|осла||whetstone}}) or {{cog|ine-pro|*ḱeh₃-||sharpen}} (whence {{cog|la|cos||whetstone}}) meet phonetic obstacles.

{{cog|kmr|hesan}}, {{cog|ckb|ھەسان}}, {{cog|zza|hesan||whetstone}} have been treated as Armenian borrowings,<ref name=HAB/><ref>{{R:zza:Asatrian:1987|page=163}}</ref> but they may be inherited.

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun}}

# [[whetstone]]

