==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{m|ar|سَفِينَة|t=ship}}.

====Root====
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[ship]]s

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|سَفِينَة|t=ship}}
* {{l|ar|سِفَانَة|t=shipbuilding}}
* {{l|ar|سَفَّان|t=shipbuilder}}

===Etymology 2===
{{unc|ar}}, potentially borrowed from {{bor|ar|pal|-}}, compare {{cog|fa|اپسان|tr=apsân}} ~ {{m|fa|افسان|tr=afsân}} ~ {{m|fa|فسان|tr=fasân}} prefixed forms of {{m|fa|سان|tr=sân|t=whetstone}}, {{m+|ar|سُنْبَاذَج|t=whetstone}}. Likewise there are native Semitic associations with {{cog|akk|𒊓𒉺𒉡|tr=sa-pa-nu|ts=sapānu|t=to level, to even out, to flatten, to smooth out}}, {{cog|akk|𒉌𒌓𒌑𒃻𒋤𒋤|tr=<sup>NA<sub>4</sub></sup>U₂.NIG₂.SU₃.SU₃|ts=sapīnu|t=smoothing-stone, stone used for flattening}}, and {{cog|arc|ספנ|tr=səpan|t=to fill in empty spaces, to patch up a hold of a ship; hence to pair wood into usable planks}} connected with [[ship-building]], {{cog|arc-imp|𐡎𐡐𐡍𐡀|tr=sp̄enā|t=plank}}, and {{cog|arc|סְפינִתָּא|tr=sǝp̄īntā|t=ship}}.

====Root====
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[pare|paring]], [[strip]]ping

=====Derived terms=====
{{ar-verb forms|I=to [[pare]], to [[strip]] off|I-vn-head=سَفْن}}
* {{l|ar|سَفَن}}, {{l|ar|مِسْفَن|t=adze, paring-knife or other smoothing implement}}

