{{also|Pakistán|Pákistán|Päkistan}}
[[File:Flag of Pakistan.svg|thumb|Flag of Pakistan]]

==English==
[[File:Un-pakistan.png|thumb|right|A map of Pakistan]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ur|پاکستان||Land of the Holy|tr=pākistān}}, from {{m|ur|پاک|t=pure, holy, immaculate, chaste, undefiled|tr=pāk}} and {{der|en|fa-cls|ـستان|tr=-stān,-istān|t=[[-stan]]}} (with the form -istān being used after consonants). The word was {{coinage|en|Q263795|nocap=1|in=1933|nobycat=1}}, who published it in the pamphlet ''Now or Never'' as an acronym of the names of the "Muslim homelands" of western India—[[Punjab|'''P'''unjab]], [[Afghania|'''A'''fghania]], [[Kashmir|'''K'''ashmir]], [[Sindh|'''S'''indh]], and [[Balochistan|Balochis'''tan''']].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpɑːkɪˈstɑːn/|/ˌpækɪˈstɑːn/|/ˌpækɪˈstæn/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpɑːkɪˈstɑːn/|/ˈpækɪˌstæn/|/ˌpækɪˈstæn/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Pakistan.ogg|a=US|IPA=/ˈpækɪˌstæn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Pakistan-2.ogg|a=US|IPA=/ˈpɑːkɪˌstɑːn/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpækəˌstæn/|/ˈpækəˌstaːn/|a=CA}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q843}}{{place|en|country|r/South Asia|capital=Islamabad|official=Islamic Republic of Pakistan}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|East Pakistan}}
* {{l|en| Hazara Pakistan}}
*{{l|en| Pakistan Zindabad}}
* {{l|en|Pakistani}}
* {{l|en|Porkistan}}
* {{l|en|West Pakistan}}

