==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{commonscat}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|en}}; possibly from {{der|en|trk|-}} {{m|tr|uz||genuine}} + {{der|en|sog|ts=bek|t=master}} (for the second element, see [[Turkish]] {{m|tr|bey}}). The suffix is known to be from {{der|en|fa-cls|ـِستان|tr=istān||[[stan]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʊzˌbɛkɪˈstɑːn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-Uzbekistan.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q265}}{{place|en|country|r/Central Asia|official=Republic of Uzbekistan|capital=Tashkent}}.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2013
|author=w:Al Gore
|title={{w|The Future: Six Drivers of Global Change}}
|url=https://archive.org/details/futuresixdrivers0000gore_k5o2/
|location=[[New York]]
|publisher=w:Random House
|ISBN=978-0-8129-9294-6
|LCCN=2012039890
|OCLC=827202765
|OL=25879719M
|page=234
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/futuresixdrivers0000gore_k5o2/page/234/
|passage=In '''Uzbekistan''', forced sterilizations apparently began in 2004 and became official state policy in 2009.}}

