{{also|hindustani|hindustání}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|Hindoostane|Hindostanee|Hindoostanee|Hindoostani|Hindustanee|Hindustane|Hindōstāni||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|inc-hnd}} {{m|ur|ہِنْدُوسْتانی}} / {{m|hi|हिंदुस्तानी}}, from {{der|en|fa-cls|هِنْدُوسْتَانِی}}, from {{m|fa-cls|هِنْدُو||Hindu, Indian}} + {{m|fa-cls|ـسْتَان||land}} + adjective suffix {{m|fa-cls|ـِی}}. Equivalent to {{af|en|Hindustan|-i}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|dated|_|outside of|_|South Asia}} Related to [[India]], varying historically from the entire Indian [[subcontinent]] to India north of the [[Deccan]], especially the plains of the [[Ganges]] and [[Jumna]].

====Translations====
{{trans-top|related to India, or historically the entire Indian subcontinent}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|هِنْدُوسْتَانِيّ}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|hindustanilainen}}
* Hindi: {{t+|hi|हिन्दुस्तानी}}
* Hungarian: {{t+|hu|hindusztáni}}
* Kashmiri: {{t|ks|ہِندوستٲنؠ}}
* Marathi: {{t|mr|हिन्दुस्तानी}}
* Portuguese: {{t+|pt|hindustani}}, {{t|pt|indostani}}
* Serbo-Croatian:
*: Cyrillic: {{t|sh|хиндустански|m}}
*: Roman: {{t+|sh|hindustanski|m}}
* Urdu: {{t|ur|ہِنْدُوسْتانی}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[person]] from India, varying historically from the entire [[subcontinent]] to India north of the [[Deccan]], especially the plains of the Ganges and Jumna.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|person from India or the Indian subcontinent}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|hindustanilainen}}
* Hindi: {{t+|hi|हिन्दुस्तानी}}
* Irish: {{t|ga|Hiondústánach|m}}
* Kashmiri: {{t|ks|ہِندوستٲنؠ}}
* Marathi: {{t|mr|हिन्दुस्तानी}}
* Portuguese: {{t+|pt|hindustani|m|f}}, {{t|pt|indostani|m|f}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|хиндуста́нец|m}}, {{t|ru|хиндуста́нка|f}}
* Serbo-Croatian:
*: Cyrillic: {{t|sh|Хиндустанац|m}}, {{t|sh|Хиндустанка|f}}
*: Roman: {{t+|sh|Hindustanac|m}}, {{t|sh|Hindustanka|f}}
* Swedish: {{t+|sv|hindustani}}
* Ukrainian: {{t|uk|гіндуста́нець|m}}, {{t|uk|гіндуста́нка|f}}
* Urdu: {{t|ur|ہِنْدُوسْتانی}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The pluricentric language of [[Hindi-Urdu]], of which [[Hindi]] and [[Urdu]] are [[literary]] [[standard]]s<ref name="Basu2017">{{cite book|last1=Basu|first1=Manisha|title=The Rhetoric of Hindutva|year=2017|publisher=[[Cambridge University Press]]|isbn=978-1-107-14987-8|language=en|text=Urdu, like Hindi, was a standardized register of the Hindustani language deriving from the Dehlavi dialect and emerged in the eighteenth century under the rule of the late Mughals.}}</ref>
#* {{RQ:Kipling Kim|chapter=XI|passage=Kim watched the stars as they rose one after another in the still, sticky dark, till he fell asleep at the foot of the altar. That night he dreamed in '''Hindustani''', with never an English word…}}
# The [[Delhi]] dialect of that language.
# {{lb|en|historical}} The [[language]] which is now known as [[Urdu]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} The [[language]] which is now known as [[Hindi]].<ref>{{cite-web|last1=Chand|first1=Tara| url=http://https://franpritchett.com/00urduhindilinks/tarachand/03misconceptions.html|title=Some Misconceptions About Hindustani|work=The Problem of Hindustani|year=1944|publisher=Indian Periodicals Ltd.|text= The name Hindustani has been used for Khari Boli. It has also been used as a synonym for Urdu by many writers, and for Modern Hindi by some.}}</ref>

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|Hindi-Urdu}}

====Translations====
