==English==

===Alternative forms===
{{wikipedia}}
* {{alter|en|Bantustan}}

===Etymology===
From a {{bor|en|bnt}} language (ultimately from {{der|en|bnt-pro|*bantʊ̀||people}}) + {{affix|en|-stan|t1=home of|pos1=suffix of {{der|en|fa|-}} origin}}, after place names such as {{m|en|Hindustan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌbantuːˈstan/|/ˌbantuːˈstɑːn/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌbæntuˈstæn/|/ˌbɑntuˈstɑn/|/ˈbæntuˌstæn/|/ˈbɑntuˌstɑn/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æn|ɑːn|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally|_|South Africa|historical}} Any of ten former [[territory|territories]] defined as [[homeland]]s for black [[South African]]s under [[apartheid]] policy
# {{lb|en|derogatory}} A political entity reminiscent of the old apartheid-era territories of the same name.

====Related terms====
{{rel3|en|Bantoid|Bantologist|Bantu|Bantuist|Bantuization|Proto-Bantu}}

