Page 64 Khuzestan: Skipped, no changes
Page 64 Khuzestan: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Locator_map_Iran_Khuzestan_Province.png|thumb|right|Location of Khuzestan within Iran]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Khūzestān}}
* {{l|en|Khuzistān}}
* {{l|en|Khouzestan}}
* {{l|en|Khoozestan}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fa-ira|خوزستان|tr=xuzestân}}, from {{m|fa-ira|خوز|tr=xuz}}, name of the indigenous people of the region, and the suffix {{m|fa-ira|ـستان|tr=-estân||[[-stan]]}}, or borrowed wholly from {{der|en|pal|hwcstʾn'}} / {{m|pal|𐭧𐭥𐭰𐭮𐭲𐭭|tr=Hūzestān|lit=land of Hūz}}, itself from {{m|pal|hwc|tr=Hūz}} + {{m|pal|-stʾn'|tr=-estān||[[-stan]]}}. The first component is from {{der|en|peo|𐎢𐎺𐎩|ts=ʰūja-||[[Elam]], [[Elamite]]}}, or from the name of [[Susa]]. Compare {{cog|grc|Οὔξιοι}}, {{cog|syc|ܒܝܬ ܗܘܙܝܐ|tr=Bêṯ Hūzāyē}}, {{cog|xcl|խուժ||wild, savage}}, {{cog|hy|խուժան||mob}}. The city name [[Ahvaz]] is also related. See {{w|Origin of the name Khuzestan}} for more.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q241119}} {{place|en|province|c/Iran|capital=Ahvaz}}.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|province of Iran}}
* Armenian: {{t|hy|Խուզեստան}}
*: Old Armenian: {{t|xcl|Խուժաստան}}
* Georgian: {{t|ka|ხუზისტანი}}
* Hindi: {{t|hi|ख़ुज़िस्तान|m}}, {{t|hi|ख़ुज़ेस्तान|m}}
* Persian: {{t+|fa|خوزستان|tr=xuzestân}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|Хузеста́н}}
* Tajik: {{t|tg|Хӯзистон}}
* Uyghur: {{t|ug|خۇزىستان}}
{{trans-bottom}}

[[Category:English terms suffixed with -stan]]
