==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:LocationUzbekistan.png|thumb|200px|Uzbekistāna (Āzijā)]]
[[File:Flag of Uzbekistan.svg|thumb|130px|Uzbekistānas karogs]]

===Etymology===
Via other European languages, ultimately borrowed from {{bor|lv|uz|Oʻzbekiston}}, itself from {{cog|uz|oʻzbek}} and {{cog|fa|ـستان|tr=-estân}}, a common ending for country names. In {{noncog|lv|-}}, the word was made into a feminine, 4th-declension noun, following the general pattern for country names.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfap|lv}}

===Proper noun===
{{lv-proper noun|f|4th}}

# {{tcl|lv|Uzbekistan|id=Q265|place_official=lv:Uzbekistānas Republika}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''Uzbekistānas''' karogs|the flag of '''Uzbekistan'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|Taškenta ir '''Uzbekistānas''' lielākā pilsēta|Tashkent is the largest city of '''Uzbekistan'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''Uzbekistāna''' ir 56. lielākā valsts pēc platības|'''Uzbekistan''' is the 56th largest country by area|inline=1}}

====Declension====
{{lv-decl-noun|Uzbekistān|a|4th|no-pl||||proper}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|lv|uzbekisks}}
* {{l|lv|uzbeks}}, {{l|lv|uzbekiete}}
* {{l|lv|uzbeku valoda}}
