Page 67 Pakistāna: Skipped, no changes
Page 67 Pakistāna: -------- begin text --------
{{also|pakistana|Pakistānā}}
==Latvian==
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=lv}}
[[File:LocationPakistan.png|thumb|200px|Pakistāna (Āzijā)]]
[[File:Flag of Pakistan.svg|thumb|130px|Pakistānas karogs]]

===Etymology===
Via other European languages, ultimately a [[borrowing]] from the local name of the country, with two converging origins: on the one hand, from {{uder|lv|ur|پاکستان||Land of the Pure}}, from {{cog|ur|پاک||pure, holy, immaculate, chaste, undefiled|tr=pak}} and {{cog|fa|ستان||land|tr=stân}}; on the other hand, a coinage by [[w:Choudhry Rahmat Ali|Choudhry Rahmat Ali]], who published it in the pamphlet ''Now or Never'' on January 28, 1933 as an acronym of the names of the "Muslim homelands" of western India: '''P'''unjab, '''A'''fghania, '''K'''ashmir, '''S'''indh, and Balochis'''tan'''. An '''i''' was later added to the English rendition of the name to ease pronunciation.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfap|lv}}

===Proper noun===
{{lv-proper noun|f|4th}}

# {{tcl|lv|Pakistan|id=Q843}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''Pakistānas''' karogs|the flag of '''Pakistan'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|mūsdienās joprojām '''Pakistānai''' ar Indiju ir konflikts par musulmaņu apdzīvoto Kašmīru|today '''Pakistan''' still has a conflict with India about the Muslim-populated (region of) Kashmir|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|1998. gadā Pakistānā dzīvoja 132 miljoni iedzīvotāji|in 1998 there lived in '''Pakistan''' 132 million inhabitants|inline=1}}

====Declension====
{{lv-decl-noun|Pakistān|a|4th|no-pl||||proper|extrawidth=-60}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|lv|Pakistānas Islāma Republika}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|lv|pakistānisks}}
* {{l|lv|pakistānietis}}, {{l|lv|pakistāniete}}
-------- end text --------
