==Chinese==
{{zh-forms|gloss=-}}
{{zh-wp}}

===Pronunciation===
{{zh-pron
|m=sītǎn
|c=si1 taan2
|mn=xm,zz:su-thán/qz:sir-thán
|cat=suf, pn
}}

===Etymology 1===
Ultimately from Indo-Iranian languages such as {{der|zh|fa|ـستان|tr=-estân}}, from {{der|zh|iir-pro|*stáHnam}}. See also {{ltc-l|震旦|gloss=Cīnastan, abode of the Cīna}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|zh|suffix}}

# [[-stan]] {{gloss|frequently found in country and region names of Central Asia}}
#* {{zh-x|她 對 幾個 斯坦 鄰居 更 是 充滿 隔閡，毫無 興趣。|She feels there's even a barrier between her few '''-stan''' neighbors, apathetic to them.|ref='''2018''' October 15, {{lang|zh|刘子超}} (Liu Zichao), {{lang|zh|《[http://static.nfapp.southcn.com/content/201810/19/c1585986.html 比什凯克　一座中亚边城的浮世绘]》}}, in {{lang|zh|《南方人物周刊》}} [''Southern People Weekly''], {{ISSN|1672-8335}}, issue 569, page 64}}
# {{lb|zh|often|humorous}} {{n-g|Used to form fictitious or metaphoric country names, often with a connotation of it being an exotic or hostile country.}}
#: {{zh-x|安資斯坦|Ancapistan}}
# {{lb|zh|neologism|derogatory|ethnic slur}} [[-stan]] {{gl|used after European and American place names to emphasize that there are many Middle Easterners or Muslims there}}
#: {{zh-x|^法蘭西斯坦|Franco'''stan''' (France)}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{zh-l|巴勒斯坦}} also ends with {{lang|zh|斯坦}}, but it is not formed with this suffix.

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|zh|巴基斯坦|吉爾吉斯斯坦|塔吉克斯坦|達吉斯坦|庫爾德斯坦|土庫曼斯坦|哈薩克斯坦|烏茲別克斯坦|突厥斯坦|塔塔爾斯坦|韃靼斯坦|興都斯坦|印度斯坦|拉賈斯坦|俾路支斯坦|巴爾蒂斯坦|班圖斯坦|維吾爾斯坦}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{bor|zh|en|Stan}}.

====Proper noun====
{{head|zh|proper noun}}

# [[Stan]] (a male [[given name]] in [[English]])

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|zh|de|Stein}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|zh|suffix}}

# -[[Stein|stein]] (''stone'', often appearing as a part of a geographical or personal name)

=====Derived terms=====
{{col3|zh|愛因斯坦|霍爾斯坦|伯恩斯坦|溫斯坦|維根斯坦}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{bor|zh|fr|Stains}}.

====Proper noun====
{{head|zh|proper noun}}

# [[Stains]] (a city in France)
