==Persian==
{{wikipedia|lang=fa|sc=fa-Arab}}

[[File:Locator_map_Iran_Khuzestan_Province.png|thumb|right|Location of Khuzestan within Iran]]

===Etymology===
From {{m|fa|خوز|tr=xuz||Susia}} and {{m|fa|ـستان|tr=-estân||place}}, meaning land of the Khuzi (Susian) people, the original inhabitants of the region. Alternatively borrowed wholly from {{der|fa|pal|𐭧𐭥𐭰𐭮𐭲𐭭|ts=hūzestān|lit=land of Hūz}}, itself from {{m|pal|tr=hwc|ts=hūz}} + {{m|pal|tr=-stʾn'|ts=-estān||[[-stan]]}}.

The first component is from {{der|fa|peo|𐎢𐎺𐎩|ts=ʰūvja-||[[Elam]], [[Elamite]]}}, or from the name of [[Susa]]. Etymologically, compare {{m|fa|اهواز}}, the Arabized broken-plural of Middle Persian {{m|pal|tr=hwc|ts=hūz|t=Susia}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fa-IPA|xōzistān}}

===Proper noun===
{{fa-regional|خوزستان|خوزستان|Хӯзистон}}
{{fa-proper noun|tr=xuzestân}}

# {{tcl|fa|Khuzestan|id=Q241119}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fa|خوزستانی|tr=xuzestâni|t=Khuzestani}}
