====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|sarā busˈtān}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=sarâbostan}}

# [[garden]] [[attached]] to a [[building]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|title={{w|Safarnama|Safarnāma}}|trans-title=Book of Travels|author={{w|Nasir Khusraw|Nāṣir-i Khusraw}}|year=c. 1060|url=https://ganjoor.net/naserkhosro/safarname/sh44|text=اندر شهر در میان سراها باغچه‌ها و اشجار باشد و آب از چاه دهند و در حرم سلطان '''سرابستان‌'''هاست که از آن نیکوتر نباشد و دولاب‌ها ساخته‌اند که آن بساتین را آب دهد|tr=andar šahr dar miyān sarā-hā u bāğči-hā u ašjār u āb az čāh dahand u dar haram-i sultān '''sarābustān'''-hā-st ki az ān nēkū-tar na-bāšad u dōlāb-hā sāxta-and ki ān basātīn rā āb dahad.|t=In the middle of the city, there are mansions and gardens. Water comes from wells. There are '''gardens attached to mansions''' in the king's private quarters, and nothing is better than that. Water wheels have been built to water those gardens.}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{af|fa|سراب|tr1=sarâb|t1=mirage|ـستان|tr2=-estân}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|sarābisˈtān}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=sarâbestan}}

# {{lb|fa|poetic}} [[world]] of [[mirage]]s; [[world]] of [[vanity]]; [[world]] of [[ephemeral]] [[thing]]s
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:دیوان شاه نعمت‌الله|trans-title=Dīvān of Shāh Ni'matullāh|author={{w|Shah Nimatullah Wali|Shāh Ni'matullāh-i Walī}}|year=c. 1400|url=https://ganjoor.net/shahnematollah/ghazalshv/sh1278|text=چون رسیدی در این '''سرابستان'''<br>هم مرادی از این سرا بستان|tr=čōn rasīdī dar īn '''sarābistān'''<br>ham murādē az īn sarā bistān|t=When you arrive in this '''world of mirages''',<br>Take away desire, too, from this mansion.}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|ota|سرابستان|tr=serâbistân}}
