# {{lb|en|musical instruments}} A concave plate of [[brass]] or [[bronze]] that produces a [[sharp]], ringing sound when struck: played either in [[pairs]], by striking them together, or singly by striking with a [[drumstick]] or the like.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|V|3|text=The trumpets, sackbuts, psalteries and fifes,<br>Tabours and '''cymbals''' and the shouting Romans,<br>Make the sun dance.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|1 Corinthians|13||text=Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, and have not charity, I am become as sounding brass, or a tinkling '''cymbal'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aureng-zebe|5|text=Trumpets and Drums shall fright her from the Throne,<br>As sounding '''Cymbals''' aid the lab'ring Moon.}}
#* '''1881–82''', {{w|Walt Whitman}}, ''Leaves of Grass'', "The Mystic Trumpeter":
#*: I see the Crusaders' tumultuous armies—hark, how the '''cymbals''' clang ...

