===Suffix===
{{head|en|suffixes}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Used to form the names of [[measuring]] [[device]]s.}}

====Usage notes====
* Whereas the spelling of the unit of length varies between British (''metre'') and American (''meter'') English, the spelling of this suffix is ''-meter'' in both. {{m|en|-metre}} is a nonstandard alternative form found in British English.
* Words with the suffix ''-'''o'''meter'' always have a primary stress on the [[antepenultimate]] syllable: ''[[barometer|ba'''rom'''eter]]'', ''[[speedometer|spee'''dom'''eter]]'', ''[[tachometer|ta'''chom'''eter]]'', etc. Words derived from ''[[meter]]'' (or ''[[metre]]'') with a prefix usually have a primary stress on the first syllable: ''[[centimeter|'''cen'''timeter]]'', ''[[millimeter|'''mil'''limeter]]'', etc.

