===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|uncountable}} [[something|Something]]; [[thing]]; [[stuff]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=VI|canto=IX|stanza=7|passage=They prayd him sit, and gave him for to feed / Such homely '''what''' as serves the simple clowne, / That doth despise the dainties of the towne{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The identity of a thing, as an answer to a question of ''what''.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Norman K. Denzin; Yvonna S. Lincoln|title=The SAGE Handbook of Qualitative Research|page=493
|passage=The emphasis on the interplay between the hows and '''whats''' of interpretive practice is paramount.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Something that is addressed by {{m|en||what}}, as opposed to a person, addressed by {{m|en|who}}.
#* '''2012''', "We Are Both", season 2, episode 2 of ''{{w|Once Upon a Time}}''
#*: Regina: What are you?
#*: Rumplestiltskin: What? What? What? My, my, what a rude question! I am not a '''what'''.

===Particle===
{{en-part}}

# {{lb|en|Manglish|Singlish}} {{n-g|Emphasizes the truth of an [[assertion]] made to [[contradict]] an evidently false assumption held by the listener.}}
#: {{ux|en|— Too bad there isn't a library nearby.<br/>— The National Library is a five-minute walk from here '''what'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=L. C. Cheong|title=Youth in the Army|page=142|year=1978|text=Most things come from Europe '''what'''.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=yansimon52|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|year=2007|passage={{...}} they can't be the same '''what'''?}}

