Page 10 -ment: -------- begin text --------
{{also|ment}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|⠰⠞}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|-ment}}, from {{der|en|fro|-ment|id=nominal}}, from {{der|en|la|-mentum}}.

===Suffix===
{{en-suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Attached to a [[verb]] to form a [[noun]] meaning the action denoted by the verb or its result}}.

====Usage notes====
Generally attached to stem without changes, except when the stem ends in ''-dge,'' where the ''-e'' is sometimes dropped, as in {{m|en|abridgment}}, {{m|en|acknowledgment}}, {{m|en|judgment}}, and {{m|en|lodgment}}, with the forms without ''-e'' being preferred in American English. Of these, ''judgment'' is the most significant, and usage varies globally; see [[w:Judgment (law)#Spelling|Judgment: Spelling]] for discussion.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|-tion}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|en}}

