==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|fr|frm|-ment|id=adverbial}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|-ment|id=adverbial}}, from {{inh|fr|la|mens|mente}}.

====Suffix====
{{fr-suffix}}

# {{senseid|fr|adverbial}} {{n-g|Attaches to an adjective in the feminine singular to form the corresponding adverb.}}
#: {{sufex|fr|franc|franchement|alt1=franche}}

=====Usage notes=====
With adjectives ending in ''-ant(e)'', ''-ent(e)'', the suffix combines with the ending to produce ''-amment'', ''-emment'' (both pronounced {{IPAchar|/a.mɑ̃/}}).

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|fr|id=adverbial}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|fr|frm|-ment|id=nominal}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|-ment|id=nominal}}, from {{inh|fr|la|-mentum}}.

====Suffix====
{{fr-suffix}}

# {{senseid|fr|nominal}} {{n-g|Forms nouns from verbs, usually indicating a resulting action or state.}}
#: {{sufex|fr|parer|parement}}
#: {{sufex|fr|abandonner|abandonnement}}
#: {{sufex|fr|manier|maniement}}

