==North Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|apc|ar|ال}}.

====Article====
{{head|apc|article|head=الـ|tr=l-}}

# [[the]]

=====Usage notes=====
* The article in fact consists solely of the consonant {{IPAchar|/l/}}, which is assimilated to the same onsets as in Standard Arabic (see above). Following the usage note there, some speakers extend this process of assimilation to the now-coronal {{m|apc|ج|tr=j|ts=ʒ}}.
* An epenthetic linking vowel is added as phonotactically necessary, be it before the article or after, in order to avoid a three-consonant cluster. Note that its notation with a schwa is not meant to represent IPA {{IPAchar|[ə]}}, as its actual value varies between {{IPAchar|/i~e~o/}} depending on context:
*: {{uxi|apc|النص المكتوب|tr=n-naṣṣ '''əl'''-maktūb|the written text}}
*: {{uxi|apc|الكتاب المقدس|tr='''lə'''-ktāb '''lə'''-mʾaddas|t=the Holy Book, i.e. the Bible}}
* Assimilation is optionally ignored when the article precedes a consonant cluster where the initial consonant would normally trigger assimilation, as the epenthetic vowel separates them if it appears:
*: {{uxi|apc|الولاد الصغار|tr=lə-wlād '''lə'''-ṣḡār|t=the small children}}

===Etymology 2===
Reduction of the definite relative pronoun {{m|apc|اللي|tr=lli}} or its alternative form {{m|apc|لي|tr=li}}.

====Pronoun====
{{head|apc|pronoun|tr=l-}}

# {{contraction of|apc|اللي|nocap=1|nodot=1}}
#* {{quote-book|apc
|title=Yara
|author=w:Said Akl
|year=1961
|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5d5V2RCo3wk
|text=يَارَا '''ال'''جّدَايِلهَا شُقْر
<!-- Probably not replaceable by automated transliteration, thanks to the j-assimilation -->
|tr=yāra '''j-'''jdāyilha šuʾr
|t=Yara, '''whose''' braids are gold
|lit=Yara '''who''' her braids are gold
}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Although this contraction is superficially identical to the definite article, some speakers do not assimilate it to a following coronal, allowing the two to be told apart in this context. Other speakers do, such as Said Akl in the reading linked from the quote above.

