==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
{{rfe|fa}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=al}}

# {{lb|fa|Dari}} [[plough]]; the beam of a plough

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|fa|ال زدن|tr=al zadan}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|fa|ar|ال}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|‿l-}}
* Can assimilate in pronunciation to following consonants, see usage notes for Arabic {{l|ar|ال}}.

====Particle====
{{head|fa|particle|tr=l-}}

# Used to join two words in compound terms and phrases from Arabic.
#: {{l|fa|بین‌المللی|t=international|tr={{xlit|fa-cls|بَیْنَ‌المِلَلِی}}/{{xlit|fa-ira|بِیْنُ‌المِلَلی}}}}
#: {{l|fa|بالکل|t=totally, entirely|tr={{xlit|fa-cls|بِالکُلّ}}/{{xlit|fa-ira|بِالکُلّ}}}} 

=====Usage notes=====
* As Persian typically borrows the uninflected form of Arabic nouns, not the definite form, Persian words from Arabic almost never contain the definite article {{l|ar|ال}}. Predominantly, the particle  only appears in compound terms derived from Arabic and acts more as a "connector" between two terms, rather than as a definite article, which is its primary purpose in Arabic.

==South Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|ال}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|l<p:l>}}

===Article===
{{head|ajp|article|head=الـ|tr=l-}}

# [[the]] {{q|definite article}}

====Usage notes====
* Phonemically, the article consists solely of the consonant {{IPAchar|/l/}}, which is assimilated to the same onsets as in Standard Arabic (see above), with some speakers extending the assimilation to the now-coronal {{m|ajp|ج|tr=j|ts=ʒ}}. While the epenthetic vowel {{IPAchar|[ɪ]}} may be added before or after in order to avoid problematic consonant clusters, different speakers may be more or less tolerant of these clusters; those who tolerate an initial two-consonant cluster may not insert the vowel before {{IPAchar|/l/}}, meaning the article may be virtually inaudible in cases that the {{IPAchar|/l/}} is assimilated.
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ال]][[ميّ]] [[ال]][[بارد|باردة]]|tr='''(i)l'''-mayy '''(i)l'''-bārde|the cold water}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-الميّ الباردة.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ال]][[شبّ|شباب]] [[ال]][[شاطر|شاطرين]]|tr='''(i)š'''-šabāb '''(i)š'''-šāṭrīn|t=the smart guys}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-الشباب الشاطرين.wav|a=Ramallah}}
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ال]][[كتاب]] [[ال]][[كبير]]|tr='''li'''-ktāb '''li'''-kbīr|t=the big book}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-الكتاب الكبير.wav|a=Ramallah}}
* Assimilation is optionally ignored when the article precedes a consonant cluster where the initial consonant would normally trigger assimilation, as the epenthetic vowel separates them if it appears:
*: {{uxi|ajp|[[ال]][[زلمة]] [[ال]][[زغير]]|tr='''(i)z'''-zalame '''li'''-zḡīr|t=the small man}}
*: {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-الزلمة الزغير.wav|a=Ramallah}}
