#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-02-22|author=w:Andrew Sparrow|title=David Cameron's swipe at Boris Johnson in the Commons – verdict|journal=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2016/feb/22/david-camerons-swipe-at-boris-johnson-in-the-commons-verdict|passage=David Cameron gives a Commons statement after every EU summit and normally they follow a predictable pattern; he says that he set out with '''X''' number of aims, and then he explains he has achieved all '''X''' of them (even if he hasn’t). The most interesting comments normally come in the exchanges with MPs.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-05-19|author=Aaron Souppouris|title=Why Google can't stop making messaging apps|journal=w:Engadget|url=https://www.engadget.com/2016-05-19-why-google-cant-stop-making-messaging-apps.html|passage=But chances are that Google will continue to float new ideas before eventually merging the best of them into a single, coherent application, as it did with Hangouts. And then it'll start the process again. In the meantime, Google will spend money developing '''''x''''' number of duplicate apps, and users will have to deal with a confusing mess of applications on their home screens.}}

