===Etymology===
From {{inh|afb|ar|فِي}}. Compare {{cog|arz|فيه|tr=fī}}, {{cog|acw|فيه|tr=fī}}, and {{cog|ajp|فيه|tr=fī}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|afb|/fi/|a=Kuwait}}

===Determiner===
{{afb-determiner|tr=fi}}

# [[there is]], [[there are]]

====Usage notes====
The past tense [[there was]] and [[there were]] is formed by adding {{l|afb|كان|tr=kān}} before في, for example {{l|afb|كان في [[دونت]] بس خلصوا|tr=kān fī dunat/donat bas ḵaḷḷaṣaw|t=there were doughnuts but they finished}}

===Preposition===
{{afb-preposition|tr=fi}}

# forms the conjugated forms of the preposition {{l|afb|بْـ|tr=b|t=in, at}}
