Page 49 لا: -------- begin text --------
{{character info|ﻻ}}
{{character info|ﻼ}}

==Arabic==
{{wikipedia|لا النافية للجنس|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*lā}}. Compare {{cog|he|לֹא|tr=lo}}, which, in older texts, is used in the negative imperative and the negative existential indicative.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لَا}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-لا.ogg}}

====Particle====
{{ar-particle|لَا}}

# [[no]]
# [[not]]; ''negates an indicative present-tense verb''
# [[do]] [[not]]; ''expresses prohibition with a jussive verb''
#: {{uxi|ar|'''لَا''' نَنْسَ…|Let us '''not''' forget…}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''لَا''' يَفُتْكُمْ|You '''shall not''' miss it.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|49|11
|passage=يَا أَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا '''لَا''' يَسْخَرْ قَوْمٌ مِنْ قَوْمٍ عَسَى أَنْ يَكُونُوا خَيْرًا مِنْهُمْ وَلَا نِسَاءٌ مِنْ نِسَاءٍ عَسَى أَن يَكُنَّ خَيْرًا مِنْهُنَّ وَ'''لَا''' تَلْمِزُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَ'''لَا''' تَنَابَزُوا بِٱلْأَلْقَابِ
|translation=O you who have believed, let '''not''' a people ridicule people; perhaps they may be better than them; nor let women ridicule women; perhaps they may be better than them. And '''do not''' insult one another and '''do not''' call each other by names.
|subst=وَ/وَ-}}
#* Zuhayr ibn Abi Sulma
#*: {{quote|ar|يَا حَارِ '''لَا''' أُرْمَيَنْ مِنْكُمْ بِدَاهِيَةٍ / لَمْ يَلْقَهَا سُوقَةٌ قَبْلِي وَلَا مَلِكُ}}
#* Al-Farazdaq
#*: {{quote|ar|إِذَا مَا خَرَجْنَا مِنْ دِمَشْقَ '''فَلَا''' نَعُدْ / لَهَا أَبَدًا مَا دَامَ فِيهَا الْجُرَاضِمُ}}
# there is [[not]], there is [[no]], there is [[nothing]], [[nothing]] is
#: {{uxi|ar|'''لَا''' طَالِبَ حَاضِرٌ.|'''No''' student is present.}}
# [[not]]; ''negates any non-verbal sentence element''
# [[neither]], [[nor]]

=====Usage notes=====
As shown in the example, sense 4 generally governs a noun in the [[determinate state]] and the accusative case — that is, a noun without [[nunation]]. However, subsequent adjectives are in the [[indeterminate state]], meaning they are nunated:
* {{uxi|ar|'''لَا''' طَالِبَ مُجْتَهِدًا حَاضِرٌ|t='''No''' hard-working student is present.}}
If, instead of an adjective, there is an attributive prepositional phrase, the initial noun can be in either state:
* {{uxi|ar|'''لَا''' طَالِبَ لَدَيْنَا مُجْتَهِدًا حَاضِرٌ|t='''No''' hard-working student of ours is present.}}
* {{uxi|ar|'''لَا''' طَالِبًا لِلْعِلْمِ مُقَصِّرٌ|t='''No''' seeker of knowledge is delinquent.}}
Additionally, sense 4 can govern a preposition alone, with an implicit third-person singular masculine subject and no visible case or state. This is the origin of {{m|ar|لَا عَلَيْكَ|t=no worries|lit=there is not [anything] on you}} and similar collocations.

{{ArabForm2}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{antsense|no}} {{l|ar|نَعَم}}
* {{antsense|expresses prohibition with a jussive verb}} {{l|ar|لِـ}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|afb|لَأْ|tr=laʔ|t=no|لا|tr2=la|t2=don't (used before imperatives)}}
* {{desc|ajp|لأ|tr=laʔ|لا|tr2=la|t2=don't (with imperative or subjunctive)}}
* {{desc|mt|la|le}}
* {{desc|sw|la|bor=1}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|لَا}}

# [[not#Conjunction|not]], and not
#: {{usex|ar|أَحْضِرْ وَثَائِقَكَ '''لَا''' كُتُبَكَ|Bring your documents, '''not''' your books.}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|ar|بَلْ}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|مُكْرَهٌ أَخَاكَ لَا بَطَلٌ|pos=proverb}}{{sic}}

====Prefix====
{{head|ar|prefix|head=لَا}}

# [[non-]], [[un-]], [[in-]]
#: {{l|ar|لَاسُلْطَوِيّ}}
#: {{l|ar|لَاسِلْكِيّ}}
#: {{l|ar|لَامُبَالَاة}}
#: {{l|ar|لَافَقَارِيَّات}}
#: {{l|ar|لَامَرْكَزِيَّة}}

