===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|لَا}}.

===Particle===
{{ajp-particle|tr=la}}

# [[don't]] {{q|negative imperative}}
#: {{syn|ajp|ما|ـش|tr1=mā|tr2=-š}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[لا]] [[نسي|تنسى]] [[عمل|تعمل]] [[واجب|واجباتك]]!|tr='''la''' tinsa tiʕmil wājbātak|t='''Don't''' forget to do your homework!}}
# may it [[not]] {{q|with subjunctive verb}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[لا]] [[كان|يكون]] [[صاب]][[ه]] [[إشي]].|tr='''la''' ykūn ṣābo ʔiši|t=May it '''not''' be that something hurt him.}}

====Usage notes====
* The negative imperative with {{l-self|ajp|لا|tr=la}} is more formal, while {{l|ajp|ما|tr=mā}} and the suffix {{l|ajp|ـش|tr=-š}} are more common in informal speech.
* {{l-self|ajp|لا [[كان|يكون]]|tr=la ykūn}} is often used a fixed expression not conjugated by person and number and might be written as one word {{l|ajp|ليكون|tr=laykūn}}.

====See also====
* {{l|ajp|لأ|tr=laʔ|t=no}}

