==Arabic==
{{ar-rootbox|ق ب ل}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَبِلَ|قَبَّلَ|قُبُل|قَبْلُ|قَبْلَ|قِبَل|قُبَل}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I|i|a}}

# to [[accept]]
#: {{ux|ar|قَبِلَ العَرِيسُ بِفَرَحٍ طَلَبَ الزَّوَاجِ.|The groom accepted the marriage proposal with joy.}}
# to [[receive]] kindly, to give a friendly [[reception]]
# to [[acquiesce]], to [[put up with]], to [[agree]], to [[consent]], to [[assent]]
# to [[admit]]
# to [[obey]], to [[yield]], to [[give in]], to [[submit]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I|i|a|passive=y|vn=قَبُول،قُبُول}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|ar|رَفَضَ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II}}

# {{senseid|ar|to kiss}} to [[kiss]]
#: {{syn|ar|بَاسَ}}
#* {{quote-book|1=ar|year=a. 965 |author=w:Al-Mutanabbi |title={{l|ar||ضَيْفٌ أَلَمَّ بِرَأْسِي غَيْرَ مُحْتَشِمِ}} |url= http://www.almotanabbi.com/poemPage.do?poemId=232 |passage='''قَبَّلْتُهَا''' وَدُمُوعِي مَزْجُ أَدْمُعِهَا // وَ'''قَبَّلَتْنِي''' عَلَى خَوْفٍ فَمًا لِفَمِ<br/>فَذُقْتُ مَاءَ حَيَاةٍ مِنْ مُقَبَّلِهَا // لَوْ صَابَ تُرْبًا لَأَحْيَا سَالِفَ الْأُمَمِ|t='''I kissed her''', and my tears mixed with hers, // and '''she kissed me''' timidly, mouth to mouth.<br/>I tasted the water of life from her kiss, // which may revive the ancestors, if it hit the earth.}}
# to go [[south]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قُبُل|head2=قُبْل|m}}

# [[fore]], [[front]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:{{w|Avicenna|ابن سينا}}<t:Avicenna>|url=https://lib.efatwa.ir/45207/1/525|title=ar:القانون في الطب<t:{{w|The Canon of Medicine|Canon Medicinae}}>|year=1025|passage=كرمدانة‏.‏<br/>الماهية‏:‏ حبها يمدحه الأطباء‏.‏<br/>أعضاء النفض‏:‏ تسخن ال'''قبل''' جداً وتسهل الماء والمرّة‏.‏|t=Myrtle seed.<br/>What it is: Its seed is praised by the physicians.<br/>Palpitating organs: It heats the '''front''' well and releases the waters and bile.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُبُل|head2=قُبْل}}

