{{character info}}
==Translingual==

===Letter===
{{head|mul|letter|sc=Phnx|tr=š}} [[Image:Phoenician sin.svg|15px]]

# The 21st letter of the [[Appendix:Phoenician abjad|Phoenician abjad]], called [[shin]].

==Phoenician==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|phn|sem-pro|*šinn-|t=tooth}}. The association of "tooth" with this letter was the result of folk etymology and its shape resembling a tooth. The letter originally depicted a [[composite bow]], which usually has the tips curving away from the archer when unstrung.<ref>{{R:American Heritage Dictionary|shin}}</ref><ref>Albright, W. F. (1948). "The Early Alphabetic Inscriptions from Sinai and their Decipherment". Bulletin of the American Schools of Oriental Research. 110 (110): 6–22 [p. 15].</ref>

Related to {{cog|syc|ܫ}}, {{cog|ar|ش}}, {{cog|he|ש}}, {{cog|arc|ܫ}}. More at [[w:Shin (letter)|Shin]].

====Letter====
{{head|phn|letter|sc=Phnx|tr=š}}

# The twenty-first letter of the Phoenician abjad, called [[shin]].

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{head|phn|noun|tr=š|head={{t2i|sc=Phnx|š}}}}

# [[sheep]]

===References===
<references/>

{{c|phn|Mammals}}
