==North Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|apc|ar|ظَلَّ}}.

===Verb===
{{head|apc|verb|tr=ḍall|nonpast|يضَلّ|f1tr=yḍall}}

# {{lb|apc|intransitive}} to [[stay]], to [[remain]]
#: {{synonyms|apc|بِقِي|tr1=biʔi}}
#: {{ux|apc|ضَلَّيْت بِالبَيْت|tr=ḍallēt bil-bēt|t=I stayed home.}}
# to [[keep]] doing {{q|construed with either a present-progressive participle, {{m|apc|عَم|tr=ʕam}}, or a subjunctive verb}}
#: {{ux|apc|هو ضل يحكي ونحنا ضلينا ماشيين|tr=huwwe ḍall yiḥki w-niḥna ḍallēna māšyīn|t=He kept talking and we kept walking.}} <!-- Unintentional rhyme, hah -->

====Usage notes====
* Uniquely, this verb can also be conjugated by substituting a matching '''object''' pronoun for the normal ending of a given conjugation. For example, {{m|apc||ضَلّْ|tr=ḍall|t=he stayed}}, {{m|apc||ضَلَّيْتُوا|tr=ḍallaytu|t=you stayed|pos=plural ''you''}}, {{m|apc||بِيضَلُّوا|tr=biḍallu|t=they stay}}, and {{m|apc||ضَلِّي|tr=ḍalli|t=stay!|pos=feminine imperative}} can alternatively be {{m|apc||ضَلُّه|tr=ḍallo|t=he stayed}}, {{m|apc||ضَلَّيْتْكُن|tr=ḍallaytkun|t=you stayed|pos=plural ''you''}}, {{m|apc||بِيضَلّْهُن|tr=biḍall(h)un|t=they stay}}, and {{m|apc||ضَلِّك|tr=ḍallik|t=stay!|pos=feminine imperative}}. The conjugation {{m|apc||ضَلَّيْنَا|tr=ḍallayna|t=we stayed}} looks the same in both paradigms.
* For some speakers, the imperative is suppleted by one fashioned on {{m|apc|خَلَّى|tr=ḵalla|t=to let be, to keep [as is]}}. This suppletive form mandatorily uses object pronouns to conjugate: its singular forms use the base {{m|apc||خَلِّيك|tr=ḵallīk-}}. The plural can either be {{m|apc||خَلُّوكُن|tr=ḵallūkun|t=stay!|pos=plural imperative}} or {{m|apc||خَلِّيكُن|tr=ḵallīkun|t=stay!|pos=plural imperative}}.

