===Etymology 1===
{{dercat|fa|ira-pro|iir-pro|ine-pro}}
From {{inh|fa|pal|BNPŠE}}, {{m|pal|𐭡𐭭𐭯𐭱𐭤|tr=xwad}}, from {{inh|fa|peo|*hvatah}}. Related to {{m|fa|خدا|tr=xodâ|t=God}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|xwad}}

====Noun====
{{fa-regional|خود|خود|худ}}
{{fa-noun|tr=xod}}

# [[self]], the [[self]]

====Pronoun====
{{fa-regional|خود|خود|худ}}
{{head|fa|pronoun|tr=xod}}

# {{lb|fa|reflexive pronoun}} [[self]], [[-self]]
#: {{syn|fa|خویش|tr=xiš|pos=literary}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|year=c. 1260|title={{w|Masnavi|The ''Masnavi''}}|author=w:Rumi|text=حمله بر خود می‌کنی ای ساده مرد، همچو آن شیری که بر خود حمله کرد.|tr=hamle bar '''xod''' mi-koni ey sâde mard, hamčo ân šir-i ke bar '''xod''' hamle kard.|t=You are attacking '''yourself''', o simple man, like that lion who attacked '''himself'''.}}
#* {{quote-song|fa|year=2009|author=w:Shadmehr Aghili|title={{l|fa||تقدیر|tr=taqdir}}|text=تو با '''خودت''' هم دشمنی.|tr=to bâ '''xod'''-et ham došman-i.|t=You are an enemy even with your'''self'''.}}
# {{lb|fa|emphatic}} one's [[own]] {{q|in possessive constructions}}
#: {{syn|fa|خویش|tr=xiš|pos=literary}}
#: {{ux|fa|مادر خود را نمی‌شناسی؟|tr=mâdar-e '''xod'''-râ ne-mi-šenâsi?|t=-|q=More literary}}
#: {{ux|fa|مادر خودت رو نمی‌شناسی؟|tr=mâdar-e '''xod'''-et-o ne-mi-šnâsi?|t=Don’t you recognize your '''own''' mother?|q=More colloquial}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|fa||خود|tr=xod}} can occur both in isolation and before a suffixed pronominal [[clitic]] such as {{m|fa|ـم|tr=-am|t=my}}, {{m|fa|ـت|tr=-at, et|t=your}}, and {{m|fa|ـش|tr=-aš, -eš|t=his/her}}. In isolation, it serves as a general reflexive pronoun for any subject:

* {{ux|fa|خود را دیدم|tr=xod-râ didam|t=I saw [my]self}}
* {{ux|fa|خود را دیدی|tr=xod-râ didi|t=you saw [your]self}}

The pronominal clitics specify the pronoun:

* {{ux|fa|خودم را دیدم|tr=xod-am-râ didam|t=I saw myself}}
* {{ux|fa|خودت را دیدی|tr=xod-at-râ didi|t=you saw yourself}}

In colloquial Persian, the suffixed forms are almost always used.

