==Persian==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|fa|The modern sense of "challenge" is not found in Steingass, and the word in general seems quite rare in classical sources. Might the modern usage be influenced by {{ncog|en|challenge}}? Compare {{m|fa|تنش|tr=taneš|t=tension}}.}}

From {{af|fa|<alt:چال><tr:čâl><pos:seemingly a variant of {{m|fa|چل|tr=čal}}, present stem of {{m|fa|چلیدن|tr=čalidan|t=to walk, to go}}>|ـش<tr:-eš>}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|čāˈliš}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=čâleš}}

# [[challenge]], [[struggle]]
# {{lb|fa|archaic}} [[exertion]] in [[battle]]; [[martial]] [[conduct]]; {{lb|fa|loosely}} [[battle]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:اسکندرنامه|trans-title=Iskandarnāma|year=1188|author={{w|Nizami Ganjavi|Niẓāmī Ganjavī}}|url=https://ganjoor.net/nezami/5ganj/sharafname/sh16|text=بفرمود شه تا دلیران روم<br>نمایند '''چالش''' در آن مرز و بوم|tr=bifarmūd šah tā dalērān-i rūm<br>nimāyand '''čāliš''' dar ān marz u būm|t=The king ordered that the brave men of Rome<br>Should display their '''martial gait''' in that borderland and country.|footer=(Classical Persian transliteration)}}
# {{lb|fa|obsolete|original sense}} [[proud]] and [[saunter]]ing [[gait]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fa|چالشی|tr=čâleši|t=challenging}}

===References===
* {{R:STEIN}}
* {{R:fa:Nourai|page=260}}
