Page 145 شاهنامه آخرش خوشه: Skipped, no changes
Page 145 شاهنامه آخرش خوشه: -------- begin text --------
==Persian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|شاهنامه آخرش خوش است|tr=šâhnâme âxareš xoš ast}}

===Etymology===
Literally means “the end of {{m|en|Shahnameh}} is the pleasant part”. Several etymological theories exist:<ref>{{fa-rtl|[http://isna.ir/fa/news/92022516938/%DA%86%D8%B1%D8%A7-%D9%85%DB%8C-%DA%AF%D9%88%DB%8C%D9%86%D8%AF-%D8%B4%D8%A7%D9%87%D9%86%D8%A7%D9%85%D9%87-%D8%A2%D8%AE%D8%B1%D8%B4-%D8%AE%D9%88%D8%B4%D9%87 چرا می‌گویند «شاهنامه آخرش خوشه»؟]}}</ref><ref>{{fa-rtl|سجّاد‌آيدنلو. [http://bukharamag.com/wp-content/uploads/downloads/2011/10/%DA%86%D8%B1%D8%A7-%D8%B4%D8%A7%D9%87%D9%86%D8%A7%D9%85-%D8%A2%D8%AE%D8%B1%D8%B4-%D8%AE%D9%88%D8%B4-%D8%A7%D8%B3%D8%AA.pdf «چرا شاهنامه آخرش خوش است؟»]. ''بخارا''. سال چهاردهم. شماره 81. خرداد - تیر 1390}}</ref>
* The end of ''Shahnameh'' is about Muslim invasion of Persia, death of {{w|Rostam Farrokhzād}} and {{w|Yazdegerd III}}, and collapse of the {{w|Sassanian Empire|Sassanian Persian Empire}}; so it is a sarcastic idiom. The end of the story of {{w|Rustam}}, a major story of the work, is tragic, too.
* According to {{w|Mohammad-Ali Eslami Nodooshan}}, it is not sarcastic, and it refers to the work's “core story”, that is, the war between Iran and {{l|en|Turan}}, and the eventual Iranian victory. However, this story is in the middle of ''Shahnameh''.
* Another explanation is that it does not refer to the stories of ''Shahnameh'', but the legendary story about {{w|Ferdowsi}} himself and the unexpected behaviour of Sultan {{w|Mahmud of Ghazni}} with him after he finished composing the work.
* There is an old tradition and ceremony between some Persian-speakers, called ''Shahnameh-Khani'', or {{m|en|naqqali}} ({{m|fa|نقالی}}) (recitation of ''Shahnameh''). The idiom may refer to the rejoicing after full recitation of the poem.

===Idiom===
{{head|fa|idiom|head=[[شاهنامه]] [[آخر]][[ش]] [[خوش]][[ه]]|tr=šâhnâme âxareš xoš-e}}

# don't judge early: things may unexpectedly end in a bad way; [[he who laughs last laughs best]]

====Usage notes====
Used when someone is insisting on doing an unwise deed.

===References===
<references/>
-------- end text --------
