* {{l|apc|هَيكِي|tr=hayke, hēke}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|apc|ar|هَٰكَذَا|t=thus, so}}, perhaps via an intermediate form like the rarer {{cog|ajp|هَيْكَا|tr=hēka|pos=also found in other varieties}}. Cognate to {{cog|arz|كِدَه|tr=keda}}, {{m|arz|كِدَا|tr=keda}}, {{cog|ary|هَكدَا|tr=hākda}}, {{m|ary|هَكَّا|tr=hākka}}, {{cog|acm|هَيچ|tr=hīč}}, and others.

===Adverb===
{{head|apc|adverb|tr=hayk, hēk}}

# [[so]], [[thus]], [[like so]]
# [[this]] [[way]] (i.e., [[direction]]), [[that]] [[way]] (i.e., [[direction]]) (e.g., to [[look]] [[this]] or [[that]] [[way]], i.e., [[in]] [[this]] or [[that]] [[direction]])
# {{lbl|apc|by extension}} [[this]], [[that]]; {{ngd|used as a pronominal object of {{m|apc|قال|tr=ʔāl|t=to say}}, {{m|apc|فكّر|tr=fakkar|t=to think}}, and similar transitive verbs of expression, {{m|apc|عِمِل|tr=ʕimil|t=to do}} and synonyms, and comparative {{m|apc|مِن|tr=min|t=than}}.}}
#: {{ux|apc|ليه قلت '''هيك'''؟ ليه عملت '''هيك'''؟ فكرتك أفضل من '''هيك'''|tr=lē ʾilt '''hēk'''? lē ʿmilt '''hēk'''? fakkartak ʾafḍal min '''hēk'''|t=Why did you say '''that'''? Why did you do '''that'''? I thought you were better than '''this'''.|lit=Why did you say '''so'''? Why did you do '''so'''? I thought you better than '''so'''}}

====Usage notes====
* The use of demonstratives like {{m|apc|هيدا|tr=hayda|t=this|pos=proximal demonstrative}} and especially {{m|apc|هيداك|tr=haydāk|t=that|pos=distal demonstrative}} in the contexts demonstrated by the last usage example, which would parallel English usage of "this" and "that", is ungrammatical.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|apc|[[مشاك]]، [[مشيك]]|tr=mišēk|t=no?|pos=tag question}} <!-- spelling?? -->

===Determiner===
{{head|apc|determiner|tr=hayk, hēk}}

# [[such]]; such kind, this kind of
#: {{ux|apc|ما فيي اتحمل هيك حكي منك!|tr=Ma fīyi tḥammal '''haik''' ḥaki minnak.|t=I can’t stand '''this kind of''' talk on your part.}}

==South Levantine Arabic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ajp|هيكي|tr=hēke}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|هَٰكَذَا|t=thus, so}}. Cognate to {{cog|arz|كِدَه|tr=keda}}, {{m|arz|كِدَا|tr=keda}}, {{cog|ary|هَكدَا|tr=hākda}}, {{m|ary|هَكَّا|tr=hākka}}, {{cog|acm|هَيچ|tr=hēč}}, and others.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|hēk<p:heːk>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-AdrianAbdulBaha-هيك.wav|a=Ramallah}}

===Adverb===
{{ajp-adverb|tr=hēk}}

# [[so]], [[thus]], [[like]] [[this]], [[like that]]
#: {{ux|ajp|[[مش]] [[هيك]]؟|tr=miš '''hēk'''?|t=Isn't that '''so'''?}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[لازم]] [[عمل|تعمل]][[ه]] [[هيك]].|tr=lāzem tiʕmelo '''hēk'''|t=You have to do it '''like this'''.}}
# {{lbl|ajp|by extension}} [[this]], [[that]]
#: {{ux|ajp|[[هو]] [[طويل|أطول]] [[من]] [[هيك]].|tr=hū ʔaṭwal min '''hēk'''|t=He's taller than '''that'''.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[ما]] [[قال|قلت]][[ش]] [[هيك]].|tr=ma ʔult-š '''hēk'''|t=I didn't say '''that'''.|lit=I didn't say '''so'''.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ajp|هيك هيك|tr=hēk hēk|t=such-and-such; anyway}}
* {{l|ajp|عشان هيك|tr=ʕašān hēk|t=therefore}}

===Determiner===
{{ajp-determiner|tr=hēk}}

# [[such]], [[like]] [[this]], [[like that]]
#: {{ux|ajp|[[ما]] [[حبّ|بحبّ]] [[تعامل|أتعامل]] [[مع]] [[هيك]] [[ناس]].|tr=mā baḥebb ʔatʕāmal maʕ '''hēk''' nās|t=I don't like to interact with '''such''' people.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[كان]] [[فيه]] [[تلاتة]] [[أربعة]] [[هيك]] [[شي]].|tr=kān fīh talāte ʔarbʕa '''hēk ši'''|t=There were about three or four.|lit=There were three, four, '''something like that'''.}}

{{cln|ajp|demonstrative adverbs}}
