==Arabic==
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|שָׁמִירָא|tr=šāmīrā}} / {{m|syc|ܫܡܝܪܐ|tr=šāmīrā|t=emery, adamant}}, having the usual <var>K</var>ā<var>L</var>ū<var>M</var> measure of Aramaisms, as {{l|ar||**سَامِير}} would be much more unfamiliar a form, while {{m|ar|س}} instead of {{m|ar|ش}} mimicks as usual the correspondence of words inheriting {{cog|sem-pro||*š}}. <!-- Also, would it be from Greek it would probable have the shape {{m|ar||**إِسْمِير}}. --><br/>Itself the Aramaic is deemed to be from {{der|ar|he|שָׁמִיר|tr=šāmī́r|t=emery, corundum, adamant}}, which is possibly related to {{cog|akk|𒉌𒌓𒌑|tr=<sup>NA₄</sup>U<sub>2</sub>|ts=šammu|t=emery, corundum, adamant}}, as well as to {{cog|egy|jsmr}}, {{m|egy|smr|t=emery}}, {{cog|grc|σμύρις|t=emery}}, {{cog|xcl|զմռնիտեան քար|t=emery}}, {{cog|sem|-}} borrowings.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَامُور}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَامُور|m}}

# [[corundum]], or other [[adamant]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَامُور}}

{{c|ar|Minerals}}
