Page 1 reference: Skipped, no changes
Page 1 reference: -------- begin text --------
{{also|référence|référencé}}
{{selfref|For information on how references should be handled on Wiktionary, see [[Wiktionary:References]]}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|mul=reference (computer science)}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}
From {{bor|en|frm|référence}}, from {{der|en|ML.|referentia}}, nominative neuter plural of {{m|la|referēns}}, present participle of {{m|la|referō||return, reply|lit=carry back}}.

Morphologically {{suffix|en|refer|ence|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛf.(ə)ɹəns/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-reference.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛfəɹɛns/|a=obsolete}}<ref>{{R:Critical Pronouncing Dictionary|Reference|448|1|ppage=1}}</ref>
* {{hyphenation|en|ref|er|ence}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛfəɹəns|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|literary|or|archaic}} A [[relationship]] or [[relation]] ({{m|en|to}} something).
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd|Charity, compoſed of all three kindes, Pleaſant, Profitable, Honeſt|3|1|3|subsection=1|page=349|url=https://archive.org/stream/2319035R.nlm.nih.gov/2319035R#page/n430|passage=A man is beloued of a man, in that he is a man, but all theſe are farre more eminent and great, when they ſhal proceed from a ſanctified ſpirit, that hath a true touch of Religion, and a '''reference''' to God.}}
# A measurement one can compare (some other measurement) to.
# [[information|Information]] about a person, provided by someone (a [[referee]]) with whom they are well acquainted.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=a. 1800|author=w:William Cowper|chapter=An Epistle to Joseph Hill, Esq.|title=The Task, Tirocinium, and Other Poems|page=180|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=_3QCAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA180|passage=Changes will befall, and friends may part, / But distance only cannot change the heart / And were I call’d to prove th’ assertion true, / One proof should serve—a '''reference''' to you.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|Ireland}} A person who provides this information; a [[referee]].
# {{lb|en|often|attributive}} A [[reference work]].
#: {{uxi|en|'''reference''' grammar|detailed linguistic description of a particular language's grammar}}
#: {{uxi|en|'''Reference''' Dictionary of Linguistics}}
# The act of referring: a submitting for information or decision.
# {{lb|en|semantics}} A [[relation]] between objects in which one object [[designate]]s, or acts as a means by which to [[connect]] to or [[link]] to, another object.
# {{lb|en|academic writing}} A short written [[identification]] of a previously published work which is used as a [[source]] for a text.
# {{lb|en|academic writing}} A previously published [[written]] [[work]] thus indicated; a source.
# {{lb|en|computing}} An object containing information which refers to data stored elsewhere, as opposed to containing the data itself.
# {{lb|en|programming|character entity}} A special sequence used to represent complex characters in markup languages, such as <code>&amp;trade;</code> for the &trade; symbol.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[appeal|Appeal]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Antony and Cleopatra|V|ii|365|1|Y’are falne into a Princely hand, feare nothing, / Make your full '''reference''' freely to my Lord, / Who is ſo full of Grace, that it flowes ouer / On all that neede.}}

