# Having [[distinct]] [[limit]]s.
#: {{ux|en|'''definite''' dimensions; a '''definite''' measure; a '''definite''' period or interval}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1837|author=w:William Whewell|title=History of the Inductive Sciences|location=London|publisher=John W. Parker|volume=3|issue_plain=book 14|chapter=8|page=145|url=https://archive.org/details/historyofinducti03unse|text={{...}} elements combine in '''''definite''''' proportions {{...}}}}
# Free from any [[doubt]].
#: {{syn|en|unquestionable}}
#: {{ux|en|'''definite''' knowledge}}
# Determined; resolved; decided.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|I|6|text={{...}} idiots in this case of favour would<br>Be wisely '''definite'''}}
# <span id="en-linguistics"> {{lb|en|linguistics}} Designating an [[identified]] or immediately [[identifiable]] person or thing, or group of persons or things</span>
