Page 6 شناختن: -------- begin text --------
==Persian==

===Etymology===
{{root|fa|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}
From {{inh|fa|pal|𐭱𐭭𐭠𐭧𐭲𐭭|tr=šnāxtan|gloss=to recognize, to know}}, from {{inh|fa|peo|𐎧𐏁𐎴𐎠𐎿𐎠𐏃𐎹|tr=xšnāsāhiy}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*jnaHŝáti}}, from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*ȷ́naHsćáti}}, from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*ǵn̥h₃sḱéti}}.<ref>{{R:ira:Cheung|page=467}}</ref>

Related to {{l|fa|دانستن|tr=dânestan|t=know}}, {{cog|kmr|zanîn}}, {{cog|ae|𐬰𐬀𐬥𐬄𐬥|t=to recognize}}, {{cog|bal|زانگ|tr=zánag}}, {{cog|en|know}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|šināx`tan}}

===Verb===
{{fa-regional|شناختن|شناختن|шинохтан}}
{{fa-verb|tr=šenâxtan|prstem=شناس|tr2=šenâs|head=شِناخْتَن}}<ref>{{R:STEIN}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dehkhoda|شناختن}}</ref>

# to [[know]], to be [[acquainted]] with
#* {{RQ:Masnavi|II|341|گر چه با تو شه نشیند بر زمین<br>خویشتن ب'''شناس''' و نیکوتر نشین‏|gar či bā tū šah nišīnad bar zamīn<br>xwēš-tan bi-'''šinās''' u nēkū-tar nišīn|Although the King sit with you on the ground,<br> '''know''' yourself and sit better.}}
#: {{lang|fa|پدرتون رو از بچگی می‌شناسم.}}
#:: Pedáretun-o az baččegí mí-šenâsam.
#::: I've known your father since childhood.
# to [[acknowledge]]
# to [[discern]], to [[distinguish]]
# to [[inform]], to [[make known]], to [[define]], to [[describe]]
# to [[recognize]]
#: {{lang|fa|فکر می‌کنم آن مرد را می‌شناسم.}}
#:: Fekr mi-konam ân mard râ mi-šenâsam.
#: {{lang|fa|فکر می‌کنم اون مرد و می‌شناسم.}}
#:: Fekr mi-konam un mard o mi-šnâsam.
#::: I think I recognize that man.

====Usage notes====
* Similar to many European languages, Persian has two verbs used for knowing something and knowing someone. Compare {{cog|de|kennen}} and {{m|de|wissen}}; {{cog|fr|savoir}} and {{m|fr|connaître}}; {{cog|es|saber}} and {{m|es|conocer}}.
* {{l|fa|دانستن|tr=dânestan}} is used for having knowledge about places or things; but {{l|fa|شناختن|tr=šenâxtan}} is used for recognizing and knowing people.

====Conjugation====
{{fa-conj/šenâxtan}}

