Page 1 mane: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Appendix:Variations of "mane"}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|mān}}, {{IPA|en|/meɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-mane.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|main|Maine}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|mane}}, {{m|enm|mayne}}, from {{inh|en|ang|manu|t=mane}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*manu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*manō|t=mane}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mony-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*mon-|t=neck}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|maan}}, {{m|nl|manen|t=mane}}, {{cog|de|Mähne|t=mane}}, {{cog|sv|man|t=horse's mane}}, {{cog|is|mön|t=mane}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|long hair of an animal}} Longer hair growth on back of neck of an animal, especially a [[horse]] or [[lion]]
#* {{RQ:Baum Wizard of Oz|23|text=Before they went to see Glinda, however, they were taken to a room of the Castle, where Dorothy washed her face and combed her hair, and the Lion shook the dust out of his '''mane''', and the Scarecrow patted himself into his best shape, and the Woodman polished his tin and oiled his joints.}}
# {{senseid|en|long hair of a person}} Long or thick hair of a person's head.
# Part of a naval sword between the [[tang button]] and the [[quillon]].

=====Derived terms=====
{{der2|en|lion's mane|mane-comb|shaggy mane}}

=====Translations=====
