==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/nuːn/}}
* {{audio|de|De-nun.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|de|gmh|nu|nu, nū}}, {{m|gmh|nuo}} with a secondary final ''-n'', already occasionally in {{inh|de|gmh|nuon}}, from {{inh|de|goh|nu}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*nū}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|de|nu||colloquial; otherwise archaic}}

====Adverb====
{{de-adv}}

# [[now]], at this moment
# [[now]], [[then]]; {{n-g|expressing a logical or temporal consequence}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir haben abgewaschen, '''nun''' müssen wir noch abtrocknen.|We've washed up, '''now''' we must dry [the dishes].}}
#: {{ux|de|Was bedeuten '''nun''' die geschilderten Entwicklungen für unser Land?|'''Now''' what do the aforementioned developments mean for our country?}}
# {{n-g|unstressed and expletive, used for minor emphasis}}
#: {{ux|de|Was soll das '''nun''' heißen?|What's that supposed to mean '''now'''?}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Although the adverb is similar and akin to English “now”, German ''nun'' is not commonly used in a strictly temporal sense, meaning “at this moment”. For that, see {{m|de|jetzt}}.

====Interjection====
{{head|de|interjection}}

# [[now]], [[well]], [[so]]
#: {{ux|de|'''Nun''', das ist eine schwierige Frage.|'''Well''', that's a tough question.}}

===Etymology 2===
{{clipping|de|nun dass|alt=nun daß}} or {{m|de|[[nun]] [[da]]}}.

====Conjunction====
{{head|de|conjunction}}

# {{tlb|de|literary|_|or|_|dated|_|colloquial}} [[now that]], given that it has occurred that the circumstances do not withstand that …

