====Verb====
{{en-verb|pres_ptc2=memeing}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|Internet slang}} To create and use humorous memes.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Eric W. Saeger|title= Russian Nazi Troll Bots!|passage=One axiom commonly seen on /pol/ is "The Left Can't '''Meme'''"; in other words, left-wing meme jokes aren't funny.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|Internet slang}} To turn into a meme; to use a meme, especially to achieve a goal in [[real life]].
#: {{syn|en|memeify}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=2016-10-31
|title=Trolls for Trump
|work=The New Yorker
|url=https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2016/10/31/trolls-for-trump
|author=Andrew Marantz
|passage=Scott Greer, a deputy editor of the Daily Caller, tweeted, “Cernovich '''memed''' #SickHillary into reality. Never doubt the power of memes.”
|accessdate=December 2, 2017}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=2017-11-06
|title=David Moyes to West Ham “memed into existence by the internet”
|work=Football Burp
|url=http://footballburp.com/news/david-moyes-to-west-ham-memed-into-existence-by-the-internet/
|passage=David Moyes succeeding Slaven Bilić as West Ham United manager is being '''memed''' into existence by the internet, Football Burp understands.
|accessdate=December 2, 2017}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/sep/22/becoming-a-meme-totally-helps-a-show-is-tv-being-written-with-epic-gifs-in-mind|title=‘Becoming a meme totally helps a show’: is TV being written with epic gifs in mind?|date=2022-09-22|author=Jess Thomson|work=The Guardian|passage=“Succession’s language is so specific, unique and captivating that nearly every line is worthy of being ‘'''memed'''’, even if it’s just somebody saying ‘fuck off’ or ‘bad tweet!’” she says.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Gabriella Paiella|url=https://www.gq.com/story/anatomy-of-a-fall-memes|title=Why ‘Anatomy of a Fall’ Became One of the Most Memed Films of the Year|work=GQ|date=2024-03-05|quotee=Messineo|passage=In my experience the films that typically get '''memed''' are either really terrible (''Madame Web''), so huge that they’re everywhere (''Barbie''), or have a cast stacked with familiar faces so the memes cast a wide net for potential sharing.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|Internet slang|by extension}} To [[joke around]].
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=May 17, 2004|author=you|title=Truth vs. Lies |url=|newsgroup=alt.slack|passage=actually, it wasn't my mental functioning.  i'm just '''meming'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en |date=Dec 13, 2018|work=Vox|title=YouTube’s most popular user amplified anti-Semitic rhetoric. Again.|author=Aja Romano|volume=|number=|passage=“[P]ewdiepie is, once again, doing exactly what neo-nazis want,” Kotaku reporter Nathan Grayson commented on Twitter in response to the incident. “[W]hether he’s just '''meming''' or he ascribes to these values, it doesn’t matter. [W]hat matters is that he normalizes these ideas as jokes on THE platform where kids increasingly get their first exposure to the world at large.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2019 |title=Savage Appetites: Four True Stories of Women, Crime, and Obsession|author=Rachel Monroe |page=|ISBN=1501188887|passage=Some of his fellow fascists thought he was just “'''meming''' and pranking”; others dismissed it as “some autistic phase.” }}

