===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|-the|id=ordinal}}, {{m|enm|-th}}, {{m|enm|-te}}, {{m|enm|-t|pos=ordinal suffix}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-þa}}, {{m|ang|-þe}}, {{m|ang|-oþa}}, {{m|ang|-oþe}}, derived from a {{der|en|ine-pro|-}} superlative suffix. {{etystub|en}}

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes|cat3=noun-forming suffixes|cat4=productive suffixes}}

# {{senseid|en|ordinal}} {{n-g|Used to form the {{l|en|[[ordinal]] [[numeral]]}} when the final term of the spelled number is not “first”, “second”, or “third”.}}
#: {{ux|en|the [[Fourth of July|4'''th'''/Four'''th''' of July]]}}
## {{lb|en|mathematics}} {{n-g|Used to form a term denoting the [[ordinal numeral]] corresponding to the [[value]], being a [[natural number]], of a mathematical [[expression]].}}
##: {{ux|en|The <math>n</math>'''th''' term of a geometrical progression whose first term is <math>a</math> and common ratio is <math>r</math> is given by <math>ar^n</math>.}}
# {{senseid|en|fraction}} {{n-g|Used to form the {{l|en|denominator}} of a {{l|en|fraction}}.}}
#: {{ux|en|one seven'''th'''; three ten'''ths'''}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Some numbers undergo a change in spelling: {{suffixusex|en|five|fifth}}, {{suffixusex|en|eight|eighth}}, {{suffixusex|en|nine|ninth}}, {{suffixusex|en|twenty|twentieth}}. See [[-eth#Etymology_2|-eth]]
* Use of this suffix with numbers ending in {{m|en|one}}, {{m|en|two}}, or {{m|en|three}} is occasionally heard in speech, particularly in forming fractions ({{m|en||**thirty-two'''th'''}}) but is considered highly nonstandard.
* In older texts, this suffix, and the other suffixes for forming ordinals, may be seen written as superscripts: 1<sup>st</sup>, 2<sup>nd</sup>, 3<sup>rd</sup>, 4<sup>th</sup>, 5<sup>th</sup>. This is considered old-fashioned; the current preference is to write (when not spelling the numbers), 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th, 5th.
* When used to suffix a mathematical expression, a hyphen is sometimes inserted: <math>n</math>-th term.

=====Coordinate terms=====
* {{l|en|-nd}}
* {{l|en|-rd}}
* {{l|en|-st}}

