==Welsh==

===Etymology===
Reduced form of {{m|cy|[[ddim]] [[o]]||not of, nothing of}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/mɔ/}}

===Particle===
{{head|cy|particle}} {{tlb|cy|causes soft mutation}}

# {{lb|cy|colloquial}} {{n-g|negative particle used when immediately preceding the definite article or a definite noun phrase}}
#: {{uxi|cy|Fwytais i '''mo'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>r moron.|I did'''n't''' eat the carrots.}}
#: {{uxi|cy|Wela i '''mo'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>r ffilm 'na.|I will '''not''' see that film.}}
#: {{uxi|cy|Chlywoch chi '''mo''' Owain.|You did'''n't''' hear Owain.}}
#: {{uxi|cy|Leician nhw '''mo''' wraig y dyn.|They would'''n't''' like the man's wife.}}

====Usage notes====
Because this form is used only when directly in front of a definite object, it only appears in the (non-periphrastic) preterite, future and conditional tenses.

In front of a pronoun, ''mo'' has personal forms the same as the preposition {{m|cy|o}}:
{{cy-personal-prep|mohono|mohonot|mohono|mohoni|mohonon|mohonoch|mohonyn}}

====See also====
* {{l|cy|dim}}, {{l|cy|ddim}} {{q|negative particle used in all other situations}}

===Mutation===
Does not mutate.

