==English==
{{wikipedia|Lunar letters}}

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|ar|حَرْف قَمَرِيّ}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|linguistics}} One of fourteen Arabic letters that do '''not''' affect the pronunciation of the "L" of a preceding definite article ({{l|ar|[[ال]]-}}). The "L" in the Arabic definite article is pronounced "L" when followed by a moon letter: e.g., {{m|ar|القُرْآن}}. The fourteen moon letters are: {{l|ar|ء}}, {{l|ar|ب}}, {{l|ar|ج}}, {{l|ar|ح}}, {{l|ar|خ}}, {{l|ar|ع}}, {{l|ar|غ}}, {{l|ar|ف}}, {{l|ar|ق}}, {{l|ar|ك}}, {{l|ar|م}}, {{l|ar|ه}}, {{l|ar|و}}, {{l|ar|ي}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|lunar letter}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|sun letter}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|moon letter}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|حَرْف قَمَرِيّ|m}} (plural: {{t|ar|حُرُوف قَمَرِيَّة|m-p}})
* French: {{t|fr|lettre lunaire|f}}
* German: {{t|de|Mondbuchstabe|m}}
* Kazakh: {{t|kk|ай әрпі|sc=Cyrl}}
* Malay: {{t|ms|huruf kamariah}}
* Maltese: {{t|mt|konsonanti qamrin}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|лу́нная бу́ква|f}}
* Spanish: {{t|es|letra lunar|f}}
* Ukrainian: {{t|uk|місячна літера|f}}, {{t|uk|місячна буква}}
{{trans-bottom}}

[[Category:en:Arabic letter names]]
