===Etymology===
From {{der|ga|sga|-imm}}. The {{m|ga||m}} is always broad (velarized) in Ulster, as if the ending were spelled {{m|ga||-(e)am}}. This pronunciation arose by leveling of this ending with the broad {{m|ga||m}} found in first-person singular prepositional pronouns such as {{m|ga|agam}}, {{m|ga|asam}}, {{m|ga|chugam}} etc. Compare {{cog|gd|-am|pos=first-person singular imperative}}.<ref>{{R:ga:Quiggin|104|292}}</ref>

