==Basque==

===Etymology===
Probably related to {{m|eu|m-}}.

===Prefix===
{{head|eu|prefix}}

# {{n-g|Non-productive prefix without a specific meaning.}}

====Usage notes====
In words where this prefix can be found, it takes the place of the first syllable of the original word, usually with no change in meaning (compare {{m|eu|udare}} and {{m|eu|madari}}, both meaning "pear"). It is likely that originally this was an expressive prefix, and that many Basque words starting with ''ma-'' contain this prefix, with the original word having been lost.

===References===
* {{R:EDB|278}}

==Bikol Central==

===Prefix===
{{head|bcl|prefix}}

# {{n-g|Used to form adjectives indicating a quality}}
#: {{prefixusex|bcl|linig|t1=to clean|malinig|t2=clean}}
# {{n-g|Object IV trigger infinitive verb prefix}}
#: {{prefixusex|bcl|dumog|t1=wet|madumog|t2=to become wet}}
# {{n-g|Object trigger to have done something; to be able to do something}}
#: {{prefixusex|bcl|tapos|t1=finish|matapos|t2=to be able to finish something}}
#: {{uxi|bcl|'''Natapos''' kong basahon an libro kasubanggi.|I was able to finish reading the book last night.}}
# {{n-g|Object trigger to perform the action of the verb unintentionally}}
#: {{prefixusex|bcl|pasa|t1=broken, break|mapasa|t2=to break something unintentionally}}
#: {{uxi|bcl|'''Napasa''' ko an salming.|I '''unintentionally broke''' the mirror.}} {{n-g|Compare it when used with the suffix '''-on''':}}
#:: {{m|bcl|pasa|t=broken, break}} + {{m|bcl|-on}} → {{m|bcl|pasaon|t=to break something on purpose}}
#::: {{uxi|bcl|'''Pinasa''' ko an salming.|I '''broke''' the mirror on purpose.}}
# to form the future tense of the verb.

==Cebuano==

===Prefix===
{{head|ceb|prefix}}

# {{n-g|Used to form adjectives indicating a quality}}
# {{n-g|Used to form the future tense of a verb}}

==Hausa==

===Etymology===
Cognate to the set of prefixes found in {{cog|ar|-}}: {{m|ar|مُ}} for agentive participles, {{m|ar|مَ}} for locatives, and {{m|ar|مِ}} for instrumentals.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ha-IPA|ma-}}

===Prefix===
{{ha-pos|prefix|ma-}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Used to form [[agentive]] nouns.}}
# {{n-g|Used to form nouns of place ([[locative]] nouns).}}
# {{n-g|Used to form [[instrumental]] nouns.}}

====Usage notes====
Each prefix forms a different template to which the noun must conform:
* Agentive nouns end in {{m|ha|-ī}} in the masculine singular, {{m|ha|-ìyā}} in the feminine singular, and {{m|ha|-ā}} in the plural, and the root has low tone in the masculine and plural, but high tone in the feminine.
* Locative nouns end in {{m|ha|-ā}} and are feminine, or uncommonly in {{m|ha|-ī}} and are masculine, with all high tone in either case. There is rarely a plural form.
* Instrumental nouns end in {{m|ha|-ī}} and are masculine, with plurals in {{m|ha|-ai}}. The tones of the singular form are all high, and in the plural the tones are all low except for the plural morpheme.

====Derived terms====
{{prefixsee|ha|ma- (agentive)}}
{{prefixsee|ha|ma- (locative)}}
{{prefixsee|ha|ma- (instrumental)}}

