====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|in the plural}} Something that a person likes (prefers).
#: {{syn|en|favorite|preference}}
#: {{ant|en|dislike|pet hate|pet peeve}}
#: {{ux|en|Tell me your '''likes''' and dislikes.}}
# {{senseid|en|internet}} {{lb|en|internet}} An individual vote showing support for, approval of, or enjoyment of, something posted on the Internet.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Brooke Warner|title=Green-Light Your Book|passage=Social media is supervisual, and there's nothing more shareable than images, so this is a way to increase shares and '''likes''' and follows.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2019|artist=Princess Nokia|title=Balenciaga|passage=Dress for myself, I don't dress for hype / I dress for myself, you dress for the '''likes'''}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2020-01-17|author=Amy Chozick|title=This Is the Guy Who’s Taking Away the Likes|work=New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/01/17/business/instagram-likes.html|passage='''Likes''' are the social media currency undergirding an entire influencer economy, inspiring a million Kardashian wannabes and giving many of us regular people daily endorphin hits.}}

