==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|م ث ل}}

Compare {{cog|he|מָשָׁל|tr=mašál|t=example}}.  

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u}}

# to [[resemble]], to [[look like]]
# to [[imitate]], to [[copy]]
# to [[compare]], to [[liken]] {{+obj|ar|acc<someone>&:بِ<with>}}
# to [[represent]], to [[mean]], to [[signify]], to [[stand for]]
# to [[present]] oneself, to [[stand]], to [[appear]] {{+obj|ar|:أَمَامَ<before>}}
# to [[come]] forth, to [[come]] forward, to [[enter]], to [[appear]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u|passive=y|vn=مُثُول}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[portray]], to [[play]], to [[present]]
# to [[represent]], to [[stand]] for, to be [[exemplary]] for, to [[account for]]
# to make to [[resemble]], to make to [[look like]]
# to make [[similar]], to make [[analogous]]
# to [[assimilate]]
# to [[quote]] as example {{+obj|ar|acc<for>|:بِ|:لِ|:عَلَى<for>}}
# to [[compare]], to [[liken]] {{+obj|ar|acc<someone>&:بِ<with>}}
# to [[punish]] severely, to [[treat]] harshly {{+obj|ar|:بِ<someone>}}
# to [[maim]], to [[mutilate]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<someone>}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II|passive=y|vn=تَمْثِيل, تَمْثَال}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِثْل|m|pl=أَمْثَال}}

# something [[similar]]
#: {{coi|ar|رَجُلٌ '''مِثْلُ'''هُ|a man '''like''' him}}
#: {{coi|ar|فِي '''مِثْلِ''' هٰذِهِ ٱلظُّرُوفِ|under circumstances '''like''' these}}
#: {{coi|ar|جَمِيعُ ٱلْأَطِبَّاءِ '''مِثْلِ'''كَ / '''أَمْثَالِ'''كَ|all doctors '''like''' you.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|هُنَاكَ عَشَرَاتٌ '''مِثْلُ'''هُ / '''أَمْثَالُ'''هُ.|There are dozens '''like''' it.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|اِفْعَلْهُ '''مِثْلَ'''نَا!|Do it '''like''' us!}}
# [[resemblance]], [[similarity]], [[likeness]]
# [[image]]
# [[equivalent]]

=====Usage notes=====
* This word is used for the meaning of "like, similar to", but it isn't considered a preposition in Arabic. It's a noun used in apposition and declined according to the noun it follows.
* It can also stand without the noun it describes, especially in accusative where an omitted masdar is often assumed {{uxi|ar|اِفْعَلْهُ (فِعْلًا) مِثْلَنَا|Do it (the way which is) like us}}.
* The dual and plural forms can be used if following a dual or plural noun, but aren't necessary.

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِثْل|pl=أَمْثَال}}

