==Persian==
{{wp|lang=fa}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|ترکمان|tr=torkamân||dated}}

===Etymology===
From a {{bor|fa|trk}} language, combining {{der|fa|otk|𐱅𐰇𐰼𐰜|t=Turk}} with a suffix *-man sometimes found in tribal and place names, cf. {{ncog|trk-oat|قرانان|tr=qarâmân|pos=Turkic dynasty in southern Anatolia}} from {{m|trk-oat|قرا|tr=qarâ|t=black}}, or {{ncog|otk|𐰚𐰇𐰏𐰢𐰤|t={{w|Sayan Mountains}}}} from {{m|otk| 𐰚𐰇𐰚|t=white}}.

The traditional etymology, dating as far back as {{w|Mahmud al-Kashgari|Mahmud Kashgari}} (eleventh century), says that the second element is from {{cog|fa|مانند|tr=mânand|t=like, resembling}}. The thirteenth-century world historian {{w|Rashid al-Din}} says that it was used for those Turks who had intermarried with Persians and lost their East Asian facial features: narrow eyes, broad noses, etc. Since they now resembled Persians in appearance, despite still retaining their Turkish customs, the Persians called them “Turk-like” rather than truly “Turk”. This etymology was accepted until the twentieth century, but is now seen as unlikely.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|turk`man,turka`man}}

===Noun===
{{fa-regional|ترکمن|ترکمن|[[туркман]], [[туркаман]]}}
{{fa-noun|tr=torkman, torkaman|pl=ترکمن‌ها|pltr=torkman-hâ, torkaman-hâ}}

# [[Turkmen]] (member of one of various Turkic ethnic groups in [[Central Asia|Central]] and [[West Asia]])
## [[Turkmen]]s of [[Turkmenistan]] and nearby regions of [[Iran]]
## [[Turkmen]]s of [[Syria]], [[Iraq]], and [[Lebanon]]
## {{lb|fa|historical}} {{w|Turkoman (ethnonym)|Turkoman}}, generic term for [[Oghuz]] [[Turk]]s in [[Central Asia|Central]] and [[West Asia]]

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|fa
|ترکمنستان<tr:torkmanestân, torkamanestân>
|ترکمنی<tr:torkmani, torkamani>
}}
