====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[remove]] ([[rock]] or [[ore]]) from the [[ground]].
#: {{uxi|en|{{w|Crater of Diamonds State Park}} is the only place in the world where visitors can '''mine''' their own diamonds.}}
# To [[dig]] into, for [[ore]] or [[metal]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1837|author=w:Andrew Ure|title=Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures and Mines
|passage=Lead veins have been traced {{...}} but they have not been '''mined'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[sow]] [[#Noun|mine]]s (the [[explosive]] devices) in (an area).
#: {{uxi|en|We had to slow our advance after the enemy '''mined''' the road ahead of us.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[damage]] (a [[vehicle]] or [[ship]]) with a [[#Noun|mine]] (an explosive device).
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To dig a [[tunnel]] or [[hole]]; to [[burrow]] in the [[earth]].
#: {{uxi|en|the '''mining''' cony}}
# To [[dig]] away, or otherwise [[remove]], the [[substratum]] or [[foundation]] of; to lay a [[#Noun|mine]] under; to [[sap]]; to [[undermine]].
#* {{RQ:Hayward Edward 6|passage=They '''mined''' the walls.}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Waverley|passage=Too lazy, perhaps, to cut [these immense trees] down, the spoilers {{...}} had '''mined''' them, and placed a quantity of gunpowder in the cavity.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension|figurative}} To [[ruin]] or [[destroy]] by [[slow]] [[degree]]s or [[secret]] [[means]].
# {{lb|en|by extension|figurative}} To [[tap]] [[into]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} To [[pick one's nose]].
# {{senseid|en|crypto}} {{lb|en|cryptocurrencies}} To [[earn]] new units of [[cryptocurrency]] by doing certain [[calculation]]s.
#: {{cot|en|mint}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Andrew Ross Sorkin|title=Bitcoin's Climate Problem|work=The New York Times|date=2021-03-09|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/03/09/business/dealbook/bitcoin-climate-change.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Bitcoin supporters say that estimates of its carbon footprint are overstated. And if the computers that '''mine''' and help transact bitcoins are attached to an electric grid that uses wind and solar power, they add, '''mining''' and using it will become cleaner over time.}}

