====Adjective====
{{en-adj|?}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|UK|_|dialectal|Scotland}} [[less]]
#* ''Le Bone Florence'' (late 1300s) {{attention|en|is this en or enm?}}
#*: The more and the '''minne'''

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|minnock}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|min}}, {{m|enm|minne}}, partly from {{inh|en|ang|myne|t=mind, intent, desire, love}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*muni}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*muniz|t=mind, memory}}; and also from {{der|en|non|minni|t=memory}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*gaminþiją|t=memory, remembrance}}; both from {{der|en|ine-pro|*men-|t=to think}}. Related to {{cog|is|minni|t=memory}}, {{cog|de|Minne|t=love}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[memory|Memory]]; [[remembrance]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|author=Joshiah Gilbet Holland|title=Sevenoaks|passage={{...}} and faith I've done that same and found me '''min'''; {{...}}}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{inh|en|enm|minnen}}, {{m|enm|mynnen}}, from {{der|en|non|minna|t=to bring to mind}}, from {{m|non|minni|t=memory}}. See above.

====Verb====
