# {{n-g|First-person singular genitive determiner:}} [[my]]

====Usage notes====
''min'' is usually used before a vowel and ''h-'', while {{m|enm|mi}} is usually used before a consonant other than ''h-'', much as with Modern {{cog|en|an}}/{{m|en|a}}.

