==Portuguese==

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA}}
* {{hyph|pt|min}}

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|m|#}}

# {{abbreviation of|pt|minuto}}
## {{n-g|Used to indicate time in relation to an hour on a 24-hour clock.}}
##: {{ux|inline=1|pt|O evento é hoje, às 20h30'''min'''|The event is today at 8:30 p.m.}}
## {{n-g|Used to indicate any sequence of time in minutes.}}
##: {{uxi|pt|O atleta completou a corrida em 1[[h]]20'''min'''45[[s]]|The athlete completed the race in 1 hour, 21 minutes and 45 seconds}}

====Usage notes====
* This abbreviation uses no spaces or points and must always follow a number (in its most common usage, a number between 00 and 59 to indicate the minutes of an hour).
* This abbreviation is often preceded by a number followed by {{m|pt|h}}, used to represent hours.
* The abbreviation can be followed by another abbreviation, {{m|pt|s}}, to represent seconds.
** Example: ''20h43min08s''

