==English==
{{wikipedia|pear (disambiguation)|pear}}
[[Image:Pears.jpg|thumb|Photo of a pair of '''pears''' on a tree]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|pere}}, from {{inh|en|ang|pere}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*peru}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*pira}}, originally the plural of {{der|en|la|pirum}} but reconstrued as a feminine singular, ultimately a loanword from an unknown Mediterranean {{der|en|qfa-sub|-}} source. Cognate with {{cog|stq|Peere||pear}}, {{cog|nl|peer||pear}}, {{cog|da|pære||pear}}, {{cog|fr|poire||pear}}, {{cog|de|Birne||pear}}, {{cog|is|pera||pear}}, {{cog|sv|päron||pear}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɛə/|[pʰeə]|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-pear.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{enPR|pâr|a=GenAm}}, {{IPA|en|/pɛɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-pear.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpiːə(r)/|a=InE}}
* {{homophones|en|pair|pare}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛə(ɹ)|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An edible fruit produced by the pear tree, similar to an [[apple]] but typically elongated towards the stem.
# A type of fruit tree ({{taxfmt|Pyrus communis|species}}).
#: {{syn|en|pear tree}}
# The wood of the pear tree ([[pearwood]], [[pear wood]]).
# [[choke pear|Choke pear]] (a [[torture]] device).
# {{lb|en|Jamaica}} [[avocado]], [[alligator pear]]
# A desaturated [[chartreuse]] yellow [[colour]], like that of a pear.
#: {{color panel|D1E231}}

====Hypernyms====
