==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
Metrical contraction in poetry.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|nak}}

====Interjection====
{{head|fa|interjection|tr=nak}}

# {{lb|fa|poetic}} {{contraction of|fa|اینک|tr=inak}}⁩

====Adverb====
{{head|fa|adverb|tr=nak}}

# {{lb|fa|poetic}} {{contraction of|fa|اینک|tr=inak}}⁩

===Etymology 2===
Metrical contraction in poetry.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|nuk}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=nok}}

#{{alternative form of|fa|نوک|tr=nuk|t=beak, tip, point|from=poetic}}.

==Saraiki==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|skr|inc-pra|𑀡𑀓𑁆𑀓}}, from {{inh|skr|inc-ash|*𑀦𑀓𑁆𑀓}}, from {{m|sa|नस्}} {{inc-ext|skr|ka}}, from {{inh|skr|iir-pro|*náHsaH}}, from {{inh|skr|ine-pro|*néh₂s|*néh₂s-eh₂|nose}}.

Cognate with {{cog|as|নাক}}, {{cog|bn|নাক}}, {{cog|en|nose}}, [[Hindustani]] {{l|hi|नाक}} / {{l|ur|ناک|nāk}}, {{cog|ru|нос}}, {{cog|syl|ꠘꠣꠇ}}. {{doublet|skr|ناس}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|skr|/nəkː/}}

===Noun===
{{skr-noun|head=نَکّ|g=m}}

# {{lb|skr|anatomy}} [[nose]]

{{C|skr|Body parts}}
