# {{non-gloss definition|equivalent of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ing}}; suffix for present participle terms}}

==Danish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|da|gem-pro|*-andz}}.

====Suffix====
{{da-suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|equivalent of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ing}}; suffix for present participle terms}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|da|gem-pro|*-dô}}, cognate with {{cog|en|-th}}. The ''-n-'' is generalized from those stems that ended in ''-n'' originally, e.g. {{m|da|tiende|ti-ende}} from {{m|gem-pro|*tehundô|*tehun-dô}}.

====Suffix====
{{da-suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|forms ordinal numbers from cardinal numbers}}

==Norwegian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|no|gem-pro|*-andz}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|no|suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|equivalent of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ing}}; suffix for present participles and adjectives}}
# {{non-gloss definition|equivalent of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-th}}, {{m|en|-eth}}; suffix for ordinal numbers}}

==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-ende}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-andī}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-andz}}. Akin to {{cog|la|-āns}}, {{m|la|-ēns}}; {{cog|grc|-ων}}, {{cog|fa|ـنده|tr=-ande}}.

====Suffix====
{{ang-suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|equivalent of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ing}}; suffix for present participles}}
#: {{uxi|ang|feall'''ende''' snāw|falling snow}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-andiją}}. Compare {{cog|non|-indi}}.

====Suffix====
{{ang-suffix|g=n}}

# {{non-gloss definition|used to form neuter nouns}}
#: {{uxi|ang|[[swǣsende]]|t=food, victuals, flattery, blandishment}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Frequently used in the plural {{m|ang|-endu}}.

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun-ja-n|-end}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ang}}

===Etymology 3===
{{nonlemma}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-suffix}}

# {{alternative form of|ang|-anne}}

===Further reading===
* {{cite-book|author={{w|Joseph Bosworth}}|editor={{w|Thomas Northcote Toller}}|title={{w|An Anglo-Saxon Dictionary}}|year=1898|location={{w|Oxford}}|publisher=[[w:Oxford University Press|Clarendon Press]]|section=<abbr title="sub verbo">''s.v.''</abbr> “-ende”|page=250/2|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/anglosaxondictio00bosw/page/250/mode/1up}}

==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*-andz}}.

===Suffix===
{{head|sv|suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|equivalent of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ing}}; suffix for present participles (used with verbs that do not end with an unstressed -a in the infinitive)}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|sv|a=deen|Eden|eden}}
