==Arabic==
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|س و ق}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سَاقَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u}}

# to [[drive]]
# to [[conscript]]
# to [[pilot]]
# to [[transport]]
# to [[send]]
# to [[utter]]
# to [[cite]], to [[quote]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u|passive=y|vn=سَوْق,سِيَاق,سِيَاقَة,مَسَاق}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|arc|שָׁקָא|tr=šāqā|gloss=shin}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|akk|𒆸|tr=sâqu|t=to be narrow, skinny, or constricted}}, cognate to native {{m+|ar|ضَيِّق|t=narrow, pressed}}; compare {{cog|syc|ܫܩܐ|tr=šāqā|t=shin}}, {{cog|he|שׁוֹק|tr=shok|t=shin}}. Connected back to the root {{ar-root|س و ق}} by the urging on of animals with one's legs when riding or by driving them forward by tapping at their legs.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سَاق}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-ساق.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سَاق|f|pl=سُوق|pl2=سُؤُوق|pl3=سِيقَان|pl4=أَسْوُق}}

# [[leg]]
# [[shank]]
# [[side]] of an [[angle]]
# [[perpendicular]]
# [[trunk]], [[stalk]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|48|29|passage=وَمَثَلُهُمْ فِي الْإِنجِيلِ كَزَرْعٍ أَخْرَجَ شَطْأَهُ فَآزَرَهُ فَاسْتَغْلَظَ فَاسْتَوَىٰ عَلَىٰ سُوقِهِ}}
# [[column]], [[pillar]]
# [[scale]] {{lb|ar|balance}}
# [[genus]], [[gender]], [[kind]]
# [[pain]], [[torment]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَاق|pl=سُوق|pl2=سُؤُوق|pl3=سِيقَان|pl4=أَسْوُق}}

===Etymology 3===
{{ar-rootbox|س ق ي}}
{{ar-active participle}} of {{m|ar|سَقَى||to [[water]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سَاقَ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سَاقٍ|m|cons=سَاقِي|pl=سَاقُونَ|pl2=سُقَاة|pl3=سُقَّاء|pl4=سُقِيّ|f=سَاقِيَة}}

# [[cupbearer]]
# [[water carrier]]
# [[barkeeper]]
# [[waiter]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|سَاقٍ|pl=سَاقُونَ|pl2=سُقَاة|pl3=سُقَّاء|pl4=سُقِيّ|fpl=sfp|fpl2=سَوَاقٍ:diin}}

