====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[take part]] in a [[#Noun|race]] (in the sense of a contest).
#: {{ux|en|The drivers were '''racing''' around the track.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|editor=John Henry Walsh|chapter=Lichfield Open Meeting|title=Coursing Calendar for the Autumn Season 1874|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Coursing_calendar_ed_by_Stonehenge/newNAAAAQAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA187&printsec=frontcover|page=187|text=Honesty '''raced''' up six lengths in front of Wandering Minstrel, turned, then '''raced''' past for the second, and lost his place at the hedge; some work followed to the plantation, but Honesty was always the faster in the racing stretches, and won easily.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=2023-05-10|title=Athletics: Dina Asher-Smith set to race at London Stadium in July|work=BBC News|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/athletics/65545521|text="I cannot wait to '''race''' in front of the amazing home crowd," she added.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[compete]] [[against]] in a [[#Noun|race]] (contest).
#: {{ux|en|I '''raced''' him to the car, but he was there first, so he got to ride shotgun.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1871|month=March|title=Our Van|journal=Baily's Magazine of Sports & Pastimes|volume=21|page=306|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=D8A_AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA306|text={{...}}a fresh fox popped out of a pit, and they '''raced''' him to Cherrington, where hounds were stopped at dark{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1928|month=November|author=Paschal N. Strong|title=Signals|journal=Boys' Life|volume=18|number=11|page=61|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=3yyRrhS776UC&pg=PA61|text=He pulled it down and saw Tech's full-back closing in.  Counting on his own fresh condition, Jimmy '''raced''' him toward the sidelines, and got around him just in time to prevent being forced out. The goal was waiting for him twenty yards away, and to the accompaniment of a deafening shout from the stands he placed the pigskin across the goal line.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[move]] or [[drive]] at [[high]] [[speed#Noun|speed]]; to [[hurry]] or [[speed#Verb|speed]].
#: {{synonyms|en|rush|shift|zip|zoom}}
#: {{ux|en|As soon as it was time to go home, he '''raced''' for the door.}}
#: {{ux|en|Her heart was '''racing''' as she peered into the dimly lit room.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Lee Mavers|authorlabel=no|title={{w|There She Goes (The La's song)|There She Goes}}|album={{w|Sixpence None the Richer (album)|Sixpence None the Richer}}|date=|year=1988|year_published=1997|artist=w:Sixpence None the Richer|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=68MKLkNSMN4|text=There she goes / There she goes again / '''Racing''' through my brain / And I just can't contain / This feeling that remains}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-21|author=[http://guardian.co.uk/profile/chico-harlan/ Chico Harlan]| volume=189| issue=2| page=30| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2013/jun/18/japan-solar-energy-fukushima-nuclear-renewable-abe Japan pockets the subsidy &hellip;]| passage=Across Japan, technology companies and private investors are '''racing''' to install devices that until recently they had little interest in: solar panels. Massive solar parks are popping up as part of a rapid build-up that one developer likened to an "explosion."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 December 2|author=Paul Bigland|title=My weirdest and wackiest Rover yet|journal=Rail|page=66|text='''Racing''' on, we parallel the M5 doing 95mph, according to the app on my smartphone.}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a motor}} To [[run]] [[rapidly]] when not [[engaged]] to a [[transmission]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1891|month=December|author=w:Arthur Conan Doyle|title=w:The Man with the Twisted Lip|journal=The Strand|text="My mind is like a '''racing''' engine, tearing itself to pieces because it is not connected up with the work for which it was built."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2005|month=June|author=James Faucett|title=Snowbirds|journal=Atlanta Magazine|volume=45|number=2|page=79|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=hQ8AAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA79|text=He put the transmission into drive and pressed the gas.  The engine '''raced''' and the motor home rocked, gently, but did not move forward.}}

