====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{obsolete form of|en|raze}}
#: {{synonyms|en|demolish|destroy|tear up|Thesaurus:destroy}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1450|year_published=1899|publisher=Early English Text Society|title=Merlin or the Early History of King Arthur|editor=Henry Benjamin Wheatley|chapter=23|page=424|volume=2|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=OXlMAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA424|text={{...}}and after he be-heilde towarde the fier, and saugh the flesshe that the knaue hadde rosted that was tho I-nough, and '''raced''' it of with his hondes madly, and rente it a-sonder in peces, and wette it in mylke, and after in the hony, and ete as a wood man that nought ther lefte of the flessh;{{...}}}}

