==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===

====Root====
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[heat]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{ar-verb forms|I=to heat; to be hot|I-vn-head=نَجْر|IV=to propose the dish {{l|ar|نَجِيرَة}} to}}

* {{l|ar|نَجْر|t=heat; violent thirst}}
* {{l|ar|نَجْرَان|t=thirsty}}
* {{l|ar|نَجِيرَة|t=heating stone; milk mixed with butter or starch}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْجَرَة|t=heating stone}}
* {{l|ar|أَنْجَرَة|t=nettle}}

===Etymology 2===
Denominal from the loanword {{m|ar|نَجَّار|t=carpenter}}.

====Root====
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[carpentry]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{ar-verb forms|I=to hew, to plane|II=to hew, to plane}}

* {{l|ar|نَجَّار|t=carpenter}}
* {{l|ar|مِنْجَرَة|t=carpenter’s plane}}
* {{l|ar|نِجَارَة|t=carpentry}}
* {{l|ar|نُجَارَة|t=what is planed off wood}}

===Etymology 3===
Unclear if from senses of heat, since heat is what moves and spawns everything, or from carpenters making door-sills, or metathesized from {{m|ar|رِجْل|t=foot}}, considering that {{bor|ar|arc|נִגְרָא}} / {{m|arc|נִיגְרָא}} / {{m|syc|ܢܓܪܐ|tr=niḡra}} is such a metathesis having both the literal sense of a foot and transferred senses, or even Late {{bor|ar|pal|-}} equalling {{cog|fa-cls|نژاد|tr=nižād|t=lineage, root, origin}}.

====Root====
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[spawn]]ing [[shape]]s, [[stock]], [[sill]], [[root]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|نَجْر|t=form, shape; root, origin, stock}}
* {{l|ar|نَجْرَان|t=door-sill}}
* {{l|ar|نُجَار|t=root, origin, stock}}

===Etymology 4===
Metathesis of {{m|ar|جُرْن|t=mortar}}, possibly influenced by the sense of carpentry since one hews in a mortar.

====Root====
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[mortar]]s

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|نِجْر|t=mortar}}

===References===
