====Pronoun====
{{en-pron|reflexive|oneself|possessive adjective|[[one's|one’s]]|plural|ones}}

# {{lb|en|impersonal pronoun|indefinite}} One thing (among a group of others); one [[member]] of a group.
#: {{ux|en|Any '''one''' of the boys.&emsp; The big '''one''' looks good.&emsp; I want the green '''one'''.&emsp; Every '''one''' of the bank’s employees.&emsp; {{nowrap|A good driver is '''one''' who drives carefully.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Sonnets|6|passage=Which happies thoſe that pay the willing [[loan|lone]]; / That's for thy ſelfe to breed an other thee / Or ten times happier be it ten for '''one''',{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|impersonal pronoun|sometimes with "the"}} The first mentioned of two things or people, as opposed to the [[other]].
#: {{ux|en|She offered him an apple and an orange; he took '''one''' and left the other.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1699|author={{w|Sir William Temple, 1st Baronet|William Temple}}|title=Heads designed for an essay on conversations|url=http://essays.quotidiana.org/temple/heads_for_conversation/
|passage=Study gives strength to the mind; conversation, grace: the first apt to give stiffness, the other suppleness: '''one''' gives substance and form to the statue, the other polishes it.}}
# {{senseid|en|indefinite personal pronoun}}{{lb|en|indefinite personal pronoun}} Any [[person]] (applying to people in general).
#: {{syn|en|generic you}}
#: {{ux|en|One’s guilt may trouble '''one''', but it is best not to let oneself be troubled by things which cannot {{nowrap|be changed.}}&emsp; {{nowrap|'''One''' shouldn’t be too quick to judge.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=1|passage=It was not far from the house; but the ground sank into a depression there, and the ridge of it behind shut out everything except just the roof of the tallest hayrick. As '''one''' sat on the sward behind the elm, with the back turned on the rick and nothing in front but the tall elms and the oaks in the other hedge, it was quite easy to fancy it the verge of the prairie with the backwoods close by.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=2|passage=She was a fat, round little woman, richly apparelled in velvet and lace,{{nb...}}; and the way she laughed, cackling like a hen, the way she talked to the waiters and the maid,{{nb...}} — all these unexpected phenomena impelled '''one''' to hysterical mirth, and made '''one''' class her with such immortally ludicrous types as Ally Sloper, the Widow Twankey, or Miss Moucher.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=5|passage=‘It's rather like a beautiful Inverness cloak '''one''' has inherited. Much too good to hide away, so '''one''' wears it instead of an overcoat and pretends it's an amusing new fashion.’}}
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=vii| text=With fresh material, taxonomic conclusions are leavened by recognition that the material examined reflects the site it occupied; a herbarium packet gives '''one''' only a small fraction of the data desirable for sound conclusions. Herbarium material does not, indeed, allow '''one''' to extrapolate safely: what you see is what you get{{nb...}}.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-09-06|author=w:Philip Hoare| volume=189| issue=13| page=48| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| title=[http://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/aug/30/martians-earth-aliens If we're all Martians, who are the aliens?]| passage='''One''' has to admire the sheer optimism of modern science: I love the fact that there is such a discipline as astrobiology, whose practitioners' task is to imagine what life might be like on other planets. Yet here on the home planet we have profoundly strange aliens of our own.}}
# {{lb|en|pronoun}} Any [[person]], [[entity]] or [[thing]].
#: {{ux|en|"driver", noun: '''one''' who drives.}}

