====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[digit]] or [[figure]] 1.
# {{lb|en|by [[ellipsis]]}} {{n-g|Used to briefly refer to a noun phrase understood by context}}
## {{lb|en|US}} A one-[[dollar]] [[bill]].
##: ''I need some '''ones''' to make change.''
## One [[o'clock]], either a.m. or p.m.
##* {{RQ:Mary Shelley Frankenstein|page=97|chapter=5|volume=I|passage=It was already '''one''' in the morning; the rain pattered dismally against the panes, and my candle was nearly burnt out, when, by the glimmer of the half-extinguished light, I saw the dull yellow eye of the creature open; it breathed hard, and a convulsive motion agitated its limbs.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|passage=The ophthalmic surgeon attends Tuesdays and Saturdays, at half-past '''one'''.|title=Metropolitan Hospitals & Medical Schools|work=w:The Lancet|date=17 September 1853|page=268|pageurl=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/The_Lancet/4j9L9gXqeCYC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA268|issue=1568|volume=62|doi=10.1016/S0140-6736(02)57971-X}}
##* {{RQ:Doyle Land of Mist|passage=It was a weary time. A carriage clock had been placed on the discoloured wooden mantelpiece, and slowly its hands crept on from '''one''' to two and from two to three.|chapter=VIII}}
## {{lb|en|cricket}} One [[run]] scored by hitting the [[ball]] and running between the [[wicket]]s; a [[single]].
## A [[joke]] or amusing [[anecdote]].
##: {{ux|en|Did you hear the '''one''' about the [[agnostic]] [[dyslexic]] [[insomniac]]?}}
# {{lb|en|followed by '''{{m|en|for}}'''}} A person (having some specified characteristic or attribute).
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:H. G. Wells|H[erbert] G[eorge] Wells]]|title=[[w:Kipps|Kipps: The Story of a Simple Soul]]|location=London|publisher=[[w:Macmillan Publishers|Macmillan and Co., Limited]]|year=1905|page=55|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/kippsstoryofsimp00well_0/page/55/mode/1up|passage=Pause. They look meaningly at one another. / "You are a '''one''' for being roundabout," says the lady.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} A particularly [[special]] or [[compatible]] person or thing.
#: {{ux|en|I knew as soon I met him that John was the '''one''' for me and we were married within a month.}}
#: {{ux|en|That car's the '''one''' &mdash; I'll buy it.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1995|author=w:Bryan Adams|title=w:Have You Ever Really Loved a Woman?| passage=When you love a woman then tell her / that she's really wanted / When you love a woman then tell her that she's the '''one''' / 'cause she needs somebody to tell her / that it's gonna last forever}}
# {{lb|en|dated|euphemism|or|derogatory}} A [[gay]] person.
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|author=w:Dorothy Parker|title=The Diary of a Lady| journal=The New Yorker| page=13| date=25 March 1933| url=https://www.newyorker.com/magazine/1933/03/25/the-diary-of-a-lady| passage=Finally got Ollie Martin. He ''couldn't'' have more poise, and what do ''I'' care if he ''is'' '''one'''?}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} The [[identity element]] with respect to [[multiplication]] in a [[ring#Etymology_3|ring]].
# {{lb|en|Internet slang|leet|sarcastic}} {{deliberate misspelling of|en|!}} {{ngd|Used to amplify an exclamation, parodying unskilled typists who forget to press the [[shift]] key while typing exclamation points, thus typing "1"}}.
#: {{ux|en|''A:'' SUM1 Hl3p ME im alwyz L0ziN!1!?1!|Someone help me; I'm always losing!?}}
#: {{ux|en|''B:'' ''y d0nt u just g0 away l0zer!!1!!'''one'''!!'''one'''!!eleven!!1!|Why don't you just go away loser!}}
#* '''2003''' September 26, "DEAL WITH IT!!!!11'''one'''!!", in alt.games.video.nintendo.gamecube, ''Usenet''
#* '''2004''' November 9, "AWK sound recorder!!!11!!11'''one'''", in comp.lang.awk, ''Usenet''
#* '''2007''' December 1, "STANFORD!!1!!1!'''one'''!11!!1'''oneone'''!1!1!", in rec.sport.football.college, ''Usenet''

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|mathematics: multiplicative identity}} {{l|en|unity}}
* {{sense|US: one-dollar bill}} {{l|en|single}}
* {{sense|sarcastic substitution for {{m|en|!}}}} {{l|en|1}}, {{l|en|eleven}}

