====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# To cause to become one; to gather into a single whole; to [[unite]].
#* {{RQ:Chaucer Workes|Boetius|passage=Toldyng of temporell ordinaunce, assembled and '''oned''' in the lokyng of the Divine thoughte}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994| title=Mysticism, Death and Dying| author=Christopher Nugent| page=55| passage=The question, of course, evokes discernment, not dogma, but we should note that the "unknowing" involves intellectual knowledge, whereas the problematic of being "'''oned'''" involves experiential knowledge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000| title=The Journey of Forgiveness: Fulfilling the Healing Process| author=Carolyn Baker| page=145| passage=And both shall be '''oned''' in eternal happiness.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=Mental Health and Spirituality in Later Life| author=Elizabeth MacKinlay| page=83| passage=Knit and '''oned''' to God human beings are irrevocably in relationship with the divine.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019 |title=Love in Thin Places: Confessions of a Cathedral Chaplain| author=David Grieve| page=43| passage=What might be if we were '''Oned'''? United, as we would say, but at a greater depth than being a season ticket holder in a football club, or a shareholder in some conglomerate.}}

