* {{pedia}}

===Etymology 2===
Analogous to several senses of {{sl|en|nan-hbl|ê|notext=1}} and {{sl|en|cmn|的|tr=de|notext=1|pos=declarative particle, [[nominalizer]], etc.|nocat=1}}. This [[Appendix:Glossary#semantic_loan|semantic loan]] might have stemmed from the apparent similarity between ''one'' as a [[pro-form|prop-word]] and {{m|cmn|的}} / {{m|nan-hbl|ê|--ê}} as a nominalizer (e.g. {{m|nan-hbl|[[青色]][[的]]|t=the green one}}). Compare {{nc|yue|嘅|tr=ge<sup>3</sup>}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/wʌn/|[wän˦]|[wän˦˧]|q3=at the end of sentences|a=SG}}

====Particle====
{{en-part}} {{lb|en|Singapore|Singlish}}

# {{ngd|Used at the end of a sentence to highlight the [[characteristics]] of someone or something.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[got#Etymology 2|Got]] almonds '''one'''.|There are almonds in it.|inline = 1}}
#: {{ux|en|How come so heavy '''one'''?|Why is it so heavy?|inline = 1}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Patricia Mok|newspaper=w:The Straits Times|location=Singapore|page=5|section=Life!|date=14 February 2000|text=‘My boyfriends very possessive '''one'''. They don’t allow me to wear clothes I want, do things I want,’ she laments.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Ethical Egoist|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|year=2004|passage=Why so special '''one'''?}}
# {{ngd|Used at the end of a sentence to highlight the [[originator]] of something.}}
#: {{ux|en|My friend send '''one'''.|It was sent by my friend.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|en|Who say '''one'''?|Who said so?|inline=1}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|author=Singrish King|newsgroup=soc.culture.singapore|year=2011|passage=ooooooooooar! you [[ownself|own self]] admit '''one''' [[ah#Particle|har]]! i never say '''one''' har!}}
# {{ngd|A [[nominalizer]]; used to form a [[noun phrase]] without a {{w|Head (linguistics)|head noun}}.}}
#: {{ux|en|The sell fruits '''one''' went home already.|The fruit seller went home.|inline=1}}

====Pronoun====
{{en-pron}} {{lb|en|Singapore|Singlish}}

# {{lb|en|relative|rare}} {{ngd|Functions as a [[relative pronoun]] at the end of a [[relative clause]].}}

====Usage notes====
''One'' (Sense 2) takes the place of the {{lg|direct object}} at the end of sentences.

