* {{desc|gmq-osw|it}}
** Finland Swedish: {{l|sv|et}}, {{l|sv|ät}}<ref>{{cite-book|last=Howe|first=Stephen|title=The Personal Pronouns in the Germanic Languages: A Study of Personal Pronoun Morphology and Change in the Germanic Languages from the First Records to the Present Day|chapter=14. Old/Middle Swedish|publisher=Walter de Gruyter|year=1996}}</ref>

