==Turkish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|tr|[ˈit]}}
* {{audio|tr|LL-Q256 (tur)-ToprakM-it.wav}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tr|ota|ایت|tr=it}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*ï̄t|t=dog}}. Compare {{cog|sah|ыт|t=dog}}.

====Noun====
{{tr-noun|i|ler}}

# {{lb|tr|often|derogatory}} [[dog]]
# {{lb|tr|derogatory}} {{l|en|scoundrel}}, [[detestable]] [[person]], [[cur]]

=====Usage notes=====
Not historically derogatory, and still used as the primary term for "dog" in the countryside. Usually, if a dog is a stray or feral, it can be referred to as "it" as well. The more usual word is {{m|tr|köpek}}, which is also pejorative and derogatory when used for a person.

=====Declension=====
{{tr-infl-noun-c|i|pred=1|poss=1}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{head|tr|verb form}}

# {{tr-verb form of|itmek}}

