==Zhuang==
{{cardinalbox|za|0|1|2|lingz|ngeih|ord=}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|za|zh|-}} {{ltc-l|一|one}}. Cognate with {{cog|th|เอ็ด}}, {{cog|lo|ເອັດ}}, {{cog|shn|ဢဵတ်း}}, {{cog|aho|𑜒𑜢𑜄𑜫}}, {{cog|pcc|idt}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{za-pron}}

===Numeral===
{{za-head|numeral}}

# [[one]]
#: {{usex|za|daih''''it'''|first}}
#: {{usex|za|song bak '''it'''|two hundred and ten}}
#: {{usex|za|'''it''' cien|one thousand}}

====Usage notes====
Used with {{m|za|ngeih}} rather than {{m|za|song}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|za|ndeu}}
-------- end text --------
Page 3 his: Skipped, no changes
Page 3 his: -------- begin text --------
{{also|HIS|His|hís|his-}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|his}}, from {{inh|en|ang|his||his; its}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hes||of this}}, genitive of {{der|en|gem-pro|*hiz||this, this one}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱe-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ḱey-||this}}. Cognate with {{cog|da|-}}, {{cog|sv|-}}, {{cog|no|-}}, {{cog|is|hans||his}}. More at {{l|en|he}}; see also {{m|en|its}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|His||honorific}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{qualifier|stressed}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈhɪz/|a=UK,US,CA,AusE}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-his.ogg|a=US}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈhɘz/|a=NZ}}
* {{a|en|unstressed}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɪ̈z/}}
** {{IPA|en|/əz/|a=weak vowel}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪz|s=1}}
<!-- 1 syllable words !-->

====Determiner====
{{head|en|determiner|cat2=possessive determiners}}

# Belonging to [[him]]. {{defdate|from 8th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|year=1596.2|book=IIII|canto=I|stanza=41|text=With that he put '''his''' ſpurres vnto his ſteed, <br> With ſpeare in reſt, and toward him did fare, <br> Like ſhaft out of a bow preuenting ſpeed.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|IV|46|No matter how early I came down, I would find him on the veranda, smoking cigarettes, or otherwise '''his''' man would be there with a message to say that '''his''' master would shortly join me if I would kindly wait.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Ivory Coast: 100 more bodies found as ethnic tensions rise|author=Xan Rice|work=w:The Guardian|date=8 Apr 2011|text=In '''his''' first televised address since the siege in Abidjan began this week, Ouattara said he would focus on returning the country to normal to ease the plight of civilians.|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2011/apr/08/ivory-coast-deaths-ethnic-tensions}}
# {{lb|en|sometimes|dated}} Belonging to a person of unspecified gender.
#* {{RQ:Hume Morals
|passage=On the contrary, those other passions, commonly denominated selfish, both produce different sentiments in each individual, according to '''his''' particular situation {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Norman L. Geisler; Winfried Corduan|title=Philosophy of Religion: Second Edition|page=9
|passage=It is our conviction that piecemeal critiques of nontheisms will not suffice. The theist must enter the arena with a positive and comprehensive case of '''his''' own.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[its|Its]]; belonging to it. (Now only when implying personification.) {{defdate|11th|17th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|url=https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k45595/f201.item|date=18 July 1530|author=[[w:John Palsgrave|Iohan Palſgrave]]|title=Leſclarciſſement de la langue francoyſe{{...}}|publisher=Richard Pynſon, Iohan Haukyns|location=London|oclc=715474564|newversion=reprinted as|year2=1972|publisher2=Slatkine Reprints|location2=Genève|title2=Lesclarcissement de la langue françoyse|chapter=The Introduction|page=32|passage=In ſo moche that if any verbe be of the thyꝛde coniugation <br> I ſet out all '''his''' rotes and tenſes{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Montaigne Florio Essayes|book=II|chapter=Of Drunkennesse|page=200|passage=My ſtomacke could not well reach ſo farre: it is very much troubled to come to an end of that which it takes for '''his''' neede.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Matthew|5|13|page=1224|column=1|text=Yee are the ſalt of the earth: But if the ſalt haue loſt '''his''' ſauour, wherewith ſhall it bee ſalted?}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} Used as a [[genitive]] marker in place of ''’s'' after a noun, especially a masculine noun ending in ''-s'', to express the possessive case. {{defdate|from 11th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|Ahab '''his''' mark}} for ''Ahab's mark''.
#: {{ux|en|{{w|Sejanus his Fall|''Sejanus '''his''' Fall''}}}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When followed by a noun, it is sometimes referred to as a ''possessive adjective'', qualifying the following noun. It is, however, the [[possessive case]] of the personal pronoun [[he]].
* {{qual|fourth sense}} See {{pedia|His genitive}}

