==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|him}}, from {{inh|en|ang|him}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*himmai|t=to this, to this one}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|him|t=him}}, {{cog|fy|him|t=him}}, Sylt {{cog|frr|ham}}, {{m|frr|höm|t=him}}, {{cog|nl|hem|t=him}}, {{cog|nds-de|hum}}, {{m|nds-de|hüm}}, {{m|nds-de|em|t=him}}, {{cog|de|ihm|t=him|pos=dative}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|hĭm|a=UK,US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈhɪm/}}, unstressed {{IPA|en|/əm/|[ɪ̈m]}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-him.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|hymn}},[['em]] for unstressed in some pronunciations.
* {{rhymes|en|ɪm|s=1}}

===Pronoun===
{{en-pron|desc=personal pronoun, objective case}}

# {{non-gloss definition|A masculine pronoun; [[he]] as a grammatical object.}}
## With [[dative]] effect or as an indirect object. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|url=https://www.google.co.nz/books/edition/A_pistle_to_the_Ch_riste_n_reader_The_Re/Vb07AAAAcAAJ|author=w:John Frith|title=A piſtle to the Chriſten reader{{...}}|year=1529|passage={{...}}therfoꝛ Chꝛiſt '''wold''' not call '''him''' abominable / But the verye abomination it ſilf.}}
##* {{RQ:Stoker Dracula|text=‘I promise,’ he said as I gave '''him''' the papers.}}
## Following a [[preposition]]. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
##* {{RQ:Austen Pride and Prejudice|text=She was in no humour for conversation with anyone but himself; and to '''him''' she had hardly courage to speak.}}
## With [[accusative]] effect or as a direct object. {{defdate|from 12th c.}}
##* {{RQ:Dickens Bleak House|text=‘He's got it buttoned in his breast. I saw '''him''' put it there.’}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} {{non-gloss definition|As a grammatical subject or object when joined with a conjunction.}}
#: ''Now '''him''' and Bernie are best friends.''
#: ''Released a [statement] warning that '''him''' and 25,000 troops were going to stage a coup.''
# {{lb|en|now|rare}} Used [[reflexively]]: (to) [[himself]]. {{defdate|from 9th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|Acts|XII|text=Apon a daye apoynted, the kynge arayed '''hym''' in royall apparell, and set '''hym''' in his seate, and made an oracion unto them.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1765|author=[[s:Author:Oliver Goldsmith|Oliver Goldsmith]]|title=[[s:The Traveller, or, A Prospect of Society|The traveller, or, A prospect of society]]
|passage=Though poor the peasant’s hut, his feasts though small,<br>He sees his little lot the lot of all;<br>[...]<br>But calm, and bred in ignorance and toil,<br>Each wish contracting, fits '''him''' to the soil.}}
# With [[nominative]] effect: [[he]], especially as a predicate after {{m|en|be}}, or following a preposition. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|V|10|text=Before my body, I throw my warlike Shield: Lay on Macduffe, And damn'd be '''him''', that first cries hold, enough.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Claire Cozens|journal=The Guardian|date=11 Jun 2003
|passage=Lowe quit the West Wing last year amid rumours that he was unhappy that his co-stars earned more than '''him'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|impressive}} {{lb|en|slang}} A person of elevated skill at a [[sport#Noun|sport]], [[game#Noun|game]], or other [[activity#Noun|activity]].
#: {{ux|en|Stop trying that, you're not '''him''' bro.}}
#: {{ux|en|Bro thinks he's '''him'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=u/baggypantsman|title=Super Mario 64 - 0 Star in 6:16 by Suigi|site=w:Reddit|url=https://www.reddit.com/r/speedrun/comments/17ghh2r/comment/k6gnaxd/|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/tr3TO|archivedate=23 December 2023|location=r/speedrun|date=25 October 2023|passage=Watched this one live, he randomly got it less than an hour into the stream while derusting for PACE. He's just '''him'''.}}

