===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A male person or animal.
#: {{syn|en|he}}
#: {{ux|en|I think this bird is a '''him''', but it may be a her.}}
#* '''1985''', {{w|Hélène Cixous}}, ''Sorties'' (translated)
#*: {{...}} daring dizzying passages in other, fleeting and passionate dwellings within the '''hims''' and hers whom she inhabits {{...}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=w:Tom Wolfe|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=jCQZwLPJpJoC&pg=PT487&dq=%22hims%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjSvJaNtuzPAhUK-mMKHcdfAKo4MhDoAQggMAE#v=onepage&q=%22hims%22&f=false|title=I Am Charlotte Simmons: A Novel
|passage=Both '''hims''' took a good look at him.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Charles J. Sullivan|title=Love and Survival|page=68|passage=By this time, she had so many questions, but she only hit him up for one answer about those “'''hims'''” and “hers.” She asked, “Do both '''hims''' and hers reproduce hummers?”}}

