===Symbol===
{{wikipedia|Voiceless glottal fricative}}
{{head-lite|mul|symbols|langname=Translingual}}

# {{lb|mul|IPA}} a [[voiceless]] [[glottal]] [[fricative]] or [[approximant]].
#: {{lb|mul|superscript {{angbr IPA|ʰ}}}} (after a consonant) [[aspiration]]; (before a consonant) [[pre-aspiration]]; otherwise a weak, fleeting or epenthetic {{IPAchar-lite|[h]}} &ndash; see [[ʰ]].
# {{lb|mul|metrology}} symbol for the [[prefix]] [[hecto-]], indicating multiplication by 100
# symbol of the [[hour]]
# {{lb|mul|italic}} [[Planck's constant]]
# [[helion]]
# [[higgson]]
# {{lb|mul|transcription}} [[aspiration]]
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Robin Wooffitt|chapter=Analysing the Organization of Successful Demonstrations of Paranormal Cognition|title=The Language of Mediums and Psychics: The Social Organization of Everyday Miracles|publisher=w:Ashgate Publishing|year=2006|page=70|isbn=0 7546 4202 X|passage={{monospace|PP: {{sup|·}}'''hh'''⎡y’know-,}} / {{monospace|R: [I used it today Doris for the first time.}} / {{monospace|You used it today?}} / {{monospace|R: yea(huh)s ''(Smiling voice)''}} / {{monospace|(0.3)}} / {{monospace|PP: t{{sup|·}}'''hhhh''' And ah’ve another voice come, an’ she says, she’s just bought a new c{{underline|oo}}ker you know. {{sup|·}}'''hh''' they know-, they get to know everyth{{underline|i:}}ng,}}|termlang=mul}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=John Heritage; Steven Clayman|chapter=Transcript Symbols|title=Talk in Action: Interactions, Identities, and Institutions|year=2010|pages=284 and 286|isbn=978-1-405-18550-9|passage={{monospace|Bee: {{sup|·}}'''hhh''' {{underline|Uh::}}, (0.3) {{underline|I}} don’know I guess she’s aw- she’s aw{{underline|r}}ight she went to thee uh:: h{{underline|h}}ospital again tih{{underline|d}}a:y,}}{{...}}Hearable aspiration is shown where it occurs in the talk by the letter '''''h''''' – the more '''''h'''''’s, the more aspiration. The aspiration may represent breathing, laughter, etc. If it occurs inside the boundaries of a word, it may be enclosed in parentheses in order to set it apart from the sounds of the word. If the aspiration is an inhalation, it is shown with a dot before it (usually a raised dot) or a raised degree symbol. {{monospace|Bee: [Ba::]sk('''h''')etb('''h''')a(h)ll? ('''h''')(°Whe('''h''')re.)}}{{...}}|termlang=mul}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Simona Pekarek Doehler; Elwys De Stefani; Anne-Sylvie Horlacher|chapter=The hanging topic construction as an interactional resource|title=Time and Emergence in Grammar: Dislocation, Topicalization and Hanging Topic in French Talk-in-Interaction|series=Studies in Language and Social Interaction|seriesvolume=28|publisher=w:John Benjamins Publishing Company|year=2015|section=section 5 (Aphoristic HT formulations as closing devices)|page=210|isbn=978 90 272 6798 6|passage={{monospace|.'''hhhh''' (0.1) donc pour moi l''es hommes eu::h''}}|termlang=mul}}

