==Arabic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ar|انا}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَنَ}}
* {{ar-IPA|أَنَا}} (in pausa)
* {{audio|ar|Ar-أنا.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔanāku}}, from {{inh|ar|afa-pro|*ˀanāku}}, hence also {{cog|ber-pro|*ənăkkʷ}} ({{cog|kab|nekk}}) and {{cog|egy|jnk}} ({{cog|cop|ⲁⲛⲟⲕ|tr=anok}}).

Cognate with {{cog|he|אני|tr=aní}}.

====Pronoun====
{{ar-pron|أَنَا|m|g2=f|tr=ʔana, ʔanā}} (''enclitic form'' {{m|ar|ـِيَ}} ''or'' {{m|ar|ـِي}} ''or'' {{m|ar|ـنِي}} ''or'' {{m|ar|ـنِيَ}})

# [[I]] (''first person singular subject pronoun'')

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|ar|أَنَا}} has four enclitic forms which are employed in different contexts and are generally not interchangeable. The enclitic forms {{m|ar|ـنِي}} and {{m|ar|ـنِيَ}} are attached to verbs, prepositions ending in {{m|ar|نْ}} with no final vowel (''e.g.'', {{m|ar|مِنْ}} and {{m|ar|عَنْ}}), and the sisters of {{m|ar|إِنَّ}} except {{m|ar|لَعَلَّ}}. The forms {{m|ar|ـِي}} and {{m|ar|ـيَ}} are used elsewhere, but in cases where {{m|ar|ـِي}} would be preceded by a long vowel, only {{m|ar|ـيَ}} is used.
# {{ux|ar|سَاعِدْ'''نِي'''|help '''me'''|inline=y}}
# {{ux|ar|كِتَابِ'''ي'''|tr=kitāb'''ī'''|'''my''' book|inline=y}}
# {{ux|ar|عَلَ'''يَّ'''|on '''me'''|inline=y}}

