* Ido: ''suffix'' {{t|io|-os}} ''after verbal roots''
* Indonesian: {{t+|id|akan}}
* Italian: ''Use the future tense'' {{t|it|-erò|alt=-rò, -rai, -rà, -remo, -rete, -ranno}}, e.g. ''And'''rò''' al negozio.''
* Japanese: ''present/future tense form is usually used''
* Khmer: {{t+|km|នឹង}} {{qualifier|prefix}}
* Korean: {{t|ko|ᆯ 것이다}}, {{t|ko|ᆯ게}}
* Kurdish:
*: Northern Kurdish: {{t+|kmr|dê}}, {{t+|kmr|ê}}
* Lao: {{t|lo|ຈະ}}, {{t|lo|ຈິ}}, {{t|lo|ຊິ}}, {{t|lo|ຈັກ}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* Latin: ''Use the future tense''
* Lithuanian: ''Use the future tense''
* Luxembourgish: {{t|lb|wäerten}}
* Macedonian: {{t|mk|ќе}} {{qualifier|+ present form}}
* Malay: {{t+|ms|akan}}
* Navajo: {{t|nv|dooleeł}}
* Norwegian:
*: Bokmål: {{t+|nb|vil}}, {{t|nb|kommer til å}}, {{t+|nb|skal}}
* Old English: ''Use the present tense''; {{qualifier|more rarely}} {{t+|ang|willan}}, {{t|ang|sċulan}}
* Persian: {{t+|fa|خواستن|tr=xâstan}}
* Polish: ''Use the future perfective'' or ''use the future of {{l|pl|być}} + imperfective infinitive''
* Portuguese: ''Use the future tense''; {{qualifier|colloquial}} ''use present indicative forms of {{t+|pt|ir}}''
* Russian: ''Use the future perfective'' or ''use the future of {{l|ru|быть}} + imperfective infinitive''
*: ''I will be going back and forth to the post office'' — Я [[быть|буду]] [[ходить|ходи́ть]] на по́чту
*: ''I will be going to the post office'' — Я [[быть|бу́ду]] [[идти|идти́]] на по́чту
*: ''I will go to the post office'' — Я [[пойти|пойду́]] на по́чту
* Serbo-Croatian:
*: Cyrillic: {{t|sh|хтети}}, {{t|sh|хтјети}}
*: Roman: {{t|sh|hteti}}, {{t+|sh|htjeti}}
* Slovak: ''Use the future perfective'' or ''use the future of {{l|sk|byť}} + imperfective infinitive''
* Slovene: {{t+|sl|biti}}
