* Swahili: {{t|sw|-ta-}}
* Swedish: {{t|sv|komma till att}}, {{t|sv|komma att}}, {{t+|sv|skola}}, {{t+|sv|vilja}}, {{t+|sv|tänka}}
*: ''I will go to the store'' — ''Jag ska gå till affären'' or ''Jag kommer att gå till affären''
* Thai: {{t+|th|จะ}}
* Turkish: (2): suffix for all verbs: [[-ecek]] (if the last vowel of a verb is e,i,ö or ü) or [[-acak]] (if the vowel is a,ı,o or u).
* Ukrainian: ''Use the future perfective'' or ''use the future of {{l|uk|бу́ти}} + imperfective infinitive''; special endings, e.g. "I will walk": {{lang|uk|ходи́тиму}} ({{l|uk|ходи́ти}} + {{lang|uk|иму}})
* Vietnamese: {{t+|vi|sẽ}}
* West Frisian: {{t|fy|sille}}, {{t+|fy|gean}}
* Yapese: {{t|yap|ra}}
* Yiddish: {{t|yi|וועלן}}
