==Arabic==

===Etymology===
{{univerbation|ar|هَـ|pos1=now interrogative {{m|ar|أَ}}|لـ|pos2=affirmative particle, found as {{m|ar||لَـ|t=truly}} and the exhortative {{m|ar||لِـ}} the vowel of which disappears between {{m|ar|فَـ}} or {{m|ar|وَ}} and a following verb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|هَلْ}}

===Particle===
{{ar-particle|هَلْ}}

# {{non-gloss definition|introduces a positive yes-no question}}
#: {{syn|ar|أَ}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''هَلْ''' [[فتح|فَتَحْتَ]] [[نافذة|النَّافِذَةَ]]؟|t=Did you open the window?}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''هَلِ''' [[ولد|ٱلْوَلَدُ]] [[فِي]] [[مدرسة|ٱلْمَدْرَسَةِ]]؟|t=Is the boy at school?}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''هَلْ''' [[أَنْتَ]] [[مِصْرِيٌّ]]؟|t=Are you Egyptian?}}
# {{non-gloss definition|indicates a suggestion}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|61|10|passage='''هَلْ''' أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَى تِجَارَةٍ تُنْجِيكُم مِنْ عَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ|t='''Shall''' I guide you to a transaction that will save you from a painful punishment?}}
# {{non-gloss definition|indicates an '''exclusive''' disjunction with {{m|ar|أَمْ|t=or}}, as in alternative questions}}
#: {{syn|ar|أَ}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:مَجْمُوع الْفَتَاوَى
|trans-title=The Collection of Rulings
|url=https://shamela.ws/book/7289/5737
|author={{w|Ibn Taymiyyah|Taqī al-Dīn ʾAḥmad ibn Taymiyyah}}
|year=13th-14th century {{CE}}
|volume=11
|page=392–393
|publisher=w:en:King Fahd Complex
|location=Medina, Saudi Arabia
|year_published=2004
|isbn=9960-770-20-6
|text=فَإِذَا أَرَادَ الْمُرِيدُ أَنَّ عُقُولَ الْعُقَلَاءِ لَمْ تَصِلْ إلَى مَعْرِفَةِ مِثْلِ هَذِهِ الْأُمُورِ فَهَذَا صَحِيحٌ وَأَمَّا إذَا أَرَادَ أَنَّ الْعُقَلَاءَ لَيْسَ عِنْدَهُمْ عِلْمٌ وَلَا يَقِينٌ بَلْ حَيْرَةٌ وَرَيْبٌ فَهَذَا بَاطِلٌ قَطْعًا. وَمَا ذُكِرَ عَنْ ذِي النُّونِ " فِي هَذَا الْبَابِ مَعَ أَنَّ ذَا النُّونِ قَدْ وَقَعَ مِنْهُ كَلَامٌ أَنْكَرَ عَلَيْهِ وَعَزَّرَهُ الْحَارِثُ بْنُ مِسْكِينٍ وَطَلَبَهُ الْمُتَوَكِّلُ إلَى بَغْدَادَ وَاتُّهِمَ بِالزَّنْدَقَةِ وَجَعَلَهُ النَّاسُ مَنْ الْفَلَاسِفَةِ فَمَا أَدْرِي '''هَلْ''' قَالَ هَذَا أَمْ لَا؟
|t=If it is meant that the minds of right-minded men have not attained knowledge of such things, then yes, this is true. If, however, it is meant that not even right-minded men have knowledge of nor are certain about anything but are rather in doubt and perplexity, this is absolutely false, together with what {{w|Dhul-Nun al-Misri|Ḏū al-Nūn}} said on this matter. {{w|Dhul-Nun al-Misri|Ḏū al-Nūn}} himself, though, did say things for which he was reproached and chastised by al-Ḥāriṯ ibn Miskīn, and he was sent for by {{w|al-Mutawakkil}} and was charged with heresy and has been deemed to be among the Philosophers, and so I do not know '''whether''' he said this or not.}}

====Usage notes====
Cannot precede a negative sentence, a conditional sentence, or {{m|ar|إِنَّ}}.

====See also====
* {{l|ar|أَ}}

===References===
* {{R:sem-pro:FS Militarev|pages=200–201}}

