==Albanian==

===Etymology===
Suffixed definite article attached on nouns ending with ''k, g'' ({{IPA|sq|[k]|[ɡ]}}). From the ending {{der|sq|ine-pro|*-osyo}}. cognate to {{cog|cms|-aihi}}.<ref>Matzinger 2015, pp. 62–66</ref><ref>Ismajli 2015, pp. 65–68.</ref><ref>Matzinger, Joachim (2017). "The Lexicon of Albanian". In Klein, Jared; Joseph, Brian; Fritz, Matthias (eds.). Handbook of Comparative and Historical Indo-European Linguistics. 3. Walter de Gruyter. </ref>

Related to {{cog|sq|-i||of the, etc.}}, {{cog|sq|i||of, the, to}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sq|[u]}}

===Article===
{{head|sq|article|g=m}}

# {{ngd|masculine singular nominative and accusative [[suffixed]] [[definite]] [[article]]}}: [[the]]
#: {{suffixusex|sq|flok|floku|t1=hair|t2=the hair}}
#: {{suffixusex|sq|treg|tregu|t1=market|t2=the market}}
#: {{suffixusex|sq|plak|plaku|t1=old man|t2=the old man}}
#: {{suffixusex|sq|zog|zogu|t1=bird|t2=the bird}}
#:: (note: {{l|sq|-u}} shifts towards {{l|sq|-i}}  among some [[Gheg]] dialects; {{m|sq|zog|zog'''i'''}} instead of {{m|sq|zog|zog'''u'''}})

====Related terms====
* {{sense|suffixed article, suffix}} {{l|sq|-a}}, {{l|sq|-e}}, {{l|sq|-ë}}, {{l|sq|-i}}, {{l|sq|-o}}, {{l|sq|-ia}}, {{l|sq|-ja}}, {{l|sq|-je}}, {{l|sq|-jë}}, {{l|sq|-at}}, {{l|sq|-et}}, {{l|sq|-ët}}, {{l|sq|-it}}, {{l|sq|-ot}}, {{l|sq|-ut}}, {{l|sq|-të}}, {{l|sq|-ri}}, {{l|sq|-ishte}}, {{l|sq|-ishtja}}
* {{sense|article, preposition}} {{l|sq|e}}, {{l|sq|i}}, {{l|sq|së}}, {{l|sq|të}}

===References===
<references/>

