===Suffix===
{{head|chk|suffix}}

# [[out]], [[outwards]]; {{non-gloss definition|used to modify verb direction}}

==Esperanto==

===Etymology 1===
Etymology unclear. Perhaps from the Greek ''-ou'' imperative (pronounced {{IPAchar|[u]}}) of {{glossary|deponent}} verbs such as ''dekhou'' “receive!”, or from the Hebrew imperative ''-û.'' It may instead—or also—be connected to the vowel of the Esperanto conditional suffix {{m|eo|-us}}, minus the ''s'' of the indicative inflections.

====Suffix====
{{head|eo|suffix}}

# {{n-g|{{glossary|volitive}} inflection of verbs, indicating that an action or state is desired, requested, ordered, or aimed for.}}
#: {{ux|eo|'''Donu''' ĝin al mi.|t='''Give''' it to me. (''expresses a request or command'')}}
#: {{ux|eo|Ni '''faru''' tion.|t=Let's '''do''' that. (''expresses a desire or aim'')}}
#: {{ux|eo|Mi '''iru''' dormi.|t=I '''ought to go''' to sleep. (''expresses desirability of the action'')}}
#: {{ux|eo|Via infano '''sukcesu''' en la vivo.|'''May''' your child '''be successful''' in life. (''wish or desire'')}}
#: {{ux|eo|Mi volas, ke vi '''helpu''' min.|t=I want you to '''help''' me. (''desire'')}}
#: {{ux|eo|Ŝi petas, ke mi '''silentu'''.|t=She asks that I '''be silent'''. (''request'')}}

===Etymology 2===
Apparently connected to the ''u'' at the end of {{m|eo|unu||one, a certain}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|eo|suffix}}

# -one. (Ending of the individual [[:Category:Esperanto correlatives|correlatives]].)
#: {{m|eo|kiu||what '''individual''', who}}
#: {{m|eo|tiu||that '''individual''', that one}}
#: {{m|eo|ĉiu||all '''individuals''', everyone}}
#: {{m|eo|iu||some '''individual''', someone}}
#: {{m|eo|neniu||no '''individual''', nobody}}
#: {{m|eo|(unofficial) [[aliu]]||another '''individual''', someone else}}

{{Universala Vortaro}}
{{eo BRO|1}}
[[Category:Esperanto endings|u]]

==Estonian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|et|urj-pro|*-w}} (as applied to stems ending in ''-e''). Cognate with {{cog|fi|-u}}.

===Suffix===
{{et-noun|suff=1|-u|-u}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Derives nouns from verbs or prefixes}}
#: [[jagama]] "to divide" → [[jagu]] "a part, a share"
#: [[kaduma]] "to disappear" → [[kadu]] "loss, losing"
#: [[sise-]] "inside" → [[sisu]] "content"
#: [[pesema]] "to wash" → [[pesu]] "wash, washing"

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|et}}

==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*-u}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*-w}} (as applied to stems ending in ''-e''). Cognate with {{cog|et|-u}}.

===Suffix===
{{fi-suffix|noun|var=y}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Forms nouns from verbs. Most common with ''e''- and ''i''-stem verbs.}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|hyppiä|gloss1=to be jumping|hyppy|gloss2=jump}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|itkeä|gloss1=to cry|itku|gloss2=cry(ing)}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|pestä|gloss1=to wash|pesu|gloss2=wash(ing)}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|potkia|gloss1=to kick|potku|gloss2=kick}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|urheilla|gloss1=to practice sport|urheilu|gloss2=sport}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Derives a number of nouns from other nouns.}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|silmä|gloss1=eye|silmu|gloss2=bud}}
#: {{suffixusex|fi|sisä-|gloss1=inside|sisu|gloss2=determination, perseverance}}

====Usage notes====
The front-harmonic variant {{m|fi||-y}} is only used when the first vowel of the word is one of the harmonic front vowels {{m-lite|fi||-y-}}, {{m-lite|fi||-ä-}}, {{m-lite|fi||-ö-}}; words beginning with neutral front vowels {{m|fi||e, i}} take the back-harmonic variant.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-valo|-|||u|a}}
{{fi-decl-palvelu|-u|a}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|fi}}
{{col-auto|fi
|-ukka
|-ula
|-uli
|-ura
}}

====See also====
* {{l|fi|-o}}
* {{l|fi|-uu}}

