==Ido==

===Etymology===
Common vowel found in pronouns in Romance languages: {{bor|io|fr|tu}}, {{bor|io|it|tu}} and {{bor|io|es|tú}}, also in {{bor|io|fr|vous}} and as an ''o'' in {{bor|io|it|voi}} and {{bor|io|es|vos}}, etc. (Compare {{m|io|tu}} and {{m|io|vu}})

===Suffix===
{{head|io|suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|suffix used to form pronouns indicating a person}}
#: {{suffixusex|io|omna|gloss1=all, every|omnu|gloss2=everyone}}

====Usage notes====
As it is used to form pronouns, you cannot use it to create nouns. Instead, to form an agent from an adjective like {{m|io|felica||happy}}, you just make it a noun: {{m|io|felico||a happy person}}.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|io}}

