==Punjabi==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|pa|ar|عَالَم}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|pa|/ɑː.lə.mᵊ/}}

====Noun====
{{pa-noun|g=m|gur=ਆਲਮ|head=عالَم}}

# [[world]]
# [[universe]]
# [[kingdom]]
# [[state]], [[condition]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|pa|ar|عَالِم}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|pa|/ɑː.lə.mᵊ/}}

====Adjective====
{{pa-adj|gur=ਆਲਮ|head=عالَم}}

# [[learned]]
# [[knowledgeable]]
# [[intelligent]]
# [[wise]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Many Arabic loanwords, such as {{l|pa|عالَم}}, can have multiple meanings in Punjabi, where in this case, one is related to the noun, while the latter meaning is used to refer to the adjective. Both are borrowed from different Arabic words, yet have the same pronunciation in Punjabi, unlike in, the sister language, Urdu ''{{l|ur|عالِم}}'', (and rarely in Hindi ''{{l|hi|आलिम}}''), where there is a distinction in pronunciation between the adjective and the noun. This can cause ambiguity as generally Punjabi speakers, who tend to also speak Hindi and Urdu, might actually mix words from either languages and not emphasise on the difference in pronunciation.

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|pa|عِلْم}}

