# {{spelling of|klj|Arabic|bəd|t=[[evil]]}}

==North Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology===
From {{der|apc|ar|بِوِدِّ}}.

===Preposition===
{{head|apc|preposition|tr=badd, bidd}}

# [[want]] to
#: {{ux|apc|بدي شوفك كل يوم، يا حبيبي|tr='''Baddi''' šūfak kill yōm, ya ḥabībi.|'''I want''' to see you every day, my dear.}}
# [[should]]; [[need]]
#: {{ux|apc|شو بدنا نئللو؟|tr=Šu '''badna''' nʾil-lu?|What '''should''' we tell him?}}

====Usage notes====
* The past is formed by adding {{m|apc|كان|tr=kēn}}, which originally would be left unchanged,<!-- because grammatically the subject is "badd" --> but is now equally commonly conjugated. Thus: {{m|apc||كان بدي شوفك|tr=kēn baddi šūfak}} or {{m|apc||كنت بدي شوفك|tr=kint baddi šūfak}}, both “I wanted to see you.”

