==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=SLYA}} / {{m|pal|tr=wt'|ts=wad|t=bad, evil}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*watah}}, with further origin {{uncertain|fa|nocap=1}}. Akin to {{cog|xcl|վատ}}, an Iranian borrowing. Unrelated to {{noncog|en|bad}}, despite phonetic and semantic similarity.
{{rfe|fa|Is the proto-Iranian from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*weh₂t-|t=raging}}? Compare {{cog|sa|वात|t=injured, hurt}}.}}

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|bad}}
* {{audio|fa|Fa-بد.ogg|a=Iran}}

====Adjective====
{{fa-regional|بد|بد|бад}}
{{fa-adj|head=بَد|tr=bad|c=+}}

# [[bad]]; not good
# [[evil]]

=====Antonyms=====
