From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=tyšnk'|ts=tišnag|sc=Phlv}}, from {{inh|fa|peo|-}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro||*tŕ̥šnakah}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*tŕ̥šnah}}, from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*tŕ̥šnas}}, from {{inh|fa|ine-pro||*tr̥s-nó-s}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ters-||dry}}.

Compare {{cog|ae|𐬙𐬀𐬭𐬱𐬥𐬀}}, {{cog|sa|तृष्णा}}, {{cog|grc|τέρσομαι}}, {{cog|la|terra}}, {{cog|xcl|թառամիմ}}, {{cog|en|thirst}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|tišˈna|prs=tišˈna,tašˈna|tg=tašˈna}}

===Adjective===
{{fa-regional|تشنه|تشنه|ташна}}
{{fa-adj|tr=tešne}}

# [[thirsty]]
#: {{uxi|fa|'''تشنه''' هستم.|tr='''tešne''' hastam.|t=I am thirsty.|q=literary}}
#: {{uxi|fa|'''تشن'''مه.|tr='''tešna'''-m-e.|t=I'm thirsty.|q=colloquial Iranian}}
# in [[drought]]
# {{lb|fa|figurative}} [[eager]], [[desiring]]
#: {{uxi|fa|'''تشنه''' آزادی|tr='''tešne'''-ye âzâdi|t='''thirsty''' for freedom}}

====Usage notes====
* In colloquial Iranian, "to be thirsty" is expressed with an enclitic pronoun attached to {{m|fa||تشنه}}, then followed by {{m|fa|ـه|tr=-e|t=is}}, as in the usage example above.

====Related terms====
