From the form {{m|apc|هَيِّي|tr=hayye, hayyi}} attested in Damascene (compare the development of {{m|apc|شويّ|tr=šwayy}} and {{m|apc|ميّ|tr=ṃayy}}), which may be an irregular {{glossary|lenition}} of an earlier form {{m|apc||*هَيْذِي|tr=hayḏe, hayḏi}}. In the Lebanese form {{m|apc|هيدي|tr=hayde, haydi}}, the {{m|apc||ذ|tr=ḏ}} of {{m|apc||*هيذي}} regularly evolved into {{m|apc||د|tr=d}} instead of leniting.

====Pronoun====
{{apc-pronoun|g=f|tr=hayy}}

# {{feminine of|apc|هاد|tr=hād}}: {{lbl|apc|Syria}} [[this]]
#: {{syn|apc|هيدي|tr=haydi|q=Lebanon}}

====Determiner====
{{head|apc|determiner|g=f|tr=hayy}}

# {{feminine of|apc|هاد|tr=hād}}: {{lbl|apc|Syria}} [[this]]
#: {{syn|apc|هيدي|tr=haydi|q1=Lebanon|هـ|tr2=ha-|q2=before the definite article|id2=determiner}}

{{cln|apc|demonstrative pronouns}}

