==Persian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal|sc=Phlv|tr=MGLTA}} / {{m|pal|sc=Phlv|tr=nʾmk'|ts=nāmag|t=book, letter, any written text}}, equivalent to {{m|pal||nām|t=name}} (itself from {{der|fa|ira-pro|*Hnā́ma|t=name}})<ref>{{R:ira:ESIJa|vol=5|page=539}}</ref> + {{m|pal||-ak|pos=derivative suffix}}, originally a "name-list" or catalogue of products made for economic or bureaucratic purposes, this being the most common use of writing in early Iranian languages.<ref>{{cite-book|chapter=Considerations on the Etymology of Persian nāmeh|last=Lurje|first=Pavel B.|year=2022|title=The Reward of the Righteous: Festschrift in Honour of Almut Hintze|pages=297—306}}</ref> {{surf|fa|نام<tr:nâm><t:name>|ـه<tr:-e>}}, but rarely analyzed or understood as such. Compare {{cog|xcl|նամակ|t=letter, writing}}, an Iranian borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|nā`ma}}
* {{audio|fa|Fa-نامه.ogg|a=Iran}}

===Noun===
{{fa-regional|نامه|نامه|нома}}
{{fa-noun|tr=nâme|pl=نامه‌ها}}

# [[letter]] (written or printed communication)
# {{lb|fa|archaic|or in compounds}} [[book]]; anything [[written]]
#: {{syn|fa|کتاب|tr=ketâb}}
#: {{coi|fa|[[روز'''نامه''']]|tr=ruz'''nâme'''|t=daily newspaper|lit=day-'''book'''}}
#: {{coi|fa|[[فیلم'''نامه''']]|tr=film'''nâme'''|t=screenplay|lit=film-'''book'''}}

