{{also|کان|كأن|گان}}
==Arabic==
{{ar-rootbox|ك و ن}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*kawan-|t=to be or exist in a place}}. Compare {{cog|gez|ኮነ}}, {{cog|akk|kânum|𒄀𒈾|tr=kânum}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|كَانَ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-كان.ogg}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u}}

# {{lb|ar|copulative}} to [[be]] {{+obj|ar|acc}}
# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to [[exist]], to [[be]], [[there be]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|280|passage=وَإِنْ '''كَانَ''' ذُو عُسْرَةٍ فَنَظِرَةٌ إِلَىٰ مَيْسَرَةٍ|translation=And if he '''is''' in unease, then [let there be] a delay until a time of ease.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|40|68|passage=هُوَ الَّذِي يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ فَإِذَا قَضَىٰ أَمْرًا فَإِنَّمَا يَقُولُ لَهُ '''كُنْ''' فَ'''يَكُونُ'''|translation=It is He who causes to live and causes to die. And when He decided a matter, he says to it, "'''Be'''", and it '''is'''.}}
#* {{RQ:SVD|Genesis|1|3|passage=وَقَالَ اللهُ: «لِ'''يَكُنْ''' نُورٌ»، فَ'''كَانَ''' نُورٌ.|t=And God said, Let '''there be''' light: and '''there was''' light. (''literally'', And God says, “Let light '''be'''”; and light '''is'''.)}}
# to [[behove]]
#: {{syn|ar|يَنْبَغِي}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|24|16|passage=وَلَوْلَا إِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوهُ قُلْتُمْ مَا '''يَكُونُ''' لَنَا أَنْ نَتَكَلَّمَ بِهَٰذَا سُبْحَانَكَ هَٰذَا بُهْتَانٌ عَظِيمٌ}}
# to [[happen]], to [[occur]], to [[take place]]
# {{lb|ar|auxiliary}} {{non-gloss definition|forms the [[past perfect]], [[past continuous]], [[future perfect]] and [[future continuous]] tenses}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''كَانَ''' (قَدْ) فَعَلَ|He had done.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''كَانَ''' يَفْعَلُ|He was doing.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''سَيَكُونُ''' (قَدْ) فَعَلَ|He will have done.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''سَيَكُونُ''' يَفْعَلُ|He will be doing.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Like all copulative verbs in Arabic, {{m|ar|كَانَ}} takes a predicate in the accusative case. This contrasts with old Indo-European languages such as Latin and Greek, in which the predicate of a copulative verb is in the nominative case.
*: {{ux|ar|'''كَانَ''' جَمَالٌ عَبْدُ ٱلنَّاصِرِ '''رَئِيسَ''' جُمْهُورِيَّةِ مِصْرَ ٱلْعَرَبِيَّةِ.|t=Gamal Abdel Nasser '''was the president''' of the Arab Republic of Egypt.}}
* In the present indicative, “to be” is most often expressed by a [[w:Nominal sentence|nominal sentence]] ({{m|ar|[[جُمْلَة]] [[اسمي|اِسْمِيَّة]]|tr=jumla ismiyya}}) with no verb. In this case, the predicate is in the nominative case.
*: {{ux|ar|عَبْدُ الْفَتَّاحِ ٱلسِّيسِي (هُوَ) '''رَئِيسُ''' جُمْهُورِيَّةِ مِصْرَ ٱلْعَرَبِيَّةِ.|t=Abdel Fattah el-Sisi '''is the president''' of the Arab Republic of Egypt.}}
* Imperfect forms of {{m|ar|كَانَ}} are not rare, however:
** They occur after certain conjunctions that must always be followed by a verb:
**: {{uxi|ar|أُرِيدُ '''أَنْ أَكُونَ''' غَنِيًّا.|I want '''to be''' rich.}}
** They are sometimes used instead of a nominal sentence to provide for a clearer sentence structure.{{attention|ar|please provide examples}}
* The jussive forms that end in [[sukun]] sometimes drop the final {{m|ar|ـن}}, giving: {{m|ar|يَكُ}}, {{m|ar|تَكُ}}, {{m|ar|أَكُ}}, {{m|ar|نَكُ}}.

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u|passive=n|vn=كَوْن,كِيَان,كَيْنُونَة}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|כאן||Judeo-Arabic}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|fr|Caen}}, q.v.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|tr=Kān}}

# {{place|ar|city|c/France|t=Caen}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|ar|fr|Cannes}}, q.v.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|كَان⁩|tr=Kān}}

# {{place|ar|city|c/France|t=Cannes}}

===See also===
{{col4|ar|لَيْسَ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|كون}}

==South Levantine Arabic==
{{ajp-root|ك و ن}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|كَانَ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|kān<p:kæːn>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Khalil.rantissi-كان.wav|a=al-Lidd}}

===Verb===
{{ajp-verb|I|tr=kān|pres=بكون|prestr=bikūn|ap=كاين|aptr=kāyen}}

# to [[be]]
#: {{syn|ajp|بقى|tr=baka|q=rural}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[شباب|الشباب]] [[كان|كانو]] [[في]] [[بيت|البيت]].|tr=iš-šabāb '''kānu''' fi l-bēt|t=The guys '''were''' in the house.}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[وين]] [[كاين|كاينة]]؟|tr= wēn '''kāyne'''?|t=Where '''have you been'''?}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[لازم]] [[كان|تكوني]] [[فهم|فاهمة]] [[على]] [[وضع]][[ه]].|tr=lāzim '''tkūni''' fāhme ʕala waḍaʕo|t=You should '''be''' understanding of his situation.}}
# {{lb|ajp|auxiliary|by extension}} {{ngd|(with subjunctive) continuous and habitual aspect marker}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[هي]] [[رح]] [[كان|تكون]] [[حكى|تحكي]] [[مع]] [[دكتور|الدكتور]].|tr=hiyye rāḥ '''tkūn tiḥki''' maʕ id-doktōr|t=She will '''be speaking''' to the doctor.}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[و]][[انا]] [[زغير]]، [[كان|كنت]] [[سافر|اسافر]] [[كتير]] [[مع]] [[أهل|اهل]][[ي]].|tr=w-ana zġīr, '''kunt asāfer''' ktīr maʕ ahli|t=When I was young, I '''used to travel''' a lot with my parents.}}
# {{lb|ajp|auxiliary|by extension}} {{ngd|(with past tense) perfect aspect marker}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[لمّا]] [[إجا|جيت]]، [[كان|كنت]] [[خلص|خلّصت]].|tr=lamma jīt, '''kunt ḵallaṣt'''|t=When you came, I '''had already finished'''.|lit=When you came, '''I was I finished''' it.}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[بكرا]] [[كان|بتكون]] [[خلص|خلّصت]][[ه]].|tr=bukra '''bitkūn ḵallaṣt'''o|t=Tomorrow you '''will have finished''' it.|lit=Tomorrow, '''you will be you finished''' it.}}
# {{lb|ajp|auxiliary}} {{ngd|(optional; always in the past tense) sets up the main clause in a counterfactual conditional}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[لو]] [[سأل|سألت]][[ني]]، ([[كان|كنت]]) [[قال|قلت]][[ل|لّك]].|tr=law saʔaltni, '''(kunt) ʔult'''illak|t=If you had asked me, I '''would have told''' you.}}
#: {{uxi|ajp|[[لو]] [[سأل|بتسأل]][[ني]]، ([[كان|كنت]]) [[قال|بقل]][[ل|ّك]].|tr=law btisʔalni, '''(kunt) baʔul'''lak|t=If you were to ask me, I '''would tell''' you.}}

====Usage notes====
* The copula "to be" is omitted in the present tense, whereas the present form of {{m-self|ajp|كان|tr=kān}} is used to express the future tense.

====Conjugation====
{{ajp-conj/DW|ك|ن|k|n}}
