==Persian==
{{wikipedia|گوشه (موسیقی)|گوشه|lang=fa}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal|tr=gwšk'|ts=gōšag|t=corner}}, which appears to be a suffixed formation from the word found now as {{m|fa|گوش|tr=guš|t=ear}}, in the sense of a lappet or protruding end of something. {{rfv-etym|fa}}

Another theory derives the word from {{der|fa|ine-pro|*gew-|t=to bend, curve; hand}}; see also {{cog|grc|γῦρος|t=ring, circle}}.<ref>{{R:grc:Beekes|290|γύης, -ου}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|gōša}}

===Noun===
{{fa-regional|گوشه|گوشه|гӯша}}
{{fa-noun|tr=guše|pl=گوشه‌ها}}

# [[corner]]
#: {{syn|fa|کنج<tr:konj>}}
#* {{quote-song|fa|year=1985|title=آشیونه [âšiune]|passage=از این گوشه دنیا<br/>به اون گوشه دنیا<br/>منو به آشیونه<br/>به یارم می‌رسونه|tr=az in guše-ye donyâ<br/>be un guše-ye donyâ<br/>man-o be âšiune<br/>be yâram mi-resune|t=from this corner of the world to that corner of the world<br/>to my nest,<br/>to my beloved, it delivers me}}
# [[angle]]
#: {{syn|fa|زاویه<tr:zâviye>}}
# {{lb|fa|music}} [[gosha]]/[[gusheh]], [[dastgah]], [[maqam]]

====Inflection====
{{fa-basic-e|گوش|guš}}
{{fa-poss-e|گوش|guš}}

