==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ص ي ر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|i}}

# {{lb|ar|copulative}} to [[become]]
#: {{syn|ar|Thesaurus:صار}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|i|passive=impers|vn=صَيْر,صَيْرُورَة,مَصِير}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ص و ر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|a|u}}

# to make, to [[incline]] or [[bend]] towards a [[shape]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|260
|passage={{...}}قَالَ فَخُذْ أَرْبَعَةً مِنَ ٱلطَّيْرِ '''فَصُرْهُنَّ''' إِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ ٱجْعَلْ عَلَى كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِنْهُنَّ جُزْءًا ثُمَّ ٱدْعُهُنَّ يَأْتِينَكَ سَعْيًا{{...}}
|translation=Take four of the birds and '''make them incline''' unto thee, then place a part of them on any hill, then hote them, they will come to thee in haste.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 1348|author={{w|Al-Dhahabi|aḏ-Ḏahabī}}|title={{w|lang=ar|تاريخ الإسلام ووفيات المشاهير والأعلام|{{lang|ar|تاريخ الإسلام}}}}|trans-title=History of Islam|url=http://www.alwaraq.net/Core/SearchServlet/searchone?docid=141&searchtext=Itin2YTZg9in2YXYriI=&option=1&offset=1&WordForm=1&exactpage=1652&totalpages=1&AllOffset=1|passage=فتح بن سعيد الموصلي. أبو نصر الزاهد، أحد سادات مشايخ الصوفية.<br/>له أحوال ومقامات. يقال إنه كان يتقوت بفلس نخالة.<br/>وورد أنه رأى صبيين، مع ذا كسرةٌ عليها كامخ، ومع الآخر كسرةٌ عليها عسل. فقال صاحب الكامخ: أطعمني من عسلك.<br/>قال: إن '''صرت''' لي كلباً أطعمتك.<br/>قال: نعم.<br/>فجعل في عنقه حبلاً وقال: انبح.<br/>قال فتح: لو قنعت بكامخك ما صرت له كلباً. ثم قال: هكذا الدنيا.|t=Fatḥ ibn Saʿīd al Mawṣilīy [d. 835]. Abū Naṣr az-Zāhid, one of the gentlemen of the Sufi sheykhs.<br/>He had years and standing. It is said he nourished himself by pennyworth bran.<br/>It happened that he saw two youngsters, one had a scrap of kāmiḵ, the other a scrap of honey.<br/>And the holder of the kāmiḵ said: Give me your honey to taste.<br/>If you '''make''' me a dog it’s your food.<br/>He said: Okay.<br/>And he put a rope onto his neck and said: Bark!<br/>Fatḥ said: If you had contented yourself with your kāmiḵ you wouldn’t have become a dog for it. Then he said: Such is the world.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|u|passive=yes|vn=صَوْر}}

==North Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|apc|ar|صَارَ}}.

====Verb====
{{head|apc|verb|tr=ṣār|non-past|يصير|f1tr=yṣīr}}

# to [[happen]]
# {{lbl|apc|copulative}} to [[become]]
# {{lbl|apc|auxiliary|by extension}} to [[come]] to
#: {{ux|apc
|كنت إكره هالأكلة بس '''صايرة''' بحبها
|tr=kint ʾikrah hal-ʾakle bas '''ṣāyra''' bḥibba
|t=I used to hate this dish, but '''I've come to''' like it
}}
# {{lbl|apc|auxiliary}} to [[start]] {{q|as a habit}}
#: {{ux|apc
|بدي '''صير''' إتعود عالفيقة بكير الصبح
|tr=baddi '''ṣīr''' ʾitʿawwad ʿa l-fayʾa bakkīr ṣ-ṣibḥ
|t=I've got to '''start''' getting used to waking up early in the morning
}}
# {{lbl|apc|auxiliary}} {{ngd|Governs an active participle, indicating that the action began in the past and continues into the present}}
#: {{ux|apc
|'''صرت''' آكل شي ميت حبّة لوز
|tr='''ṣirt''' ʾākil šī mīt ḥabbit lōz
|t=I''''ve''' eaten like a hundred almonds
}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Like other copulative verbs, {{m-self|apc|صَار}} is allowed to follow its predicate.

===Etymology 2===
Fused from {{compound|apc|صَار|ل|tr1=ṣār|alt2=إِلـ|tr2=ʔil-|t2=belonging to}}, where the latter can be used idiomatically in the meaning “{{q|of time}} passing relative to”. For the ultimate fusing-together, where the once-freestanding {{m|apc|ل|إلـ|tr=ʔil-}} adopted the shape of {{m|apc|ـلـ|tr=-l-|pos=dative suffix}}, compare the development of {{m|apc|بَعدِلّـ|tr=baʕdill-|t={{q|of time}} remaining for}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|apc|adverb|tr=ṣar, ṣār}}

# {{lb|apc|false verb}} {{ngd|Used with {{m|apc|ـلـ|tr=-l-}} and a past duration of time to refer to something that has been happening over this duration of time}}
#: {{usex|apc|'''صرلك''' سنين بتحبها|tr='''ṣar'''-lak snīn bitḥibba.|You'''’ve''' loved her for years.}}
#: {{usex|apc|'''صرلي''' تلات تيام ما شفته|tr='''ṣar'''-li tlāt tiyyām mā šifto.|I '''have'''n’t seen him in three days.}}
#: {{usex|apc|'''صرلن''' صحبة من الصف التاني|tr='''ṣar'''-lun ṣuḥbe min ṣ-ṣaff t-tāni.|They'''’ve''' been friends since second grade.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Sentences with ''ṣar-l-'' tend to have some adverbial of time in them. As can be seen from the examples, the construction can be followed by either a verbal or a nominal sentence.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{m|apc|صَرّـ|tr=ṣarr-}}
* {{m|apc|صَلّـ|tr=ṣall-}}

==South Levantine Arabic==
{{ajp-root|ص ي ر}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|صَارَ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|ṣār<p:sˤɑːrˤ>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Khalil.rantissi-صار.wav|a=al-Lidd}}

===Verb===
{{ajp-verb|I|tr=ṣār|pres=بصير|prestr=biṣīr|ap=صاير|aptr=ṣāyer}}

# to [[happen]]
#: {{ux|ajp|[[بكرا]] [[شاف|منشوف]] [[شو]] [[صار|بصير]].|tr=bukra minšūf šū '''biṣīr'''.|t=Tomorrow we'll see what '''happens'''.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[شو]] [[صار|صاير]]؟|tr=šū '''ṣāyer'''?|t=What's going on?|lit=What's '''happening'''?}}
# to [[become]]
#: {{ux|ajp|[[صار|صرت]] [[أطول]] [[من|منّ]][[ي]].|tr='''ṣirt''' aṭwal minni.|t='''You've become''' taller than me.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[شاف|شوف]] [[إذا]] [[صار]] [[كيلو]].|tr=šūf iza '''ṣār''' kīlo.|t=See if it's a kilo yet.|lit=See if '''it became''' a kilo.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[صار|صارت]] [[دنيا|الدنيا]] [[ليل]].|tr='''ṣārat''' id-dinya lēl.|t=It '''got''' dark.|lit=The world '''became''' night.}}
# {{lbl|ajp|auxiliary}} to [[start]] (an action), to [[come to]] (a state of affairs)
#: {{ux|ajp|[[بنت|البنت]] [[صار|صارت]] [[بكى|تبكي]].|tr=il-bint '''ṣārat''' tibkī.|t=The girl '''started''' to cry.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[صار]] [[عند]][[ه]] [[مصاري]].|tr='''ṣār''' ʕendo maṣari.|t=He's got money now.|lit=He '''came to''' have money.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[رنّ]][[ل|لي]] [[إذا]] [[صار|بصير]] [[مع]][[ك]] [[وقت]].|tr=rinnli iza '''biṣīr''' maʕak waqt.|t=Call me if you '''come to''' have some time.}}

====Conjugation====
{{ajp-conj/DY|ص|ر|ṣ|r}}
-------- end text --------
