{{fa-poss-e|آواز|âvâz}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|fa|پرآوازه<tr:por-âvâze>
}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|fa|sog|ʾʾwzyy|tr=*ōwazē|sc=Latn}} ([[w:Manichean alphabet|Manichean]]), {{m|sog|ʾʾwzʾk|tr=*āwaze, *āwāz|sc=Latn}}, possibly from {{der|fa|akk|𒍪𒀊|tr=apsu}}, {{der|fa|sux|𒍪𒀊|tr=abzu}}. Possibly related to {{cog|pal|tr=ʾpzn'|ts=ābzan}}, {{cog|xcl|աւազ||sand}}, and {{cog|ar|حَوْض}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|fa|آوزه|tr=âvaze}}
* {{alt|fa|اوزه|tr=avaze}}

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|āvāza}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr=âvâze}}

# {{lb|fa|rare}} [[swamp]]
#: {{syn|fa|تالاب|tr=tâlâb}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|year=10th century|author=w:[[Hudud al-'alam|Ḥudūd-ul-ʿĀlam]]
|text=آب‌هایی که آن را بطیحه خوانند بسیار است ولیکن آنچه معروف است نُه بطیحه است ... و هفتم بطیحه بخارا، آن را '''آوازه''' بیکند خوانند، اندر بیابان است.
|tr=âb-hâê ki ân râ batîha xwânand bisyâr ast valîkan ânča ma'rûf ast nuh batîha ast ... va haftum batîha-i buxârâ, ân râ âvâza-i baykand xwânand, andar bêâbân ast.
|t=There are a lot of waters which are called swamps, but those which are [the most] famous are nine ... and the seventh—the swamp of Bukhara, it is known as Āwāza of Baykand, [it] is in desert.}}
# {{lb|fa|rare}} [[pool]]
#: {{syn|fa|آبگیر<tr:âbgir>|آبزن<tr:âbzan>}}
#* {{cite-book|fa|year=11th century|author=w:Abul-fazl-i Bayhaqī|title=w:[[Tarikh-i Bayhaqi|Tārīx-i Bayhaqī]]
