{{C|ota|Tools|Bones|Board games}}

==Persian==
{{wikipedia|lang=fa}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal||tr=mwhlk'|ts=muhrag|t=bead, vertebra, piece (in backgammon, etc.)}}. Compare {{cog|xpr|tr=mwhrg|ts=muhrag}}. Equivalent to {{af|fa|مهر|ـه|tr1=mohr|t1=seal|tr2=-e}}. Note especially the meanings of a ''polished'' parchment or papyrus found in {{cog|ar|مُهْرَق}}, apart from {{cog|xcl|մուրհակ|t=deed}}, {{cog|tmr|מוהרק|tr=mūhraq|t=writ}} and the many senses of {{cog|sa|मुद्रा|g=f|t=seal}}, from which the meanings of a bead or shell must be transferred. For comparison, one even derived, by way of an absurd literary meaning-guessing, the sense of a “mirror” for {{m|ar|سَجَنْجَل|t=glossy papyrus leaves}}, the original meaning being a hapax against copious abuse. Akin to {{cog|mzn|میرکا|tr=mirkâ||bead}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|muh`ra|tg=mūh`ra}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=mohre|pl=مهرگان|pltr=mohregân|pl2=مهره‌ها}}

# [[bead]]
# [[shell]] of a [[mollusk]] or [[particularly]] the [[smaller]] kind thereof
# {{C|fa|Bones}} [[vertebra]]
# {{lb|fa|board games}} [[piece]]
# {{C|fa|Tools}} [[grind]]ing [[shell]] or [[stone]] or other [[polishing]] [[instrument]]
#: {{syn|fa|رنده|tr=rande}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fa|مهره‌دار|tr=mohre-dâr}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|fa|مهر|tr=mohr}}

====Descendants====
* {{desctree|trk-oat|مهره|tr=mühre|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:fa:Steingass}}
* {{R:fa:Vullers|L|II|pages=1241a–1242b}}
