Page 221 बत्तख़: -------- begin text --------
{{also|बत्तख}}
==Hindi==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|hi|बत्तख|बत्तक|बतख़|बतख|बतक}}

===Etymology===
Somehow derived from {{bor|hi|fa-cls|بت|tr=bat||duck}} (perhaps with the diminutive suffix {{m|fa|ـه|tr=-a}}), a [[Wanderwort]] related to {{cog|ar|بَطَّة}}, {{m|ar|بَطّ}}, {{cog|xcl|բադ}}, among others.

Cognate with {{cog|pa|ਬਤਕ}}, {{m|pa|ਬੱਤਖ਼}}, {{cog|gu|બતક}}, {{cog|sd|بَدَڪَ|tr=badaka}} / {{cog|sd|बदक|tr=badaka}}, {{cog|mr|बदक}}, {{cog|kok|बदक}}, {{cog|or|ବତକ}}, {{cog|ks|بَطُخ|tr=batux}}, and perhaps in the Dravidian languages, {{cog|te|బాతు}}, {{cog|kn|ಬಾತುಕೋಳಿ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{hi-noun|g=f|ur=بطخ}}

# [[duck]] {{gloss|aquatic bird of the family Anatidae}}
#: {{uxa|hi|'''बत्तख़ें''' ज़्यादातर मछली खाती हैं।|'''Ducks''' generally eat fish.}}

====Declension====
{{hi-ndecl|<F>}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:hi:McGregor|head=bataḵẖ}}
* {{R:hi:Dasa|बतख}}
* {{R:Fallon|ur|بَط؟}}
* {{R:Platts|بطخ|ur}}
* {{R:ur:Shakespear|بطخ}}

{{topics|hi|Ducks}}
