[[File:Spot Billed Duck Kaveri Srirangapatna Jul22 D72 24503.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|gu|બતક}}]]

===Etymology===
A {{glossary|wanderwort}} of {{unc|gu|nocap=1}} ultimate origin. Likely entered Gujarati via {{bor|gu|fa-cls|بت|tr=bat||duck}} (perhaps with the diminutive suffix {{m|fa|ـه|tr=-a}}). While {{glossary|folk etymology}} derives it from {{inh|gu|sa|वर्तक||quail}}.<br>Compare {{cog|inc-hnd}} {{m|ur|بطخ}} / {{m|hi|बत्तख़}}, {{cog|ks|بَطُخ|tr=batux}}, {{cog|kok|बदक}}, {{cog|mr|बदक}}, {{cog|pa|ਬਤਕ}}, {{cog|or|ବତକ}}, and {{cog|sd|بَدَڪَ}} / {{m|sd|बदक|tr=badaka}}.

{{rel-top|further related words}}
Similar words can also be found in: {{cog|ar|بَطّ}}, {{cog|hy|բադ}}, {{cog|bg|патка}}, {{cog|ce|бад}}, {{cog|syc|ܒܛܐ|tr=baṭṭāʾ}}, {{cog|dar|бятӏ}}, {{cog|ka|ბატი}}, {{cog|lki|بەت}}, {{cog|lez|пӏатӏ}}, {{cog|kmr|bet}}, and {{cog|es|pato}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{gu-IPA}}
* {{rhyme|gu|ək|s=2}}
* {{hyph|gu|બ|તક}}

===Noun===
{{gu-noun|g=f}}

# [[duck]] {{gloss|aquatic bird of the family Anatidae}}

{{topics|gu|Ducks}}
