==Kazakh==
{{kk-scripts|шаһар|شاهار|شهر}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|kk|fa-cls|شهر|tr=šahr|t=a city, a town}}, from {{der|kk|pal|𐭱𐭲𐭥𐭩|tr=štry|ts=šahr|sc=Phli}}, from {{der|kk|ira-pro|*xšaθram}}, from {{der|kk|iir-pro|*kšatrám|g=n}}. Vowels of both syllables had become {{w|Vowel harmony#Kazakh|back}} due to the influence of {{w|intervocalic}} Persian {{w|glottal consonant}} {{m|fa-cls|ه|ـهـ|tr=-h-}}.

Compare also {{nc|tt|шәһәр}}; {{nc|uz|shahar}}, {{nc|ug|شەھەر}}; {{nc|az|şəhər}}, {{nc|tr|şehir}}; etc.

