==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|ar|en|gender}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جِنْدَر|m}}

# [[gender identity]]

===Etymology 2===
By surface natively derived as from the root {{ar-root|ج د ر}}. Maybe from {{bor|ar|fa-cls|جندر|tr=jandar|t=clothes}} or {{m|fa|جندره|tr=jandara|t=calender, mangle; smoothening}} in the sense of giving a new look to something, as the present verb is said to specifically apply to garments or fabrics, and writing materials.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|Iq}} {{tlb|ar|classical}}

# to [[restore]], to [[reestablish]], to [[renew]] the [[figure]] of

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|Iq}}

====References====
* [http://arabiclexicon.hawramani.com/جدر/ Classical Arabic dictionaries s.v.]
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=313}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|page=338b}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=389c}}
* {{cite-book|ar|first=George Dimitri|last=Sawa|page=262|title=Musical and Socio-Cultural Anecdotes from ''Kitāb al-Aghānī al-Kabīr''. Annotated Translations and Commentaries|doi=10.1163/9789004383654|series=Islamic History and Civilization|seriesvolume=159|isbn=978-90-04-38362-3|publisher=Brill|location=Leiden|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Musical_and_Socio_Cultural_Anecdotes_fro/OMuDDwAAQBAJ?gbpv=1&dq=%22jandara%22&pg=PA262&printsec=frontcover}}

==Egyptian Arabic==
{{arz-root|ج ن د ر}}

===Etymology===
{{denominal verb|arz|جندرة|tr=gandara}}.

===Verb===
{{arz-verb|Iq|tr=gandar}}

# to [[mangle]], to [[calender]], to [[press]] by [[roll]]

====Conjugation====
{{arz-conj/Iq-sound-a|ج|ن|د|ر|g|n|d|r}}

===References===
* {{R:arz:HindsBadawi|page=175a}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-6-de|جندر|page=156b}}

==Persian==

===Etymology===
{{unk|fa|May}} have been obtained by {{back-formation|fa|جندره|tr=jandara|nocap=1}}, if Morgenstierne is not right to deny this by reason that the suffix {{m|fa|ـه|tr=-a}} has not been used in the sense of an instrument employed in handling the thing which the original word denotes; this could be otherwise if, as a consequence of that word’s Indian origin, the present word was considered an Arabism with the suffix {{m|ar|ـَة}} or a {{ar-form|Iq|nocap=1}} verbal noun, although even with {{m|ar|جَنْدَرَ|t=to renew the figure of}} existing there wouldn’t likely be a {{ar-noun of place|lc=1|nocat=1}} of this form; or if another {{cog|ira|-}} language did her part.

===Noun===
{{head|fa|noun|tr=jandar}}

# {{C|fa|Clothing}} [[clothes]]
# {{C|fa|Rooms}} [[place]] to [[keep]] [[clothes]] or also other [[domestic]] [[implement]]s

===References===
* {{R:fa:Steingass}}
* {{R:fa:Vullers|L|I|page=532b}}
* {{R:ira:Morgenstierne:1923|page=264}}
-------- end text --------
