==Arabic==

===Etymology===
* The sense of a god: From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʾil-}}, it might have been reinforced by {{bor|ar|he|אֵל}} or {{bor|ar|phn|𐤀𐤋}}.
* Kinship, noble origin: See {{ar-root|ء و ل}}
* Vow: See {{ar-root|ء ل و}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِلّ}}
* {{ar-IPA|إِل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِلّ|head2=إِل|m|g2=f}} {{lb|ar|uncountable}}

# [[god]], [[deity]], [[God]], [[El]] {{lb|ar|singular|proper noun}}
# a [[vow]]
# [[kinship]]
# [[hatred]], [[enmity]]
# a [[noble]] [[origin]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِلّ|head2=إِل}}

==South Levantine Arabic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ajp|لإلـ|tr=laʔil-}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|لِـ}}.

===Preposition===
{{ajp-prep|head=إلـ|tr=ʔil-}}

# [[to]]; [[for]] {{lb|ajp|detached version of the indirect object suffix {{l|ajp|ـلـ|tr=-l-}}, used for emphasis}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[كتب]] [[إل|إلي]]، [[مش]] [[إل|إلك]].|tr=katab '''ʔili''', miš '''ʔilak'''.|t=He wrote '''to me''', not '''to you'''.}}
# [[belonging]] to {{lb|ajp|mine, yours etc.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[ه]][[كتاب|الكتاب]] [[إل|إلك]].|tr=hāl-kitāb '''ʔilak'''|t=This book is '''yours'''.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[هو]] [[صاحب]] [[إل|إله]].|tr=huwwe ṣāḥeb '''ʔilo'''|t=He's a friend '''of his'''.}}
# {{lb|ajp|by extension}} to [[have]]
#: {{syn|ajp|عند|tr=ʕind|مع|tr2=maʕ}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[إل|إلي]] [[أخ]] [[و]][[أخت]].|tr='''ʔili''' ʔaḵḵ w-ʔuẖt|t='''I have''' a brother and sister.|lit='''Mine''' are a brother and a sister.}}

====Inflection====
{{ajp-prep-inflection
|base={{l-self|ajp|إلـ|tr=ʔil-}}
