Page 348 متعود: -------- begin text --------
==South Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology===
{{ajp-etym-ap|تعوّد|tr=tʕawwad|t=to get used to}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|mitʕawwid<p:mɪtˈʕaw.wɪd>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-متعوّد.wav|a=Ramallah}}

===Adjective===
{{ajp-adj|head=متعوّد|tr=mitʕawwed|f=متعوّدة|ftr=mitʕawwde|cpl=متعوّدين|cpltr= mitʕawwdīn}}

# [[used to]], [[accustomed]] to {{ajp-cprep|على}}, {{ajp-cprep|إنّـ}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[ال]][[ولد]] [[متعوّد]] [[إنّه]] [[صحى|يصحى]] [[و]][[ما]] [[لقى|يلاقي]] [[أهل]][[ه]] [[ب]][[ال]][[بيت]] [[لإن]][[هم]] [[راح|بيروحوا]] [[ع]][[ال]][[شغل]] [[بكّير]].|tr=il-walad '''mitʕawwed''' ʔinno yiṣḥɑ w-mā ylāʔi ʔahlo bil-bēt laʔinhom birūḥu ʕaš-šuḡl bakkīr.|t=The boy is '''used to''' waking up and not finding his parents at home because they go to work early.}}

====Usage notes====
* The preposition {{l|ajp|على|tr= ʕala}} is used to say that someone is '''used to''' "something".
* The conjunction {{l|ajp|إنّـ|tr=ʔinn-}} is used to say that someone is '''used to''' "doing something".
-------- end text --------
Page 349 Appendix:Maltese roots/h-n-j: Skipped, no changes
Page 349 Appendix:Maltese roots/h-n-j: -------- begin text --------
==Maltese==

===Etymology===
From {{m+|ar|-}} {{ar-root|ه ن ء|nocat=1}}.

The outcome of root-initial {{m|ar|ه}} in modern Maltese is irregular; it was either vowelised or merged into {{IPAchar|/ħ/}}. Generally one or the other happened throughout a given root, but in the case of {{m|mt||h-n-j}} the irregularity continues even within the root. It is spelt with {{m|mt|h}} because of the rule that {{m|mt|ħ}} can never be silent.

===Root===
{{mt-root}}

# {{ngd|Related to [[happiness]].}}

====Derived terms====
{{rootsee|mt}}
-------- end text --------
Page 362 عطاك عمره: Skipped, no changes
Page 362 عطاك عمره: -------- begin text --------
==Gulf Arabic==

===Etymology===
{{l|afb|عطى|tr=ʕaṭa|t=to give}} + {{l|afb|عمر|tr=ʕumur|t=age, life}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|afb|/ʕətˤaːk ʕʊmrə/}}

===Verb===
{{afb-verb|head=[[عطى|عطاك]] [[عمر]][[ه]]|tr=ʿaṭāk ʿumra}}

# {{lb|afb|idiomatic|euphemistic}} used to [[report]] someone has [[pass away|passed away]].
#: {{syn|afb|توفى|tr=tawaffa|مات|tr2=māt}}

====Usage notes====
The verb ({{l|afb|عطى}}) must be conjugated and a pronominal suffix must be attached to its object ({{l|afb|عمر}}) to reflect the gender and number of the person(s) who passed away and the person(s) being spoken to. For example, if a female had died and the news is being told to a male, the correct form would be {{l|afb|عطتك عمرها|tr=ʕaṭitik ʕumurha|lit=she gave you (m) her age}}.
-------- end text --------
