Page 436 Appendix:Abjad numerals: Skipped, no changes
Page 436 Appendix:Abjad numerals: -------- begin text --------
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Noun===
'''[[abjad]] [[numeral]]s'''

* Abjad numerals are Arabic letters used as numbers. When Arabic letters are used as numbers, they follow a traditional order based on the Hebrew alphabet. Sometimes the numbers are marked by an overline.

*'''The traditional abjad sequence is:'''
:{{lang|ar|أ ب ج د ه‍ و ز ح ط ي ك ل م ن س ع ف ص ق ر ش ت ث خ ذ ض ظ غ}}

*The abjad is grouped into these words to facilitate memory:
:{{lang|ar|[[ابجد|أبجد]] هوز حطي كلمن سعفص قرشت ثخذ ضظغ}}
:[[abjad|’ábjad]] háwwaz ħáṭṭī kálaman sáʕfaṣ qárašat θáχað ḍáẓaġ.

*'''Units 1–9:'''
:{{lang|ar|[[أ]] ب ج د ﻫ و ز ح ط}}

*'''Tens 10–90:'''
:{{lang|ar|[[ي]] ك ل م ن س ع ف ص}}

*'''Hundreds 100–900:'''
:{{lang|ar|[[ق]] ر ش ت ث خ ذ ض ظ}}

*'''One thousand:'''
:{{lang|ar|[[غ]]}}

*'''Examples:'''
:'''i. {{lang|ar|[[أ]]}} –''' {{overline|غتصب}} &emsp;—&emsp;&emsp; 1492
:'''ii. {{lang|ar|[[ب]]}} –''' {{overline|غذعــو}} &emsp;—&ensp;&emsp; 1776
:'''iii. {{lang|ar|[[ج]]}} –''' {{overline|غضيب}} &emsp;—&nbsp;&emsp; 1812
:'''iv. {{lang|ar|[[د]]}} –''' {{overline|غطمــه}} &emsp;—&nbsp;&emsp; 1945
:'''v. {{lang|ar|[[ﻫ]]}} –''' {{overline|غطفــــد}} &emsp;—&ensp;&emsp; 1984

[[Category:Arabic language]]
[[Category:Abjad numerals]]
[[Category:Numerical appendices|Abjad]]
-------- end text --------
