=====References=====
<references/>

====Determiner====
{{head|en|determiner}}

# {{lb|en|AAVE}} {{synonym of|en|his}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The game of [[tag]], or [[it]], in which the player attempting to catch the others is called "he".
# The player who chases and attempts to catch the others in this game.
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[male]].
#: {{ux|en|Is your cat a '''he''' or a she?}}

===Etymology 2===
Transliteration of various Semitic letters, such as {{translit|en|phn|sc=Phnx|𐤄|tr=h|notext=1}}, {{translit|en|he|sc=Hebr|ה|tr=h|notext=1}}, {{translit|en|syc|sc=Syrc|ܗ|tr=h||hē|notext=1}}, and {{translit|en|sem-srb|sc=Sarb|𐩠|tr=h|notext=1}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|hay}}
* {{l|en|hei}}
* {{l|en|hey}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/heɪ/}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|?}}

# The name of the fifth letter of many [[Semitic]] alphabets ([[Phoenician]], [[Aramaic]], [[Hebrew]], [[Syriac]], [[Arabic]] and others).
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1658|author=w:Thomas Browne|title=The Garden of Cyrus|page=210|publisher=Folio Society|year_published=2007
|passage=The same number in the Hebrew mysteries and Cabalistical accounts was the character of Generation; declared by the Letter '''''He''''', the fifth in their Alphabet.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1988|author=w:Milorad Pavić|translator=Christina Pribićević-Zorić|title=Dictionary of the Khazars|page=7|publisher=Vintage|year_published=1989
|passage=This Nehama claimed that in his own hand he recognized the consonant “'''he'''” of his Hebrew language, and in the letter “vav” his own male soul.}}
# The name of the first letter of the [[Old South Arabian]] abjad.

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|fifth letter of the various Semitic alphabets}}
* Catalan: {{t+|ca|he|f}}
* Finnish: {{t+|fi|he}}
* French: {{t+|fr|hè|m}}, {{t+|fr|hê|m}}, {{t+|fr|he|m}}
* Hebrew: {{t+|he|הֵא|f|tr=hé|sc=Hebr}}, {{t+|he|ה}} {{qualifier|symbol}}
* Malay: {{t+|ms|ha}}
* Yiddish: {{t|yi|הא|tr=hey|sc=Hebr}}
{{trans-bottom}}

====See also====
* [[Appendix:Hebrew alphabet]]

====Further reading====
* {{pedia|He (letter)}}

===Etymology 3===

====Interjection====
{{head|en|interjection}}

# {{lb|en|uncommon|usually|reduplicated}} {{n-g|An expression of laughter.}}
#: {{syn|en|ha|hehe}} {{q|more common}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1897|author=Charles Dudley Warner; Hamilton Wright Mabie; Charles Henry Warner; Lucia Isabella Gilbert Runkle|title=Library of the World's Best Literature: A-Z|page=1791
|passage=If e'er he went into excess, / 'Twas from a somewhat lively thirst; / But he who would his subjects bless, / Odd's fish!—must wet his whistle first; / And so from every cask they got, / Our king did to himself allot / At least a pot. / Sing ho, ho, ho! and '''he, he, he'''! / That's the kind of king for me.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1921|author=Norman Davey|title=The Pilgrim of a Smile|page=247
|passage="Well, what is your next tale?" said Sumner, a little brusquely. "'''He, he! he, he! . . . he, he!'''" chuckled the bottle, "the text tale I'm going to tell you in a very funny one. It will make you laugh. There's a lady in it—'''he, he!'''—a very comic affair."}}

