Page 2 behold: -------- begin text --------
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kel-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|beholden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|behealdan||to hold, have, occupy, possess, guard, preserve, contain, belong, keep, observe, consider, behold, look at, gaze on, see, signify, avail, effect, take care, beware, be cautious, restrain, act, behave}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*bihaldan||to hold with, keep}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|be|hold}}. Cognate with {{cog|stq|behoolde|t=to keep}}, {{cog|nl|behouden||to keep, restrain, preserve}}, {{cog|de|behalten||to keep, restrain, remember}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|no|beholde||to keep}} and {{cog|sv|behålla||to keep}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈhəʊld/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/bɪˈhoʊld/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-behold.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊld|oʊld|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|beholds|beholding|beheld|past_ptc2=beholden|past_ptc2_qual=rare}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[look at]] or [[see#Verb|see]] (someone or something), especially [[appreciatively]]; to [[descry]], to [[look upon]].
##: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:look}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice Q1|act=V|scene=i|page=204|passage=There's not the ſmalleſt orbe [in the sky] vvhich thou '''beholdſt''', / But in his motion like an Angell ſings, / Still quiring to the young [[eyed|eide]] Cherubins; / Such harmony is in immortall ſoules, / But vvhilſt this muddy veſture of decay [''i.e.'', the human body] / Doth groſſely cloſe in it, vve cannot heare it.}}
##* {{RQ:R. F. Burton Arabian Nights|night=532|passage={{...}} [[w:Aladdin|Alaeddin]] ate and drank and was cheered and after he had rested and had recovered spirits he cried, "Ah, O my mother, I have a sore grievance against thee for leaving me to that accursed wight who strave to compass my destruction and designed to take my life. Know that I '''beheld''' Death with mine own eyes at the hand of this damned wretch, whom thou didst certify to be my uncle; {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=VIII|passage=The humor of my proposition appealed more strongly to Miss Trevor than I had looked for, and from that time forward she became her old self again;{{nb...}}. Now she had come to look upon the matter in its true proportions, and her anticipation of a possible chance of teaching him a lesson was a pleasure to '''behold'''.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|lyricist={{w|Bobby Pickett|Bobby "Boris" Pickett}} and {{w|Lenny Capizzi}}|title={{w|Monster Mash}}|artist=Bobby (Boris) Pickett and The Crypt-Kickers|year=1962|text=I was working in the lab late one night<br>When my eyes '''beheld''' an eerie sight<br>For my monster, from his slab, began to rise<br>And suddenly, to my surprise<br>He did the Mash<br>He did the Monster Mash.}}
## To [[contemplate]] (someone or something).
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[look#Verb|look]].

====Usage notes====
Rarely used in informal speech. The past participle [[beholden]] now has a meaning detached from the other forms of the word.

====Conjugation====
{{en-conj|old=1|past=beheld|past_ptc2=beholden|past_ptc2_qual=note1|note1=Rare.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|en|unbeheld|beholder|eye of the beholder|lo and behold|long and behold|sight to behold|beholdable}}

====Translations====
