{{also|'aitch|Aitch|Aitch.}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|haitch||dialectal or nonstandard}}
* {{alter|en|ache#Etymology_3||rare}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ache}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|ache}}, from {{der|en|VL.|*acca}}. (Compare {{cog|it|acca}}.) The source is unclear, but may descend from the vowelless alphabetic sequence {{m|la|ha}} {{m|la|ka}} 'H, K' (becoming [aka] when the [h] ceased to be pronounced), as K had low frequency in Late Latin.<ref>{{cite-web |url = http://blog.oup.com/2013/08/alphabet-soup-letter-h-y-origin-etymology/ |title = Alphabet soup, part 2: H and Y |last=Liberman|first=Anatoly|date=7 August 2013|work=Oxford Etymologist|publisher=Oxford University Press|accessdate=3 October 2013}}</ref> {{doublet|en|ecchi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|āch}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪt͡ʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-aitch.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪtʃ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{Latn-def|en|name|H|h}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1773|journal=The Monthly Review Or Literary Journal Enlarged|month=October
|passage=The word length, which contains only four sounds l e ng th, is usually spell'd thus, el ee en gee tee '''aitch'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1898|author=w:H.G. Wells|title=w:The War of the Worlds|publisher=William Heinemann|location=London|page=257|passage="If you've got any drawing-room manners, or a dislike to eating peas with a knife or dropping '''aitches''', you'd better chuck 'em away. They ain't no further use."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1959|year_published=1972|author=w:Anthony Burgess| title=Beds in the East| series=The Malayan Trilogy| page=469| passage=She frowned, hearing Lim Cheng Po's voice, so English, so refined, so very English upper-class. And often she had had to tell Joe about his '''aitches'''.}}
#: ''The word [[hour]] is written with a silent '''aitch'''.''
#: ''[[Cockney]]s drop their '''aitches'''.''

====Usage notes====
* Often used in reference of [[w:H-dropping|H-dropping]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|aitchbone}}
* {{l|en|aitchless}}
* {{l|en|aitch-dropping}}

====Descendants====
