===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|en|nan-hbl|欸|tr=[[--eh]]}} and {{bor|en|cmn|欸|tr=ê̄ / ế / ê̌|pos=interjection}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|en|SG}} 
** {{IPA|en|[ˈe˦˧]|[ˈe˧]|q1=Sense 1}}
** {{IPA|en|[eɪ˧˨]|q1=Sense 2}}
** {{IPA|en|[eɪ˩˦]|q1=Sense 3}}

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}} {{lb|en|Singapore}}

# {{lb|en|Singlish|usually impolite}} {{cap|hey}}, [[oi]]; {{n-g|said to get someone's [[attention]].}}
# {{lb|en|uncommon}} {{n-g|An interjection expressing [[disapproval]].}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Eh''', please don't say that...}}
# {{lb|en|with rising pitch}} {{cap|huh}}?; {{n-g|expresses confusion.}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|en|eh eh eh}} {{i|interjection, possibly related to the above}}

===Etymology 3===
Probably of multiple motivations, the sounds having been chosen for [[functional]] reasons.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/eɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|Eh-sound.ogg|a=UK}}

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|MLE|MTE|regional|_|AAVE|Chicano}} {{n-g|an attention grabber}}
#: {{syn|en|hey|oi|I say}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Eh''', come here!}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Eh''', what do you have?}}
#* '''2017''', Dirty Heads, ''Vacation''
#*: '''E-''', '''e-''', '''eh''', I'm on vacation / Every single day 'cause I love my occupation

