==Persian==

===Etymology 1===
{{bor+|fa|ar|عَجَب}}.{{root|fa|ar|ع ج ب}}

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|'a`jab}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr='ajab|head=عَجَب}}

# [[wonder]], [[marvel]], [[astonishment]], [[amazement]]
#* {{RQ:Masnavi|III|1394|در چنین مستی مراعات ادب، خود نباشد ور بود باشد عجب|dar čonin masti mora'at-e adab, xod na-bâšad v-ar bovad bâšad ''''ajab'''.|In such [mystical] intoxication [as his], the observance of due respect [to the letter of the Qur'an] will not be there at all; or if it be, 'tis a '''wonder'''.}}

====Interjection====
{{head|fa|interjection|tr='ajab|head=عَجَب}}

# what a [[wonder]], [[how]] [[strange]], [[amazing]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:منطق الطیر|trans-title={{w|The Conference of the Birds}}|volume=lines 733—737|author={{w|Attar of Nishapur|Farīd ud-Dīn ʿAṭṭār}}|year=1177|text=ابتدای کار سیمرغ ای عجب، جلوه‌گر بگذشت بر چین نیم شب، در میان چین فتاد از وی پری، لاجرم پر شور شد هر کشوری.|tr=ebtedâ-ye kâr-e simorğ ey ''''ajab''', jelow-gar be-gozašt bar čin nim-šab, dar miyân-e čin fatâd az vey par-i, lâ-jaram por-šur šod har kešvar-i.|t=The beginning of [this] affair of the {{w|Simorgh}}, oh '''how wondrous'''! It passed in China in full splendor one midnight, and a feather fell from it in the middle of China. Consequently, each country became ardent [to see the feather].}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|fa|ar|عُجْب}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|'ujb}}

====Noun====
{{fa-noun|tr='ojb|head=عُجب}}

# [[pride]], [[vanity]], [[conceit]]

==South Levantine Arabic==
{{ajp-root|ع ج ب}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ajp|أعجب|tr=ʔaʕjab||MSA-influenced form}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ajp|ar|أَعْجَبَ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ajp-IPA|ʕajab<p:ˈʕa.ʒab><p:ˈʕa.d͡ʒab>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Khalil.rantissi-عَجَب.wav|a=al-Lidd}}

====Verb====
{{ajp-verb|I|tr=ʕajab|pres=بعجب|prestr=biʕjeb|ap=عاجب|aptr=ʕājeb}}

# to [[amaze]], to [[impress]]
# {{lb|ajp|by extension|transitive}} to be [[pleasing]]
#: {{syn|ajp|جنّن|tr=jannan}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[عجب|عجبت]][[ني]] [[كتير]] [[أغنية|اغنيت]][[ها]].|tr='''ʕajbatni''' ktīr oḡnyetha.|t=I really '''liked''' her song.|lit=Her song was very '''pleasing''' to me.}}
#: {{ux|ajp|[[مش]] [[عجب|عاجب]][[هم]] [[شغل|الشغل]] [[مع|معها]].|tr=miš '''ʕājeb'''hom iš-šoḡol maʕha.|t=They don't '''like''' working with her.|lit=Work with her is not '''pleasing''' to them.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Pragmatically, this verb means "to [[like]]", with the agent grammatically expressed as the object of pleasure; this construction is analogous to the Spanish verb "{{m|es|gustar}}".

=====Conjugation=====
{{ajp-conj/A1|ع|ج|ب|ʕ|j|b}}

