{{also|اللی}}
==North Levantine Arabic==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|apc|ياللي|tr=yalli}} {{i|see usage notes below}}

===Etymology===
From or related to {{der|apc|ar|اَلَّذِي}} and {{m|ar|اَلَّتِي}}.

===Pronoun===
{{head|apc|pronoun|tr=lli, illi}}

# {{lb|apc|relative}} [[who]]; [[whom]]; [[which]]; [[that]]; [[what]]
#: {{usex|apc|هيدا المستشفى اللي بتشتغل إمي فيه|tr=Hayda l-mistašfa lli btištaḡil ʾimmi fīh.|This is the hospital in which my mother works.}}

====Usage notes====
* In some phonetic environments, particularly in fast speech, the pronoun may be contracted to just ''-ll-'' or ''-l-''.
* The variant {{m|apc|ياللي|tr=yalli}} can be used interchangeably, but it occurs most often when used without an antecedent, that is in the senses “he who”, “that which”, etc.:
:: {{usex|apc|فيك تقول ياللي بدك|tr=Fīk-i tʾūl yalli baddak.|You can say what you want.}}

==South Levantine Arabic==

===Etymology===
From or related to {{der|ajp|ar|اَلَّذِي}} and {{der|ajp|ar|اَلَّتِي}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|lli<p:ˈ(ɪ)l.li>}}
* {{audio|ajp|LL-Q55633582 (ajp)-Muhammad (AdrianAbdulBaha)-اللي.wav|a=Ramallah}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|ajp|pronoun|tr=illi, lli}}

# {{lb|ajp|relative}} [[who]]; [[whom]]; [[which]]; [[that]]
#: {{ux|ajp|[[بنت|البنت]] [[اللي]] [[شاف|شفت]][[ها]] [[مبارح]] [[اشتغل|بتشتغل]] [[مع|معي]].|tr=il-bint '''illi''' šuft-ha mbāreḥ btištḡel maʕi|t=The girl I saw yesterday works with me.|lit=The girl '''that''' I saw her yesterday works with me.}}
# the person [[who]], [[whoever]]; [[that]] [[which]], [[whatever]] {{lb|ajp|at the beginning of a sentence}}

====Usage notes====
* When referring back to a noun, which is the object of the verb that follows, a suffix pronoun should be added to that verb.
* {{m-self|ajp|اللي|tr=illi}} is used referring to a definite noun, but usually omitted if the noun is indefinite.
