{{reconstructed}}
==Proto-Indo-European==

===Particle===
{{head|ine-pro|particle|head=*ḱi- ~ *ḱe- ~ *ḱo-|head2=*-ḱe}}

# {{n-g|Deictic particle}}, [[here]]
# {{n-g|Post-positional demonstrative particle}}, [[this]]

====Usage notes====
The particle in Proto-Indo-European was indeclinable. Some daughter languages, particularly Balto-Slavic, Germanic and Armenian added pronominal inflection later, as also occurred with particles {{m|ine-pro|*de}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ew}}, and {{m|ine-pro|*gʰe}}.

Although it does not have an exact equivalent in English, {{m+|fr|là}} and {{m+|ar|ها|tr=-hā}} are used in the same way.

====Descendants====
* {{desc|itc-pro|*-ke|*ke-}}
** Latin: -c (e.g. {{l|la|hic}}, {{l|la|illic}}, {{l|la|tunc}})
** Latin: -ce (e.g. {{l|la|ecce}})

