==Persian==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|fa|ar|[[دنيا|الدُّنْيَا]] [[وَ]][[مَا]] [[فِي]][[هَا]]|lit=the world and what's in it.}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fa|[d̪oɲ.jɒ́ː væ mɒː.fiː.ɦɒ́ː]|a=IR}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=donyâ va mâfihâ}}

# {{lb|fa|poetic}} the [[world]] and [[everything]] in it; all of [[material]] [[existence]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:دیوان ترکی شیرازی|author=Mohammad Hossein Âğuli Torki-ye Shirâzi|year=c. 1911|url=https://ganjoor.net/torki/divan/f1/sh1|text=بنازم دست ساقی را که تا می ریخت در جامم<br>من از جا می فکندم از نظر '''دنیا و مافیها'''|tr=benâzam dast-e sâqi râ ke tâ mey rixt dar jâm-am<br>man az jâ mi-fekandam az nazar '''donyâ va mâfihâ'''|t=I caress the hand of the cupbearer, for as long as he poured wine in my goblet,<br>I could hurl out of sight '''the world and all that's in it'''.}}
-------- end text --------
Page 1 fear: Skipped, no changes
Page 1 fear: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Fear|féar|fear-}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/fɪə/|a=Australia,RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/fɪɚ/|/fɪɹ/|a=GenAm}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-fear.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪə(ɹ)|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*per-|id=risk}}
From {{inh|en|enm|feer}}, {{m|enm|fere}}, {{m|enm|fer}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fǣr}}, {{m|ang|ġefǣr|t=calamity, sudden danger, peril, sudden attack, terrible sight}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*fērō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*fērą|t=danger}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*per-|t=to attempt, try, research, risk}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|gevaar|t=danger, risk, peril}}, {{cog|de|Gefahr|t=danger, risk, hazard}}, {{cog|sv|fara|t=danger, risk, peril}}, {{cog|la|perīculum|t=danger, risk, trial}}, {{cog|sq|frikë|t=fear, danger}}, {{cog|ro|frică|frică}}. Doublet of [[peril]].

The verb is from {{inh|en|enm|feren}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fǣran|t=to frighten, raven}}, from the noun. Cognate with the archaic {{cog|nl|-}} verb {{m|nl|varen|t=to fear; to cause fear}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|uncountable: unpleasant emotion caused by actual or perceived danger}}{{lb|en|uncountable}} A strong, unpleasant [[emotion]] or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or threat.
#: {{ux|en|He was struck by '''fear''' on seeing the snake.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=I corralled the judge, and we started off across the fields, in no very mild state of '''fear''' of that gentleman's wife, whose vigilance was seldom relaxed.}}
#* {{RQ:Vance Outsider|page=382|column=1|passage=Turning back, then, toward the basement staircase, she began to grope her way through blinding darkness, but had taken only a few uncertain steps when, of a sudden, she stopped short and for a little stood like a stricken thing, quite motionless save that she quaked to her very marrow in the grasp of a great and enervating '''fear'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=18|passage=‘Then the father has a great fight with his terrible conscience,’ said Munday with granite seriousness. ‘Should he make a row with the police{{nb...}}? Or should he say nothing about it and condone brutality for '''fear''' of appearing in the newspapers?’}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[phobia]], a sense of fear induced by something or someone.<!--not a self-referential definition: the word "fear" here is used in the previous sense-->
#: {{ux|en|Not everybody has the same '''fears'''.&emsp; {{nowrap|I have a '''fear''' of [[ant]]s.}}}}
#* {{RQ:Hough Purchase Price|chapter=I|text=Serene, smiling, enigmatic, she faced him with no '''fear''' whatever showing in her dark eyes. The clear light of the bright autumn morning had no terrors for youth and health like hers.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[terrified|Terrified]] [[veneration]] or [[reverence]], particularly towards [[God]], [[god]]s, or [[sovereign]]s.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Psalm|CXI|10|text=The '''feare''' of the Lord is the beginning of [[wisdom|wisedome]].}}
#* {{RQ:Ruskin Modern Painters|volume=II|page=121|passage=That sacred dread of all offence to him, which is called the '''Fear''' of God.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|with definite article, "the fear"}} A feeling of [[dread]] and [[anxiety]] when waking after drinking a lot of [[alcohol]], wondering what one did while drunk.
#: {{syn|en|hangxiety}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2019|author=Ruth Kelly|title=The Little Vineyard in Provence
|passage=Her feeling of humiliation had intensified as the day had gone on and her hangover had worsened. She now also had ''''the fear'''' to contend with, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2020|author=Mark Ratcliffe|title=The Step Down: A Very Scottish Crime
|passage=He had '''the fear''', that feeling of dread that you've done something really embarrassing. '''The fear''' was a hundred times worse than the hangover. No, a thousand times worse.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|an emotion caused by actual or perceived danger; a sense of fear induced by something or someone}} ''See'' '''[[Thesaurus:fear]]'''
