====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|feel fear about (something)}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To be afraid of (something or someone); to consider or expect (something or someone) with alarm.
#: {{ux|en|I '''fear''' the worst will happen.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Comedy of Errors|I|2|text=I greatly '''fear''' my money is not safe.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Matthew|10|28|text=And '''fear''' not them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather '''fear''' him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.}}
#* {{RQ:Besant Ivory Gate|II
|passage=At twilight in the summer there is never anybody to '''fear'''—man, woman, or cat—in the chambers and at that hour the mice come out. They do not eat parchment or foolscap or red tape, but they eat the luncheon crumbs.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-19|author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/marktran Mark Tran]
|volume=189|issue=6|page=1|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=[http://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2013/jul/12/war-denying-children-education Denied an education by war]
|passage=One particularly damaging, but often ignored, effect of conflict on education is the proliferation of attacks on schools{{...}}as children, teachers or school buildings become the targets of attacks. Parents '''fear''' sending their children to school. Girls are particularly vulnerable to sexual violence.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To feel fear.
#: {{ux|en|Never '''fear'''; help is always near.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Luke|12|32|text='''Fear''' not, little flock; for it is your Father’s good pleasure to give you the kingdom.}}
# {{senseid|en|worry about, feel concern for}}{{lb|en|intransitive|used with ''for''}} To [[worry]] about, to feel [[concern]] for, to be [[afraid]] for. <!-- https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/fear%20for -->
#: {{ux|en|She '''fears''' for her son’s safety.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To venerate; to [[feel]] [[awe]] towards.
#: {{ux|en|People who '''fear''' [[God]] can be found in [[Christian]] churches.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To regret.
#: {{ux|en|I '''fear''' I have bad news for you: your husband has died.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To cause fear to; to [[frighten]].
#* {{RQ:Mlry MrtDrthr|7.10|2|V|x|passage=Thenne the knyghte sayd to syre Gawayn / bynde thy wounde or thy blee chaunge / for thou bybledest al thy hors and thy fayre armes /{{...}}/ For who someuer is hurte with this blade he shalle neuer be staunched of bledynge / Thenne ansuerd gawayn hit greueth me but lytyl / thy grete wordes shalle not '''feare''' me ne lasse my courage}}
<!--Prior quote:‘Be God,’ sayde Sir Gawayne, ‘his grevys me but lytyll; yet shalt thou nat '''feare''' me for all thy grete wordis.-->
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|III|IV|page=448|text=Ythrild with deepe disdaine of his proud threat,<br>She shortly thus; Fly they, that need to fly;<br>Wordes '''fearen''' babes.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|I|2|text=Tush, tush! '''fear''' boys with bugs.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Measure for Measure|II|1|text=We must not make a scarecrow of the law,<br>Setting it up to '''fear''' the birds of prey,<br>And let it keep one shape, till custom make it<br>Their perch and not their terror.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To be [[anxious]] or [[solicitous]] for.
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Edward 2|year=1622|text='''Fearst''' thou thy person? thou shalt haue a guard:}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|III|5|text=The sins of the father are to be laid upon the children: therefore, I promise ye, I '''fear''' you.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To suspect; to doubt.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-2|I|4|text='''Fear''' you not her courage?}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|feel fear about (something)}} be [[afraid]] of, be [[frightened]] of, be [[scared]] of, be [[terrorise]]d/[[terrorize]]d
* {{sense|venerate; to feel awe towards}} be in awe of, [[revere]], [[venerate]]

=====Antonyms=====
