===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|fere}}, {{m|enm|feore}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fēre|t=able to go, fit for service}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*fōriz|t=passable}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*per-|t=to put across, ferry}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|fere}}, {{m|sco|feir|t=well, active, sound}}, {{cog|gmh|gevüere|t=able, capable, fit, serviceable}}, {{cog|sv|för|t=capable, able, stout}}, {{cog|is|færr|t=able}}. Related to {{l|en|fare}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|dialectal}} [[able|Able]]; [[capable]]; [[stout]]; [[strong]]; [[sound]].
#: {{ux|en|hale and '''fear'''}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|en|feer}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=aefr|FERA|Fera|Rafe|fare|reaf}}

