==English==
{{slim-wikipedia|Phobia (disambiguation)}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰegʷ-}}
c 1790, from words ending in {{m|en|-phobia}}, from {{uder|en|grc|φόβος||fear}}. Compare {{m|en|ism}}, from {{m|en|-ism}}, {{m|en|itis}}, from {{m|en|-itis}}, and {{m|en|ana}}, from {{m|en|-ana}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfoʊbi.ə/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfəʊbɪə/}} (UK)
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-phobia.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊbiə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|phobiae|phobiæ}}

# An [[irrational]], [[abnormal]], or [[obsessive]] [[fear]] (of something).
#: {{ux|en|I know someone with a strange '''phobia''' of ladders.}}
# An [[aversion]] or [[dislike]] (of something).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914|title=McClure's Magazine|page=140
|text=Some patients have the '''phobia''' of light, and others have the '''phobia''' of darkness. Another common aversion is that of high places. The phobiac of this type can not sit in the gallery {{...}} }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|month=06|author=Michael G. Peletz|title=Gender Pluralism: Southeast Asia Since Early Modern Times|publisher=Routledge|isbn=9781135954895|page=162
|text=For as interviewer Than Win Htut expressed it, “misunderstandings about, and '''phobia''' of, gay life and homosexuality are very common in Burma.” Than Win Htut went on to observe that in Burma{{nb...}}}}
#* {{seeMoreCites|en}}

====Hyponyms====
* See [[:Category:en:Phobias]].

====Derived terms====
{{der2|en|social phobia|specific phobia}}

{{suffixsee|en|head=-phobia}}

