==Ottoman Turkish==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ota|trk-pro|*korkug||fear}},<ref>{{R:trk:Clauson|entry=korkuğ|page=654}}</ref> a development of {{m|trk-pro|*kork-||to fear}}, whence {{m|ota|قورقمق|tr=korkmak|t=to fear}}. Cognate with {{cog|az|qorxu}}, {{cog|alt|корку}}, {{cog|tk|gorky}} and {{cog|uz|qoʻrquv}}.

===Noun===
{{ota-noun|tr=korku}}

# [[fear]], [[fright]], [[terror]], [[dread]], an unpleasant [[emotion]] caused by actual or perceived [[danger]]
#: {{syn|ota|بیم|tr1=bim|ترس|tr2=ters|خوف|tr3=havf|هراس|tr4=hıras}}
# [[threat]], [[menace]], an [[indication]] of [[potential]] or [[imminent]] danger that can [[harm]] a person
# [[danger]], [[peril]], [[hazard]], [[jeopardy]], an impending [[exposure]] to likely [[harm]], a [[lack]] of [[safety]]
#: {{syn|ota|بیم|tr1=bim|تهلكه|tr2=tehlike|مخاطره|tr3=muhatara}}
# [[alarm]], a sudden [[surprise]] with [[fear]] or [[terror]] excited by [[apprehension]] of danger

