==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|offence||UK|Canada|Australia|New Zealand}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|offence}}, from {{der|en|fro|offense}}, from {{der|en|la|offensa||a striking against; displeasure; injury}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈfɛns/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-offense.ogg|a=US}}
* {{sense|team sports senses, especially in the U.S.}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɔf.ɛns/|/ˈɑf.ɛns/}})
* {{hyph|en|of|fense}}

* {{rhymes|en|ɛns|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}} {{lb|en|American spelling}}

# The [[act#Noun|act]] of [[offending#Noun|offending]].
## A [[crime]] or [[sin#Noun|sin]].
##* {{RQ:Douglass Bondage|chapter=3|passage=The slave fully appreciates the saying, "where ignorance is bliss, 'tis folly to be wise." When old master's gestures were violent, ending with a threatening shake of the head, and a sharp snap of his middle finger and thumb, I deemed it wise to keep at a respectable distance from him; for, at such times, trifling faults stood, in his eyes, as momentous '''offenses'''; and, having both the power and the disposition, the victim had only to be near him to catch the punishment, deserved or undeserved.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=w:Edwin Black
|title=Internal Combustion
|chapter=2|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL4103950W
|passage=The popular late Middle Ages fictional character Robin Hood, dressed in green to symbolize the forest, dodged fines for forest '''offenses''' and stole from the rich to give to the poor. But his appeal was painfully real and embodied the struggle over wood.}}
## An [[affront#Noun|affront]], [[injury]], or [[insult#Noun|insult]].
##* {{RQ:Ovid Epistles|chapter=Preface|page=26|passage=Thus I have ventur'd to give my Opinion on this Subject againſt the Authority of two great men, but I hope without '''offence''' either to their Memories, for I both lov'd them living, and reverence them now they are dead.}}
# The state of being offended or [[displease]]d; [[anger]]; [[displeasure]].
# {{lb|en|team|_|sports}} A [[strategy]] and [[tactics]] employed when in position to [[score]]; ''contrasted with'' [[defense]].
# {{lb|en|team|_|sports}} The portion of a [[team]] dedicated to scoring when in position to do so; ''contrasted with'' [[defense]].

