* {{rhymes|sv|ɑːr|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|sv|non|hvar}}, from {{der|sv|gem-pro|*hwar}}.

====Adverb====
{{sv-adv|-}}

# [[where]]; at which place
#: {{syn|sv|vart|q=informal, nonstandard}}
#: {{uxi|sv|'''Var''' är mina nycklar?|'''Where''' are my keys?}}
#: {{uxi|sv|'''Var''' var jag?|'''Where''' was I?}}

=====Related terms=====
{{col-auto|sv
|vart
|varifrån
}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|sv|conjunction}}

# [[where]]; the situation in which

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|sv|non|hverr}} (paradigm merged with a descendant of {{m|gem-pro|*hwaz}} and a descendant of {{der|sv|gem-pro|*hwarjaz|t=who (of many)}}. A cognate to {{cog|is|hver#Etymology 2|hver}}.

====Determiner====
{{head|sv|determiner|neuter|vart}}

# {{lb|sv|dated}} [[every]]
#: {{uxi|sv|'''Var''' dag är en sällsam gåva|'''Every''' day is a peculiar gift}}
#* {{circa|1847}}, Carl August Hagberg, translation of Shakespeare's ''As You Like It'' (c. 1599), [https://runeberg.org/hagberg/f/0237.html act 3, scene 2]
#*: {{quote|sv|Att för '''hvart''' öga som i skogen ser / Det må ett vittne till min dyrkan blifva.|That '''every''' eye which in this forest looks / Shall see thy virtue witness'd every where.}}
#: {{syn|sv|varje}}
# [[each]]; per person/thing involved
#: {{uxi|sv|Vi fick två bananer '''var'''|We got two bananas '''each'''}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|sv
|lite varstans
|vardag<t:weekday>
|var för sig<t:separately>
|var och en<t:one and all>
|varsågod
}}

===Etymology 3===
{{rfe|sv}}{{attention|sv|are these two or three separate etymologies?}}

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|n|g2=c}}

# {{lb|sv|uncountable}} [[pus]]; a mixture of dead [[bacteria]] and [[white blood cell]]s, occurring in areas of [[infection]]s {{g|n}}
# [[pillowcase]] {{g|n}}
# various species of [[flatfish]] of the family {{taxfmt|Scophthalmidae|family}}, such as [[megrim]], [[whiff]], [[butt]], [[turbot]] {{g|c}}

