==Turkish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|tr|/vɑɾ/}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tr|ota|وار|tr=var}}, from {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*bār}}.  Compare {{cog|otk|𐰉𐰺|tr=bar}}.

====Adjective====
{{tr-adj|-}}

# [[there is]], [[there are]] (not a verb)
#: {{ux|tr|[[İstanbul]]'da [[bir]] [[kervansaray]] '''var'''.|'''There is''' a caravanserai in Istanbul.|lit=A caravanserai '''exists''' in Istanbul.}}
#: {{ux|tr|[[yedi|Yedi]]ye [[yirmi]] [[beş]] '''var'''.|It's twenty-five to seven.|lit='''There are''' twenty-five [minutes] to seven.''}}
# it [[exist]]s
#: {{ux|tr|[[pirinç|Pirinç]] var mı? — [[evet|Evet]], '''var'''.|Is there any rice? — Yes, '''there is'''.}}
# Expressing [[possession]], equivalent of [[have]].
#: {{ux|tr|[[iki|İki]] [[teyze]]m [[ve]] bir [[dayı]]m '''var'''.|I have two aunts and an uncle.|lit=My two aunts and my uncle '''exist'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
• As an adjective, ''var'' is only used [[predicatively]].

• In the phrases “var olmak” and “var etmek”, the word is pronounced with a long vowel (''va:r'').

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|tr|yok}} {{qualifier|there isn't, not have}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{head|tr|verb form}}

# {{tr-verb form of|varmak}}

==Yola==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|yol|/vɔː/}}   

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|yol|enm|fer|far}}, from {{inh|yol|ang|feorr}}.

====Adjective====
{{head|yol|adjective|comparative|valler}}

# [[far]]
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|line=4-6|page=116|title=CONGRATULATORY ADDRESS IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage=Yer name var zetch avancet avare ye, e'en a dicke '''var''' hye, arent whilke ye brine o'zea an ye craggès o'noghanes cazed nae balke.|translation=Your fame for such came before you even into this '''retired''' spot, to which neither the waters of the sea below nor the mountains above caused any impediment.}}

====Adverb====
{{head|yol|adverb}}

# [[far]]
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|chapter=THE WEDDEEN O BALLYMORE|number=4|page=96|title=SONGS, ETC. IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage=An neeat wooden trenshoorès '''var''' whiter than snow.|translation=And neat wooden trenchers '''far''' whiter than snow.}}

===Etymology 2===

====Preposition====
{{head|yol|preposition}}

# {{alt form|yol|vor}}
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|page=39|title=GLOSSARY OF THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage='''Var''' faade?|translation='''For''' what?}}
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|chapter=ABOUT AN OLD SOW GOING TO BE KILLED|number=2|page=106|title=SONGS, ETC. IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage=Gooude '''var''' nat oan dhing, niether treesh ar thraame;|translation=Good '''for''' not one thing; neither for the trace, nor the car.}}
#* {{quote-book|yol|year=1867|line=14-15|page=116||title=CONGRATULATORY ADDRESS IN THE DIALECT OF FORTH AND BARGY|passage=till ee zin o'oure daies be '''var''' aye be ee-go t'glade.|translation=until the sun of our lives (be '''for''' ever) be gone down the dark valley (of death).}}

===References===
* {{R:Poole 1867|page=74}}
