==Persian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal||tr=xwš|ts=xʷaš|sc=Phlv|t=pleasant, sweet, nice}}, {{cog|xmn|𐫟𐫇𐫢|ts=xʷaš|t=pleasant, good}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|-}}. Cognate with {{cog|xpr|𐫇𐫟𐫢|ts=wxaš|t=pleasant, sweet}}, {{cog|kmr|xweş}}, {{cog|zza|weş}}, {{cog|hac|tr=wäš}}, {{cog|bal|وش|tr=waš(š)}} and possibly {{cog|kho|khaṣṣa-|t=pleasant}}. {{doublet|fa|وش|tr1=vaš|id1=good}}.

The reconstruction of the Proto-Iranian form and its further relations are {{unc|fa|nocap=1}}. Perhaps {{inh|fa|ira-pro||*hwarša-}}, from {{inh|fa|iir-pro||*swarćša-}}, from {{inh|fa|ine-pro||*swelḱs|t=taste (sweet)}}, and cognate with {{cog|ysc|horz}} and {{cog|xcl|քաղցր}}.<ref>{{R:pal:Klingenschmitt|page=204}}</ref><ref>{{R:bal:Korn|page=132}}</ref> An older proposal explains as {{inh|fa|ira-pro||*hw-aši-}}, from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|[[*Hsu-]][[*Hákši|Hákši]]|t=provided with beautiful sight, beautiful to the eye, or with a kind eye|lit=good-eye}}.<ref>{{R:ira:Müller:1891|page=352}} </ref><ref>{{R:fa:Horn|page=508|section=113}}</ref><ref>{{R:ira:ESIJa|vol=III|page=415}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|xwaš|dari=xwaš,xōš}}
* {{audio|fa|LL-Q9168 (fas)-Darafsh-خوش.wav|a=Iran}}

