==Old Armenian==
[[File:Linum usitatissimum 2019-05-21 3559.jpg|thumb|right|{{taxfmt|Linum usitatissimum|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
The origin is {{unk|xcl|title=unknown}}.

Perhaps connected with {{cog|arc|בּוּצָא|tr=būṣā}}, {{cog|syc|ܒܘܨܐ|tr=būṣā}}, {{cog|he|בּוּץ|tr=būṣ}}, {{cog|grc|βύσσος}} and {{cog|xcl|բեհեզ}}. Also recalls {{cog|xpu|𐤐𐤔𐤕|ts=pišt|t=flax; linen}}, {{cog|he|פֵּשֶׁת|tr=pēšeṯ|t=flax; linen}}, {{m|he|פִּשְׁתָּה|tr=pištā́|t=flax}}, {{cog|uga|𐎔𐎘𐎚|t=linen}}, which is not necessarily unrelated. Even more, {{cog|fa|وش|tr=vaš|t=flax or [[boll]] thereof; uncleaned cotton; a kind of rich satin or other textile}}. If the primitive meaning refers to the [[seed vessel]]s of flax, then {{cog|syc|ܘܐܪܫܐ|tr=wʾršʾ}}, {{m|syc|ܘܪܘܫ|tr=wrwš}}, {{m|syc|ܘܪܝܫܐ|tr=wryšʾ}}, {{m|syc|ܘܪܫܐ|tr=wršʾ}}, {{cog|ar|وَرْس}}, {{m|ar|وُرْس}}, {{m|ar|وُرُس}}, {{m|ar|وَرَس|t={{taxlink|Flemingia macrophylla|species}}, especially its glands}} may be related.

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun}}

# [[flax]] (plant)
# [[tow]], [[hard]]s of flax, flaxen tow, [[stuffing]]; [[oakum]]
#* {{Q|xcl|ՍԳր.|Daniel|3|46|quote=Եւ ոչ դադարէին որք արկին զնոսա սպասաւորք թագաւորին ի հնոցն բորբոքելոյ նաւթիւ եւ ձիթով եւ '''վշով''' եւ որթով:|trans=Now the king’s servants who threw them in kept stoking the furnace with naphtha, pitch, '''tow''', and brushwood.|transauthor=New Revised Standard Version Catholic Edition|refn=<ref>{{R:xcl:Daniel|page=170}}</ref>}}

====Declension====
{{xcl-noun-ո||վշ}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|xcl|վշագործ}}

