==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|van}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|fan||from}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*fanē}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*h₂poneh₁||from}}, from {{der|nl|ine-pro|*h₂epo}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₂pó||off, of}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|fana}}, {{m|osx|fan||from}}, {{cog|ofs|fan}}, {{m|ofs|fon||from}}, {{cog|goh|fona}}, {{m|goh|fon||from}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/vɑn/}}
* {{a|nl|Northern}} {{IPAchar|[fɑn]}}
* {{a|nl|Suriname}} {{IPAchar|[fan]}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-van.ogg|a=Netherlands}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|van}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ɑn|s=1}}

===Preposition===
{{head|nl|preposition}}

# [[of]] {{gloss|possession, property}}
#: {{ux|nl|de hoed '''van''' het meisje|t=the hat '''of''' the girl}}
#: {{ux|nl|het gewicht '''van''' een olifant|t=the weight '''of''' an elephant}}
# [[of]] {{gloss|general association}}
#: {{ux|nl|Zij was '''van''' adel.|t=She was '''of''' noble stock.}}
#: {{ux|nl|een stad '''van''' één miljoen inwoners|t=a city '''of''' one million inhabitants}}
#: {{ux|nl|Hij is een man '''van''' eer.|t=He's a man of honour.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Dat is hier niet '''van''' toepassing.|t=That's not applicable here.}}
#: {{ux|nl|de trein '''van''' tien uur|t=the train '''of''' ten o'clock}}
# [[by]], [[of]] {{gloss|creator}}
#: {{ux|nl|een schilderij '''van''' Rubens|t=a painting '''by''' Rubens}}
#: {{ux|nl|een plaat '''van''' de Beatles|t=a record '''of''' the Beatles}}
# [[from]] {{gloss|origin}}
#: {{ux|nl|Hij komt '''van''' Griekenland.|t=He's '''from''' Greece.}}
# [[from]] {{gloss|starting point of a movement or change}}
#: {{ux|nl|Hij ging '''van''' deur tot deur.|t=He went '''from''' door to door.}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''van''' vader op zoon.|t='''from''' father to son.}}
# [[from]] {{gloss|starting point in time}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''van''' toen af aan.|t='''from''' then onwards}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''van''' 's avonds laat tot 's morgens vroeg|t='''from''' late at night till the early morning}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''van''' dag tot dag|t='''from''' day to day}}
# [[from]], [[off]] {{gloss|removal of something from off something else}}
#: {{ux|nl|het vlees '''van''' de beenderen snijden.|t=to cut the meat '''from''' the bones}}
# [[of]], [[out of]], [[from]], [[with]] {{gloss|cause}}
#: {{ux|nl|sidderen '''van''' angst|t=to tremble '''with''' fear}}
#: {{ux|nl|tranen '''van''' geluk|t=tears '''of''' joy}}
# [[of]], [[out of]], [[with]] {{gloss|material or resource}}
#: {{ux|nl|Deze tafel is gemaakt '''van''' hout.|t=This table is made '''(out) of''' wood.}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''Van''' dit geld kan ik een basgitaar kopen.|t='''With''' this money I'm able to buy a bass.}}
# [[of]], [[out of]], [[among]] {{gloss|out of a larger whole; [[partitive]]}}
#: {{ux|nl|de jongste '''van''' zijn dochters|t=the youngest '''of''' his daughters}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''Van''' alle mensen ben ik de mooiste.|t='''Out of''' all people I am the most beautiful.}}
#: {{ux|nl|Drink niet te veel '''van''' dat bier, het is erg sterk.|t=Don't drink too much '''of''' that beer, it is very strong.}}
# [[from]], [[was]], [[formerly]] {{gloss|indicating a change in price}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''van''' 5 €, voor 3 €|t='''was''' €5, now €3}}
# {{lb|nl|colloquial}} {{l|en|like}} {{gloss|[[quotative]] (used to introduce [[direct speech]])}}
#: ''Ik dacht '''van''' hé wat gek.'' &mdash; I thought, hey, how strange.

