==German==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-inne}}, {{m|gmh|-in}}, from {{inh|de|goh|-inna}}, {{m|goh|-in}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*-ini}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*-inī}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|de|-inn|-inne||both obsolete}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|de|/ɪn/|[ɪn]}}
* {{audio|de|De--in.ogg}}
* For speakers who realise {{m|de|-en}} as {{IPAchar|[ən]}}, the distinction between both may at times be weak. However, most speakers have a syllabic nasal in {{m|de||-en}} and hence keep a very clear distinction.

====Suffix====
{{head|de|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|g=f|genitive|-in|plural|-innen}}

# {{senseid|de|feminine}} {{n-g|creates the female form for many nouns for living beings; [[umlaut]] usually occurs in monosyllables, but rarely in polysyllables}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Arbeitgeber|t1=[[employer]]|Arbeitgeberin|t2=employer (female person or sexless company)}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Autor|t1=[[author]]|Autorin|t2=author (female person, i.e. a [[female]] [[author]] or [[authoress]], or sexless company, abstract thing)}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Gott|t1=[[god]]|Göttin|t2=female god, [[goddess]]}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Hund|t1=[[dog]]|Hündin|t2=female dog, she-dog, [[bitch]]}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Katze|g1=f|t1=[[cat]]|Kätzin|t2=female cat, she-cat}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Sänger|t1=[[singer]]|Sängerin|t2=female singer}}
#: {{suffixusex|de|Pastor|t1=[[pastor]]|Pastorin|t2=female pastor}}
## {{lb|de|dated}} names the wife of a person
##: {{suffixusex|de|Pastor|t1=[[pastor]]|Pastorin|t2=[[wife]] of a pastor}}
## {{lb|de|dated}} {{n-g|creates female personal names (for wives and daughters)}}
##: {{m|de|Schwarz|pos=proper noun}} → {{l|de|Schwarzin}} (''a female person with the name ''Schwarz'', that is the wife or daughter of someone named ''Schwarz''<nowiki />'')
##* {{quote-text|de|year=1743|title=Grosses vollständiges Universal Lexicon aller Wissenschaften und Künste, Welche bishero durch menschlichen Verstand und Witz erfunden und verbessert worden […] Fünf und Dreyßigster Band Schle-Schwa|publisher=Leipzig & Hallle|page=2007
|passage=Schwartz'''in''', (Sibylle) […] war eine Tochter Christian Schwartzens, […] gebohren 1621 […] und starb 1638 den 13 Jul.
|translation=Schwartz (Sibylle [given name]) […] was a daughter of Christian Schwartz, […] born in 1621 […] and died on 13th July 1638.}}

