==Tagalog==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|tl|-hin}}
* {{alt|tl|-nin}}
* {{alt|tl|-rin}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|tl|phi-pro|*-ən}}, from {{inh|tl|poz-pro|*-ən}}, from {{inh|tl|map-pro|*-ən}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{tl-pr|+,-en<q:colloquial>}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-verb|b=+|b2=in}}

# {{non-gloss definition|object trigger}}: to perform the action of the verb to someone or something
#: {{ux|tl|Lulutu'''in''' ko ang isda.|inline=1|I will cook the fish|lit=The fish will be cooked by me.}} {{q|'''The fish''' is focused.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|directional trigger}}: to do something in the (physical or psychological) direction of
#: {{ux|tl|D'''in'''alaw namin ang lola ni Olivia.|inline=1|We visited the grandmother of Olivia.|lit=Olivia's grandmother was visited by us.}} {{q|'''The grandmother''' is focused.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|actor trigger}}: to be affected or overtaken by a condition, feeling or phenomenon
#: {{ux|tl|B'''in'''abaha ang bahay niya.|inline=1|His house gets flooded.}} {{q|'''His house''' is focused.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|object trigger}}: {{q|with root word reduplication}} to do something occasionally, at random, a little, a bit, now and then or here and there
#: {{ux|tl|'''Iniisip''' ko minsan ang nakaraan ko.|inline=1|I sometimes think about my past.|lit=My past is sometimes thought about by me.}} {{q|'''My past''' is focused.}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-adj|b=+|b2=in}}

# [[prone]] to, [[susceptible]] to
#: {{suffixusex|tl|lagnat|t1=fever|lagnatin|t2=prone to fever}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|sakit|t1=illness|sakitin|t2=prone to illness}}

===Suffix===
{{tl-noun|b=+|b2=in}}

# {{non-gloss definition|an object of the action expressed by the root}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|awit|t1=singing, song|awitin|t2=song}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|aral|t1=lesson, studying|aralin|t2=studies}}
# {{lb|tl|Tayabas}} {{ngd|nature and origin suffix}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Quezon|t1=province|Quezonin|t2=a native of Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|Sampaloc|t1=municipality|Sampalukin|t2=a native of Sampaloc, Quezon}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|bayan|t1=town center or poblacion|bayanin|t2=a local from the town center}}
#: {{suffixusex|tl|linang|t1=farm or remote area|linangin|t2=a local from the farm}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally, {{IPAchar|/h/}} is inserted before -in when the root word ends with a vowel that is not followed by a glottal stop. In some cases, phoneme change can occur and {{IPAchar|/h/}} becomes {{IPAchar|/n/}}.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sabi|altsuf=-'''h'''in|sabihin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|talo|altsuf=-'''n'''in|talunin}}

* Sometimes, the final vowel of the root word disappears when the suffix is added.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|sunod|sundin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|kamit|kamtin}}

* Due to [[allophony]], {{IPAchar|/d/}} turns into {{IPAchar|/r/}} when inserted before ''-in''.
*: {{suffixusex|tl|hangad|[[hangarin|hanga'''r'''in]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|baligtad|[[baligtarin|baligta'''r'''in]]}}
*: {{suffixusex|tl|bayad|[[bayarin|baya'''r'''in]]}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|tl}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|tl|a=in|ni}}

==Turkish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*-niŋ}}.

====Suffix====
{{tr-suffix|inflectional}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Genitive case suffix for the nouns which end in a consonant}}
#: {{suffixusex|tr|öğretmen|t1=teacher|öğretmenin|t2=teacher's/of the teacher}}

=====Usage notes=====
* It's used only when the word's last vowel is "e" or "i". It may change into {{m|tr|-ün}}, {{m|tr|-ın}} and {{m|tr|-un}} according to the last vowel of the word.
*: {{suffixusex|tr|yüz|altsuf=-ün|yüzün}} (the last vowel is "ö" or "ü")
*: {{suffixusex|tr|saç|altsuf=-ın|saçın}} (the last vowel is "a" or "ı")
*: {{suffixusex|tr|yol|altsuf=-un|yolun}} (the last vowel is "o" or "u")
* If the word ends in "p", "ç", "t" or "k", it may change them into "b", "c", "d" and "ğ" (see below).
*: {{suffixusex|tr|sebep|sebebin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|köpek|köpeğin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|çekiç|çekicin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|senet|senedin}}
* It may cause the last vowel of the word dropped.
*: {{suffixusex|tr|beyin|alt1=bey'''i'''n|beynin|alt2='''beyn'''in}}
* If the word ends in a vowel, it's used with an auxiliary consonant; "n".
*: {{suffixusex|tr|peri|altsuf=-nin|perinin}}
* It must be used with an [[apostrophe]] if it's appended to a proper noun. It cannot cause consonant voicing (point 3).
*: {{suffixusex|tr|Canberk|Canberk'in}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|tr|trk-pro|*-iŋ}}.

====Suffix====
{{tr-suffix|inflectional}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Second-person singular possessive suffix denoting singular possession in words ending in a consonant.}}
#: {{suffixusex|tr|ev|t1=house|evin|t2=your house}}
#: {{suffixusex|tr|ofis|t1=office|ofisin|t2=your office}}

=====Usage notes=====
* If the noun ends in a vowel, it becomes {{m|tr|-n}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|kedi|altsuf=-n|kedin}}
* It's used only when the word's last vowel is "e" or "i". It may change into {{m|tr|-ün}}, {{m|tr|-ın}} and {{m|tr|-un}} according to the last vowel of the word.
*: {{suffixusex|tr|yüz|altsuf=-ün|yüzün}} (the last vowel is "ö" or "ü")
*: {{suffixusex|tr|saç|altsuf=-ın|saçın}} (the last vowel is "a" or "ı")
*: {{suffixusex|tr|yol|altsuf=-un|yolun}} (the last vowel is "o" or "u")
* If the word ends in "p", "ç", "t" or "k", it may change them into "b", "c", "d" and "ğ".
*: {{suffixusex|tr|sebep|sebebin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|köpek|köpeğin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|çekiç|çekicin}}
*: {{suffixusex|tr|senet|senedin}}
* It may cause the last vowel of the word dropped.
*: {{suffixusex|tr|beyin|alt1=bey'''i'''n|beynin|alt2='''beyn'''in}}
* It must be used with an [[apostrophe]] if it's appended to a proper noun.
*: {{suffixusex|tr|Canberk|Canberk'in}}

===Etymology 3===

====Suffix====
{{tr-suffix|verb}}

# {{senseid|tr|reflexive}} {{non-gloss definition|Reflexive suffix}}
#: {{suffixusex|tr|giymek|alt1=giy-|t1=to wear|giyinmek|alt2=giyin-|t2=to dress oneself}}

==Welsh==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*-in}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*-īnos}}, from {{inh|cy|ine-pro|*-iHnos}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|cy|/ɪn/}}
* {{rhymes|cy|ɪn|s=1}}

===Suffix===
{{head|cy|suffix|g=f}}

# {{non-gloss definition|forms nouns characterised by root}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|{{l|cy|hysb|hesb}}|t1=barren, sterile|hesbin|t2=young ewe}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|crib|t1=comb|cribin|t2=rake}}
# {{lb|cy|obsolete}} {{non-gloss definition|forms adjectives from nouns, usually nouns of material}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|pridd|t1=soil, earth|priddin|t2=earthen}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|aur|t1=gold|eurin|t2=golden}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|lledr|t1=leather|lledrin|t2=leathern}}
# {{non-gloss definition|forms adjectives from other adjectives}}
#: {{suffixusex|cy|garw|t1=rough|gerwin|t2=severe, harsh}}

====Usage notes====
''-in'' causes i-[[affection]] of preceding vowels, e.g., {{suffixusex|cy|aur|t1=gold|eurin|t2=golden}}, {{suffixusex|cy|garw|t1=rough|gerwin|t2=severe, harsh}}.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|cy}}

===References===
* {{R:cy:GPC}}

