==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|-ty}}, from {{inh|en|ang|-tiġ||-ty}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*tigiwiz}}, plural of {{m|gem-pro|*teguz||group of ten}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*deḱ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*déḱm̥||ten}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|-ty||-ty}}, {{cog|fy|-tich||-ty}}, {{cog|nl|-tig||-ty}}, {{cog|de|-zig||-ty}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐌹𐌲𐌿𐍃||group of ten, decade}}. Related to {{l|en|ten}}.

====Suffix====
{{en-suffix}}

# {{senseid|en|multiple}} {{non-gloss definition|[[nonproductive|Nonproductive]] suffix indicating single-digit integer multiples of ten}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{rel-top|terms derived using -ty (multiples of ten)}}
