Page 33 Template:ar-adj-an/documentation: Skipped, no changes
Page 33 Template:ar-adj-an/documentation: -------- begin text --------
{{documentation subpage}}
This template is for displaying the headword line of Arabic adjectives that end in {{m|ar|ـًى}} (e.g. {{m|ar|مُثَنًّى||[[double]]}}). The feminine, plural and feminine plural are regular but complex, and it is easier to have a template produce them.

Certain other templates are available for other types of regular adjectives:
# Adjectives with a regular feminine and sound masculine plural, such as {{m|ar|مُفَضَّل||[[preferable]]}} and other augmented participles, should use {{temp|ar-adj-sound}}.
# {{ar-etym-nisba|nocat=1|pl=1}}, such as {{m|ar|شَرْقِيّ||[[eastern]]}}, should use {{temp|ar-nisba}}.
# Adjectives ending in ''-in'', such as {{m|ar|مُسَاوٍ||[[equal]]}} or {{m|ar|عَالٍ||[[high]]}}, should use {{temp|ar-adj-in}}.

==Parameters==
; {{para|1}}
: Vocalized headword.
; {{para|pl}}
: Override the default masculine plural.
; {{para|el}}
: Specify an elative.

==Examples==

The code <code><nowiki>{{ar-adj-an|مُثَنًّى}}</nowiki></code> produces the following:

{{ar-adj-an|مُثَنًّى}}

The declension section for an adjective like this looks as follows (note the use of <code>sp</code> to signal the sound masculine plural in {{m|ar|ـَوْن}}):

<pre>
====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|مُثَنًّى|pl=sp}}
</pre>

<includeonly>
[[Category:Arabic headword-line templates|adj-an]]
</includeonly>
