==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{calque|en|ar|جَمْع سَالِم}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{c|en|Semitic linguistics}} In [[Semitic]] and other [[Afro-Asiatic]] languages, a [[regular]] plural formed by adding a [[suffix]], without changes to the [[stem]]. An example in [[Arabic]] is {{m|ar|مُسْلِمُونَ||Muslims}}, the plural form of {{m|ar|مُسْلِم||Muslim}}, formed by adding the suffix {{m|ar|ـُونَ}}, and {{m|ar|مُسْلِمَاتٌ|t=Muslim women}}, formed by adding the suffix {{m|ar|ـَاتٌ}}.
#: {{ant|en|broken plural}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|in Arabic and other languages, regular plural formed by adding a suffix}}
* Arabic: {{t|ar|جَمْع سَالِم|m}}
* French: {{t|fr|pluriel externe|m}}
* German: {{t|de|gesunder Plural}}
* Italian: {{t|it|plurale sano|m}}
* Persian: {{t-needed|fa}}
{{trans-bottom}}
