==Arabic==
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}
{{swp|Illiyin|lang=en}}
{{ar-rootbox|ع ل ي}}

===Etymology 1===
{{suffix|ar|عَلِيّ|ـُونَ}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-pl|عَلِيُّونَ}}

# {{plural of|ar|عَلِيّ}}

===Etymology 2===
{{suffix|ar|عِلِّيّ|ـُونَ}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-pl|عِلِّيُّونَ}}

# {{plural of|ar|عِلِّيّ}}

===Etymology 3===
From a merger of {{bor|ar|he|עֶלְיוֹן|tr=ʿelyṓn|t=high, upper; God}} and the root {{ar-root|ع|ل|ي}}, with the last segment of the Hebrew word being taken to be a masculine plural suffix appended to {{m|ar|عِلِّيّ}}, hence blending with the pluralizing inflection {{suffix|ar|عِلِّيّ|ـُونَ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عِلِّيُّون}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|عِلِّيُّون|m}} {{tlb|ar|hapax|in the singular}}

# {{def-uncertain|ar}} {{ant|ar|سِجِّين}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|83|18-19
|passage=كَلَّا إِنَّ كِتَابَ الْأَبْرَارِ لَفِي عِلِّيِّينَ وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا عِلِّيُّونَ
|translation=Forsooth the record of the righteous is in ''ʿilliyyīn'', and what makes you know what ''ʿilliyyūn'' is?}}
## [[God]], [[Allah]]
## the [[heaven]], [[Heaven]], the [[empyrean]], or the [[welkin]], a [[place]] that’s only [[accessible]] to [[divine]]s. It’s usually decipted higher than the seven heavens and the Heavenly chamber.
## the [[paradise]] (garden group), [[Paradise]], [[Elysium]], or the [[Garden of Eden]].
##: {{syn|ar|جَنَّة|نَعِيم}}
### the uppermost paradise of the celestial garden.
###: {{syn|ar|فِرْدَوس}}
## a [[list]] of [[deed]]s of [[mortal]]s kept in such a [[place]]
## [[godly]] [[warden]]s who keep a [[list]] of [[deed]]s of [[mortal]]s or other [[special]] [[knowledge]]
## the {{w|Heaven in Judaism|seventh heaven}}; [[Araboth]].

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|-|pl=عِلِّيُّونَ|state=ind-def}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Ahrens-Christliches|page=20}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel-V|page=23}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=157}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=28}}
