Page 3 پرستیدن: Skipped, no changes
Page 3 پرستیدن: -------- begin text --------
==Persian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|fa|pal|plstytn'|tr=paristīdan|t=to serve; to worship; to minister in a ritual}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*pari-|t=around, peri-}} + {{m|ira-pro|*staH-|t=to place, set, stand}}. The former prefix is from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*pári}}, from {{inh|fa|ine-pro|*per-|*péri}}, and the latter is from {{inh|fa|iir-pro|*stáH-}}, from {{inh|fa|ine-pro|*steh₂-|t=to stand}}.

Related to Old Armenian {{m|xcl|պաշտեմ}}, an Iranian borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|parastī`dan}}

===Verb===
{{fa-regional|پرستیدن|پرستیدن|парастидан}}
{{fa-verb|tr=parastidan|prstem=پرست|tr2=parast}}

# to [[worship]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:نوروزنامه|author={{w|Omar Khayyam|ʿUmar Khayyām}}|year=c. 1080|text=و از پس او طهمورث بنشست، و سی سال پادشاهی کرد، و دیوان را در طاعت آورد، و بازارها و کوچها بنهاد، و ابریشم و پشم ببافت، و رهبان بزسپ در ایام او بیرون آمد، و دین صابیان آورد، و او دین بپذیرفت، و زنار بر بست، و آفتاب را '''پرستید'''، و مردمان را دبیری آموخت{{...}}|tr=u az pas-i ō tahmōras binišast, u sī sāl pādšāhī kard, u dēwān rā dar tā'at āward, u bāzār-hā u kōča-hā binihād, u abrēšum⁠ u pašm bibāft, u ruhbān-i buzasp dar ayām-i ō bērūn āmad, u dīn-i sābiyān āwarad, u ō dīn bipaḏīruft, u zunnār bar bast, u āftāb rā '''parastīd''', u mardumān rā dabīrī āmōxt{{...}}|t=And after him, Tahmōras sat [on the throne] and ruled for thirty years. He forced the demons into submission, built markets and alleyways, and wove with silk and wool. Buzasp the Monk appeared in his days, and he [Tahmōras] accepted the faith of the Sabians, bound the girdle on himself, and '''worshipped''' the sun. And he taught people the arts of writing{{...}}|footer=(Classical Persian transliteration)}}
# to [[idolize]], to [[regard]] extremely [[highly]]

====Conjugation====
{{prs-conj|پرستید|parastīd|پرست|parast}}
{{fa-conj|پرستید|parastid|پرست|parast}}

===References===
* {{R:ira:Cheung|pages=358-61}}
