==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|خ و ر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I|i|a|vn=خَوَر|passive=n}}

# to get weakened, to get weaker, to make/become weak/weaker
# to gradually disappear
# to become less strong/active/violent
# to cease functioning
# to break down
# to be [[feeble]], to be weak and fragile
# to grow tired, to lose [[vigour]]
# to be extinguished
# to be/become [[limp]]
# to grow feeble, to lack vitality, to live under [[enfeebling]] conditions
# to be/become weak/thin, to [[dwindle]]
# to [[languish]]
# to lose [[lustre]]
# to become [[slack]], relaxed, not tense or tight
# to be [[slender]]/[[ropy]]/trivial
# to relent, to give way, to succumb to temptation

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I|a|vn=خَوَر|passive=n}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[attribute]] [[weakness]] to, to call [[feeble]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|خ و ر}}
Compare the frequent {{cog|arc|חוֹרָא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܘܿܪܴܐ|t=hole|tr=ḥōrā}}, {{cog|he|חור|חֹר|tr=ḥōr|t=hole}}, {{cog|akk|𒆢𒁕|ts=ḫurru}}. Compare also {{cog|xcl|խոր}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ar-IPA|خَوْر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|خَوْر|m|pl=أَخْوَار}}

# an [[inlet]] (e.g. [[estuary]], [[lagoon]], [[creek]], [[bay]])
#: {{uxi|ar|خور دبي|tr=Khawr Dubayy|t=Dubai Creek}}
#: {{uxi|ar|خور العديد|tr=Khawr al-ʿUdayd|t=Inland Sea}}
# a coastal [[lake]] or [[pond]]
#: {{uxi|ar|خور البليد|tr=Khawr al-Balīd|t=Al-Baleed Lake}}
# {{lb|ar|Sudan}} a [[wadi]], [[ravine]] or [[canyon]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَوْر|pl=أَخْوَار}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|sw|hori|bor=1}}

===Etymology 3===

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-pl|خُور|p}}

# {{plural of|ar|خَوَّار}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Corriente|volumehalf=I.1|page=336}}

