==Old Armenian==

===Etymology===
From {{m|xcl||*պարշտեմ}}, from {{m|xcl||*պարիշտեմ}}, from {{m|xcl||*պարիշտ}}, from {{uder|xcl|xpr|sc=Latn||*parišt-}}, from {{uder|xcl|ira}} {{m|und||*pari-štā-|lit=standing around}}. Compare {{cog|pal|plst-|tr=parist-}}, {{m|pal|plstytn'|tr=paristīdan||to serve; to minister in a ritual; to worship}}, {{cog|fa|پرستـ|tr=parast-}}, {{m|fa|پرستیدن|tr=parastidan||to worship}}. The earlier form {{m|xcl||*պարիշտ}} survives in compounds: {{m|xcl|բարեպարիշտ}}, {{m|xcl|կռապարիշտ}}, {{m|xcl|ամբարիշտ}}, etc. See also {{m|xcl|պաշտօն}}.

===Verb===
{{xcl-verb}}

# {{lb|xcl|transitive}} to [[minister]], to [[serve]], to [[wait on]]
# {{lb|xcl|transitive}} to [[administer]], to [[confer]]; to [[officiate]]; to [[provide]], to [[furnish]]; to [[exercise]], to [[employ]]
#: {{ux|xcl|պաշտել զխորհուրդս|t=to administer the Sacraments|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|պաշտել զծառայութիւն|t=to serve|inline=1}}
# {{lb|xcl|in mediopassive|intransitive}} to serve, to be useful, to be employed

