==Ottoman Turkish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ota|چومچه|tr1=çumça, çümçe, çömçe|چمچق|tr2=çamçak|چمشق|tr3=çamşak}}

===Etymology===
Likely not inherited in this form in {{cog|trk-ogz|-}}, but borrowed from {{bor|ota|fa|چمچه|tr=čamče}},<ref>{{cite-book|last=Golden|first=Peter Benjamin|editor=Cătălin Hriban|authorlink=Peter Benjamin Golden|chapter=Georgio-Turcica: Some Marginal Notes on Pre-Ottoman/Safavid Oğuz and Non-Oğuz Turkic Elements in Georgian|pages=252–253|title=Studies on the Peoples and Cultures of the Eurasian Steppes|year_published=2011|year=1993|location=Bucharest|publisher=Brăila|isbn=978-973-27-2152-0}} = {{cite-book|title=Archivum Ottomanicum|editor=György Hazai|volume=XIII|year=1993–1994|page=106|pages=101–116|publisher=Harrassowitz|location=Wiesbaden|isbn=978-3-447-08879-4}}</ref> which itself is a borrowing from Turkic. Compare dialectal {{m|ota|چمچ|tr=çömüç}}, also from {{inh|ota|trk-pro|*kamïč}}.

===Noun===
{{ota-noun|tr=çamça, çemçe, çumça, çümçe, çömçe, çömçü}}

# [[drink]]ing-[[tray]], [[bowl]], [[nap]]
# [[scoop]], [[ladle]], [[spattle]]
#: {{syn|ota|صوساق|tr=susak}}

====Descendants====
