* {{R:ota:Redhouse|page=730}}
* {{R:ota:Zenker|volume=1|page=365}}

{{topics|ota|Vessels|Kitchenware}}

==Persian==

===Etymology===
{{bor|fa|trk}} borrowing. Found in {{cog|kk|шөміш}}, {{cog|ky|чөмүч|sc=Cyrl}}, {{cog|ba|сүмес}}, {{cog|uz|choʻmich}}, {{cog|chg||tr=čömüš}},<ref>More {{R:trk:VEWT|page=117b}}</ref> and compare probably separate but similarly formed {{cog|ug||tr=qemič}}, {{cog|xqa||tr=qamɨč}}, {{cog|tyv|хымыш}}, {{cog|sah|хомуос}}, {{cog|dlg|комуос}}, {{cog|xbo||tr=xumǯa}}<ref>More {{R:trk:ESTJa|vol=5|pages=249–250}}</ref> from {{der|fa|trk-pro|*kamïč}},<ref>[http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2falt%2fturcet&text_number=+988&root=config Starling: Proto-Turkic: *kamɨč]</ref> all meaning “scoop, ladle”. In Persian the stem of the former word appears suffixed {{af|fa|^|ـچه|pos2=diminutive|tr2=-če}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|čam`ča,čum`ča}}

===Noun===
{{fa-regional|چمچه|چمچه|чумча}}
{{fa-noun|tr=čamče, čomče}}

# {{lb|fa|archaic}} [[spoon]]
#: {{syn|fa|قاشق|tr1=qâšoq}}
