Page 17 Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/kʷís: -------- begin text --------
{{reconstructed}}
==Proto-Indo-European==

===Etymology===
{{root|ine-pro|ine-pro|*kʷ-}}
A PIE interrogative-indefinite paradigm built from the stems {{m|ine-pro|*kʷi-}} and {{m|ine-pro|*kʷe-}} (parallel to anaphoric {{m|ine-pro|*éy|*i-, *e-}}), the former on nominative and accusative cases of all genders, the latter elsewhere, with no distinction of feminine forms, mostly "human" – "non-human". A stem {{m|ine-pro|*kʷos|*kʷo-}}, an ''o''-stem adjective, with its corresponding feminine ''*kʷeh₂-'', was originally separate, but in most languages there was some conflation with the other two, as it is from this function that the relative pronoun evolves. Ultimately from {{m|ine-pro|*kʷ-}}.

===Pronoun===
{{head|ine-pro|pronoun}}

# [[who]], [[what]] (interrogative)
# [[who]], [[which]], [[that]] (relative)

