==Persian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|گرچه<tr:garče>|ارچه<tr:arče>||poetic}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|fa|اگر|چه|tr1=agar|tr2=če}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|ˈ'agarči}}
* {{audio|fa|LL-Q9168 (fas)-Mazanin (مازنین)-اگرچه.wav|a=Iran}}

===Conjunction===
{{fa-regional|اگرچه|اگرچه|агарчи}}
{{head|fa|conjunction|tr=agarče}}

# [[although]]
#: {{syn|fa|هرچند|tr=harčand|با این که|tr2=bâ in ke}}
#: {{ux|fa|'''اگرچه''' امروز هوا گرم است، اما ما غذای داغ خوردیم.|tr='''agarče''' emruz havâ garm ast, ammâ mâ ğazâ-ye dâğ xordim.|'''Although''' the weather is warm today, we ate hot food.}}
#: {{ux|fa|'''اگرچه''' قبلا شما را ندیده باشم، ولی اسمتان به من آشنا بود.|tr='''agarče''' qablan šomâ râ nadide bâšam, vali esmatân be man âšnâ bud.|'''Although''' I hadn't seen you before, your name was familiar to me.}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally used together with a conjunction like {{m|fa|اما|tr=ammâ}}, {{m|fa|ولی|tr=vali}}, or {{m|fa|لیکن|tr=liken}} in the next clause, unlike in English.<ref>{{cite-book|en|title=The Iranian Languages|chapter=Persian and Tajik|chapter_number=8|text=Concessive clauses (...) are introduced by the following phrases, all 'though, although, despite the fact that': agar-če/agar-či, lit. 'if, though'; har čand ke/har cand(-e ki), lit. 'however much that'; bā (vojud-e) in ke/bo (vujud-i) in ki, lit. 'with the existence of this that'. They usually take the present or past subjunctive, according to time reference. The matrix clause may be introduced by vali/vale, amma/ammo, liken/lekin 'but, still'.|author=Gernot Windfuhr; John R. Perry|year=2009|page=521|url=https://theswissbay.ch/pdf/Books/Linguistics/Mega%20linguistics%20pack/Indo-European/Iranian/Persian%20and%20Tajik%20%28Windfuhr%20%26%20Perry%29.pdf|termlang=fa}}</ref>

====Descendants====
* {{desc|az|əgərçi|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tr|gerçi|eğerçi|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ur|اَگَرْچِہ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ckb|ئەگەرچی|bor=1}}

====References====
<references/>
