==Arabic==

===Etymology===
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*dʰwer-}}
From the {{bor|ar|pal|-}} equivalent to {{cog|fa|دریچه|tr=dariče|t=panel, pane; window, lid, cover for an opening|lit=little door}}, from {{m|fa|در|tr=dar|t=door}} + {{m|fa|ـچه|tr=-če|pos=diminutive suffix}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|ine-pro|*dʰwer-}} (compare {{m|ar|ترس|tr=t-r-s}}, from the same root but via Greek). Compare also {{cog|afb|دريشة|tr=darīša|t=window}} and {{cog|sw|dirisha|t=window, opening}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَرَقَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَرَقَة|f|pl=دَرَق|pl2=دِرَاق|pl3=أَدْرَاق}}

# [[shield]] {{gloss|usually of [[leather]]}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|title=ar:الفروسية|trans-title=Horsemanship|author=w:Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya|year=c. 1346|url=https://ar.wikisource.org/wiki/%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%81%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A9
|passage=لَا يَتَمَكَّنُ صَاحِبُكَ مِن حَمْلِكَ مَعَ تُرْسٍ وَلَا '''دَرَقَةٍ''' وَلَا تَرْكَاشٍ وَلَا شَيْءٍ مِن أَنْوَاعِ السَلَاحِ
|translation=Your companion cannot bear you with a scutum and not with '''a leather shield''' and not with a quiver and not with any kind of weapon.
|tr=lā yatamakkanu ṣāḥibuka min ḥamlika maʿa tursin wa-lā '''daraqatin''' wa-lā tarkāšin wa-lā šayʾin min ʾanwāʿi s-salāḥi}}
# [[skullcap]], {{taxlink|Scutellaria barbata|species}}

