===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|cy|wlm|chwi}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*swīs}} (compare {{cog|br|c’hwi}}, {{cog|kw|hwi}}, {{cog|sga|síi}}), from {{inh|cy|ine-pro|*wos}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|cy|chwi}} {{qualifier|literary}}

====Pronoun====
{{head|cy|pronoun|cat2=personal pronouns}}

# [[you]] {{qualifier|plural; polite}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In the singular, {{m|cy|chi}} is a polite form like French {{m|fr|vous}} or German {{m|de|Sie}}.
* {{m|cy|chi|Chi}} is a feature of most registers of Modern Welsh, whereas very literary Welsh employs {{m|cy|chwi}}.
* In certain southwestern dialects, {{m|cy|chi}} is used as the indefinite personal pronoun like English {{m|en|you}}.

