:''This page is for cleanup jobs. Request jobs are at [[Wiktionary:Task lists]].''
[[fr:Wiktionnaire:Maintenance et nettoyage]]__NEWSECTIONLINK__
{{shortcut|WT:TODO|WT:CDPR}}
[[Category:Things to do|*Todo]][[Category:Requests|Todo]]
{{tocright}}
This page lists cleanup requests affecting multiple entries. These may include updating templates, categories or generic entry structure, but '''not''' specific terms, which should be tagged with {{temp|rfc}} and put on [[WT:RFC]]. Therefore, tasks that have previously been divided across discussion and user pages are grouped together in one place where they are easier to find.

==Frequently updated todo lists==

;Todo Lists project: Please see '''[[WT:Todo/Lists]]''' for a set of regularly updated cleanup lists.
;JeffDoozan's cleanup lists: See '''[[User:JeffDoozan]]''' for lists of entries with formatting or layout errors.

==Regular tasks==
In this section, you will find relatively easy cleanup tasks.

===Categories===
Updated live.
* [[:Category:Non-empty category redirects]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Non-empty category redirects}} currently.
* [[:Category:Pages with broken file links]]: {{#expr:{{formatnum:{{PAGESINCATEGORY:Pages with broken file links}}|R}}-1}} currently. Many of these are spelling errors or remains of file moves and easy to fix.
* [[:Category:Pages with module errors]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Pages with module errors}} currently.
* [[:Category:Pages with ParserFunction errors]]: {{#expr:{{formatnum:{{PAGESINCATEGORY:Pages with ParserFunction errors}}|R}}-1}} currently.
* [[:Category:Pages using deprecated templates]]: {{#expr:{{formatnum:{{PAGESINCATEGORY:Pages using deprecated templates}}|R}}-1}} currently.
* [[:Category:Categories that are not defined in the category tree]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Categories that are not defined in the category tree}} categor{{#ifexpr:{{formatnum:{{PAGESINCATEGORY:Categories that are not defined in the category tree}}|R}}=1|y|ies}} currently.
* [[:Category:Translation table header lacks gloss]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Translation table header lacks gloss}} page{{#ifexpr:{{formatnum:{{PAGESINCATEGORY:Translation table header lacks gloss}}|R}}=1||s}} currently.
* [[:Category:Pages with incorrect ref formatting]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Pages with incorrect ref formatting}} currently.
* [[:Category:Orphaned documentation subpages]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Orphaned documentation subpages}} currently.
* [[:Category:Limit of template reached]]: {{PAGESINCATEGORY:Limit of template reached}} page{{#ifexpr:{{formatnum:{{PAGESINCATEGORY:Limit of template reached}}|R}}=1||s}} currently.

===Special pages===
Updated a couple of times a week.
* [[Special:UncategorizedPages]] (entries).
* [[Special:BrokenRedirects]].
* [[Special:DoubleRedirects]].

===Todo lists===
Updated weekly.
* {{todo list|Blank or extremely short pages}}

==Semi-regular tasks==

Usually dump-analyzed:
* [[/unhelpful abbreviations|Unhelpful abbreviations]] — These should use the full term.
* Occasionally, soft hyphens or other invisible/zero-width characters <code>(­|​|‌|‍)</code> sneak into the content of entries or even the pagenames; the soft hyphens should be removed; the other characters should be discussed.
* People sometimes type <nowiki>{[</nowiki>, <nowiki>}]</nowiki> etc when they mean <nowiki>{{</nowiki> / <nowiki>}}</nowiki>. It is useful to periodically scan dumps for instances of this. Here is some regex: <code><nowiki>([^\[\{]\[\{[^\[\{]|[^\[\{]\{\[[^\[\{]|[^\]\}]\]\}[^\]\}]|[^\]\}]\}\][^\]\}])</nowiki></code>. Simply searching for <code><nowiki>]}</nowiki></code> will not work, because there are many valid instances of it, e.g. {{temp|m|en|<nowiki>a [[link]]</nowiki>}}.
* Every few months, check for instances of the common but nonstandard headers "Alternative form", "Alternative spelling" and "Alternative spellings" (which should be "Alternative forms") and "Usage note" (which should be "Usage notes"). Many other nonstandard headers exist, but none are as common as those. Also, no L1 headers should exist in the main namespace (language headers should always be L2, and all other headers should always be L3 or more). See [[User:Erutuon/mainspace headers]] for a full list of non-language headers and [[User:Erutuon/mainspace headers/possibly incorrect]] for a list of possibly incorrect headers.
* Check for entries using modifier letters or deprecated IPA characters.
* Search for (using the site search function) and fix <code>"Etymology 2" -"Etymology 1"</code> and other cases of higher-number etymologies without the full complement of lower-number etymologies.
* Check for misindented quotations (pages with a line containing <code>{{quote-</code> but not starting with #* or ##*)
* Check for entries that use [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%8B%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%8C&diff=76476763&oldid=66992688 Template:sense], [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=%D7%91%D7%9E%D7%94&diff=76476854&oldid=76032195 Template:a], [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=%D0%BF%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BB%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%8C&diff=76476824&oldid=66995027 manual formatting], etc. instead of {{tl|lb}}
* People, and some other online dictionaries, write /e/ where the actual IPA symbol is /ɛ/, e.g. [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=breadfruit&diff=77439603&oldid=76673807], [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=biomedical&diff=77439583&oldid=75712712], [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=nonrepresentativity&diff=prev&oldid=77440405]

To be monitored manually:
* Check periodically for [[Wiktionary:Todo/Misspellings|misspellings]].
* Check periodically that things in [[:Category:English countable proper nouns]] aren't mislabelled common nouns.
* Periodically fix entries in [[:Category:Terms borrowed back into the same language]] that are not twice-borrowed, like [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=glower&diff=prev&oldid=49335449 this].
* Periodically fix entries in "Category:Terms borrowed from Proto-" categories (see [https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Special:PrefixIndex?prefix=Terms+borrowed+from+Proto-&namespace=14]) like [[:Category:Terms borrowed from Proto-Slavic]] that were not actually "borrowed" by the L2 language (e.g. [//en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=bedna&type=revision&diff=49708056&oldid=48040210 here]).
* Check for incorrect characters (for instance, {{scripttaglink|ي}} vs {{scripttaglink|ی}} and {{scripttaglink|ك}} vs {{scripttaglink|ک}} in Arabic, Persian, Urdu, Azeri, and other languages) that look identical in certain positions and are often mixed up. Lists of instances in common linking templates are found at [[User:Erutuon/wrong script]].
* Check for transliterations containing incorrect characters. These usually indicate errors of some kind. [[User:Erutuon/bad transliteration]] lists transliterations with non-Latin characters, except for those with CJK script and Latin script, such as {{temp|t+|ja|言葉|tr=ことば, kotoba}}.
* Periodically fix entries in [[:Category:English terms derived from Greek]] that are in fact from Ancient Greek (<code>grc</code>) rather than (Modern) Greek (<code>el</code>).
* Periodically check [[/Citations without citations]]
* Periodically check for translations that aren't templatized (but use bare links, like <nowiki>* French: [[foo]]</nowiki>)

Also:
* Uses of the language code <code>aaa</code> ([[:Category:Ghotuo language|Ghotuo]]) in translations tables are often vandalism.
* <code>pdc</code> ([[:Category:Pennsylvania German language|Pennsylvania German]]) and <code>pdt</code> ([[:Category:Plautdietsch language|Plautdietsch]]), <code>aja</code> ([[:Category:Aja language|Aja]]/Adja of Sudan) and <code>ajg</code> ([[:Category:Adja language|Adja]]/Aja of Benin) need to be kept separate.<!-- per User:-sche -->

== Useful search queries ==
* [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=default&fulltext=Search&search=insource%3A%2F%5C%23+%5C%28%5C%5B%5C%5B%2F+-insource%3A%2FChinese%2F&searchToken=alf1rke12kqhy99an1px8jz8o insource:/\# \(\[\[/ -insource:/Chinese/]
*: Mostly, the matched texts need to use {{temp|label}} template. It's also possible to search by a specific label (<code><nowiki># ([[botany]]</nowiki></code>)
* [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&fulltext=Search&search=insource%3A%2F%3D.%5C%7B%5C%7Bsense%2F&searchToken=ahdjpgb7wkwwuzmv949mv7kp insource:/=.\{\{sense/]
*: Mostly {{temp|sense}} should be preceded with an asterisk.
* [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?search=insource%3A%2F%5C%3D%5C%3DEtymology+2%2F+-insource%3A%22Etymology+1%22&title=Special:Search&profile=advanced&fulltext=1&ns0=1 insource:/\=\=Etymology 2/ -insource:"Etymology 1"]
*: Entries with Etymology 2 but not Etymology 1 (there are a few false positives where "Etymology 2" is inside a comment)
* [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?limit=500&search=insource%3A%2F%5B%5Ea-zA-Z%5D%5BTt%5Dhe%5C+the%5B%5E%5C%7Ba-zA-Z%5C-%5D%2F&ns0=1&searchToken=cacchlt09ko95yx5rl9ddyyj2 Instance of "the the" in the entry] - these errors keep on occurring, it's pretty crazy. [[User:GreyishWorm|GreyishWorm]] ([[User talk:GreyishWorm|talk]]) 01:53, 12 November 2022 (UTC)
* [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?sort=last_edit_desc&search=insource%3A%2F%5C%7Btrans%5C-top%2F+-incategory%3A%22English+lemmas%22+-incategory%3A%22Translingual+lemmas%22+-intitle%3A%22translations%22&title=Special:Search&profile=advanced&fulltext=1&ns0=1 Has "trans-top" but not in English or Translingual lemmas]
*: There are some English nonlemmas that ''should'' have translations, but there are also entries in the wrong language or with the wrong headword template, as well as some translations that should be at the lemma.
* [[Special:Search/insource:"Wikipedia.org"]], [[Special:Search/insource:"Wiktionary.org"]]
* Unwanted language code in {{tl|w}}: [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?search=insource%3A%2F%5C%7Bw%5C%7Cen%5C%7C%2F&title=Special:Search&profile=advanced&fulltext=1&ns0=1 insource:/\{w\|en\|/]. The language code (for other than English Wikipedia) is in the {{para|lang}} parameter, so {{tl|w|en|...}} links to the page "{{w|En}}" on English Wikipedia. The "en" can be replaced in the search box to search for other language codes, in which case they would be fixed by either deleting the language code in the first parameter or adding "lang=" in front of it.
* Pages with templates missing parameter {{para|1}}: [[Special:WhatLinksHere/Unsupported_titles/`lcub``lcub``lcub`1`rcub``rcub``rcub`]] (you can use namespace filtering to weed out userspace, and change the "1" to view other positional parameters)
* Fodder for {{tl|etymid}}- hard-coded links to a numbered etymology section: [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?search=insource%3A%2F%5C%23Etymology+%5B0-9%5D%2F&title=Special:Search&profile=advanced&fulltext=1&ns0=1 Special:Search/insource:/\#Etymology+[0-9&rbrack;/]
If the search gives a warning (and even if it doesn't!), see [https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Help:CirrusSearch#Regular_expression_searches Help:CirrusSearch] for ways of making the search much less demanding on the servers and much more likely to provide a complete list of problem entries.

