=== Erroneous Greek characters ===

Any place that the character [[ϕ]] is used in place of [[φ]] or [[ϑ]] in place of [[θ]] in a string that is marked as being <code>grc</code> or <code>el</code> should be listed so that an editor can look them over and fix mistakes. I just found one lying around in a {{temp|term}}, which made me think that these shouldn't be overly hard to find. —[[User:Metaknowledge|Μετάknowledge]]<small><sup>''[[User talk:Metaknowledge|discuss]]/[[Special:Contributions/Metaknowledge|deeds]]''</sup></small> 21:01, 12 May 2015 (UTC)
: {{Ping|Metaknowledge}} Never knew this page existed. Ironically I came across this why searching for incorrect uses of {{lang|grc|ϕ}}. For future reference, [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϕ%2F&fulltext=1 here is the search for {{lang|grc|ϕ}}] and [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϑ%2F&fulltext=1 here is the search for {{lang|grc|ϑ}}] (other incorrect characters are {{lang|grc|2=[https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϖ%2F&fulltext=1 ϖ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϛ%2F&fulltext=1 ϛ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϰ%2F&fulltext=1 ϰ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϱ%2F&fulltext=1 ϱ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϐ%2F&fulltext=1 ϐ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϵ%2F&fulltext=1 ϵ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϲ%2F&fulltext=1 ϲ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fϗ%2F&fulltext=1 ϗ] [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Special:Search&profile=all&search=Ancient+Greek+insource%3A%2Fȣ%2F&fulltext=1 ȣ]}}; there may be more). --[[User:Wikitiki89|Wiki]][[User talk:Wikitiki89|Tiki]][[Special:Contributions/Wikitiki89|89]] 13:20, 21 April 2017 (UTC)
: If nothing has been done about this, I can make [[Module:script utilities]] search for these characters when it tags text, and add a tracking template or a category. — [[User:Erutuon|Eru]]·[[User talk:Erutuon|tuon]] 23:50, 20 May 2017 (UTC)
: {{reply to|Metaknowledge|Wikitiki89}} {{diff|43037096||Done.}} — [[User:Erutuon|Eru]]·[[User talk:Erutuon|tuon]] 00:02, 21 May 2017 (UTC)
:: {{Ping|Erutuon}} It's never done, people will keep adding them. --[[User:Wikitiki89|Wiki]][[User talk:Wikitiki89|Tiki]][[Special:Contributions/Wikitiki89|89]] 15:03, 22 May 2017 (UTC)
::: Oh sorry, you were referring to having [[Module:script utilities]] search for them. It's not that nothing has been done, I went through and removed over a hundred of these. But again, people will keep adding them. --[[User:Wikitiki89|Wiki]][[User talk:Wikitiki89|Tiki]][[Special:Contributions/Wikitiki89|89]] 15:05, 22 May 2017 (UTC)
:::: Right. I just found one in {{m|en|polypharmacy}}... 🙄 — [[User:Erutuon|Eru]]·[[User talk:Erutuon|tuon]] 18:14, 22 May 2017 (UTC)

:[[User:Erutuon]], should we add an actual cleanup ''category'' to entries using these? I just cleaned up ''[[hypophora]]'', which had no indication on the page itself (that I noticed) of the problem (though someone who knew where the tracking template was could find the page). I'm going at ask in the [[WT:GP]] if we could catch these with an edit filter. [[User:-sche|- -sche]] [[User talk:-sche|(discuss)]] 11:13, 12 November 2022 (UTC)
:: {{reply to|-sche}} Unfortunately that isn't a good idea because adding a category will cause changes in parsing in certain cases. We don't do that at all when language-tagging text at the moment and so language-tagged text can be used in cases where a link wouldn't be allowed. For instance, if language-tagged text is inside the text of a page link (<code><nowiki>[[some page|{{lang|grc|ϑ}}]]</nowiki></code>), adding a category link (the equivalent of <code><nowiki>[[some page|{{lang|grc|ϑ}}[[Category:Bad Ancient Greek text]]]]</nowiki></code>) next to it would break the page link. — [[User:Erutuon|Eru]]·[[User talk:Erutuon|tuon]] 21:28, 13 November 2022 (UTC)

:As of a while ago, I implemented (with an IP's help) one filter which warns against a few of the most-wrong of the characters above, which has already helped some users to replace them before saving their edit, and another filter which silently tracks ''all'' of the characters. [[User:-sche|- -sche]] [[User talk:-sche|(discuss)]] 02:38, 2 August 2023 (UTC)

=== Not click characters ===

All over the dictionary, e.g. in the name and content of [[!nawas]] and in [//en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Angola&diff=prev&oldid=32122562 this translation], <tt>!</tt> turns up for <tt>ǃ</tt>, and I wouldn't be surprised to find other substitutions for click consonants. The best way I can think of to find such uses is: create a list of all languages that use clicks, or as a presumably easier-to-make approximation of that a list of all Khoisan languages, then search a database dump for all translations, language sections, and {{temp|m}}/{{temp|l}}s of those languages that contain <tt>!</tt>. I've just cleaned up the few pages which misused <tt>!</tt> in their pagenames (only 31 pages on Wiktionary used <tt>!</tt> in their pagenames at all). [[User:-sche|- -sche]] [[User talk:-sche|(discuss)]] 18:42, 25 August 2015 (UTC)

== 2017 ==

=== Check IDs ===

As discussed at {{section link|Wiktionary:Grease pit/2017/May#Adding ids to enable linking to headwords}}, we need to check for sense ids in {{temp|senseid}} and the {{para|id}} parameter of headword templates that are on the same page and have the same language and have the same id string: that is, those that would create the exact link when input into an entry linking template. Each sense id for a given language on a given page should be unique. — [[User:Erutuon|Eru]]·[[User talk:Erutuon|tuon]] 16:57, 19 May 2017 (UTC)

=== Usage note template naming ===

[[User:-sche/Usage note templates]] lists some usage-note templates which could be moved to fit our usual naming scheme, as described on the page and [https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Wiktionary:Beer_parlour/2014/June#Naming_scheme_for_templatized_usage_notes]. [[User:-sche|- -sche]] [[User talk:-sche|(discuss)]] 22:01, 26 May 2017 (UTC)

