=== "Raw" inflection tables in entries ===
Numerous entries contain hard-coded, non-templated inflection tables. Languages especially affected include Hunsrik, Pennsylvania German, Albanian, Old Marathi, and Sanskrit. Some of them have probably been subst'ed by accident, but  in other cases, no inflection template exists. The development of a new one will be necessary.

See [https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?search=insource%3A%2Finflection-table%2F&title=Special:Search&profile=advanced&fulltext=1&ns0=1 the search], which currently returns 198 pages. [[User:This, that and the other|This, that and the other]] ([[User talk:This, that and the other|talk]]) 05:45, 14 August 2023 (UTC)
:In the English Wikipedia I instituted a system whereby certain accidentally substituted templates (cleanup tags) were easily de-substituted.  I think someone else improved it so that they de-substituted themselves, though this required some magic somewhere. ''[[User:Rich Farmbrough|Rich]]&nbsp;[[User talk:Rich Farmbrough|Farmbrough]]'', <small>15:43, 13 December 2023 (UTC).</small><br />

