===Etymology 2===
Perhaps related to {{der|fa|ine-pro||*tḱey-m̥no-}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*tḱey-|gloss=to cultivate, settle, live}}. Compare with {{cog|ae|𐬱𐬀𐬌𐬌𐬀𐬥𐬀|t=place of residence}}, {{cog|xcl|շէն}}, and {{cog|syc|ܫܝܢܐ|tr=šaynā}}. {{noncog|sog|tr=šyn|ts=šēn}}, which is often glossed as “resting place” and adduced as a cognate, in reality means “bed” and is borrowed from {{noncog|sa|शयन|gloss=bed}}, which is from the unrelated root {{m|ine-pro|*ḱey-|gloss=to be lying down}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{fa-IPA|šan}}

====Suffix====
{{fa-noun|head=شَن|tr=šan}}

# [[place]]
#: {{syn|fa|گاه<tr:gāh>|کده<tr:kade>}}

