==Armenian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|hy|xcl|քաղաք}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hy-pron}}
* {{audio|hy|Hy-քաղաք.ogg|a=Eastern Armenian}}

===Noun===
{{hy-noun}}

# [[city]], [[town]]

====Declension====
{{hy-noun-ի-ներ}}
{{hyw-noun-ի-ներ}}
{{hyw-noun-ի-ներ||քաղք}}

==Old Armenian==

===Etymology===
Probably an {{bor|xcl|ira}} borrowing. Compare {{cog|pal|tr=klʾk|ts=*kalāk|sc=Phlv|t=name of a fortress in Khorasan (in {{w|Bundahishn}})}}, {{cog|mzn|کلا|tr=-kalā|pos=suffix forming names of inhabited places}}, {{cog|fa|کلات|tr=kalât}}, {{m|fa|کلاته|tr=kalâte|gloss=fortress, castle; market town}}, {{cog|kmr|kelek}}, {{cog|ckb|کەڵەک|t=pile of stones, dry stone wall}}, {{cog|lrc|کٱل|tr=kal|t=castle, house, hill}}. Bailey explains the Iranian words from {{m+|ira-pro||*kata-}} which forms names for any "covered place": {{cog|ae|𐬐𐬀𐬙𐬀|t=habitation}}, {{cog|fa|کده|tr=kade|t=house}}, {{cog|wbl|kut||roof}}, {{cog|ps|کلی|tr=këlay|t=village}} etc. with further cognates in {{cog|sla-pro|*kotьcь||cottage, pigsty}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌴𐌸𐌾𐍉||chamber}}, {{cog|sa|चतति|tr=cátati|t=to hide oneself}}. He assumes a dialectal *''t'' → ''l'' sound change in Western Iranian languages, as in Pashto. Klingenschmitt offers an alternative derivation of the Iranian terms from {{m+|ine-pro|*kelH-||hill}}, with the same semantic development as in {{m+|gem-pro|*burgz||fortification}} from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰerǵʰ-||high}}.<ref>{{R:pal:Justi|page=199ab}}</ref><ref>{{R:Bailey:1959|pages=118–120}}</ref><ref>{{R:kho:DKS|pages=398a, 50b}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:Klingenschmitt|pages=201–202}}</ref> Note also {{cog|huy|kalaki|t=living room}}.

Alternatively, the Armenian and Iranian may be independently borrowed from {{bor|xcl|sem}}, namely from {{der|xcl|akk|𒌷𒆗𒄷|tr=<sup>URU</sup>kal-ḫu|ts=Kalḫu}}, {{m|akk|𒌷𒆗𒄭|tr=<sup>URU</sup>kal-ḫi|ts=Kalḫi}}, {{m|akk|𒌷𒆗𒄩|tr=<sup>URU</sup>kal-ḫa}}/{{m|akk|𒌷𒆕𒄩|tr=<sup>URU</sup>kàl-ḫa|ts=Kalḫa}}, less frequently written {{m|akk|𒌷𒅗𒈛|tr=<sup>URU</sup>ka-làḫ}}, the ancient city capital of Assyria on the Tigris, called {{w|Calah}} in the Bible. The city name is rendered as {{cog|grc|Χαλαχ}} in the Septuagint.<ref name=HAB>{{R:xcl:HAB|vol=IV|pages=542–543}}</ref><ref>{{R:Bielmeier:1985|pages=37–41}}</ref> Another possibility is {{m+|akk|𒇥|tr=TUL<sub>2</sub>|ts=kalakku|t=excavation, trench; pit; underground store, silo, cellar}}, a loanword from {{m+|sux|𒇥|tr=kalak|t=excavation, trench, store-cellar}}.<ref name=HAB/>

It is often assumed {{cog|ar|قَلْعَة|t=fortress, fort, castle}} is somehow connected. Further often connected with {{cog|syc|ܟܪܟܐ|tr=karəḵā|t=walled city or town, fortress; enclosure}}, {{cog|he|כרך|tr=kəraḵ|t=large city}}.

Unconvincing native {{cog|ine-pro|-}} etymologies have also been proposed.<ref>{{R:xcl:Winter:1955|page=8}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Winter:1965|page=105}}, connecting with {{m+|grc|πτόλις}}, {{m|grc|πόλις}}, {{m+|sa|पुर्|tr=púr}} and deriving from {{m|ine-pro||*pwl̥H-s}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Olsen|page=952}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun}}

# [[city]], [[town]]
#* {{Q|xcl|ՍԳր.|Genesis|4|17|quote=Եմուտ Կային առ կին իւր, եւ յղացաւ եւ ծնաւ զԵնոք։ Եւ շինէր '''քաղաք''', եւ դնէր անուն '''քաղաքին''' յանուն որդւոյ իւրոյ Ենոքայ։|trans=And Cain knew his wife, and having conceived she bore Enoch; and he built a '''city'''; and he named the '''city''' after the name of his son, Enoch.|transauthor=Brenton Septuagint Translation|refn=<ref>{{R:xcl:Genesis|page=162}}</ref>}}
#* {{Q|xcl|ՍԳր.|Deuteronomy|3|5|quote=ա՟մ '''քաղաքք''' ամուրք բարձրապարիսպք դրամբք եւ դռնափակօք․ թող '''ցքաղաքսն''' փերեզացոց բազում յոյժ|trans=all strong '''cities''', lofty walls, gates and bars; besides the very many '''cities''' of the Pherezites|transauthor=Brenton Septuagint Translation|refn=<ref>{{R:xcl:Cox:1981|page=86}}</ref>}}
#* {{Q|xcl|ՍԳր.|Job|24|12|quote=Որք ի '''քաղաքաց''' եւ ի տանց իւրեանց զընկեցան, անձինք տղայոց մեծամեծս հեծեծեցին․ եւ նա այնմ այցելութիւն ընդէ՞ր ոչ առնիցէ։|trans=Those who cast them out of the '''cities''' and their own houses, though the souls of the young groaned very loudly—and he, why does he not pay a visit to that one?|transauthor=Claude E. Cox|refn=<ref>{{R:xcl:Cox:2006|page=189}}</ref>}}
#* {{Q|xcl|ՍԳր.|Daniel|3|28|quote=եւ իրաւունս ճշմարտութեան արարեր ըստ ամենայնի զոր արարեր մեզ եւ '''քաղաքի''' սրբոյ հարցն մերոյ Երուսաղէմի, զի ճշմարտութեամբ եւ յիրաւի ածեր զայս ամենայն վասն մեղաց մերոց|trans=In all the things that thou hast brought upon us, and upon the holy '''city''' of our fathers, even Jerusalem, thou hast executed true judgment: for according to truth and judgment didst thou bring all these things upon us because of our sins.|transauthor=Brenton Septuagint Translation|refn=<ref>{{R:xcl:Daniel|page=168}}</ref>}}

