Page 17 նաւակատիք: -------- begin text --------
==Old Armenian==

===Etymology===
An {{uder|xcl|ira|-}} borrowing, {{suffix|xcl||ք}}.

The first part goes back to an Iranian descendant of {{cog|ine-pro|*néwos||new}} (compare {{cog|ae|𐬥𐬀𐬎𐬎𐬀}}), the second is of {{unc|xcl|nocap=1}} origin.
Hübschmann identified it with {{cog|ira-pro|*kata-||house}} (compare {{cog|ae|𐬐𐬀𐬙𐬀|𐬐𐬀𐬙𐬀-|habitation}}, {{cog|fa|کده||tr=kade|habitation}}). But according to Jahukyan, it goes back to {{uder|xcl|ira}} {{m|und|*kāti-||wish, desire}} (compare {{cog|sa|काति||wishing, desiring}}), from {{cog|ira-pro|*kā-||to strive for, to desire}} (compare the Iranian etymon of {{m|xcl|կամք}}) with the verbal suffix {{m|ira-pro|*-ti-}}.

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun|g=pl}}

# [[inauguration]], [[dedication]], [[consecration]] ceremony
#: {{ux|xcl|առնել զնաւակատիս շինուածոյ|t=to inaugurate a building|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|նաւակատիս առնել սեղանոյն|t=to dedicate or consecrate an altar|inline=1}}
# [[feast]], [[festival]], [[rejoicing]] celebrated at the anniversaries of building inaugurations, weddings, etc.
# {{lb|xcl|Christianity}} the eve of five “Tabernacle” feasts of the [[Armenian Apostolic Church]], when the fasting rules are relaxed

====Declension====
{{xcl-noun-ո-ա-pl||նաւակատ}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|hy|նավակատիք}}

===References===
* {{R:xcl:Bedr}}
* {{R:xcl:NHB}}
* {{R:xcl:HAB}}
* {{R:xcl:GB}}
* {{R:xcl:AG|page=202}}
* {{R:hy:HBB}}
* {{R:xcl:Jahukyan:1995}}
-------- end text --------
