{{unc|en}}; possibly from ''[[blew]]'' (past tense of ''blow'').

====Verb====
{{en-verb|blues|blueing|pres_ptc2=bluing|blued}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|dated}} To [[spend]] (money) extravagantly; to [[blow]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1974|author=w:GB Edwards|title=The Book of Ebenezer Le Page|page=311|year_published=2007|location=New York
|passage=They was willing to '''blue''' the lot and have nothing left when they got home except debts on the never-never.}}

