==Persian==

===Etymology===
The form from {{bor|fa|ar|دِهْقَان}}, from {{inh|fa|pal|tr=dhywkʾn'|ts=dahigān|t=countryman, farmer}}, also found as {{doublet|fa|دهگان|tr1=dehgân|دهخان|tr2=dehxân|notext=1}}. {{surf|fa|ده<tr:deh><t:village>|ـگان<tr:-gân><t:pertaining to, -er>}}. Akin to {{cog|xcl|դեհկանութիւն|դեհկան-ութիւն}}, {{cog|syc|ܕܗܩܢܐ|tr=dahqānā}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|dih`qān|haz=dēğū|kbl=dē`qān}}

===Noun===
{{fa-regional|دهقان|دهقان|деҳқон}}
{{fa-noun|tr=dehqân}}

# [[farmer]], [[peasant]]
#: {{syn|fa|کشاورز<tr:kešâvarz>}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|author=w:Hafez|trans-title={{w|The Divan of Hafez}}|title=fa:دیوان حافظ|year=c. 1390|chapter=Ghazal 486|url= https://ganjoor.net/hafez/ghazal/sh486|text='''دهقان''' سال‌خورده چه خوش گفت با پسر<br>کای نور چشم من! به‌جز از کشته ندروی|tr='''dihqān'''-i sāl-xwarda či xwaš guft bā pisar<br>k-ay nūr-i čašm-i man! ba joz az kišta na-dirawī|t=How well the aged '''peasant''' spoke to his son:<br>"O light of my eyes! You reap nothing but what was planted."|footer=(Classical Persian romanization)}}
# {{lb|fa|historical}} {{w|dihqan}} (local aristocrat in late [[Sasanian]] and early Islamic Iran)
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:شاهنامه|trans-title={{w|Shahnameh|Book of Kings}}|year=c. 1011|author={{w|Ferdowsi|Abu'l-Qāsim Firdawsī}}|chapter=The Reign of Bahrām Gōr|url=https://ganjoor.net/ferdousi/shahname/bahgoor/sh39|text=نه بازارگان ماند ایدر نه شاه<br>نه '''دهقان''' نه لشکر نه تخت و کلاه|tr=na bāzārgān mānd andar na šāh<br>na '''dihqān''' na laškar na taxt u kulāh|t=No merchant remained there, nor a king,<br>No '''lord''' nor army nor throne and crown.|footer=(Classical Persian romanization)}}
# {{lb|fa|obsolete|by extension from "Persian aristocrat"}} [[Persian]], [[Iranian]] (as opposed to Arabs and Turks)
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:شاهنامه|trans-title={{w|Shahnameh|Book of Kings}}|year=c. 1011|author={{w|Ferdowsi|Abu'l-Qāsim Firdawsī}}|chapter=The Reign of Yazdgird|url=https://ganjoor.net/ferdousi/shahname/yazdgerd3/sh2|text=نه '''دهقان''' نه ترک و نه تازی بود<br>سخن‌ها به کردار بازی بود|tr=na '''dihqān''' na turk u na tāzī buwad<br>suxan-hā ba kirdār-i bāzī buwad|t=They will be neither '''Persian''' nor Turk nor Arab,<br>Their words will be in the manner of a joke.|footer=(Classical Persian romanization)}}

