Page 21 ատեան: Skipped, no changes
Page 21 ատեան: -------- begin text --------
==Old Armenian==

===Etymology===
The origin is {{unc|xcl|nocap=1}}.

Traditionally considered an inheritance from {{noncog|ine-pro|*sed-||to sit}} and cognate with {{cog|la|solium||throne, seat}}, {{cog|sga|suide||seat}}, but the vocalism is irregular. A sense development “session, sitting, meeting of an assembly; assembly” → “place and time of such an assembly” → “time in general” is assumed; compare {{cog|fa|گاه|tr=gâh||time; place}}.<ref>{{R:xcl:Meillet:1894|page=154}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Hübschmann:1899|page=47}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:Pedersen:1900|page=98}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:HAB|vol=I|pages=286–287}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:HLPatm|vol=I|pages=38–39}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Morani:1994|page=395}}</ref>

But more likely a {{bor|xcl|sem}} borrowing, {{der|xcl|akk|adānum|𒄩𒁲𒀀𒉏|tr=adiānum|t=fixed date}}, which has also reached {{cog|ar|عِدّان|t=a time something is set; a place of remaining}}, a relation already made by {{w|David Heinrich Müller|D. H. Müller}}.<ref>{{R:xcl:Bittner:1901|page=411}}</ref> The borrowing would have to be very old due to the {{m|hyx-pro||*d}} → {{m|xcl|տ}} sound shift, as in {{m|xcl|պարտէզ}}.

Bad Iranian etymologies have also been proposed.<ref>{{R:xcl:Müller:1893|page=376}}</ref><ref>{{R:fa:Müller:1896|page=273}}</ref><ref>{{R:Perikhanyan:1973|page=442}}</ref><ref>{{R:ira:Gippert:1993|vol=I|pages=24–25}}</ref><ref>{{R:xcl:Olsen|page=xl}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{xcl-noun}}

# [[assembly]], [[council]]; [[assembly]] of judges, [[tribunal]]; [[session]] of an assembly
#: {{ux|xcl|յատեան մատնել|t=to call before a tribunal or council|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|գումարել զատեան|t=to convoke, to call together an assembly|inline=1}}
# [[assembly]] hall, [[court]] hall
# [[tribunal]], [[seat]]
# [[trial]] before a court
# the space in front of the [[sanctuary]] in [[temple]]s
# [[time]]
#: {{ux|xcl|ատեան հողմոյ|t=time when the wind blows|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|xcl|յատենի|t=right on time|inline=1}}

