==Hindi==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|hi|fa-cls|جایگاه|tr=jāygāh}}, {{m|fa|جاگه|tr=jāgah}}, from {{m|fa|جا|tr=jā}}, {{m|fa|جای|tr=jāy||place}} + {{m|fa|ـگاه|tr=-gāh|t=location suffix}}. Cognate with {{cog|as|জেগা}}, {{cog|bn|জায়গা}}, {{cog|gu|જગ્યા}}, {{cog|mr|जागा}}, {{cog|ne|जग्गा}}, Old {{cog|dcc|جاگاہ|tr=jāgāh}}, {{cog|or|ଜାଗା}}, {{cog|pa|ਜਗ੍ਹਾ}}.

The shortening of the vowels may be due to influence from {{m|hi|जगत्||[[world]]}}.<ref>{{cite-journal|title=The Etymology of Hindi 'Jagah': A Problem in Diffusion|last=Burton-Page|first=J|journal=Bulletin of the Deccan College Research Institute|volume=20|issue=1/4|year=1960|pages=288–290|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/42929747}}</ref>

