===Pronunciation===
{{fa-IPA|bārˈgāh}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=bârgâh}} {{tlb|fa|historical}}

# [[hall]] of [[audience]], [[reception]] [[hall]]; place where [[guest]]s, [[envoy]]s, etc., are [[greet]]ed or [[sent away]]
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:شاهنامه|trans-title={{w|Shahnameh|Book of Kings}}|year=c. 1011|author={{w|Ferdowsi|Abu'l-Qāsim Firdawsī}}|chapter=The reign of Manūchihr|url=https://ganjoor.net/ferdousi/shahname/manoochehr/sh14|text=چو آمد به نزدیکی '''بارگاه'''<br>پیاده شد و راه بگشاد شاه|tr=čū āmad ba nazdīkī-yi '''bārgāh'''<br>piyāda šud u rāh bugšād šāh|t=When he came close to the '''audience hall''',<br>He went on foot, and the king opened the road.|footer=(Classical Persian romanization)}}
# {{lb|fa|transferred sense}} [[palace]], [[court]], [[royal]] [[tent]]
#: {{syn|fa|کاخ <tr:kâx>|دربار<tr:darbâr>}}
#* {{RQ:Gulistan|88|منعم به کوه و دشت و بیابان غریب نیست<br>هر جا که رفت خیمه زد و '''بارگاه''' ساخت|mun'am ba kōh u dašt u biyābān ğarīb nēst<br>har jā ki raft xayma zad u '''bārgāh''' sāxt|A rich man is never a stranger, be he in the mountains, on the plains, or in the desert.<br>Everywhere he goes he pitches a tent and holds '''court'''.}}
# {{lb|fa|transferred sense|obsolete}} [[royal]] [[etiquette]] of [[greeting]] and [[dispatch]]ing [[guest]]s
#: {{syn|fa|استقبال<tr:esteqbâl>}}
#* {{quote-book|fa|title=fa:شاهنامه|trans-title={{w|Shahnameh|Book of Kings}}|year=c. 1011|author={{w|Ferdowsi|Abu'l-Qāsim Firdawsī}}|chapter=The tale of Rustam and Isfandyār|url=https://ganjoor.net/ferdousi/shahname/esfandyar/sh31|text=همی بود بهمن به زابلستان<br>به نخچیر گر با می و گلستان<br>سواری و می خوردن و '''بارگاه'''<br>بیاموخت رستم بدان پور شاه|tr=hamē būd bahman ba zābulistān<br>ba naxčīr gar bā may u gulistān<br>sawārī u may xwardan u '''bārgāh'''<br>biyāmūxt rustam bad-ān pūr-i šāh|t=Bahman remained in Zābulistān,<br>Either hunting or with wine and rose gardens.<br>Rustam taught that royal son<br>Riding, wine-drinking, and '''welcoming guests'''.|footer=(Classical Persian romanization)}}
# {{rfv-sense|fa}} [[shrine]]

