Page 2 blaze: Skipped, no changes
Page 2 blaze: -------- begin text --------
{{also|Blaze}}
==English==
[[File:Chance_and_a_Half,_Posing.jpg|thumb|horse with a blaze (3)]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bleɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-blaze.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪz|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰel- (shiny)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|blase}}, from {{inh|en|ang|blæse}}, {{m|ang|blase|t=firebrand, torch, lamp, flame}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*blasā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*blasǭ|t=torch}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-|t=to shine, be white}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds|blas|t=burning candle, torch, fire}}, {{cog|gmh|blas|t=candle, torch, flame}}. Compare {{cog|nl|bles|t=blaze}}, {{cog|de|Blesse|t=blaze, mark on an animal's forehead}}, {{cog|sv|bläs|t=blaze}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[fire]], especially a fast-burning fire producing a lot of flames and light.
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|III|passage=Long after his cigar burnt bitter, he sat with eyes fixed on the '''blaze'''. When the flames at last began to flicker and subside, his lids fluttered, then drooped; but he had lost all reckoning of time when he opened them again to find Miss Erroll in furs and ball-gown kneeling on the hearth and heaping kindling on the coals,{{nb...}}.}}
# Intense, direct [[light]] accompanied with heat.
#: {{ux|en|to seek shelter from the '''blaze''' of the sun}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=Samson Agonistes|page=13|passage=O dark, dark, dark, amid the '''blaze''' of noon,}}
# The white or lighter-coloured [[marking]]s on a horse's face.
#: {{ux|en|The palomino had a white '''blaze''' on its face.}}
# A [[high-visibility]] orange colour, typically used in warning signs and hunters' clothing.
#: {{color panel|ff6700}}
#: {{syn|en|safety orange|international orange}}
# A bursting out, or active display of any quality.
#: {{syn|en|outburst}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Troilus and Cressida|IV|v|passage=his '''blaze''' of wrath}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|3|page=56|passage=For what is glory but the '''blaze''' of fame?}}
# A spot made on trees by chipping off a piece of the bark, usually as a surveyor's mark.
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The New Purchase: Or, Early Years in the Far West - Page 71| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=rEVBAQAAMAAJ| author=w:Baynard Rush Hall| year=1855| passage=The '''blaze''' is a longitudinal cut on trees at convenient intervals, made by cutting off the bark with an axe or hatchet: three '''blazes''' in a perpendicular line on the same tree indicating a legislative road, the single '''blaze''', a settlement or neighbourhood road.}}
# {{lb|en|poker}} A [[hand]] consisting of five [[face card]]s.

=====Derived terms=====
{{col-auto|en|blazeless|blazer|blazy|emblaze|imblaze|outblaze|reblaze|rekern|upblaze|ablaze|blazar|blazen|blaze of glory|blaze orange|blaze-up}}

