{{trans-bottom}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|blasen}}, from {{der|en|enm|blase|t=torch}}. See above.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be on fire, especially producing bright flames.
#: {{ux|en|The campfire '''blazed''' merrily.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To send forth or reflect a bright light; shine like a [[flame]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1793|author=w:William Wordsworth|title=Descriptive Sketches
|passage=And far and wide the icy summit '''blaze'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage=Pretty soon I struck into a sort of path{{nb...}}. It twisted and turned,{{...}}and opened out into a big clear space like a lawn. And, back of the lawn, was a big, old-fashioned house, with piazzas stretching in front of it, and all '''blazing''' with lights.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|poetic}} To be conspicuous; shine brightly a brilliancy {{q|of talents, deeds, etc.}}.
# {{lb|en|transitive|rare}} To set in a blaze; [[burn]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to [[shine]] forth; [[exhibit]] vividly; be [[resplendent]] with.
# {{lb|en|transitive|only in the past participle}} To mark with a white spot on the face {{q|as a horse}}.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To set a mark on {{q|as a tree, usually by cutting off a piece of its bark}}.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=105|passage=They had, just as we expected they would, cut Stuart's tracks, and had actually slept one night in one of his old camping-places, finding the trees "'''blazed'''" and marked "S.," as were all the trees at intervals along his line of exploration.}}
#* {{RQ:Doyle Lost World|passage=We drew them up, therefore, and concealed them among the bushes, '''blazing''' a tree with our axes, so that we should find them again.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To indicate or mark out {{q|a [[trail]], especially through vegetation}} by a series of blazes.
#: {{ux|en|The guide '''blazed''' his way through the undergrowth.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[mark off]] or [[stake]] a claim to land.
#: {{ux|en|He '''blazed''' his claim on the land.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To set a [[precedent]] for the [[take on|taking-on]] of a challenge; [[lead by example]].
#: {{ux|en|Darwin '''blazed''' a path for the rest of us.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To be furiously angry; to speak or write in a rage.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1929|author=Reginald Charles Barker|title=The Hair-trigger Brand|page=160
|passage="I'll die before I let my grandad pay you that much money!" '''blazed''' the girl.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} To smoke [[marijuana]].
#* {{quote-song|en|title=We Major|artist=Kanye West|feat=Really Doe; Nas|album=Late Registration|year=2005|passage=I take a hit of that chronic, it got me stuck / But really what's amazing is how I keep '''blazing'''}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2015|author={{w|Jme (musician)|Jme}}|artist=Jme|title=Pulse 8|album={{w|Integrity (album)|Integrity>}}|track=1|passage=Fam, I don't '''blaze''' / But I can bill up, so if I get bored / I might mm, bill it / At studio, I'm like mm, kill it}}

