==English==
[[File:Jementah Hill.jpg|thumb|A hill]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kelH-}}
From {{der|en|enm|hil}}, from {{der|en|ang|hyll||hill}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*hulliz||hill}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kl̥Hnís||top, hill, rock}} (compare also {{m+|gem-pro|*halluz||stone, rock}}).

Cognate with {{cog|dum|hille}}, {{m|dum|hulle||hill}}, {{cog|nds|hull||hill}}, {{cog|non|hóll||hill}}, {{cog|la|collis||hill}}, {{cog|lt|kalnas}}, {{cog|sq|kallumë||big pile, tall heap}}, {{cog|ru|холм||hill}}, {{cog|ang|holm||rising land, island}}. More at {{l|en|holm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|hĭl}}, {{IPA|en|/hɪl/}}
** {{IPA|en|[hɪɫ]|a=RP,US}}
** {{IPA|en|[hɪo̯]|[hɪʊ̯]|a=[[w:L-vocalization|l-vocalizing]]:,_,UK,AU,NZ}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hill.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪl|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|he'll}} (in some dialects)

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[elevated]] [[landmass]] smaller than a [[mountain]].
#: {{ux|en|The park is sheltered from the wind by a '''hill''' to the east.}}
#* {{RQ:Ferguson Zollenstein|IV
|passage=So this was my future home, I thought!{{...}}Backed by towering '''hills''', the but faintly discernible purple line of the French boundary off to the southwest, a sky of palest Gobelin flecked with fat, fleecy little clouds, it in truth looked a dear little city; the city of one's dreams.}}
# A [[sloping]] [[road]].
#: {{ux|en|You need to pick up speed to get up the '''hill''' that's coming up.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} A [[heap]] of [[earth]] surrounding a [[plant]].
# {{lb|en|US}} A single cluster or group of plants growing close together, and having the earth heaped up about them.
#: {{ux|en|a '''hill''' of corn or potatoes}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The pitcher’s [[mound]].
# The raised portion of the surface of a [[vinyl record]].
#: {{antonyms|en|dale}}

