==Yemeni Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{unknown|ayn|title=Disputed}} etymology:
* From {{inh|ayn|ar|كُرَة|tr=|t=a ball, a mass, a clump; tuber or bulb}}, in reference to the shape of its {{l|en|corm}}; being the source of {{cog|es|cará|t=taro}} and {{cog|pt|cará|t=yam}}.
* From {{bor|ayn|pt|cará}}:
** Borrowed from a language from the coast of Guinea.
** Derived from {{der|ayn|LL.|-}} or {{der|ayn|VL.|cara}}, borrowed from {{der|ayn|grc|κᾰ́ρᾱ|t=head}}, from {{der|ayn|ine-pro|*ḱerh₂-|*ḱr̥h₂-(e)s-n-}}; also in reference to the shape of its {{l|en|corm}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ayn|كَرِير|tr=kerīr}}

====Noun====
{{head|ayn|noun|head=كُرّ|tr=kurr}}

# [[eddo]] (''[[Colocasia antiquorum]]'', usually accepted as a syn. of {{taxfmt|Colocasia esculenta|species}})

===Etymology 2===
Variant of {{der|ayn|ar|كُرَة|tr=|t=a ball, a mass, a clump}}.

====Noun====
{{head|ayn|noun|head=كُرّ|tr=kurr|head2=كَرّ|tr2=karr|plural|كُرُور|f1tr=kurūr}}

