{{also|Appendix:Variations of "ist"}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|-ist}}, {{m|enm|-iste}}, from {{der|en|fro|-iste}} and {{der|en|la|-ista}}, from {{der|en|grc|-ιστής}}, from {{affix|grc|-ίζω|t1=[[-ize]], [[-ise]]|pos1=verbal suffix|-τής|pos2=agent-noun suffix|nocat=1}}. Equivalent to {{compound|en|-ism|-t}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/-ɪst/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl--ist.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/-əst/|a=weak vowel}}
* {{homophones|en|-est}}

===Suffix===
{{en-suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|cat3=adjective-forming suffixes}}

# Added to words to form nouns denoting:
## a person who studies or practices a particular discipline;
##: [[botanist|botan'''ist''']], ''one who studies plants''
##: [[psychiatrist|psychiatr'''ist''']], ''one who practices psychiatry''
## a person who uses a device of some kind;
##: [[violinist|violin'''ist''']], ''one who plays a violin''
##: [[bicyclist|bicycl'''ist''']], ''one who rides a bicycle''
##: [[autoist|auto'''ist''']], ''one who drives an automobile''
##: [[pianist|pian'''ist''']], ''one who plays the piano''
##: [[vapist|vap'''ist''']], ''one who uses a vaping device''
## one who engages in a particular type of activity;
##: [[adventurist|adventur'''ist''']], ''one who takes risks or goes on adventures''
##: [[artist|art'''ist''']], ''one who makes art''
##: [[bigamist|bigam'''ist''']], ''one who commits bigamy''
##: [[terrorist|terror'''ist''']], ''one who causes terror''
##: [[tourist|tour'''ist''']], ''one who tours''
##: Note, many of these are related to [[-ism]]s: [[adventurism|adventur'''ism''']], [[terrorism|terror'''ism''']], [[tourism|tour'''ism''']]
## one who suffers from a specific condition or syndrome
##: [[autist|aut'''ist''']], [[egoist|ego'''ist''']]
##: Note, these are related to [[-ism]]s: [[autism|aut'''ism''']], [[egoism|ego'''ism''']]
## one who subscribes to a particular [[theological]] [[doctrine]] or religious [[denomination]];
##: [[Buddhist|Buddh'''ist''']], [[baptist|Bapt'''ist''']], [[monotheist|monothe'''ist''']]
##: Note, these are related to [[-ism]]s: [[Buddhism|Buddh'''ism''']], [[monotheism|monothe'''ism''']]
## one who has a certain ideology or set of beliefs;
##: [[Marxist|Marx'''ist''']], [[modernist|modern'''ist''']], [[nihilist|nihil'''ist''']], [[existentialist|existential'''ist''']], [[fascist|fasc'''ist''']], [[pacifist|pacif'''ist''']], [[activist|activ'''ist''']], [[environmentalist|environmental'''ist''']],
##: Note, these are related to [[-ism]]s: [[Marxism|Marx'''ism''']], [[modernism|modern'''ism''']], [[nihilism|nihil'''ism''']], [[existentialism|existential'''ism''']], [[fascism|fasc'''ism''']], [[pacifism|pacif'''ism''']]
## one who owns or manages something;
##: [[capitalist|capital'''ist''']]; [[industrialist|industrial'''ist''']]
##: Note, these are related to [[-ism]]s: [[capitalism|capital'''ism''']]; [[industrialism|industrial'''ism''']]
## a person who holds [[bigot]]ed, [[partial]] views.
##: [[sexist|sex'''ist''']], [[racist|rac'''ist''']]: Note, these are related to [[-ism]]s: [[sexism|sex'''ism''']], [[racism|rac'''ism''']]

