#: {{ux|afb|الاستاذ قرا الدرس وايد بسرعة، ما فهمت منه ولا شي!|The teacher read the lesson so fast [that] I did not understand anything from it!}}

==Hijazi Arabic==

===Etymology===
{{acw-root|ق ر ي}}
From {{inh|acw|ar|قَرَأَ|t=to read}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|acw|/ɡara/}}

===Verb===
{{acw-verb|I|tr=gara|np=يقرا|nptr=yigra}}

# to [[read]]
#: {{syn|acw|قري|tr=giri|قرأ|tr2=garaʼ|q2=classicized form}}
#: {{ux|acw|قريت الكتاب|tr='''garēt''' al-kitāb|I read the book}}

====Usage notes====
Speakers alternate between the past forms for the verb "to read" {{m|acw|قري|tr=giri}} and {{m|acw|قرا|tr=gara}}, while the present and imperative are the same for both forms. the classicized form with the final hamza {{m|acw|قرأ|tr=garaʼ}} is also used.

