{{also|Round|'round}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|around}}
* {{alter|en|ron||Bermuda}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaʊnd/|a=RP,GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-round.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊnd|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|round}}, {{m|enm|rounde}}, from {{der|en|fro-nor|rount|roünt}}, {{m|fro|rund}}, {{der|en|fro|ront}}, {{m|fro|runt}}, {{m|fro|reont}} ( > {{cog|fr|rond}}), from both {{der|en|LL.|retundus}} and the original {{der|en|la|rotundus}}. The noun developed partly from the adjective and partly from the corresponding French noun {{m|fr|rond}}. {{dbt|en|rotund}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# {{lb|en|physical}} {{n-g|Of shape:}}
## [[circular|Circular]] or [[cylindrical]]; having a [[circular]] cross-section in one direction.
##: {{ux|en|We sat at a '''round''' table to make conversation easier.}}
##* {{RQ:Tolkien Fellowship of the Ring|chapter=A Long-Expected Party|passage=The flowers glowed red and golden: snapdragons and sunflowers, and nasturtians{{sic}} trailing all over the turf walls and peeping in at the '''round''' windows.}}
## [[spherical|Spherical]]; shaped like a [[ball]]; having a [[circular]] cross-section in more than one direction.
##: {{ux|en|The ancient Egyptian demonstrated that the Earth is '''round''', not flat.}}
## Loosely or approximately circular.
##: {{ux|en|a '''round''' face, a '''round''' belly}}
##* {{RQ:Christie Autobiography|II|2|passage=If I close my eyes I can see Marie today as I saw her then. '''Round''', rosy face, snub nose, dark hair piled up in a chignon.}}
## Lacking sharp [[angle]]s; having gentle [[curve]]s.
##: {{ux|en|Our child's bed has '''round''' corners for safety.}}
## [[plump|Plump]].
##: {{ux|en|He was tall and thin but his wife was short and '''round'''.}}
# [[complete|Complete]], [[whole]], not lacking.
#: {{ux|en|The baker sold us a '''round''' dozen.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Idylls|page=47|passage='''Round''' was their pace at first, but slackened soon: / A stranger meeting them had surely thought, / They rode so slowly and they look'd so pale, / That each had suffer'd some exceeding wrong.}}
# {{lb|en|of a [[number]]}} Convenient for [[#Verb|round]]ing other numbers to; for example, ending in a [[zero]].
#: {{ux|en|One hundred is a nice '''round''' number.}}
# {{lb|en|phonetics}} [[pronounce|Pronounced]] with the lips drawn together; [[rounded#Adjective|rounded]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1959|year_published=1972|author=w:Anthony Burgess|title=Beds in the East|series=The Malayan Trilogy|page=421|passage="Supposing somebody sees you, with all those flowers too? Supposing somebody writes him a letter? Ooooh!" (a pure '''round''' open Tamil O.)}}
# Outspoken; plain and direct; unreserved; not [[mince words|mincing words]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''round''' answer; a '''round''' oath}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1867|author=w:Matthew Arnold|title=On the Study of Celtic Literature
|passage=the '''round''' assertion}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|act=II|scene=iii|page=261|column=2|passage=''Sir Toby'', I muſt be '''round''' with you.}}
# Finished; polished; not defective or abrupt; said of authors or their writing style.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1622|author={{w|Henry Peacham (born 1578)|Henry Peacham}}|title=The Compleat Gentleman
|passage=In his satires Horace is quick, '''round''', and {{...}} pleasant.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Consistent; fair; just; {{n-g|applied to conduct}}.
#* {{RQ:Bacon Essayes|chapter=Of Truth|passage='''Round''' dealing is the honour of man's nature.}}
# Large in [[magnitude]].
#* {{RQ:Dickens Little Dorrit|passage=I have a good banker in this city, but I would not wish to draw upon the house until the time when I shall draw for a '''round''' sum.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Physiology of Taste: Or, Transcendental Gastronomy|author=Brillat-Savarin|page=108|passage=By raising turkeys the farmers were able the more surely to pay their rents. Young girls often acquired a very sufficient dowry, and towns-folk who wished to eat them had to pay '''round''' prices for them.|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=djEEAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22By%20raising%20turkeys%20the%20farmers%20were%20able%20the%20more%22&pg=PA108#v=onepage&q=round%20prices&f=false|year=1854}}
# {{lb|en|authorship|of a fictional character}} Well-written and well-[[characterization|characterized]]; complex and reminiscent of a real person.
#: {{ant|en|flat}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} [[vaulted|Vaulted]].
# Returning to its starting point.
#: {{ux|en|[[round trip|'''round''' trip]], round '''journey''', round '''walk'''}}

