===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|rounen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rūnian||to whisper, talk low, talk secrets, consipre, talk secretly}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rūnōną||to talk secrets, whisper, decide}}, {{m|gem-pro|*raunijaną||to investigate, examine, prove}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(e)rewə-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(e)rwō-||to trace, find out, look out}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|roun||to converse with in whispers, speak privately}}, {{cog|gml|rūnen||to whisper}}, {{cog|dum|ruinen||to whisper}}, {{cog|de|raunen||to whisper, murmur}}, {{cog|ang|rūn||whisper, secret, mystery}}, {{cog|sv|röna||to meet with, experience}}. More at {{l|en|rune}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|archaic|or|dialectal|Northern England|Scotland}} To [[speak]] in a [[low]] [[tone]]; [[whisper]]; speak [[secret]]ly; take [[counsel]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic|or|dialectal|Northern England|Scotland}} To [[address]] or speak to in a whisper, [[utter]] in a whisper.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King John|3|1|passage= '''rounded''' in the ear }}
#* '''c. 1617''', David Calderwood (quoted as saying to King James VI)
#*: The Bishop of Glasgow '''rounding''' in his ear, "Ye are not a wise man," {{...}} he '''rounded''' likewise to the bishop, and said, "Wherefore brought ye me here?"
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd|I|2|4|IV|text=Tiberius the emperor {{...}} perceiving a fellow '''round''' a dead corse in the ear, would needs know wherefore he did so {{...}}}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|roun}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rūn||whisper, secret, mystery}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rūnō}}, {{m|gem-pro|*raunō||a whisper, secret, secret sign}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(e)rewə-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(e)rwō-||to trace, find out, look out}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|roun}}, {{m|sco|round||a whisper, secret story}}, {{cog|de|raunen||to whisper, say secretly}}, {{cog|sv|rön||findings, observations, experience}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|archaic|or|dialectal|Northern England|Scotland}} A [[whisper]]; [[whispering]].
# {{lb|en|archaic|or|dialectal|Northern England|Scotland}} [[discourse|Discourse]]; [[song]].

