===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[remove]] dust from.
#: {{ux|en|The cleaning lady needs a stool to '''dust''' the cupboard.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=12|passage=There were many wooden chairs for the bulk of his visitors, and two wicker armchairs with red cloth cushions for superior people. From the packing-cases had emerged some Indian clubs,{{nb...}}, and all these articles{{nb...}} made a scattered and untidy decoration that Mrs. Clough assiduously '''dusted''' and greatly cherished.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To remove dust; to clean by removing dust.
#: {{ux|en|'''Dusting''' always makes me cough.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To make [[dusty]], to [[soil]] with dust.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|or|reflexive}} Of a bird, to [[cover]] itself in sand or dry, dusty earth.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[spray]] or [[cover]] (something) with fine powder or liquid, to [[sprinkle]].
#: {{ux|en|The mother '''dusted''' her baby’s bum with talcum powder.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To sprinkle (a substance) in the form of dust.
# {{lb|en|intransitive|chiefly|US|_|slang}} To [[leave]] [[quickly]]; to [[rush]] off.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1939|author=w:Raymond Chandler|title=w:The Big Sleep|page=75|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2011
|passage=He added in a casual tone: ‘The girl can '''dust'''. I’d like to talk to you a little, soldier.’}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[drink up]] [[quickly]]; to [[toss off]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To reduce to a fine powder; to [[pulverize]], to [[levigate]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1667|author=w:Thomas Sprat|title=History of the Royal Society of London|passage=good Powder differs from bad {{...}}in having more Peter and less Coal; and lastly, in the well '''dusting''' of it}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|now|colloquial|or|dialectal}} To [[strike]], [[beat]], [[thrash]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|chiefly|US|_|slang}} To [[defeat]] [[badly]], to thrash.
# {{lb|en|transitive|chiefly|US|_|slang}} To [[kill]].
#* {{quote-av|en|title=w:The Terminator|year=1984|actor=w:Michael Biehn|role=Kyle Reese|location=Los Angeles, Calif.|publisher=w:Orion Pictures; distributed by [[w:MGM Home Entertainment|MGM Home Entertainment]]|year_published=1984|passage=<span style="font-variant:small-caps">Kyle Reese:</span> You have to be careful because the [Hunter-Killer robots] use infrared. They’re not too bright. John taught us ways to '''dust''' them.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|baseball}} To [[deliberately]] [[pitch]] a ball [[close]] to (a [[batter]]); to [[brush back]].
# {{lb|en|cryptocurrency}} To attempt to [[identify]] the [[owner]] of (a [[cryptocurrency]] [[wallet]]) by sending tiny amounts of cryptocurrency.

