==Romanian==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|ro|ine-pro|*gʰerdʰ-|t=to enclose, to encircle}}; possibly a {{der|ro|qfa-sub}} word from a {{der|ro|xdc|*garda}}, akin to Albanian {{m|sq|gardh}} (or borrowed from it), or more likely an early borrowing from {{der|ro|sla-pro|*gȏrdъ}}, perhaps predating the metathesis occurring in Slavic languages (however this is uncertain as other related terms such as {{m|ro|grădină}}, {{m|ro|ogradă}}, {{m|ro|îngrădi}} had already undergone it when borrowed from Slavic). Other suggested possibilities include a link to {{der|ro|gem-pro|*gardaz}}. <ref>{{R:DEX}}</ref>

Other Indo-European cognates include {{cog|la|hortus}}, {{cog|en|garden}}, {{m|en|yard}}, {{m|en|gird}}, {{cog|sa|गृह|sc=Deva||house, home}}, {{cog|cu|градъ}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐌰𐍂𐌳𐍃}}, {{cog|de|Garten}}, {{cog|da|gård}}, {{cog|sv|gård}} and {{cog|no|gård}} or {{m|no|gard}}; {{m|no|garde}}, {{m|no|gjerde}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ro|[ɡard]}}
* {{audio|ro|LL-Q7913 (ron)-Filosoful-gard.wav}}

===Noun===
{{ro-noun|n|garduri}}

# [[fence]]

====Declension====
{{ro-noun-n-uri}}

