==Persian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|fa|غر||misspelling}}

===Etymology===
{{w|Francis Joseph Steingass}} speculates that it is from {{der|fa|ar|قِرْد|t=monkey, ape}}. His nineteenth-century dictionary gives "monkey" as the only noun definition while marking {{m|fa||قر دادن|tr=qer dâdan}} as a "modern colloquial" verb for "to coquette about, sway the body as in a dance",<ref>{{R:fa:Steingass|قر}}</ref> so perhaps the verb emerged first with a literal meaning of "to give the monkey", and the current meaning of the noun is a backformation from the verb.

{{w|Davud Monshizadeh|Monši-Zâde}} instead suspects a connection with {{m|fa|گرد|tr=gerd|t=circular}}, and also a play on a form of {{m|fa|غربال|tr=ğarbâl|t=searce}} due to the fashion a sieve is worked.<ref>{{R:fa:Monchi-Zadeh:1990|page=72 Nr. 215}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
[[File:Rachel Brice 3 DSC 0115.JPG|thumb]]
{{fa-IPA|qir}}

===Noun===
{{fa-noun|tr=qer|pl=قرها}}

# {{lb|fa|informal}} [[twerk]], [[twerk]]ing; [[gyrate|gyrating]] one's [[hip]]s (used for both men and women)
# {{lb|fa|figurative|informal}} [[flirting]]; [[coquetry]]

====Usage notes====
* {{m|fa||قر|tr=qer}}, rolling the hips, is the most common dance move in Iran and is not as sexualized as it is in the West.

====Derived terms====
