# {{lb|fa|obsolete}} [[nomad]]
#* '''1224-1228''', {{w|Yaqut al-Hamawi}}, ''Mu’jam ul-Buldān'' (Persian translation)
#*: {{quote|fa|گروهی از '''اکراد''' در کوههای میان اصفهان و خوزستان و این نواحی بدیشان شناخته آید و بلاد لر خوانند و هم لرستان و لور گویند.|tr=goruh-i az '''akrâd''' dar kuh-hâ-ye muyân-e esfehân o xuzestân, o in navâhi bedišân šenâxte âyad o balad lor xânand o ham lorestân o lur guyand.|t=[ {{w|Lurs}} are ] a group of '''nomads''' who live in the mountains between {{w|Isfahan}} and {{w|Khuzestan}} and these territories are known to be theirs and they are called the {{w|Lur people}} and they are also called “Luristan” and “Lur”.}}

===Etymology 2===
Apparently identical to the above word for a “herder”.  More at [[w:Kurds#Name|Kurds]].

