====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|dated|uncommon}} To make [[happy]] or [[cheerful]]. {{defdate|since at least the 1920s}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1922|author=Thomas Hardy|title=Late lyrics and earlier: with many other verses|page=119
|passage=''SAYING GOOD-BYE'' (song)<br>WE are always saying / "Good-bye, good-bye! / In work, in playing, / In gloom, in '''gaying''' {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1952|title=American Childhood|volume=38|page=2
|passage='''''Gaying''' Things Up For Christmas.'' JESSIE TODD, Laboratory School, University of Chicago.<br>EVERY schoolroom in America is '''gayed''' up for Christmas.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|uncommon}} To cause (something, e.g. [[AIDS]]) to be associated with homosexual people. {{defdate|popularized in the 1990s}}

