* [[re-gay]]

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|?}}

# {{lb|en|Scotland|Northern England}} [[considerably|Considerably]], [[very]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1833|author=John Sim Sands|title=Poems on Various Subjects|page=115
|passage=And, tho' his guts ware lank and toom, / They're twice as big's this '''gay''' big room.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1869|author=Joseph Carr|title=Sketches of village life, by “Eavesdropper”|page=60
|passage=Now, to end my story, if o' t' village beauties wad git t' religion that good auld parson Jenkins recommends, it wad '''gay''' sharply mak' t' dirty women clean, {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|author=Dickinson|title=Cumbriana; Or, Fragments of Cumbrian Life|page=8
|passage={{...}} an' be t' Silver Cwove, an' than throo t' Pillar, an' a '''gay''' rough bit o' grund it is!}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1886|author=Thomas Farrall|title=Betty Wilson's Cummerland Teals|section=42
|passage=When a fellah com' in 'at was '''gay''' free wid spendin.}}
#* '''1892-3''', Mrs. Humphry Ward, ''The History of David Grieve'', volume I, page 19:
#*: She'll mak naw moor mischeef neets—she's '''gay''' quiet now!

