==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|fi|nominal}}
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*-i|id=nominal}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*-j}} (specifically its fusion with the stem vowel). Originally allomorphic with {{m|fi|-o}} (< {{m|urj-fin-pro|*-oi}}, in which the *''-i-'' caused labialization of the preceding *''a'').

====Suffix====
{{head|fi|suffix}}

# {{n-g|A non-productive nominal suffix deriving nouns from nominal stems.}}
#: {{sufex|fi|ukko|t1=(old) man|ukki|t2=grandfather}}
# {{n-g|Forms nouns from some verbs.}}
# {{lb|fi|archaic}} {{n-g|Used to mark the first part of a [[compound word]].}}
#: {{sufex|fi|lehmä|t1=cow|lehmi-}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|fi|id=nominal}}

====See also====
* {{l|fi|-kki}}
* {{l|fi|-ri}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|fi|adverbial}}
Conflated:
* from {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*-i|id=adverbial}} (from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*-j|pos=lative suffix}})
* from {{m|urj-fin-pro|*-ik}} (from earlier {{m|urj-pro||*-jek}}, probably a combination of the aforementioned and {{der|fi|urj-pro|*-k|pos=lative suffix}}).

====Suffix====
{{head|fi|suffix}}

# {{n-g|Forms [[Appendix:Finnish adverbial cases#Lative|lative]] adverbs.}}
#: {{sufex|fi|aueta|t1=to open|auki|t2=open}}
#: {{sufex|fi|ylä-|t1=upper, high|yli|t2=over}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|fi|id=adverbial}}

====See also====
* {{l|fi|-lti}}
* {{l|fi|-sti}}
* {{l|fi|-ti}}

