==Greenlandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{kl-IPA}}

===Suffix===
{{kl-suffix|v-v|trunc}}

# {{ngd|Intransitivizes.}}

====Usage notes====
Sometimes additive after ''r'' stems.

Many verbs are intransitivized simply by changing the inflectional ending, without changing the stem; of those that do use an affix, it is not predictable which of ''-i'', {{m|kl|-nnig}}, {{m|kl|-ller}} and {{m|kl|-si}} are used. Also, verbs may use more than one of these, with similarly unpredictable results (e.g. {{m|kl|errorsivoq||wash clothes}} vs. {{m|kl|erruivoq||do dishes}}, both from {{m|kl|errorpaa}}). If a verb uses one of these affixes, the unaffixed intransitive form may be passive, reciprocal or reflexive w.r.t. the transitive form.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|kl|-nnig}}, {{l|kl|-ller}}, {{l|kl|-si}}

===References===
* {{R:GG|p=pp. 67-68}}
* {{R:VGG|page=106-107}}

==Hungarian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hu-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|hu|i|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Adjective-forming suffix.

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|adjective}} {{lb|hu|adjective-forming suffix}} Added to [[proper noun]]s, certain [[common noun]]s and [[postposition]]s to form [[adjective]]s:
## {{senseid|hu|toponym}} names of places ([[toponym]]s)
##: {{afex|hu|Amerika|t1=America|amerika'''i'''|t2=American}}
## {{senseid|hu|eponym}} names of people ([[anthroponym]]s, thus [[eponym]]s)
##: {{afex|hu|Freud|t1=Freud|freud'''i'''|t2=Freudian}}
## certain common nouns
##: {{afex|hu|város|t1=city|város'''i'''|t2=urban}}
##: {{afex|hu|kémia|t1=chemistry|kémia'''i'''|t2=chemical}}
## postpositions (as part of the phrase in which they occur)
##: {{afex|hu|[[az]] [[ablak]] '''[[alatt]]'''|t1='''under''' the window|az ablak [[alatt'''i''']] [[szék]]|t2=the chair under the window}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Final {{m|hu||-o}} and {{m|hu||-ö}} (which only occur in non-Hungarian words) change to {{m|hu||-ó}} and {{m|hu||-ő}}.<ref>{{R:hu:AkH2015|section=216}}</ref>
*: {{m|hu|Oslo}} → {{m|hu|osl'''ó'''i|t=Oslovian}}
*: {{m|hu|Malmö}} → {{m|hu|malm'''ő'''i|t=Malmö-based}}
*: {{m|hu||Victor Hugo}} → {{m|hu|Victor Hug'''ó'''-i|t=Hugolian, Hugonian, Hugoesque}}
* If the suffix {{m|hu||-i}} were to follow word-final {{m|hu||-i}}, only one is retained (so one needs to know the original form).<ref>{{R:hu:AkH2015|section=173}}</ref><ref>{{R:hu:AkH2015|section=215}}</ref>
*: {{m|hu|Helsinki}} → {{m|hu|helsink'''i'''|t=Helsinkian}}
*: {{m|hu|Zamárdi|pos=a town in Somogy County, Hungary}} → {{m|hu|zamárd'''i'''|t=from Zamárdi|pos=in theory, it could also derive from a non-existent *Zamárd}}
* The other word-final short vowels ({{m|hu||a, e, u, ü}}) remain unchanged (just like long ones and consonants).
*: {{m|hu|Prága|t=Prague}} → {{m|hu|prág'''a'''i|t=Praguian}}
*: {{m|hu|Goethe}} → {{m|hu|goeth'''e'''i|t=Goethean}}
*: {{m|hu|Peru}} → {{m|hu|per'''u'''i|t=Peruvian}}
*: {{m|hu|Öskü|pos=a village in Veszprém County, Hungary}} → {{m|hu|ösk'''ü'''i|t=from Öskü}}
:* The fact that word-final {{m|hu||a}} and {{m|hu||e}} remain short before the '''adjective-forming''' {{m|hu||-i}} often becomes distinctive against the multiple-possession possessives of words that end in {{m|hu||a}} and {{m|hu||e}}, e.g. {{m|hu|form'''a'''i|t=formal}} and {{m|hu|form'''á'''i|t=his/her/its forms}} or {{m|hu|megy'''e'''i|t=county-level}} and {{m|hu|megy'''é'''i|t=his/her/its counties}}.
* [[Appendix:Hungarian fleeting-vowel words|Names with a fleeting vowel]]: {{m|hu|Eger}} → {{m|hu|egri}}, as well as names ending in {{m|hu|halom|-halom}}, e.g. {{m|hu|Szigethalom}} → {{m|hu|szigethalmi}}.
* Names ending in {{m|hu|falu|-falu}} (e.g. {{m|hu|Leányfalu}}) may be suffixed in three ways: The official way is retaining the full form, e.g. {{m|hu||leányfalui}}; in the vernacular, {{m|hu||leányfalusi}} may be heard; and forms like {{m|hu||leányfalvi}} are increasingly rare.<ref name="Nyelvmuv">{{R:GretsyKemeny 2005}}</ref>
* Names ending in a possessive suffix such as {{m|hu|falva|-falva}}, {{m|hu|halma|-halma}}, {{m|hu|háza|-háza}}, {{m|hu|földje|-földe}} (outside elements of proper names: {{m|hu||földje}}), {{m|hu|telke|-telke}}: Official usage increasingly prefers retaining the whole name (e.g. {{m|hu||nyíregyházai}} from {{m|hu|Nyíregyháza}}), though in common parlance the word-final {{m|hu||a}} and {{m|hu||e}} tend to be dropped (e.g. {{m|hu||nyíregyházi}}). The drawback of the latter is that the original form cannot be established (as {{m|hu||nyíregyházi}} could theoretically derive from a non-existent {{m|hu||*Nyíregyház}}).<ref name="Nyelvmuv"/>
* For non–proper noun elements with a possessive suffix, native speakers often have a hard time trying to add this suffix, e.g. whether the last element of {{m|hu|útja|(Erzsébet királyné) útja}} and {{m|hu|tere|(Örs vezér) tere}} should become {{m|hu|úti}} and {{m|hu|téri}} (losing the mark of the possessive) or {{m|hu|útjai}} and {{m|hu|terei}} (having an ambiguous sense, primarily used for multiple possessions). As a rule of thumb, the former solution may be preferable.<ref name="Nyelvmuv"/>

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|hu|-beli}} <!-- such as "egyesült államokbeli", sometimes this "-beli" is the only option after geographical names -->

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|hu|pos=adjective}}
{{suffixsee|hu}}

====Further reading====
* [http://www.nytud.hu/kenesei/publ/MultifunctAfxHung2013.pdf On a multifunctional derivational affix: Its use in relational adjectives or nominal modification, and phrasal affixation in Hungarian] by István Kenesei (see the Conclusion on page 19)

===Etymology 2===
Possessive plural.

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|possessive}} {{n-g|possessive suffix for multiple possessions}}
## {{lb|hu|with no noun for possessor}} [[his]], [[her]], [[its]] ……[[-s#English: regular plural|-s]] {{gloss|third-person singular; the pronoun {{m|hu|ő||s/he}} being optional for emphasis}}
##: {{m|hu|kapu||gate}} → {{m|hu|kapui|a kapu'''i'''|'''his'''/'''her'''/'''its''' gate'''s'''}}, {{m|hu|kapui|az ő kapu'''i'''|'''his/her''' gate'''s'''}}
##: {{m|hu|érme||coin}} → {{m|hu|érméi|az érmé'''i'''|'''his'''/'''her'''/'''its''' coin'''s'''}}, {{m|hu|érméi|az ő érmé'''i'''|'''his/her''' coin'''s'''}}
## {{lb|hu|with no noun for possessor|formal|nocat=y}} [[your]] ……[[-s#English: regular plural|-s]] {{gloss|second-person singular, grammatically resembling the third person sg.}}<!-- this cannot have a plural sense unless "önök" or "maguk" is supplied-->
##: {{m|hu|kapu||gate}} → {{m|hu|kapui|a kapu'''i'''|'''your''' [formal] gate'''s'''}}, {{m|hu|kapui|az ön kapu'''i''', a maga kapu'''i'''|'''your''' [formal] gate'''s'''}}
## {{construed with|hu||a noun}} {{n-g|or certain pronouns as the possessor:}} ……[[-'s#English: possessive|’s]] ……[[-s#English: regular plural|-s]], ……[[-s#English: regular plural|-s]] [[of#English: possession|of]] …… {{gloss|third-person sg. or pl., depending on the noun or pronoun}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[kapui|az ember(nek a) kapu'''i''']]|the person'''’s''' gate'''s'''}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[érméi|a gyerek(nek az) érmé'''i''']]|the child'''’s''' coin'''s'''}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[kapui|az emberek(nek a) kapu'''i''']]|the people'''’s''' gate'''s'''}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[érméi|a gyerekek(nek az) érmé'''i''']]|the children'''’s''' coin'''s'''}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[kapui|az önök kapu'''i''', a maguk kapu'''i''']]|'''your''' (plural, formal) gate'''s'''}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[kapui|azok(nak a) kapu'''i''']]|the gate'''s of''' those}}
##: {{uxi|hu|[[érméi|ki(k)nek az érmé'''i'''?]]|who'''se''' coin'''s'''?}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{U:hu:pos-i}}

===Etymology 3===
Personal suffix.

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|personal}} {{lb|hu|personal suffix}} {{ngd|Forms the [[Appendix:Glossary#definite|definite]] [[Appendix:Glossary#third person|third-person]] singular present tense of verbs (indicative mood).}}
#: {{afex|hu|kér|t1=to request|kér'''i'''|t2='''he/she''' ask'''s''' him/her or for that thing, '''he/she is''' ask'''ing''' him/her or for that thing}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{q|personal suffix}} See harmonic variants in the table below.
{{U:hu:conj-pres-def}}

===Etymology 4===
Diminutive suffix.

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|diminutive}} {{lb|hu|diminutive suffix}} {{ngd|Added to nouns or their [[clipping|clipped]] form; mostly used by the younger generation or in informal conversations.}}
#: {{m|hu|fagylalt}} → {{m|hu|fagy'''i'''|t=ice cream}}

===Etymology 5===
See {{m|hu|-e}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|hu|suffix}}

# {{senseid|hu|possessive singular}} {{lb|hu|dialectal|except for some set forms}} {{alternative form of|hu|-e|id=possessive|pos=third-person singular single-possession possessive suffix}}
#: {{uxi|hu|[[se szeri, se száma|se szer'''i''', se száma]]|(instead of {{m|hu|szere|szer'''e'''}})}}<ref name="nyelvmuvelo">''birtokos személyjelek alaki változatai'' [“form variants of possessive suffixes”] in {{R:GretsyKemeny 2005}}</ref>
# {{lb|hu|dialectal|except for some set forms}} {{alternative form of|hu|-é|id=combining|pos=combining form of the above}}
#: {{uxi|hu|[[íziben|íz'''i'''ben]]&emsp;[[a mindenit|a minden'''i'''t]]&emsp;[[töviről hegyire|töv'''i'''ről hegy'''i'''re]]&emsp;[[jószerivel|jószer'''i'''vel]]&emsp;[[frissiben|friss'''i'''ben]]&emsp;[[dögivel|dög'''i'''vel]]&emsp;[[bőviben|bőv'''i'''ben]]&emsp;[[sebtiben|sebt'''i'''ben]]&emsp;[[felibe|fel'''i'''be]]/[[fölibe|föl'''i'''be]]&emsp;[[köribe|kör'''i'''be]]&emsp;[[közibe|köz'''i'''be]]|<small>(instead of standard {{m|hu|íze|íz'''é'''ben}}, {{m|hu|mindene|a minden'''é'''t}}, {{m|hu|[[töve|töv'''é'''ről]] [[hegye|hegy'''é'''re]]}}, {{m|hu|jószerével|jószer'''é'''vel}}, {{m|hu|friss|friss'''é'''ben}} {{q|uncommon}}, {{m|hu|dög|dög'''é'''vel}} {{q|uncommon}}, {{m|hu|bővében|bőv'''é'''ben}}, {{m|hu|sebtében|sebt'''é'''ben}}, {{m|hu|[[felébe|fel'''é'''be]]/[[fölé|föl'''é'''be]]}}, {{m|hu|[[köré|kör'''é'''be/​kör'''é'''je]]}}, {{m|hu|[[közé|köz'''é'''be/​közéje/​közé]]}})</small>}}<ref name="nyelvmuvelo"/>

