** {{IPA|ms|[-i]|a=after a consonant}}
** {{IPA|ms|[-ʔi]|a=etymology 1; after a vowel}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ms|poz-pro|*-i|pos=local transitive suffix}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|ms|suffix|Jawi spelling|-ي|active|meng- -i|3rd person passive|di- -i}}

# {{n-g|Gives a [[causitive]] meaning or a meaning of causing something to form imperative transitive verbs.}}
#: {{suffixusex|ms|hamba|hambai|t1=slave|t2=enslave}}
#: {{suffixusex|ms|baik|baiki|t1=good|t2=to make something good; to fix}}
# {{n-g|Gives a [[locative]] meaning, that is, of stating a locational element to imperative verbs}}.
#: {{suffixusex|ms|tumpah|tumpahi|t1=to fall out|t2=fall onto}}
#: {{suffixusex|ms|dekat|dekati|t1=close, near|t2=get closer or nearer to; to approach}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This suffix is never used after verbs ending in final ''-i'' for euphonic reasons and to avoid near-homophony with bare forms (''-∅''). Thus, {{m|ms|beli|bel'''i'''|to buy}} does not derive into ''*belii''.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{q|first sense|generally before an inanimate object, but not always}} {{l|ms|-kan}}

