==Old High German==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|goh|gmw-pro|*-ī}}, from {{inh|goh|gem-pro|*-į̄}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|goh|suffix|head=-ī}}

# {{non-gloss definition|[[productive]] suffix used to form abstract nouns from adjectives}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|manag|t1=many|menigī}}, {{m|goh|managī|t=crowd, amount}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|tiuf|t1=deep|tiufī|t2=depth}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|finstar|t1=dark|finstrī}}, {{m|goh|finstarī|t=darkness}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|hōh|t1=high|hōhī|t2=height}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|lang|t1=long|lengī|t2=length}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|breit|t1=broad|breitī|t2=breadth}}

=====Declension=====
{{goh-decl-noun-in-f|-}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|goh}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|gmh|-e}}
** {{desc|de|-e}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|goh|gem-pro|*-īniz}}. Cognate to {{cog|got|-𐌴𐌹𐌽𐍃}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|goh|suffix|head=-ī}}

# {{non-gloss definition|non-[[productive]] suffix used to form action nouns from weak verbs}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|toufen|t1=to baptise|toufī|t2=baptism}}
#: {{suffixusex|goh|wellen|t1=to choose|welī|t2=choice}}

=====Usage notes=====
In Old High German, this suffix is neither frequent nor productive. Many weak verbs have action nouns with {{m|goh|-unga}} instead.

=====Declension=====
Female n-declension

