==Romanian==

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ro|la|-us|-ī|second-declension plural ending}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ro|/ʲ/|/j/|/i/}}

====Suffix====
{{head|ro|suffix}}

# {{senseid|ro|plural}} {{ngd|Used to form [[plurals]]}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This form of the plural is indefinite, and used for masculine nouns in the nominative/accusative and genitive/dative cases, regardless of singular form. The suffix may cause phonetic changes or vowel deletion (or both):
* {{suffixusex|ro|lup|lupi}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|tată|tați}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|fiu|fii}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|frate|frați}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ro|head=-i (plural)}}

===Etymology 2===
{{inh+|ro|la|illī}}, nominative masculine plural of {{m|la|ille}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ro|/j/|/i/}}

====Suffix====
{{head|ro|suffix|g=m}}

# {{senseid|ro|article}} {{q|definite article}} [[the]] {{lb|ro|masculine plural, [[nominative]] and [[accusative]]}}

=====Usage notes=====
This form of the definite article is used for masculine plural nouns in the nominative and accusative cases (as attached to the indefinite plural, which always ends in a vowel):
* {{suffixusex|ro|lupi|lupii}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|tați|tații}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|fii|fiii}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|frați|frații}}
* {{suffixusex|ro|copii|copiii}}

The suffix is also used with masculine and neuter singular plural adjectives in the nominative and accusative cases to make the articulated definite form, often for emphasis, and it is used before the noun it modifies.

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ro|head=-i (article)}}

=====Related terms=====
{{top2}}
* {{l|ro|-l}} {{q|masculine/neuter singular nominative and accusative}}
* {{l|ro|-a}} {{qualifier|feminine singular nominative and accusative}}
* {{l|ro|-le}} {{qualifier|feminine plural nominative and accusative}}
* {{l|ro|-lui}} {{q|masculine/neuter singular genitive and dative}}
* {{l|ro|-ei}} {{qualifier|feminine singular genitive and dative}}
* {{l|ro|-lor}} {{qualifier|plural genitive and dative}}
{{bottom}}

===Etymology 3===
{{inh+|ro|la||-īre}}, the ending of the present active infinitive form of [[Appendix:Latin fourth conjugation|fourth conjugation]] verbs. Cognate with {{cog|es,fr|-ir}}, {{cog|it|-ire}}, etc.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ro|/i/}}

====Suffix====
{{head|ro|suffix}}

# {{senseid|ro|infinitive}} {{non-gloss definition|A suffix forming infinitives of many verbs.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Most verbs with infinitives in {{m|ro||-i}} are marked by the once-inchoative infix {{m|ro||-esc-}} in many parts of their conjugation, as well as in various derived words; two such verbs are {{m|ro|vorbi|t=to say}} and {{m|ro|iubi|t=to love}}.
* A sizable group of verbs have infinitives in {{m|ro||-i}} but do not use the infix {{m|ro||-esc-}}, and are otherwise fairly regular; these include, among others, the common verb {{m|ro|dormi|t=sleep}}, {{m|ro|simți|t=feel}}, {{m|ro|auzi|t=hear}}.
* There is a variant form, {{m|ro||-î}}, derived from the same Latin source.

=====Conjugation=====
{{ro-conj-i}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ro|head=-i (infinitive)}}

====See also====
* {{l|ro|-ea}}
* {{l|ro|-î}}
* {{l|ro|-e}}
* {{l|ro|-a}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{m|ro|e|t=is}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|ro|suffix}}

# {{senseid|ro|is}} [[is]]

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ro|head=-i (is)}}

==Skolt Sami==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|sms|smi-pro|*-jē}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|sms|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes}}

# {{senseid|sms|agent noun}}{{n-g|Forms agent nouns from verbs.}}

=====Inflection=====
{{rfinfl|sms|noun}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|sms|id=agent noun}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|sms|smi-pro|*-jëj}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|sms|suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes}}

# {{senseid|sms|abundance}}{{n-g|Forms adjectives indicating an abundance of something.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Phonologically, the suffix is actually the consonant ''j'', and so it forms a diphthong with the final vowel of the base word's stem rather than replacing that vowel.

=====Inflection=====
{{rfinfl|sms|adjective}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|sms|id=abundance}}

==Swahili==

===Etymology 1===

====Suffix====
{{head|sw|suffix}}

# {{lb|sw|without TAM infix}} {{n-g|general negative marker}}
#: {{uxi|sw|siju'''i'''|I '''don't''' know}}
#* {{RQ:Abdallah bin Ali Inkishafi|line=11|passage=مُيُ وَاغُ نِنِ هُزُدُكَانِ ، لِكُغُرِيِلُ هِيْلَ نِنْنِ ،|tr=Moyo wangu nini huzundukan'''i''', likughuriyelo hela ni-n'ni?|translation=Soul, why '''not''' awake? Hi! what is it that cheats you?|trans_from=allen}}

=====Usage notes=====
Borrowed verbs with indicative form not ending in {{m|sw|-a}} do not take this suffix.

====See also====
{{table:sw-TAM}}

===Etymology 2===

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|sw|-zi|q1=after a vowel}}

====Suffix====
{{head|sw|suffix}}

# {{lb|sw|often with spirantization of the preceding consonant}} {{n-g|suffix used in nominal forms of verbs, in conjunction with a noun class prefix}}
#: {{suffixusex|sw|penda|alt1=-penda|t1=to love|mpenzi|t2=lover}}
#: {{suffixusex|sw|andika|alt1=-andika|t1=to write|maandishi|t2=writing, script}}

====See also====
{{suffixsee|sw}}

