==Northern Kurdish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|kmr|ira-pro|-}}, ultimately from {{der|kmr|ine-pro|*-ikos}}; cognates include {{cog|sa|-कस}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*-ъkъ}}, {{cog|la|-icus}}, {{cog|ang|-iġ}}, {{cog|en|-y}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|kmr|-yî||appended to vowel-final words}}

====Suffix====
{{head|kmr|suffix|cat2=adjective-forming suffixes|Arabic spelling|f1sc=ku-Arab|ـی}}

# {{n-g|Added to nouns and adjectives to form adjectives meaning “having the quality of”}}: [[-y]], [[-ish]], [[-like]]
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|av|t1=water|avî|t2=watery, liquid}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|bajar|t1=city|bajarî|t2=urban}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|zîv|t1=silver|zîvî|t2=silvery, argentous}}
# {{n-g|Added to [[placename]]s (or roots thereof) or [[ethnonym]]s to form adjectives meaning “of or pertaining to”}}: [[-ian]], [[-ese]], [[-ic]], [[-ish]]
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|kurd|t1=Kurd|kurdî|t2=Kurdish}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|ereb|t1=Arab|erebî|t2=Arabic}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|Çîn|t1=China|çînî|t2=Chinese}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|Yewnanistan|alt1=Yewnan(istan)|t1=Greece|yewnanî|t2=Greek}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|kmr|-î (adjectival)}}
{{suffixsee|kmr|-yî (adjectival)}}
{{suffixsee|kmr|-î (belonging)}}
{{suffixsee|kmr|-yî (belonging)}}

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{cog|fa|ـی|tr=-i}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|kmr|suffix|cat2=noun-forming suffixes|Arabic spelling|f1sc=ku-Arab|ـی}}

# {{n-g|Used to derive abstract nouns from adjectives}}: [[-ness]], [[-ity]], [[-hood]]
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|qenc|t1=good|qencî|t2=goodness}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|xirab|t1=bad|xirabî|t2=badness, evil}}
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|sor|t1=red|sorî|t2=redness, ruddiness}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|kmr|-î (abstract noun)}}

====See also====
{{col3|kmr|-ahî|-ayî|-tî}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{der|kmr|ine-pro|*h₁ésti}}, athematic root present of the root {{m|ine-pro|*h₁es-||to be}}.

====Suffix====
{{head|kmr|suffix|Arabic spelling|f1sc=ku-Arab|ـی}}

# {{n-g|Used for conjugation of the second person singular (tu)}}:
#: {{ux|kmr|tu [[gotin|dibêjî]]|inline=1|you speak}}
#: {{ux|kmr|tu [[hatin|hatî]]|inline=1|you came}}

===Etymology 4===

====Suffix====
{{head|kmr|suffix|Arabic spelling|f1sc=ku-Arab|ـی}}

# {{n-g|Added to placenames to make a gendered noun of origin or nationality}}:
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|gund|t1=village|gundî|t2=villager}}
# [[his]] or [[her]]:
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|ser|t1=head|serî|t2=his head, her head}}, same as ''"serê wê/wî"''
#: {{suffixusex|kmr|dest|t1=hand|destî|t2=his hand, her hand}}, same as ''"destê wê/wî"''
# {{lb|kmr|oral|nonstandard}} {{n-g|Used for present tense conjugation of the third person singular}}:
#: {{ux|kmr|ew dibêjî|inline=1|he speaks}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|kmr|-î}}

==Romanian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ro|la|-īre}}, the ending of the present active infinitive form of [[Appendix:Latin fourth conjugation|fourth conjugation]] verbs. Cognate with {{cog|es|ir}} and {{cog|fr|-ir}}, {{cog|it|-ire}}, etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ro|/ɨ/}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ro|suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|A suffix forming infinitives of many verbs.}}

====Usage notes====
* Most verbs with infinitives in ''-î'' are marked by the once-inchoative infix {{m|ro|-esc-|-ăsc-}} in many parts of their conjugation, as well as in various derived words; two such verbs are {{m|ro|urî|a urî|to hate}} and {{m|ro|hotărî|a hotărî|to decide}}.
* A sizable group of verbs have infinitives in ''-î'' but do not use the infix {{m|ro|-ăsc-}}, and are otherwise fairly regular; these include, among others, the common verb {{m|ro|coborî|a coborî|to descend}}.
* There is a variant form, {{m|ro|-i}}, derived from the same Latin source.

====Conjugation====
{{ro-conj-î}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ro}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ro|-ea}}
* {{l|ro|-i}}
* {{l|ro|-e}}
* {{l|ro|-a}}

====See also====
* {{l|ro|-re}}

==Walloon==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|wa|/iː/}}

===Suffix===
{{head|wa|suffix}}

# {{non-gloss definition|Indicates a person who does (as a profession) the action described by the root word. Roughly equivalent to English ''[[-er]]''.}}
# {{n-g|A verb ending for [[infinitives]].}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|wa}}
