==Hindi==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
All forms are ultimately from {{inh|hi|sa|-इक}}:
* Direct singular {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इउ|tr=-iu|nocap=1}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau|-𑀇𑀕𑁄}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इकः}}
* Oblique singular {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इहे|tr=-ihĕ/-ihi|nocap=1|pos=genitive singular}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau|-𑀇𑀕𑀲𑁆𑀲}} or {{m|pra-sau|-𑀇𑀅𑀲𑁆𑀲}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इकस्य}}
* Vocative singular {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इअ|tr=-ia|nocap=1}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau|-𑀇𑀕}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इक}}
* Direct plural {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इअ|tr=-ia|nocap=1}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau|-𑀇𑀕𑀸}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इकाः}}
See {{m|hi|-इयों}} and {{m|hi|-इयो}} for the etymologies of those endings specifically. <ref>{{R:hi:Oberlies|7}}</ref>

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|g=m|ur=ـی}}

# {{n-g|suffix for some [[masculine]] [[noun]]s}}

=====Declension=====
{{hi-ndecl|<M>}}

===Etymology 2===
All forms are ultimately from {{inh|hi|sa|-इका}}. Specifically,
* Direct singular {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इअ|tr=-ia|nocap=1}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इकाः|pos=nominative singular}}
* Oblique singular {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इहे|tr=-ihĕ/-ihi|nocap=1}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इकायाः|pos=genitive singular}}
* Vocative singular {{inh+|hi|inc-sap|-इए|tr=-iĕ|nocap=1}}, from {{inh|hi|pra-sau}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इके|pos=vocative singular}}
See {{m|hi|-इयाँ}}, {{m|hi|-इयों}}, and {{m|hi|-इयो}} for the etymologies of those endings specifically. <ref>{{R:hi:Oberlies|9}}</ref>

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|g=f|ur=ـی}}

# {{n-g|suffix for many [[feminine]] [[noun]]s}}

=====Declension=====
{{hi-ndecl|<F>}}

===Etymology 3===
{{inh+|hi|pra-sau|-𑀇𑀅}}, from {{inh|hi|sa|-इक}} or {{inh|hi|sa|-ईय}}. Later influenced by {{bor|hi|fa-cls|ـی|tr=-ī}}, from {{der|hi|pal|-yk'}} / {{m|pal|𐭩𐭪𐭩|ts=-īg|pos=adjectival suffix}}, a cognate of {{m+|sa|-इक}} through {{der|hi|iir-pro|*-kas}}. Also influenced by {{bor|hi|ar|ـِيّ|pos=[[nisba]] suffix}}, which in Classical Persian becomes {{m|fa-cls|ـی|tr=-ī}}.

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|ur=ـی}}

# [[relating]] to, ''forms adjectives from nouns''
#: {{suffixusex|hi|पहाड़|t1=mountain|पहाड़ी|t2=mountainous}}

===Etymology 4===
Borrowed from the nominative singular form of {{bor|hi|sa|-इन्|t=doer, possessor}}.

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|g=m|ur=ـی}}

# [[doer]], [[possessor]]
#: {{suffixusex|hi|सुख|t1=happiness|सुखी|t2=happy, possessing happiness}}
#: {{suffixusex|hi|यात्रा|t1=travel|यात्री|t2=traveller}}

===Etymology 5===
{{bor+|hi|fa-cls|ـی|tr=-ī}}, from {{der|hi|pal|𐭩𐭧|ts=-īh}} (forms nouns from adjectives).<ref>https://www.jahanshiri.ir/fa/en/suffix-i</ref> {{doublet|hi|-गी}}.

====Suffix====
{{hi-suffix|g=f|ur=ـی}}

# {{non-gloss definition|forms abstract nouns from adjectives or common nouns}}
#: {{suffixusex|hi|दोस्त|दोस्ती|t1=friend|t2=friendship}}
#: {{suffixusex|hi|बेवक़ूफ़|बेवक़ूफ़ी|tr1=bevaqūf|tr2=bevaqūfī|t1=foolish|t2=foolishness}}

=====Declension=====
{{hi-ndecl|<F>}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|hi}}

===References===
<references/>

----

