Page 235 قانی قاینامق: Skipped, no changes
Page 235 قانی قاینامق: -------- begin text --------
==Ottoman Turkish==

===Etymology===
From {{com|ota|قان|tr1=kan|t1=blood|ـی|tr2=-ı|pos2=possessive suffix|قاینامق|tr3=kaynamak|t3=to boil|lit=for one's blood to boil}}. This idiom is probably of {{inh|ota|trk-cmn|-}} origin, as can be seen by the large number of cognates such as {{cog|az|qanı qaynamaq|t=to feel affection for someone}}, {{cog|ba|ҡан ҡайнау|t=to get filled with anger}}, {{cog|crh|[[къаны къайнамакъ|къан(ы) къайнамакъ]]}} / {{m|crh|[[qanı qaynamaq|qan(ı) qaynamaq]]}}, {{cog|kk|қаны қайнау|t=to get excited}}, {{cog|kum|къаны къайнамакъ}}, {{cog|tk|gany gaýnamak|t=to get excited}}, {{cog|tt|кан кайнату|tr=-}} / {{m|tt|qan qaynatu|t=to get filled with anger}},  {{cog|uz|qoni qaynamoq|t=to get filled with anger}}. <!--Perhaps also {{ncog|cv|юн вĕрет}} through calquing, indicating a possible {{ncog|trk-pro|-}} origin.-->

===Phrase===
{{head|head=[[قان|قانی]] [[قاینامق]]|ota|phrase|tr=kanı kaynamak}}

# {{lb|ota|idiomatic}} to be [[lively]], [[active]], [[enthusiastic]]
# {{lb|ota|idiomatic}} to have sincere [[affection]] for someone

====Descendants====
* {{desc|tr|kanı kaynamak}}
* {{desc|el|βράζει το αίμα μου|clq=1}}
* {{desc|pnt|το γαίμα μ' βράζει|clq=1}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ota:Redhouse|قاینامق|page=1430}}
-------- end text --------
