====Preposition====
{{en-prep}}

# {{lb|en|now|archaic|or|dialect}} [[before|Before]]; [[ere]]. Followed by "ever" or "ere".
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Ecclesiastes|12|6-7|passage='''Or''' euer the siluer corde be loosed, or the golden bowle be broken, or the pitcher be broken at the fountaine, or the wheele broken at the cisterne. Then shall the dust returne to the earth as it was: and the spirit shall returne vnto God who gaue it.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1834|author=Samuel Taylor Coleridge|title=The Rime of the Ancient Mariner
|passage=I looked to heaven, and tried to pray;<br>But '''or''' ever a prayer had gusht,<br>A wicked whisper came, and made<br>My heart as dry as dust.}}
#* {{RQ:Dunsany Time||3|And Time went forth into the worlds to obey the commands of the gods, yet he cast furtive glances at his masters, and the gods distrusted Time because he had known the worlds '''or''' ever the gods became.}}

