===Etymology===
From {{inh|fa|pal|LHMA|tr=nān||bread, food}}, from {{inh|fa|peo|-}}, from {{inh|fa|ira-pro|*nagna-}}.

Compare {{cog|sog|tr=nγn-|ts=naγn|t=bread}}, Manichaean {{cog|xpr|ngn|tr=naγn|sc=Mani}}, {{cog|kho|tr=nāṃji}}, {{cog|kmr|nan}}, {{cog|zza|nan}}, {{cog|ckb|نان}}, {{cog|lrc|نۆ|tr=nø}}, {{cog|bal|نگن|tr=nagan}}, {{cog|ps|نغن|tr=naγan}}, {{cog|lki|نان|tr=nan}}, {{cog|ntz|نون|tr=nun}}, {{cog|hac||tr=nāna}}, {{m|hac|tr=nān|t=bread, food}}, {{cog|sa|नग्नहु}}, and possibly the {{cog|xcl|-}} loanword {{m|xcl|նկան}}.

