==Arabic==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|ar|ـِيّ|ة}}

===Suffix===
{{head|ar|suffix|head=ـِيَّة}}

# Used to form [[abstract noun]]s from other nouns and from adjectives. Usually there is a parallel [[nisba]] adjective in {{m|ar|ـِيّ}}, with a parallel meaning. For example, {{m|ar|اِشْتِرَاكِيَّة||[[socialism]]}} is formed from {{m|ar|اِشْتِرَاك||[[sharing]], [[cooperation]]}}, with a corresponding [[nisba]] adjective {{m|ar|اِشْتِرَاكِيّ||[[socialist]]}}. It is possible to analyze cases like these as e.g. {{m|ar|اِشْتِرَاكِيّ||[[socialist]]}} suffixed with {{m|ar|ـَة}} to form an abstract noun. However, there are other cases, such as {{m|ar|جَاذِبِيَّة||[[attraction]], [[gravity]]}} derived from {{m|ar|جَاذِب||[[attractive]]}} or {{m|ar|أَهَمِّيَّة||[[importance]]}} derived from {{m|ar|أَهَمّ||more [[important]]}}, of formation of nisba nouns from non-nisba adjectives where no corresponding nisba adjective exists.
# Used to form nouns of various types from other nouns, e.g. device nouns such as {{m|ar|بُنْدُقِيَّة||[[rifle]]}} from {{m|ar|بُنْدُق||[[hazelnut]], [[bullet]]}}.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ar}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa-cls|ـِیَّت|ـِیَّه|ـِیَّة|bor=1}}
** {{desc|fa-ira|ـیت<tr:-iyyat>|ـیه<tr:-iyye><qq:dated>}}
** {{desc|tg|-ият}}
** {{desc|az|-iyyət|bor=1}}
** {{desc|inc-hnd|bor=1}}
**: {{desc|ur|ـِیَت|tr=-iyat}}
** {{desctree|ota|یت<alt:ـِیَّت><tr:-iyyet>|bor=1}}
** {{desc|ps|ـيت|tr=-iyat|bor=1}}
** {{desc|pa|ـِیَت|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tk|-iýet|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ug|ـىيەت|bor=1}}
* {{desc|uz|-iyat|bor=1}}

{{cln|ar|noun-forming suffixes}}

