{{trans-top|strong desire}}
* Bulgarian: {{t+|bg|копнеж|m}}, {{t+|bg|жадуване|n}}
* Dutch: {{t+|nl|verlangen|n}}, {{t+|nl|hartstocht|f}}
* Maori: {{t|mi|matenui}}, {{t|mi|tōrere}}
* Plautdietsch: {{t|pdt|Janka|m}}
* Spanish: {{t+|es|deseo|m}}, {{t+|es|ganas|f-p}}
{{trans-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To have a [[strong]] [[desire#Noun|desire]] for.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=F[rancis] K[ildale] Robinson|title=A Glossary of Words Used in the Neighbourhood of Whitby|series=Series C. Original Glossaries, and Glossaries with Fresh Additions|seriesvolume=IV|location=London|publisher=Published for the English Dialect Society by Trübner & Co., 57 & 59, {{w|Ludgate Hill}}|year=1876|page=227|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=rCU_AAAAYAAJ&pg=PA227|oclc=24890139|passage='''Yenning''', groaning, longing after.|brackets=on}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Alfred Bester|title=[[w:Who He?|“Who He?”]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Dial Press|year=1953|page=205|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=8QAS4PSVI0wC&pg=PA205|oclc=1509090|passage="Listen, I'm in Tom Bleutcher's suite at The Brompton House. Been here the whole Almighty morning. Olga wants you to have lunch with us." / "Olga? Who's she?" / "His daughter. You made a big hit with her last time they was in town. Come on down." / "Get the new writer." / "I got no new writer. Anyway she '''yens''' for you. Come on down."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Peter Jordan|chapter=Acknowledgements|chapterurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=C7ju0i_dZUwC&pg=PA7|title=Re-Entry: Making the Transition from Missions to Life at Home|location=Seattle, Wash.|publisher=[[w:Youth With a Mission|YWAM Publishing]]|year=1992|isbn=978-0-927545-40-2|passage={{w|C. S. Lewis}} warned, "The yen to publish is spiritually dangerous." The "yen" in this case is spread around, so perhaps the danger is diminished! This book has been "'''yenned'''" into existence by many, and is a two-team effort&nbsp;….}}

